The strategy follows the proposal''s numbers exactly, and every number in the rule is unchanged:
- **4h candles:** built from the 1h bars in UTC blocks starting at 00, 04, 08, 12, 16 and 20, and attached with `merge_informative_pair(ffill=True)`.
- **When signals fire:** only on the 1h candle that completes a 4h block (opening at 03, 07, 11, 15, 19 or 23 UTC). On every other candle, and on zero-volume or undefined values, there is no entry or exit.
- **KAMA(10,2,30):** seeded at the 10th 4h bar with the average of the first 10 closes, then updated with the proposal''s formula. If the efficiency ratio''s denominator is 0, it is set to 0.
- **Entry:** 4h close above 1.015 × KAMA, with KAMA higher than it was 6 bars earlier.
- **Exit:** 4h close below KAMA.
- **Constants:** `stoploss = -0.08`, `minimal_roi = {"0": 100.0}`, `startup_candle_count = 4000`, no cooldown or trailing stop.

Two things to know:
- **Incomplete 4h blocks are dropped.** I only use a 4h block when all four of its 1h bars are present. A block with a missing hour, or a partial block at the start or end of the data, is skipped. This is my reading of "built from closed 1h bars"; the proposal doesn''t say how to handle gaps.
- **One test series was changed.** In the start-up test, a straight-line price series never got 1.5% above KAMA, so that test had no entry to check. I swapped in a steeper exponential series. Only the test data changed, not the rule.

The test also checks a hand-calculated KAMA value. For the look-ahead check, the shorter series ends partway through a 4h block, so a half-built block can''t leak into earlier rows.

