**What the strategy does:** it runs on `1h`, long only, with a 5% stop, `startup_candle_count = 800` and no cooldown. It enters when all of these hold on a closed bar:
- the 12-bar return is at most minus one times the scaled 720-bar volatility, which leaves out the current bar''s return;
- the 12-bar return is at most -1.5%;
- the 12-bar volume sum is below the median of the previous 60 non-overlapping 12-bar sums, which leaves out the current window;
- every input is defined and the bar''s volume is above zero.

**Exits:** both exits depend on the open trade, so they live in `custom_exit`, following the earlier H-050 strategy. It exits on the first closed bar after entry whose close reaches the pre-drop price `close(t-12)` from the signal bar. Otherwise it exits at the close of bar t+12, so the order fills at the open of bar t+13. It never exits on a bar with zero volume.

**One change to the test, not the rule:** my first synthetic price series fell gradually, so it crossed -1.5% on several bars in a row and the rule correctly fired on each of them. I changed the test data to a single-bar drop so it produces exactly one entry. The strategy itself was not changed.','2026-11-06T20:45:07.031998+00:00');

