How the rule maps onto Freqtrade:
- **Settings:** 1h timeframe, long only, fixed 4% stop-loss, 800 warm-up bars, no ROI target and no cooldown.
- **Entry signal:** fires on a bar opening between 01:00 and 18:00 UTC when that bar is the first one of the day to reach the threshold. The threshold is the mean plus 0.75 × the standard deviation of the previous 30 daily returns, and the move from the day''s open must also be at least 1%. The statistics use only completed days, and bars with zero volume or missing values never signal.
- **One entry per UTC day:** enforced at fill time, so a trade from earlier in the day blocks a new entry even if it has already closed. A second crossing later the same day can still enter if the first one was blocked by an open position, which is what the rule says.
- **Failure exit:** each entry records its day''s open price. The trade sells at the next open after any bar closes below it, including bars on the following day.
- **Time exit:** the trade sells at the open exactly 24 bars after the entry fill.

Choices the proposal didn''t spell out:
- **Missing day:** if a whole UTC day has no data, the mean and standard deviation are treated as undefined for the 30 days whose window includes that gap, so no entries fire on those days.
- **Missing 00:00 bar:** the first bar of a day has no earlier bar that day to compare with. So if the 00:00 bar is missing and the move first crosses on the 01:00 bar, it does not count as a first crossing.
- **Zero volume:** a bar with zero volume can''t trigger the failure exit. The 24-hour time exit always fires, so no trade is held longer than 24 hours.','2026-11-06T22:31:14.474093+00:00');

