**One change from the proposal:** the warm-up is 400 bars, not the 200 it suggested. At 200, the repo''s own strategy check failed the full suite, because it requires at least 400 bars of warm-up for any strategy using an EMA. A longer warm-up only means more history is loaded before trading starts; it doesn''t change any part of the rule.

**How the rule is built:**
- **Breadth:** the up/down share is counted across the nine pairs on every candle time any of them has. A pair is only counted when it has candles at exactly t and t−1h; pairs with an unchanged close or a missing candle are left out. When no pair counts, the share is 0.5. The share is smoothed with a 10-bar exponential average.
- **Thrust:** the smoothed share is above 0.615 now, and its lowest value over the previous 10 bars is below 0.40. The strategy buys only on the first bar this becomes true, and only if the pair''s close is above its close exactly 10 hours earlier. Freqtrade already prevents a second position in the same pair.
- **Exits:** the 3% stop is the native stop-loss, so it triggers mid-candle. The 24-hour time exit and the breadth-collapse exit (smoothed share below 0.40) are checked in `custom_exit`. The time exit fires on the candle dated fill + 23h, so the sale happens at the next open, 24 hours after the fill. The collapse exit ignores the fill bar itself. There is no take-profit, trailing stop or cooldown.

**What the test covers:** the class settings, a small hand-worked breadth example, that signals are only ever 1, no signals on zero-volume candles or before the indicators have values, no change in earlier rows when future candles are added, and both custom exits. The synthetic price series does produce entries, so the signal checks aren''t passing on an empty','2026-11-07T19:30:32.695489+00:00');

