The rule is implemented as written; no numbers were changed. Things worth knowing:

- **4h tide:** the 4h candles are built from the 1h bars in UTC blocks starting at 00:00, and a partial first block is dropped. A 4h bar only becomes visible on the 1h bar that closes it.
- **Stop:** L = min(low(s), low(s+1)) is stored in the entry tag and stays fixed for the whole trade. `custom_stoploss` returns the distance to L, with -10% as the backstop. An entry is rejected at the fill price if R/P is below 0.4%, which also covers R ≤ 0.
- **Take-profit:** the contract asked for `custom_exit`, but that only sees candle closes. To fill exactly at P + 2R within the bar, I added `custom_roi` (set to that price, net of fees). `custom_exit` also exits if the price is already at or above the target. This copies the approach of the archived H-083 strategy.
- **Time exit:** `custom_exit` closes the trade once 12 hours have passed since the fill. The tide-down exit is an exit signal that fills at the next open.
- **Settings left to the run config:** whole-balance sizing and "one position at a time" across all pairs aren''t set in the strategy file.

My first full-suite run failed one check: the warm-up check needs each EMA period to be a literal or a module-level constant, and mine went through a helper function. I wrote the EMA calls out directly; the periods are unchanged.

The second run had 6 errors in `test_lab_dashboard` because `lab/dashboard_assets/results.js` was briefly missing, so something else seems to have been changing that folder at the time. I didn''t touch it. The file was back afterwards, and the third run passed.','2026-11-08T18:11:27.113432+00:00');

- **Entry timing:** the idea said "entries only on bars opening 00:00-16:00 UTC". I fixed this as signal bars opening 00:00-15:00, so every buy fills between 01:00 and 16:00. That avoids a 23:00 signal filling at the start of the next day, but it is narrower than the other readings.
- **Time exit:** I worded the 23:00-or-12-bars exit two equivalent ways for the developer (by fill time and by signal bar).
- **Expected trades:** I estimate about 200-450 per year per pair, at or below the low end of the owner''s 400-1500 target.
- **Sources:** I could not find a tradingstrategy.ai page for the idea''s source. I cited three real pages I found by search but did not open: the Caporale & Plastun and Shen et al. papers on intraday crypto momentum, and a QuantInsti Donchian article.

