Warm-up is 40 bars, stated literally in the rule, with startup_candle_count = 50.

I couldn''t find evidence that this edge exists at hourly horizons, so the rationale says so plainly. The mechanism is tested on Bitcoin hourly price moves and on daily relative strength, not on relative strength over hours. One study of daily relative-strength rules across large coins reported losses, and I cite it as counter-evidence. The exit (ratio falls below its 4-bar mean) is tight, so the average gross move per trade may not cover the 0.30–0.45% round trip.

Choices I made where the idea was vague:
- **Entry window:** the signal bar must open between 00:00 and 15:00 UTC, so orders fill at the 01:00–16:00 opens.
- **Day limit:** the 2-entries-per-day cap counts by the time the entry order fills.
- **Time exit:** the 12-hour exit never applies. Every entry fills by 16:00 UTC, so the 23:00 exit always comes first.
- **Basket:** for the six non-major pairs, the ratio''s denominator is the cube root of BTC × ETH × BNB.

Sources:
- [Ratio Charts (LuxAlgo)](https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/ratio-charts.md)
- [Bitcoin Intraday Time-Series Momentum](https://reading-9.eprints-hosting.org/100181/3/21Sep2021Bitcoin%20Intraday%20Time-Series%20Momentum.R2.pdf)
- [Cross-sectional momentum in crypto (FXEmpire)](https://www.fxempire.com/education/article/cross-sectional-momentum-in-crypto-how-to-trade-the-strongest-trends-1535830)
- [Erasmus thesis (counter-evidence)](https://thesis.eur.nl/pub/59629/Final_Thesis_Draft_494850-1-.pdf)

