INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-001','SmaTrendBaseline','SMA20/SMA50 cross, close > SMA200, stop -10%','2026-10-20T00:00:00Z','BTC/USDT 1h through 2026-10-20','frozen reference','Original result (1 trade) was a harness artifact. Re-tested 2026-11-02 under the corrected harness (exploration, BTC/ETH/BNB): rejected on all three, drawdown 44-50% at base, 74-88% at stress; lookahead and recursive pass. [Frozen for dry-run by the autopilot policy 2026-11-10T15:01:19.054965+00:00, commit f7ab4db851, strategy sha256 aed7d33e31d2; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-002','DonchianBreakoutBaseline','Close > prior 20-candle high; exit below prior 10-candle low; stop -10%','2026-10-20T00:00:00Z','BTC/USDT 1h through 2026-10-20','rejected at exploration','Corrected harness, exploration on BTC/ETH/BNB: positive only at the optimistic cost, drawdown 60-98%. Do not select by return alone.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-003','BollingerMeanReversionBaseline','Lower 20-band, RSI14 < 30, close > SMA200; exit at middle band; stop -10%','2026-10-20T00:00:00Z','BTC/USDT 1h through 2026-10-20','rejected at exploration','Not yet tested under the corrected harness. Trend-failure risk. [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: correction: the ''not yet tested'' remark above is outdated. Re-run under the corrected harness 2026-10-30 (exploration): rejected on BTC, ETH and BNB. Base net profit BTC -14.8, ETH -19.9, BNB +48.7; profit factor 0.82/0.72/1.60. Source: research/audit/H-003-exploration-metrics.json. Protected baseline, stays in the strategy path.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-004','SlowTimeSeriesMomentum','Use closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. ENTRY: close > highest high of the prior 1440 bars (60 days, excluding current bar) AND close > SMA(4800 bars, 200 days) of close AND no open position. EXIT: close < lowest low of the prior 720 bars (30 days, excluding current bar), OR close below entry price by 15% (hard stop, checked on closed bars). After any exit, no re-entry until at least 168 bars (7 days) have passed. No other filters, no pyramiding, no take-profit.','2026-10-30T13:28:34.345485+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h through 2026-10-30; no result data viewed beyond the context file''s exploration summaries','invalid: implementation deviated from rule','Exploration ran on an implementation that used min_periods=1440 on the 4800-candle SMA (to satisfy a too-short smoke window) and without the 168-candle cooldown (backtest ran without --enable-protections). Both harness flaws are fixed. The rule itself is untested. Recorded results: research/experiments/H-004-exploration/ and the 20261030T133614Z-h-004-* manifests. Strategy file removed 2026-11-03 (implementation flawed; the 4800-bar SMA exceeds the loadable warm-up). Recoverable from git history (commit 544a3d5). [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: classified invalid (rule untested). File removed from the strategy path without going to _archive/; documented exception, recoverable from git 544a3d5.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-005','VolatilitySqueezeBreakout','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. Definitions (all use completed bars): R(t) = (highest high of the 168 bars ending at t - lowest low of the 168 bars ending at t) / close(t). Squeeze(t) is true if R(t) is <= the 20th percentile of R over the 2160 bars ending at t-1 (rolling quantile 0.20, excluding the current bar). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) Squeeze was true on at least one of the previous 24 bars (t-24..t-1); (2) close(t) > highest high of the prior 168 bars (t-168..t-1, excluding current bar); (3) close(t) > SMA(2400) of close; (4) no open position; (5) cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 336 bars (t-336..t-1, excluding current), or via the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: fixed 8% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 72 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2400 bars.','2026-10-30T13:49:38.324198+00:00','No price data viewed; only the context file and validation protocol (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h description through 2026-10-30).','rejected at exploration','Long breakout after a multi-day volatility squeeze in an established uptrend');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-006','RegimeGatedPullbackTrend','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. REGIME at bar t (all must hold): (a) close(t) > SMA(4800) of close; (b) SMA(2400)(t) > SMA(4800)(t); (c) SMA(4800)(t) > SMA(4800)(t-720). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND min(close over bars t-48..t-1) <= 0.95 * max(high over bars t-336..t-1) (a pullback of at least 5% from the 14-day high occurred within the last 48 bars) AND close(t) > SMA(48) of close AND close(t-1) <= SMA(48) at t-1 (fresh recovery cross above the 2-day mean) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when any of: close(t) >= max(high over bars t-336..t-1) (prior 14-day high retested); close(t) < SMA(4800)(t) (regime lost); 240 bars have elapsed since entry (time stop). STOP-LOSS: fixed 5% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 48 candles after any exit. No pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 5520 bars.','2026-10-30T17:42:27.332302+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h through 2026-10-20; exploration results listed in the context file only','failed','Bull-regime-only pullback re-entry with long-term slope gate and tight fixed stop Strategy file removed 2026-11-03 (never ran: warm-up 5520 > 4500). Idea re-implemented as H-010. Recoverable from git history (commit 544a3d5). [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: classified invalid (never ran). File removed without going to _archive/; documented exception, recoverable from git 544a3d5.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-007','RisingTrendBreakoutGate','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. REGIME at bar t (all must hold): (a) SMA(1200)(t) > SMA(2400)(t); (b) SMA(2400)(t) > SMA(2400)(t-480) (long mean rising over the last 20 days); (c) close(t) > SMA(1200)(t). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND close(t) > highest high of the prior 480 bars (t-480..t-1, excluding current bar) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 240 bars (t-240..t-1, excluding current bar) OR close(t) < SMA(1200)(t) (regime lost). STOP-LOSS: fixed 6% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 120 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2880 bars (SMA(2400) plus 480-bar slope lag); startup_candle_count should be set to 2880 or a bit more (at most 4500) so recursive analysis is stable.','2026-10-30T18:29:04.404068+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h exploration-period summary results listed in the context file only, through 2026-10-30; no validation results seen','rejected at exploration','20-day breakout only inside a confirmed, rising multi-month uptrend, with 10-day channel exit [2026-11-03 step 0.3: has_bias on BNB traced to an 11 h data gap at 2019-05-15 03:00-12:00 plus analyzer truncation, not to the code; see research/h007-bnb-lookahead-2026-11-03.md. Decision unchanged.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-008','VolatilitySqueezeBreakout','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole balance. Definitions (all use completed bars): R(t) = (highest high of the 168 bars ending at t - lowest low of the 168 bars ending at t) / close(t). Squeeze(t) is true if R(t) is <= the 20th percentile of R over the 2160 bars ending at t-1 (rolling quantile 0.20, excluding the current bar). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) Squeeze was true on at least one of the previous 24 bars (t-24..t-1); (2) close(t) > highest high of the prior 168 bars (t-168..t-1, excluding current bar); (3) close(t) > SMA(2400) of close; (4) no open position; (5) cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 336 bars (t-336..t-1, excluding current), or via the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: fixed 8% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 72 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2400 bars. EXPOSURE (the only change from H-005): each trade uses 20% of the account (tradable_balance_ratio 0.20), the rest stays in cash. Rule for the number: the largest exposure on a 5% grid for which the seeded block-bootstrap (lab/bootstrap.py, block 3, 4000 resamples, seed 1) 95th-percentile closed-trade max drawdown of the H-005 exploration trades is <= 25% on BTC, ETH and BNB at once; that gives 20% (p95 20%/22%/24%; 25% gives 24%/27%/29%). Only exploration trades were used; the validation split and the final test were not read.','2026-11-02T23:39:49.008873+00:00','H-005 exploration trade lists and metrics (BTC, ETH, BNB) through 2026-10-30; no validation or final-test results seen.','not approved at validation','Exploration: candidate on BTC/ETH/BNB (drawdown 12-14%). Validation (read once, 2024-07..2026-10): profit positive on all three (+6.3/+6.9/+10.3 on 100) with drawdown 2.4-7.7%, but only 12/10/8 trades (gate needs 30, so inconclusive) and profit without the best trade negative on BTC and BNB. Not a candidate. [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: IS->OOS base profit per day: BTC -76%, ETH -76%, BNB -82%. Exploration max drawdown on closed trades 10-13%, mark-to-market 20-30%. Source: research/audit/fase2-diagnostico.md.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-009','WeeklyBreakoutRegime','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. REGIME at bar t: SMA(720)(t) > SMA(2160)(t) AND close(t) > SMA(720)(t). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND close(t) > highest high of the prior 168 bars (t-168..t-1, excluding current bar) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 72 bars (excluding current bar) OR close(t) < SMA(720)(t). STOP-LOSS: fixed 6% below entry (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: 24 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2160 bars. EXPOSURE: each trade uses a fixed share of the account (tradable_balance_ratio), the rest stays in cash. The share is the largest value on a 5% grid for which the seeded block-bootstrap (lab/bootstrap.py choose_exposure: block 3, 4000 resamples, seed 1) 95th-percentile closed-trade max drawdown is <= 25% on BTC, ETH and BNB at once, computed from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost with full exposure (a calibration run, exploration split only). The value is recorded in the notes after calibration; the rule for choosing it is fixed now. If the calibration run shows fewer than 30 trades on any pair the hypothesis is dropped, not retuned. Validation split and final test not read.','2026-11-02T23:59:40.709384+00:00','Context summaries plus H-005/H-007/H-008 results and general literature (tradingstrategy.ai learn pages: Donchian/trend and moving-average timing); no result of this rule seen.','candidate at exploration','7-day breakout in a 30d/90d uptrend: more trades per year than H-007 (20-day breakout), regime gate shortened to match. Textbook horizons, no tuning. Calibrated exposure: 0.25 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.11619927151132928, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.2167829050039351, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.23302999449418582}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 58, ''ETH/USDT'': 81, ''BNB/USDT'': 80}. [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: classified candidate at exploration; validation NOT read. Reviewers: no lookahead or fidelity error. Caveats: largest BNB trade = 80% of profit; bootstrap 95% CI of total return includes 0 on ETH and BNB; base_2x Sharpe beats buy-and-hold and Sma200Baseline (same exposure) on BTC only; daily correlation with Sma200Baseline 0.71 on BNB; mark-to-market drawdown 11%/25%/32% vs gate 7.2%/18.5%/14.5%. research/proposals/H-009.json does not exist. Source: research/audit/H-009-exploration-metrics.json.] [Frozen for dry-run evidence collection 2026-11-04T21:39:32.190375+00:00, commit c48de4fff8, strategy sha256 c6baa8220d58; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-010','UptrendPullbackRecovery','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. REGIME at bar t: close(t) > SMA(2400)(t) AND SMA(720)(t) > SMA(2400)(t). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND min(close over bars t-48..t-1) <= 0.95 * max(high over bars t-336..t-1) (a pullback of at least 5% from the 14-day high within the last 48 bars) AND close(t) > SMA(48)(t) AND close(t-1) <= SMA(48)(t-1) (fresh recovery cross) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) >= max(high over bars t-336..t-1) OR close(t) < SMA(2400)(t). STOP-LOSS: fixed 5% below entry (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: 48 candles after any exit. No time stop, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 2400 bars. EXPOSURE: each trade uses a fixed share of the account (tradable_balance_ratio), the rest stays in cash. The share is the largest value on a 5% grid for which the seeded block-bootstrap (lab/bootstrap.py choose_exposure: block 3, 4000 resamples, seed 1) 95th-percentile closed-trade max drawdown is <= 25% on BTC, ETH and BNB at once, computed from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost with full exposure (a calibration run, exploration split only). The value is recorded in the notes after calibration; the rule for choosing it is fixed now. If the calibration run shows fewer than 30 trades on any pair the hypothesis is dropped, not retuned. Validation split and final test not read.','2026-11-02T23:59:40.709384+00:00','Context summaries plus H-005/H-007/H-008 results and general literature (tradingstrategy.ai learn pages: Donchian/trend and moving-average timing); no result of this rule seen.','rejected at exploration','H-006 idea (never ran: 5520-bar warm-up) with a 2400-bar long mean so it fits the 4500 limit; no time stop. Untested before. Calibrated exposure: 0.10 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17472074793385642, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.24208648328033058, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.20134252321239815}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 145, ''ETH/USDT'': 187, ''BNB/USDT'': 173}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-011','TripleBottomReversal','Closed candles only; signal at candle close, order at next open. Long only, one position, no averaging down. Pivot low at i = lowest low of [i-5,i+5] (ties allowed on the left only), KNOWN only at the close of candle i+5. Three consecutive pivot lows L1,L2,L3 (i1<i2<i3) form the support zone if (max L - min L)/mean L <= 2%, consecutive bottoms >= 12 candles apart, i3-i1 <= 150 candles. Recoveries: H1 = highest high in (i1,i2), H2 = highest high in (i2,i3); both must be >= mean bottom * 1.03. Neckline = max(H1,H2). ENTRY at the first close above the neckline at t in [i3+5, i3+5+30] and before a fourth pivot is confirmed, if no earlier close since i3 was above it, no low since i3 is below min bottom * 0.98, volume(t) >= mean volume of the previous 20 candles. Optional filters OFF in the tested rule: RSI14 higher at i3 than at i1 (positive divergence), close > EMA200. STOP at min bottom - 0.5*ATR14(t) (fixed at entry, via custom_stoploss from the signal candle). TARGET neckline + 1.0*(neckline - mean bottom). TIME STOP 150 candles. Min R/R filter configurable, OFF (0.0) because stop below support and entry at the neckline make R/R < 1 by construction. A pattern signals once and a later pattern must start after the previous signalled pattern''s last bottom (no duplicate entries). Warm-up: 800 bars. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, computed from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; calibration run; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Validation and final test not read. Parameters are textbook values fixed before any result.','2026-11-03T14:11:52.700407+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h and 4h candles through 2026-10-30 (4h downloaded 2026-11-03); results of H-001..H-010 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 (a different rule on the same 2024-07..2026-10 window) - the validation split is therefore not blind for this family of ideas. No result of THIS rule seen.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Triple bottom reversal, 1h. User-requested; reversal pattern, structurally R/R<1. DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 9, ''ETH/USDT'': 5, ''BNB/USDT'': 6} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-012','EMASnapbackATR','Closed candles only; signal at candle close, order at next open. Long only, one position, no DCA, no martingale. z(t) = (close - EMA20)/ATR14. STRETCH: min z over the previous 6 candles (t-6..t-1) <= -2.0. ENTRY at close of t when stretch AND close(t) > EMA200(t) AND close(t) > high(t-1) (recovery confirmation) AND close(t) < EMA20(t) AND no open position AND cooldown. Optional RSI (min RSI14 over the lookback <= 35) and volume (>= mean of previous 20 candles) filters are OFF in the tested rule. STOP close(t) - 2.0*ATR14(t), fixed at entry. EXIT first close >= EMA20 (executed next open); time stop after 48 candles; alternative exit ''rr'' (1.5R target) exists as a documented option and is only an ablation. COOLDOWN 6 candles after any exit. Warm-up: 800 bars. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Validation and final test not read. Parameters are textbook values fixed before any result.','2026-11-03T14:11:52.708727+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h and 4h candles through 2026-10-30 (4h downloaded 2026-11-03); results of H-001..H-010 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 (a different rule on the same 2024-07..2026-10 window) - the validation split is therefore not blind for this family of ideas. No result of THIS rule seen.','rejected at exploration','EMA20 ATR-normalised snapback inside an EMA200 uptrend, 1h. User-requested; mean reversion, a family that failed before (H-003). Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.14187785490232907, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.18023420143817828, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.22869875887657765}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 121, ''ETH/USDT'': 114, ''BNB/USDT'': 129}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-013','TripleBottomReversal','Closed candles only; signal at candle close, order at next open. Long only, one position, no averaging down. Pivot low at i = lowest low of [i-5,i+5] (ties allowed on the left only), KNOWN only at the close of candle i+5. Three consecutive pivot lows L1,L2,L3 (i1<i2<i3) form the support zone if (max L - min L)/mean L <= 2%, consecutive bottoms >= 12 candles apart, i3-i1 <= 150 candles. Recoveries: H1 = highest high in (i1,i2), H2 = highest high in (i2,i3); both must be >= mean bottom * 1.03. Neckline = max(H1,H2). ENTRY at the first close above the neckline at t in [i3+5, i3+5+30] and before a fourth pivot is confirmed, if no earlier close since i3 was above it, no low since i3 is below min bottom * 0.98, volume(t) >= mean volume of the previous 20 candles. Optional filters OFF in the tested rule: RSI14 higher at i3 than at i1 (positive divergence), close > EMA200. STOP at min bottom - 0.5*ATR14(t) (fixed at entry, via custom_stoploss from the signal candle). TARGET neckline + 1.0*(neckline - mean bottom). TIME STOP 150 candles. Min R/R filter configurable, OFF (0.0) because stop below support and entry at the neckline make R/R < 1 by construction. A pattern signals once and a later pattern must start after the previous signalled pattern''s last bottom (no duplicate entries). Timeframe 4h, same constants in candles. Warm-up: 800 bars. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, computed from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; calibration run; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Validation and final test not read. Parameters are textbook values fixed before any result.','2026-11-03T14:11:52.712481+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h and 4h candles through 2026-10-30 (4h downloaded 2026-11-03); results of H-001..H-010 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 (a different rule on the same 2024-07..2026-10 window) - the validation split is therefore not blind for this family of ideas. No result of THIS rule seen.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Same rule as H-011 on 4h candles (counts as a variant of the family). DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 5, ''ETH/USDT'': 3, ''BNB/USDT'': 1} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-014','EMASnapbackATR','Closed candles only; signal at candle close, order at next open. Long only, one position, no DCA, no martingale. z(t) = (close - EMA20)/ATR14. STRETCH: min z over the previous 6 candles (t-6..t-1) <= -2.0. ENTRY at close of t when stretch AND close(t) > EMA200(t) AND close(t) > high(t-1) (recovery confirmation) AND close(t) < EMA20(t) AND no open position AND cooldown. Optional RSI (min RSI14 over the lookback <= 35) and volume (>= mean of previous 20 candles) filters are OFF in the tested rule. STOP close(t) - 2.0*ATR14(t), fixed at entry. EXIT first close >= EMA20 (executed next open); time stop after 48 candles; alternative exit ''rr'' (1.5R target) exists as a documented option and is only an ablation. COOLDOWN 6 candles after any exit. Timeframe 4h, same constants in candles. Warm-up: 800 bars. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Validation and final test not read. Parameters are textbook values fixed before any result.','2026-11-03T14:11:52.715708+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h and 4h candles through 2026-10-30 (4h downloaded 2026-11-03); results of H-001..H-010 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 (a different rule on the same 2024-07..2026-10 window) - the validation split is therefore not blind for this family of ideas. No result of THIS rule seen.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Same rule as H-012 on 4h candles (counts as a variant of the family). DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 33, ''ETH/USDT'': 27, ''BNB/USDT'': 32} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-015','TimeSeriesMomentum','Closed DAILY candles (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair), executed on 1h at the next open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no stop-loss, no sizing hooks. mom(d) = close(d)/close(d-N days) - 1. ENTRY while mom > 0 (and, with the regime, regime_on() true = daily close > SMA(200); vol_regime off per the step-1.4 ablation). EXIT when mom <= 0 (or the regime turns off). GRID (pre-declared, complete): N in {30, 60, 90, 120, 180} x regime in {off, on} = 10 configurations; N_trials for the DSR = 10. Each configuration is also a test at costs base and base_2x on each of BTC, ETH, BNB. Warm-up 400 bars (daily and 1h). PASS CRITERIA TO READ VALIDATION (fixed before running, all required): DSR of the best configuration (N=10) >= 0.95; PBO (CSCV, 16 slices) <= 0.5; plateau (neighbouring N with the same regime flag reach >= 70% of the best Sharpe); Sharpe above buy-and-hold AND above Sma200Baseline at base_2x in the IS; >= 30 trades per pair; lab/config/gates.json clear on exploration. Fail = family rejected and archived. The validation split is then read ONCE, for the configuration chosen in the IS. Final test / prospective holdout not read.','2026-11-04T00:11:34.975802+00:00','BTC, ETH, BNB 1h/4h/1d candles through 2026-11-02; results of H-001..H-014 known, including the one-time validation read of H-008 and the Sma200Baseline cycle table (so the validation window is not blind for trend-following ideas). No result of THIS rule seen. Regime-filter ablation (IS only) known.','rejected (family): configuration H-016 not approved at validation','Step 2, family 1 of 3 (TSMOM). Pre-registered grid of 10; textbook horizons. [2026-11-03 grid explored on the IS (research/grids/H-015-exploration.json): best N30_noreg; DSR 0.999, PBO 0.31, plateau pass, beats B&H and Sma200 at base_2x, >= 89 trades per pair; selected cell registered as H-016.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-016','TimeSeriesMomentum','Same rule as H-015 with N_DAYS = 30 and no regime filter (the H-015 grid winner at base_2x in the exploration split: pooled Sharpe 1.49 vs buy-and-hold 1.15 and Sma200Baseline 1.05; DSR(N=10) 0.999; PBO 0.31; plateau 0.83 of the best at N=60). Closed daily candles via merge_informative_pair, executed on 1h at the next open; long only, one position, no stop-loss, no sizing hooks. ENTRY while close(d)/close(d-30) > 1; EXIT when it is <= 1. N_trials inherited from H-015 = 10 (this is not a new draw: it is the selected cell of that grid; the family counts 11 registered hypotheses). Exposure: fixed share chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure). Gates of lab/config/gates.json on exploration; only if all clear, the validation split is read ONCE. Final test / prospective holdout not read.','2026-11-04T00:34:35.725730+00:00','Same as H-015 plus the full exploration grid of H-015 (which is where this configuration was chosen). The validation split has not been read for this rule; it was read once for H-008 (a different rule).','not approved at validation','Child of H-015. Winner at the grid edge (N=30, the shortest horizon): the plateau test has one neighbour only. Calibrated exposure: 0.15 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.19407518252890127, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.15886218231018612, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.20444195374091295}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 94, ''ETH/USDT'': 89, ''BNB/USDT'': 96}. [Validation read once (exposure 0.15): BTC rejected (profit ex-best trade -5.2), ETH candidate, BNB rejected (ex-best -3.2). Report: research/grids/H-015-report.md. Code archived.] [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: IS->OOS base profit per day: BTC -96%, ETH -63%, BNB -96%. Exploration cross-pair consistency (min/max profit per day) 0.22, below the 0.25 portfolio minimum. Mark-to-market drawdown 24%/25%/48% vs gate 14.0%/11.4%/9.7%. Source: research/audit/fase2-diagnostico.md.] [Frozen for dry-run evidence collection 2026-11-05T17:29:09.726808+00:00, commit 6d59a5711a, strategy sha256 456e194f571e; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-017','WeeklyBreakoutRegime','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance (same exposure rule as H-009). Identical to H-009 except for ONE added regime condition. REGIME at bar t: SMA(720)(t) > SMA(2160)(t) AND close(t) > SMA(720)(t) AND SMA(2160)(t) > SMA(2160)(t-720) (the 90-day mean is higher than it was 30 days ago, i.e. the slow trend is rising). ENTRY at close of bar t when REGIME holds AND close(t) > highest high of the prior 168 bars (t-168..t-1, excluding current bar) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) < lowest low of the prior 72 bars (excluding current bar) OR close(t) < SMA(720)(t). STOP-LOSS: fixed 6% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 24 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. The slope lag of 720 bars is fixed ex ante (30 days); no other value is run, the grid is the single cell {720}, with H-009 (no slope condition) as the reference. Warm-up: 2880 bars.','2026-11-04T13:36:02.214749+00:00','Context file research/context/H-017.md with exploration-only audit facts for H-009; no price data, validation or final test results were viewed.','rejected at exploration','Weekly breakout gated by a rising 90-day mean to avoid post-peak failed breakouts Calibrated exposure: 0.3 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17130307434664505, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.24866607440735666, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.19669332877281875}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 54, ''ETH/USDT'': 70, ''BNB/USDT'': 62}. [Audit 2026-11-04, provisional (gates.json PROPOSED), exploration only: rejected at exploration. ETH failed the gate on max drawdown at the stress cost (25.5% > 25%) at the rule-calibrated exposure 0.3; BTC and BNB passed. Paired against H-009 on the same window and costs: daily-return correlation 0.86 (BTC) / 0.89 (ETH) / 0.98 (BNB); H-017 in-position time lies 100% inside H-009''s; base_2x Sharpe at exposure 0.3: 0.78 vs 1.12 (BTC), 0.54 vs 0.58 (ETH), 0.64 vs 0.61 (BNB); redundant. Longest losing streak fell (9->7, 14->11, 11->6) but the mark-to-market drawdown barely changed (H-017 12%/27%/34% vs H-009 at the same exposure 13%/29%/34%). Single-cell grid by design: DSR, PBO and plateau not computed. Validation not read. Source: research/audit/H-017-exploration-metrics.json, H-009x30-exploration-metrics.json. Archived.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-018','DonchianEnsemble','Protocol docs/protocolo-validacao-v3.md section 2.2. Signals come from CLOSED daily candles (merge_informative_pair, ffill, as in Sma200Baseline) and are executed on the 1h chart at the next open. Four members (N, M) = (20,10), (55,20), (100,50), (200,100). Member state is a two-level latch computed on the daily frame: ON when daily close > max(daily high of the N days before the current day) ; OFF when daily close < min(daily low of the M days before the current day) ; otherwise the previous state is kept ; undefined (NaN) channel values give OFF. Channels use rolling(N).max().shift(1) and rolling(M).min().shift(1) on the daily frame before the merge. ENTRY: at least 2 of the 4 members are ON and the strategy is flat (level entry, including the first candle of a split if already ON). EXIT: fewer than 2 members ON. No stop-loss (stoploss attribute -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract), no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown. Exposure is the fixed share chosen by the lab rule (bootstrap.choose_exposure on exploration trades). Sensitivities reported, never selectable: threshold 1 and 3 of 4, each member alone, the vote without member (20,10), thresholds counted in the DSR N. Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles; the state at the first day of a split was verified equal to the full-history state for 400, 600 and 900 days on BTC, ETH and BNB).','2026-11-04T18:26:46.153196+00:00','Protocol v3 and exploration-only audit facts; no validation or holdout result was used for this rule.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Donchian ensemble: majority vote of four daily channels, no stop. Protocol v3 (docs/protocolo-validacao-v3.md); decisions D-1..D-10 per the user''s 2026-11-04 ''use all proposals''; gates.json/portfolio.json still PROPOSED, so every decision is provisional. DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 17, ''ETH/USDT'': 14, ''BNB/USDT'': 16} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned. [Smoke, lookahead and recursive clean on BTC, ETH, BNB before the calibration. Result: inconclusive by the 30-trade rule (protocol D-2 kept); no gate decision, no validation read, no sensitivity run. Archived. Consequence: the Donchian family cannot be evaluated at daily horizons under the current gate; any change of the 30-trade rule is a user decision (D-2) and cannot be made after seeing this result for H-018.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-019','DailyRSI2Dip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no sizing hooks. Indicators on daily closes: RSI(2) with Wilder smoothing (alpha = 1/2, seeded with the simple average of the first 2 changes); SMA(200 days); SMA(5 days). ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: daily close > SMA(200) AND RSI(2) < 10 AND no open position. EXIT when a daily candle closes with: daily close > SMA(5) OR daily close < SMA(200). STOP-LOSS: none in the rule (published exit only); the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop. No cooldown. No other filters. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). All numbers fixed ex ante from the published rule: RSI length 2, threshold 10, exit average 5 days, trend average 200 days; no grid. Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for SMA(200) plus 200 for Wilder RSI to stabilise; the 1h startup_candle_count is set to 400 as in H-015/H-018, well under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-04T21:41:04.194059+00:00','No price data seen; only research/context/H-019.md exploration-level summaries and the protocol; BTC, ETH, BNB 1h through 2026-11-04 exist but were not inspected.','rejected at exploration','Daily RSI(2) oversold dip buy inside a 200-day uptrend, exit above 5-day SMA Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17410420469738616, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.21622252679628054, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.15089732849803617}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 53, ''ETH/USDT'': 54, ''BNB/USDT'': 57}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-020','Double7ChannelDip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no time exit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Indicators on daily closes: SMA(200 days) of daily close; lowest daily close of the last 7 days INCLUDING the current (just closed) day; highest daily close of the last 7 days INCLUDING the current day. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: daily close > SMA(200) AND daily close <= lowest daily close of the last 7 days (including that day) AND no open position. EXIT when a daily candle closes with: daily close >= highest daily close of the last 7 days (including that day). STOP-LOSS: none in the published rule; the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop. Lookbacks: 7 days entry channel, 7 days exit channel, 200 days trend filter; no grid, no tuning. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for the SMA(200) plus 200 spare; startup_candle_count 400 as in H-015/H-019, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T15:45:17.012151+00:00','No price data viewed; only the research context file (hypothesis list and exploration summaries) and the validation protocol; BTC, ETH, BNB 1h data not inspected.','not approved at validation','Daily Double 7: buy a 7-day closing low above the 200-day mean, sell a 7-day closing high Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.07103916095809959, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.21304422295439313, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.16275232274666154}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 58, ''ETH/USDT'': 66, ''BNB/USDT'': 64}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-021','DailyIBSDip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no time exit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. Daily IBS = (close - low) / (high - low) of the closed daily candle; days with high == low are skipped (no signal, state unchanged). SMA200 = simple mean of the last 200 daily closes including the just-closed day. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with IBS < 0.2 AND daily close > SMA200 AND no open position. EXIT (first that occurs) when a later daily candle closes with IBS >= 0.8, OR a daily candle closes below SMA200 (safety exit), OR the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 12% below the entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: none. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: IBS entry threshold 0.2, IBS exit threshold 0.8, trend mean 200 days, stop 12%. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for the SMA200 plus 200 spare; startup_candle_count 400 as in H-015/H-019/H-020, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T17:23:13.785085+00:00','No price data viewed; only the research context file with exploration-level summaries of earlier hypotheses (data up to 2026-11-05 not inspected).','failed: causality checks','Daily internal bar strength dip buy inside a 200-day uptrend');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-022','ThreeDayLowerRangeDip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no add-ons, no profit target, no time exit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Indicators on daily data: SMA(200) of daily close and SMA(5) of daily close, both including the just-closed day. Let H(d), L(d) be the daily high and low of day d, d = the just-closed day. THREE-DAY FALLING RANGE: H(d)<H(d-1) AND L(d)<L(d-1) AND H(d-1)<H(d-2) AND L(d-1)<L(d-2) AND H(d-2)<H(d-3) AND L(d-2)<L(d-3) (strict inequalities). ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close(d) > SMA200(d) AND close(d) < SMA5(d) AND the three-day falling range holds AND no open position. EXIT (first that occurs): a daily candle closes above SMA5; OR a daily candle closes below SMA200 (safety exit); OR the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 12% below the entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: none. All numbers fixed ex ante from the published method, no grid: 200-day trend mean, 5-day exit/entry mean, 3 falling days, 12% stop. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for SMA(200) plus 200 spare; startup_candle_count 400 as in H-015/H-019/H-020/H-021, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T18:40:32.938103+00:00','No price data seen. Only research/context/H-022.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and research/validation-protocol-v2.md; BTC, ETH, BNB 1h.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Connors 3-day lower highs and lows pullback inside a 200-day uptrend (daily signals, 1h execution) DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 25, ''ETH/USDT'': 31, ''BNB/USDT'': 32} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-023','DailyR3Streak','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (Freqtrade informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no time exit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Indicators on daily closes: RSI(2) with Wilder smoothing (alpha = 1/2, seeded with the simple average of the first 2 changes); SMA(200 days) including the just-closed day. Let RSI(0) be the RSI of the just-closed day d, RSI(1), RSI(2), RSI(3) the values 1, 2, 3 days earlier. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close(d) > SMA200(d) AND RSI(0) < RSI(1) AND RSI(1) < RSI(2) AND RSI(2) < RSI(3) (strict, three consecutive falls) AND RSI(3) < 60 AND RSI(0) < 10 AND no open position. EXIT when a daily candle closes with RSI(0) > 70. STOP-LOSS: none in the published rule; the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop. No cooldown. All numbers fixed ex ante from the published rule, no grid: RSI length 2, entry threshold 10, prior-reading cap 60, exit threshold 70, 3 falling days, trend mean 200 days. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 400 bars (daily candles on the informative frame: 200 for SMA(200) plus 200 for the Wilder RSI to stabilise; the 1h startup_candle_count is set to 400 as in H-015/H-019/H-020, well under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T18:56:37.346980+00:00','No price data inspected; only the context file''s exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h, exploration split) through 2026-11-05.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Daily R3: three falling RSI(2) days ending below 10 in a 200-day uptrend DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 18, ''ETH/USDT'': 20, ''BNB/USDT'': 22} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-024','DailyMaxJumpMomentum','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no other filters. Definitions on daily closes C(d), d = just-closed day: r(d) = C(d)/C(d-1) - 1. MAX(d) = largest r over the 30 most recent daily returns r(d-29..d), including the just-closed day. Jump regime is ON when MAX(d) >= median of the 150 values MAX(d-150..d-1) (excluding today). SMA50 = mean of the last 50 daily closes including d; SMA20 = mean of the last 20 daily closes including d. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: jump regime ON AND C(d) > SMA50(d) AND C(d) > highest daily close of the 10 days d-10..d-1 (excluding d) AND no open position AND cooldown satisfied. EXIT when a daily candle closes with C(d) < SMA20(d), or via the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 12% below the entry price (native intrabar stop, not a closed-bar check). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 72 candles (3 days) after any exit. No grid; all numbers fixed ex ante: 30-day MAX window, 150-day median window, median threshold, 50-day trend mean, 10-day breakout, 20-day exit mean, 12% stop, 3-day cooldown. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 4400 bars (longest daily chain is 1 return + 29 more for MAX plus 150 for the median = about 180 days = 4320 hourly bars, plus one partial day of margin; startup_candle_count 4400, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T19:12:28.530245+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file research/context/H-024.md with exploration-split summary results of earlier hypotheses (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h, exploration only; validation and final test not read).','not approved at validation','Daily lottery-jump (MAX) persistence gate with 20-day mean exit Calibrated exposure: 0.25 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.16914283121968346, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.15549983612983403, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.22363946613512}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 43, ''ETH/USDT'': 36, ''BNB/USDT'': 39}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-025','DailyKeltnerBreakout','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no profit target, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Daily indicators (d = just-closed day, included): EMA20 = EMA of daily close, span 20 (alpha 2/21), seeded with the first daily close; TR(d) = max(high-low, |high-close(d-1)|, |low-close(d-1)|); ATR20 = Wilder smoothing of TR (alpha 1/20, seeded with the mean of the first 20 TRs); UpperBand(d) = EMA20(d) + 1.5*ATR20(d); SMA100 = mean of the last 100 daily closes including d. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close(d) > UpperBand(d) AND close(d-1) <= UpperBand(d-1) (fresh cross) AND close(d) > SMA100(d) AND no open position. EXIT when a daily candle closes with close(d) < EMA20(d), or via the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 8% below the entry price (native intrabar stop); about 2 daily ATRs of these pairs, not tuned. No grid; all numbers fixed ex ante: EMA length 20, ATR length 20, band multiplier 1.5, trend mean 100 days, stop 8%. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 3700 bars (150 daily candles = 3600 hourly bars plus one partial day and margin: 100 days for SMA100, and about 130 days for EMA20 and Wilder ATR20 to forget their seeds; startup_candle_count 3700, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T19:40:05.035504+00:00','No price data was viewed. Exploration-split summary results of earlier hypotheses (H-001 to H-024) in the context file only; no validation or final-test data.','not approved at validation','Daily Keltner upper-band close breakout in uptrend, exit at daily EMA20 Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.12562327750912983, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.0978692427772229, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.23838007584618998}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 33, ''ETH/USDT'': 33, ''BNB/USDT'': 41}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-026','NearHighAnchorGate','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Definitions on daily candles, d = just-closed day: H(d) = highest daily HIGH of the 182 daily candles ending at d (d included). N(d) = close(d) / H(d). ENTRY when a daily candle closes with N(d) >= 0.95 AND no position is open. EXIT when a daily candle closes with N(d) < 0.85. While 0.85 <= N(d) < 0.95 the current state is held (hysteresis: no entry, no exit). STOP-LOSS: none in the rule; the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop (the 0.85 exit is the risk control). If H(d) is undefined (fewer than 182 daily candles) no signal. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: window 182 days, entry 0.95, exit 0.85. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 4400 bars (182 daily candles = 4368 hourly bars plus a partial day of margin; under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T20:08:41.257475+00:00','Context file research/context/H-026.md only (exploration-split summaries); no price data and no validation or final-test results were viewed.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Daily nearness-to-26-week-high anchoring gate with hysteresis exit DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 16, ''ETH/USDT'': 19, ''BNB/USDT'': 17} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-027','DailySupertrendFlip','Signals use CLOSED DAILY candles (UTC) built from the 1h data (informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); orders execute on the 1h chart at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no cooldown, no other filters. Daily definitions (d = just-closed day, included): TR(d) = max(high-low, |high-close(d-1)|, |low-close(d-1)|); ATR(d) = Wilder smoothing of TR with length 10 (alpha 1/10, seeded with the mean of the first 10 TRs); hl2 = (high+low)/2; BasicUpper = hl2 + 3.0*ATR; BasicLower = hl2 - 3.0*ATR. FinalUpper(d) = BasicUpper(d) if BasicUpper(d) < FinalUpper(d-1) or close(d-1) > FinalUpper(d-1), else FinalUpper(d-1). FinalLower(d) = BasicLower(d) if BasicLower(d) > FinalLower(d-1) or close(d-1) < FinalLower(d-1), else FinalLower(d-1). Trend state: initial state is DOWN on the first day with a defined ATR. If state(d-1) is DOWN and close(d) > FinalUpper(d) the state becomes UP; if state(d-1) is UP and close(d) < FinalLower(d) the state becomes DOWN; otherwise it is unchanged. The Supertrend line is FinalLower in UP and FinalUpper in DOWN. ENTRY when a daily candle closes and the state flips from DOWN to UP on that day, and no position is open (flip only; a state that is already UP is not an entry, including on the first candle of a split). EXIT when a daily candle closes and the state flips from UP to DOWN (daily close below the Supertrend line). STOP-LOSS: none in the rule; the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, never a binding stop (the Supertrend line is the trailing exit, evaluated on daily closes). No cooldown. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: ATR length 10, multiplier 3.0. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 3700 bars (150 daily candles = 3600 hourly bars plus a partial day and margin, so the Wilder ATR seed and the ratcheting bands forget their start; under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T20:27:07.052658+00:00','Only the context file research/context/H-027.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the validation protocol; no validation or final-test results; no price data inspected.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Daily Supertrend (ATR 10, x3) long-only flip trend follower on 1h execution DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 26, ''ETH/USDT'': 24, ''BNB/USDT'': 20} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-028','IntradayEarlySessionMomentum','Closed 1h candles only, UTC clock; signals evaluated at bar close, orders executed at the next bar open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. DEFINITION: for each UTC day, O0 = open of the 00:00 UTC bar; C3 = close of the 03:00 UTC bar (the bar covering 03:00-04:00); r = C3 / O0 - 1. ENTRY: at the close of the 03:00 UTC bar, if r >= 0.01 and no position is open, buy at the open of the next bar (04:00 UTC). If the 00:00 or 03:00 bar is missing, no signal that day. EXIT: at the close of the 15:00 UTC bar (the bar covering 15:00-16:00), sell at the open of the 16:00 UTC bar regardless of price (time exit, fixed clock). STOP-LOSS: one fixed 2.5% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (the scout''s original ''closed 1h bar 2.5% below entry'' check is replaced by this intrabar form). At most one trade per day per pair: entry is only possible at the 04:00 open, so this holds by construction. No cooldown needed. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: entry window 00:00-04:00 UTC, threshold +1.0%, exit 16:00 UTC, stop 2.5%. Warm-up: 24 bars (longest lookback is 4 bars from the 00:00 open to the 03:00 close; 24 bars guarantee a full UTC day is present; startup_candle_count 24, well under 4500).','2026-11-05T23:01:54.301603+00:00','No price data viewed; only the research context file for H-028 (exploration-split summary numbers of earlier hypotheses) and the validation protocol; BTC, ETH, BNB 1h as available through 2026-11-05 for the developer.','rejected at exploration','Early-UTC-day 1% rally predicts same-day continuation: buy 04:00, sell 16:00 UTC Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.09899915214743901, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.12515588019739626, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.15248672787544665}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 357, ''ETH/USDT'': 501, ''BNB/USDT'': 485}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-029','MondayEffectLong','Closed 1h candles for execution, UTC clock; the trend filter uses CLOSED DAILY candles built from the 1h data (informative 1d merged with merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed). Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. FILTER: on the Monday 00:00 UTC bar, the last closed daily candle is Sunday''s; the filter holds when Sunday''s daily close > SMA(50) of daily closes (50 closed daily candles including Sunday). ENTRY: buy at the open of the Monday 00:00 UTC 1h bar (signal evaluated on the closed Sunday daily candle and the 23:00 Sunday bar) if the filter holds and no position is open. If the Monday 00:00 bar or the daily SMA is missing, no trade. EXIT: sell at the open of the Tuesday 00:00 UTC bar (time exit after exactly 24 hourly bars, fixed clock, regardless of price). STOP-LOSS: one fixed 3% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (the scout''s closed-bar check is replaced by this intrabar form). At most one trade per week per pair by construction (entry only at the Monday 00:00 open). Cooldown: none needed. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: trend mean 50 days, entry Monday 00:00 UTC, hold 24 hours, stop 3%. Warm-up: 1200 bars (50 daily candles = 1200 hourly bars; the SMA is not recursive; startup_candle_count 1200, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T23:19:08.209236+00:00','No price data inspected. Only the research context (hypotheses and exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses for BTC, ETH, BNB 1h) and the Quantpedia page, as of 2026-11-05.','failed: causality checks','Monday-session long in daily uptrend, flat at Tuesday 00:00 UTC');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-030','OvernightDropReversal','Closed 1h candles, UTC clock; signals evaluated at bar close, orders executed at the next bar open. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters, no cooldown. DEFINITIONS: for each UTC day, O0 = open of the 00:00 UTC bar; C7 = close of the 07:00 UTC bar (the bar covering 07:00-08:00); d = C7 / O0 - 1 (the 8-bar overnight return). DAILY FILTER: build 1d candles from the 1h data (informative 1d via merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so only completed daily candles are visible); at 08:00 UTC the last closed daily candle is the previous day''s; the filter holds when that previous day''s daily close > SMA(100) of daily closes (100 closed daily candles including that previous day). ENTRY: at the close of the 07:00 UTC bar, if d <= -0.015 AND the daily filter holds AND no position is open, buy at the open of the next bar (the 08:00 UTC bar). If the 00:00 or 07:00 bar or the daily SMA is missing, no signal that day. EXIT: sell at the open of the 16:00 UTC bar of the same day (time exit after 8 hourly bars, fixed clock, regardless of price). STOP-LOSS: one fixed 3% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (the scout''s closed-1h-bar check is replaced by this intrabar form). At most one trade per day per pair by construction: entry is only possible at the 08:00 open and the trade is always closed by 16:00. No cooldown needed. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: window 00:00-08:00 UTC, drop threshold -1.5%, trend mean 100 days, exit 16:00 UTC, stop 3%. Warm-up: 2500 bars (100 daily candles = 2400 hourly bars for the SMA(100), which is not recursive, plus a partial day and margin; startup_candle_count 2500, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-05T23:58:43.559204+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file research/context/H-030.md (idea I-013 from the scout, exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and research/validation-protocol-v2.md. The source page was cited from the scout''s note and was not opened by me.','rejected at exploration','Overnight thin-liquidity drop reversal: buy 08:00 UTC after a 00-08 UTC fall of 1.5% or more in an uptrend Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.13128614470588906, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.16457553777213707, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.1825626279763417}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 153, ''ETH/USDT'': 235, ''BNB/USDT'': 260}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-031','CrossPairCatchUp','Closed 1h candles of BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT and BNB/USDT only (the other two pairs are read as informative 1h pairs, closed bars only, aligned on the same candle timestamp). Long only, spot, one position per traded pair, whole allowed balance. Signal at the close of bar t, order filled at the open of bar t+1. Definitions for traded pair X at bar t: r(t) = close_X(t)/close_X(t-2) - 1. For each of the other two pairs Y, r_Y(t) = close_Y(t)/close_Y(t-2) - 1. L(t) = arithmetic mean of the two r_Y(t). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) L(t) >= 0.015; (2) r(t) <= L(t) - 0.010; (3) no open position in X; (4) cooldown satisfied. EXIT: time exit after 4 bars held: if the entry fill is at the open of bar e, the exit signal is at the close of bar e+3 and fills at the open of bar e+4 (position held 4 hours). STOP-LOSS: one fixed 1.5% below the entry price, native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it, not on a close). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 4 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters, no trend filter. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: 2-bar return length, jump threshold 1.5%, gap 1.0%, hold 4 bars, stop 1.5%, cooldown 4 bars. Warm-up: 50 bars (longest lookback is 2 bars; no recursive indicators; 50 bars covers alignment of the informative pairs).','2026-11-06T00:21:48.601429+00:00','Context file research/context/H-031.md (hypothesis list and exploration-only audit facts); no price data or validation results seen.','rejected at exploration','Cross-pair catch-up: buy the laggard after the other two pairs jump on 1h Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.16674868150293887, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.16344308057157353, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.1609015428298164}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 702, ''ETH/USDT'': 575, ''BNB/USDT'': 763}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-032','VolumeSpikeCrashRebound','Closed 1h candles only; signal evaluated at bar close t, order filled at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks, no other filters. Definitions (completed bars only): r1(t) = close(t)/close(t-1) - 1. S(t) = population-free sample standard deviation (ddof=1) of r1 over the 720 bars ending at t-1 (bars t-720..t-1). V(t) = volume(t) / mean volume of the 168 bars ending at t-1 (bars t-168..t-1). Pos(t) = (close(t)-low(t))/(high(t)-low(t)); if high(t)==low(t) there is no signal. ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: r1(t) <= -3.0*S(t); r1(t) <= -0.015; V(t) >= 3.0; Pos(t) >= 0.5; no open position; cooldown satisfied; all inputs defined (no NaN). Store the open of the crash bar t as TARGET (fixed at entry). EXIT: at the close of the first bar u >= t+1 (the entry bar is the first one checked) with close(u) >= TARGET, filled at the open of bar u+1; or time exit at the close of bar t+18 (18 bars after the signal bar), filled at the open of bar t+19, whichever comes first. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 4% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (replaces the scout''s closed-bar check). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 6 candles after any exit. No take-profit other than the TARGET exit. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: 720-bar volatility window, 3.0 sigma, 1.5% minimum drop, 168-bar volume window, volume multiple 3.0, range position 0.5, time exit 18 bars, stop 4%, cooldown 6. Warm-up: 800 bars (longest lookback is 721 closes for 720 returns; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count 800, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-06T09:30:28.082802+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file research/context/H-032.md (tried hypotheses and exploration summaries) and the abstract of the cited paper.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','Volume-spike hourly crash closing off its low: rebound to crash-bar open DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 18, ''ETH/USDT'': 20, ''BNB/USDT'': 13} (< 30 on at least one pair); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-033','HourlyShockOverreaction','Closed 1h candles only; signal evaluated at bar close t, order executed at the next bar open (t+1). Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. Definition: r4(t) = close(t)/close(t-4) - 1. ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) r4(t) <= -0.04; (2) close(t) > SMA(1200) of close at t (not a long-term downtrend); (3) no open position; (4) cooldown satisfied. Pre-drop price P = close(t-4), stored at signal time. EXIT (signal at a bar close, executed at the next open) when the first of these occurs: (a) close >= P (pre-drop price regained); (b) 24 bars have elapsed since the signal bar t (close of bar t+24, executed at open of t+25). STOP-LOSS: one fixed percentage, 5% below the entry price, as the engine''s native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it, not on a close). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 12 candles after any exit. All thresholds fixed in advance and not tuned: shock window 4 bars, shock threshold -4.0%, trend SMA 1200 bars, max hold 24 bars, stop 5%, cooldown 12 bars. Warm-up: 1200 bars (SMA(1200); no recursive indicators; set startup_candle_count to 1200 or slightly more, at most 4500).','2026-11-06T09:46:33.560545+00:00','No price data viewed; only the context file research/context/H-033.md (idea I-016 and tried-hypothesis list, partially read) and research/validation-protocol-v2.md, as of 2026-11-06.','rejected at exploration','Hourly negative-shock overreaction: buy 4h crash close above SMA1200, 24h hold Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.10967774312486653, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.18501567310289702, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.1911558714718198}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 99, ''ETH/USDT'': 171, ''BNB/USDT'': 190}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-034','SessionOpeningRangeBreakout','Closed 1h candles only, UTC clock; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding. OPENING RANGE of each UTC day = the 1h candle opening at 00:00 UTC (covers 00:00-01:00, the same hour the scout''s four 15m bars cover): range high RH = its high, range low RL = its low, height H = RH - RL, midpoint M = (RH + RL)/2. The day is ARMED only if H / RL >= 0.008 (0.8%). ENTRY: on a 1h candle whose open time is between 01:00 and 11:00 UTC inclusive (so its close is at or before 12:00 UTC), if the day is armed, the strategy is flat, no trade has yet been entered that UTC day, and close > RH; order at next open. One trade per day per pair; no re-entry the same day. EXIT at bar close (executed next open), first of: (a) close < M; (b) close >= RH + 1.5 * H (profit target); (c) the candle opening at 19:00 UTC closes (the 20:00 UTC time exit, executed at the 20:00 open). STOP-LOSS: fixed 4% below entry price (native intrabar stop; a safety net wider than the typical half-range midpoint exit, no other stop). Cooldown: none beyond the one-trade-per-day rule. No trend filter, no volume filter, no other filters. Fixed values RH/RL/H/M are frozen from the 00:00 candle and not updated during the day. Positions are never held past 20:00 UTC. The 15m version of the scout (four 15m bars) is replaced by the single 1h candle on the 1h chart as directed; no number is tuned. Warm-up: 48 bars (no indicator; the current day''s 00:00 candle is at most 23 bars back, 48 gives margin).','2026-11-06T10:06:46.254662+00:00','No price data seen; only the exploration-split context file research/context/H-034.md (hypothesis list and cost scenarios) and the validation protocol, as of 2026-11-06.','rejected at exploration','UTC-day opening-range breakout on 1h, wide ranges only, midpoint exit and 20:00 time exit Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.1574684987812517, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.16762179657139728, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.18271047756759975}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 761, ''ETH/USDT'': 965, ''BNB/USDT'': 1030}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-035','HourlyRangeExpansionDrift','Closed 1h candles, UTC; signal evaluated at bar close t, order executed at the open of bar t+1. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks. Definitions: Range(t)=high(t)-low(t). TR(t)=max(high-low, |high-close(t-1)|, |low-close(t-1)|). ATR(t)=simple mean of TR over the 24 bars t-24..t-1 (excluding the current bar). Pos(t)=(close(t)-low(t))/(high(t)-low(t)); if high==low the bar does not qualify. ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) Range(t) >= 3.0*ATR(t); (2) Pos(t) >= 0.8; (3) close(t) > open(t); (4) close(t) > SMA(480) of 1h closes at t; (5) no open position; (6) cooldown satisfied. Buy at the open of t+1. EXIT: (a) signal exit: first bar close (bar u>t) with close(u) < low of the entry-signal bar t, executed at the open of u+1; (b) time exit: 24 bars after entry, executed at that bar''s open (i.e. sell at the open of the 24th bar after the entry bar). STOP-LOSS: fixed 5% below the entry price (native intrabar stop; a catastrophic-loss backstop required by the engine contract, the signal-bar-low exit is the designed exit). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 6 candles after any exit. No other filters. Warm-up: 500 bars (SMA(480) is the longest lookback; ATR needs 25 bars; no recursive indicators).','2026-11-06T10:29:00.378628+00:00','Context file research/context/H-035.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses only); no price data or validation results viewed; idea I-018 text from the scout.','rejected at exploration','Hourly range-expansion bar closing at its high, 24-hour continuation hold in uptrend Calibrated exposure: 0.25 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17594119551913687, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.12327484474042484, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.24195534639108884}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 136, ''ETH/USDT'': 123, ''BNB/USDT'': 98}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-036','USOpenVolumeContinuation','Closed 1h candles only, UTC clock; signal evaluated at bar close, order filled at the next bar open. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. SIGNAL BAR: the 1h bar opening at 14:00 UTC (covers 14:00-15:00). V = its volume. Vref = arithmetic mean of the volume of the 14:00 UTC bars of the previous 20 calendar days (days d-20..d-1, excluding the current day; 480 bars back at most). ENTRY at the close of the 14:00 bar when ALL hold: (1) V >= 2.0 * Vref; (2) close > open; (3) close/open - 1 >= 0.007; (4) close > SMA(200) of 1h closes at that bar; (5) no open position. Buy at the open of the next bar (15:00 UTC). If the 14:00 bar, Vref (fewer than 20 prior 14:00 bars) or the SMA is missing, no signal. EXIT: at the close of the 18:00 UTC bar of the same day (the bar covering 18:00-19:00), sold at the open of the 19:00 bar, i.e. 4 hourly bars held (15,16,17,18), regardless of price. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 1.5% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (replaces the scout''s closed-bar check). At most one trade per day per pair by construction (entry only after the 14:00 bar, trade always closed by 19:00). No cooldown needed. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: signal hour 14:00 UTC, volume multiple 2.0, reference 20 days, min bar return +0.7%, trend mean 200 bars, hold 4 bars, stop 1.5%. Warm-up: 500 bars (longest lookback is the 14:00 bar 20 days back = 480 bars; SMA(200) is shorter; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count 500, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-06T10:53:44.759413+00:00','No price data; only the research context file listing tried hypotheses and exploration summaries (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h), as of 2026-11-06.','rejected at exploration','US-open volume-surge continuation: 14:00 UTC 1h bar, 4-hour hold Calibrated exposure: 0.5 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.16024009361259794, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.21061864795592833, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.24011482961790173}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 40, ''ETH/USDT'': 57, ''BNB/USDT'': 62}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-037','MultiTimeframeMACDTrend','Closed candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, orders executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks. Hourly indicators on 1h closes: MACD line = EMA(12) - EMA(26); signal = EMA(9) of the MACD line (standard recursive EMAs, adjust=False). Daily indicators: build closed UTC daily candles from the 1h data (informative 1d via merge_informative_pair, forward-filled so a daily value is visible only after that day has closed); daily MACD line = EMA(12) - EMA(26) of daily closes, daily signal = EMA(9) of the daily MACD line. DAILY UP at a 1h bar = last closed daily MACD line > last closed daily signal. ENTRY at the close of 1h bar t when: hourly MACD(t) > signal(t) AND hourly MACD(t-1) <= signal(t-1) (cross-up) AND DAILY UP AND no open position; buy at next open. EXIT at the close of bar t (sell at next open) when hourly MACD(t) < signal(t) AND MACD(t-1) >= signal(t-1) (cross-down), OR when DAILY UP becomes false after a daily close (checked on the 1h bar where the new daily value first appears). STOP-LOSS: fixed 5% below entry price (native intrabar stop). No cooldown, no other filters. Warm-up: 4200 bars (175 days: gives the daily EMA26 and the daily signal EMA9 about 7x their span to stabilise; hourly EMAs need far less). startup_candle_count = 4200.','2026-11-06T11:23:09.535008+00:00','No price data viewed; only the research context file (tried hypotheses and exploration summaries through 2026-11-05), the validation protocol, and the Quantpedia page.','failed: causality checks','Hourly MACD cross-up gated by daily MACD uptrend, exit on hourly cross-down');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-038','HourlyFailedBreakdownReclaim','Closed 1h candles only; signals at bar close t, order at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no sizing hooks. DEFINITIONS (bar t = latest closed bar): PL = lowest low of the 480 bars t-483..t-4 (the 480 bars before bar t-3). The bar that set PL must be at index <= t-96 (at least 4 days before t); if the lowest low is tied, use the most recent tied bar. SWEEP: min(low over bars t-3..t) < PL. RECLAIM: close(t) > PL AND (close(t-1) <= PL OR low(t) < PL), i.e. the first close back above PL. ENTRY at close of t when SWEEP and RECLAIM hold, the PL age condition holds, no position is open and the cooldown is satisfied. One entry per sweep (the first reclaim close only). TARGET = highest high of the 24 bars ending at t, fixed at the signal bar. EXIT at the first bar close >= TARGET (executed next open), or at the close of the 48th bar after entry (time stop, executed next open). STOP-LOSS: fixed 3% below entry price (native intrabar stop). This replaces the scout''s ''close below S'' stop with the engine''s fixed percentage stop; S itself is not used. COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 24 candles after any exit. No other filters, no pyramiding. Warm-up: 500 bars (longest lookback 483 bars; no recursive indicators).','2026-11-06T11:46:23.098779+00:00','No price data; only the context file research/context/H-038.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the scout idea I-023.','rejected at exploration','Turtle Soup on 1h: failed 20-day-low sweep reclaimed within 3 bars Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.15948409556081067, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.20976678743322874, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.13365580724882023}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 42, ''ETH/USDT'': 54, ''BNB/USDT'': 44}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-039','WeekendDaytimeSession','Timeframe 1h, UTC clock, closed candles only. Long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance. DAILY SIGNAL: build the daily candle from 1h data (informative 1d via merge_informative_pair, forward-filled so only the last COMPLETED daily candle is visible). UPTREND(d) is true if the last completed daily close is above the SMA(50) of daily closes (50 completed days, including that day). ENTRY: on Saturday and Sunday only (UTC), when UPTREND is true and no position is open, buy at the open of the 13:00 UTC 1h bar (signal evaluated on the close of the 12:00 UTC bar, so the order fills at the 13:00 open). One entry per calendar day at most; if the 12:00 or 13:00 bar is missing, skip that day. EXIT: sell at the open of the 21:00 UTC bar (signal at the close of the 20:00 UTC bar), i.e. a holding period of 8 hourly bars (13:00-21:00). Also force the exit if the position is still open at that time for any reason; never hold overnight. STOP-LOSS: fixed 3% below the entry price, native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it). No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters, no cooldown (the entry is at most once per day by construction). Weekday definition: day-of-week of the candle open time in UTC, Saturday=5, Sunday=6. Expected trades: about 104 weekend days per year, UPTREND true on roughly half to two thirds, so about 50-70 trades per year per pair. Warm-up: 1300 bars (SMA(50) of daily closes = 1200 hourly bars plus 100 bars margin for day alignment and the merge).','2026-11-06T12:11:26.541506+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file research/context/H-039.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and research/validation-protocol-v2.md, as of 2026-11-06. BTC, ETH, BNB 1h/1d candles were not inspected.','rejected at exploration','Weekend US-daytime session long (Sat/Sun 13:00-21:00 UTC) in a 50-day daily uptrend Calibrated exposure: 0.15 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17485390325020234, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.16010904597536457, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.23332921320288014}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 365, ''ETH/USDT'': 367, ''BNB/USDT'': 368}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-040','DailyNR7Breakout','Closed candles only; strategy runs on 1h. Daily candles are built from completed UTC days (informative 1d via merge_informative_pair, only closed days used). Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit. DEFINITIONS: for UTC day D, range(D) = high(D) - low(D). Day D is NR7 when range(D) is strictly smaller than range of each of the 6 days D-1..D-6. SMA50d = simple mean of the last 50 closed daily closes. SIGNAL DAY = the UTC day after an NR7 day D (day D+1); only the most recent closed day D = yesterday is considered, so no entries on any other day. ENTRY: on signal day, if the last closed daily close (close of D) > SMA50d computed at D, then at the first 1h bar t of the signal day whose close > high(D) AND whose close time is at or before 20:00 UTC (i.e. bar open hour <= 19:00 UTC), signal at the close of bar t and order executed at the next 1h open. At most one entry per NR7 day; if no qualifying bar occurs, nothing is entered that day. If a position is already open, the signal is ignored. EXIT (evaluated at 1h bar close, executed at next open), whichever first: (a) 1h close < low(D) of the NR7 day that triggered the entry; (b) 48 1h bars elapsed since entry (time exit). STOP-LOSS: one fixed native intrabar stop at 3% below entry price (a catastrophic-loss cap; the NR7-low exit in (a) is the normal exit and is checked on closed bars as an exit signal, not as a stop). COOLDOWN: none beyond the one-entry-per-NR7-day rule. No other filters. Fixed parameters: NR window 7 days, SMA 50 days, entry cutoff 20:00 UTC, time exit 48 bars, stop 3%. Exposure: fixed share of the account chosen by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning). Warm-up: 1500 bars (50 daily closes = 1200 1h bars plus the 7-day NR window and margin for the incomplete first day).','2026-11-06T12:35:12.686740+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file research/context/H-040.md (tried-hypothesis list, exploration summaries for other families) and the idea I-022 text. Intended data: BTC, ETH, BNB 1h through the exploration split.','not approved at validation','Daily NR7 compression day, next-day upside breakout entered on 1h in a 50-day uptrend Calibrated exposure: 0.35 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.14513556160277166, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.12667573855511524, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.24240659460074057}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 95, ''ETH/USDT'': 80, ''BNB/USDT'': 87}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-041','WeeklyAnchoredVWAPReclaim','Closed 1h candles, UTC; signals at bar close, order at next bar open; long only, one position, whole allowed balance. Weekly VWAP(t) = sum(typical*volume)/sum(volume) over all 1h bars from Monday 00:00 UTC through bar t inclusive, typical=(high+low+close)/3; it re-anchors (resets) every Monday 00:00 UTC. dev(t)=close(t)/VWAP(t)-1. A bar is ELIGIBLE if its open time is Monday 11:00 UTC or later in the same week (at least 12 bars of the week completed, i.e. 12 bars including the signal bar). BELOW-RUN: consecutive bars with close < VWAP, all inside the current week. SETUP: the BELOW-RUN that ended at bar t-1 has length >= 8 bars AND min dev over that run <= -0.010 (lowest close at least 1.0% below the VWAP of its own bar). ENTRY at close of bar t when: ELIGIBLE, close(t) > VWAP(t) (first close above VWAP after the run, so close(t-1) < VWAP(t-1)), the SETUP holds, close(t) > SMA(480) of 1h closes at t, bar t is not the Sunday 23:00 bar, and no open position. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) on the first of: (a) close(t) < VWAP(t)*(1-0.007); (b) bar t is the Sunday 23:00 UTC bar (week end); (c) 48 bars have elapsed since the entry bar. STOP-LOSS: fixed 3% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: none (0 candles); a new entry needs a fresh SETUP. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 500 bars (SMA(480) plus margin; VWAP is non-recursive and needs only the current week, at most 168 bars).','2026-11-06T13:31:29.138879+00:00','No price data seen; only the research context file for H-041 (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the validation protocol.','rejected at exploration','Weekly Monday-anchored VWAP reclaim after a sustained dip, in an SMA(480) uptrend Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.1202444313119522, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.08921277301058608, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.18171919203567055}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 210, ''ETH/USDT'': 236, ''BNB/USDT'': 252}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-042','HourlyInsideBarBreakout','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close, order executed at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. Index bars by t. DEFINITIONS: for a bar i, it is an INSIDE BAR setup when high(i) < high(i-1) AND low(i) > low(i-1) (mother bar M = bar i-1), AND the mother range (high(M)-low(M))/low(M) >= 0.012, AND close(i) > SMA(240) of 1h closes at bar i. The setup is created at the close of bar i. SETUP WINDOW: the 6 bars i+1..i+6. ENTRY: at the close of the first bar t in i+1..i+6 with close(t) > high(M), if the setup is still unused and no position is open, buy at the open of bar t+1. If no bar in the window closes above high(M), the setup is void. While a setup window is open, a newer inside bar does not create a new setup (the earliest unexpired setup is used); a setup is also void once used. EXIT at the close of the first bar after entry with close < (high(M)+low(M))/2 (mother-bar midpoint, fixed at entry from the setup), executed at the next open; this also covers a close below the mother low. TIME EXIT: sell at the open following the 24th bar after the entry bar if still open. STOP-LOSS: fixed 4% below entry price (native intrabar stop; a disaster stop, the midpoint exit normally acts first because it lies at least 0.6% below the mother high). No cooldown, no take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 300 bars (SMA(240) is not recursive; 60 bars extra margin).','2026-11-06T13:53:56.535690+00:00','No price data seen; only the exploration-split summary statistics and tried-hypothesis list in research/context/H-042.md, through 2026-11-06.','failed: causality checks','Hourly inside-bar breakout of a wide mother bar, SMA240 trend filter, midpoint invalidation');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-043','HourlyWilliamsVolBreakout','Closed 1h candles only; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. UTC days built from 1h bars. For UTC day D: O = open of the 00:00 bar of D; R = (highest high - lowest low) of the 24 bars of day D-1; level = O + 0.6*R; TrendDay = close of the last bar (23:00) of day D-1 > SMA(50) of daily closes, where the daily closes are the 23:00-bar closes of the last 50 completed UTC days up to and including D-1 (equivalent to a 1h series of 1200 bars sampled at day ends; all use completed days only). ENTRY at the close of a 1h bar whose open time is between 01:00 and 18:00 UTC inclusive on day D when ALL hold: close > level; R/O >= 0.02; TrendDay true; no open position; no trade already entered on day D. The buy fills at the next bar open. At most one entry per day, no re-entry on the same day after an exit. EXIT, whichever first: (a) a 1h bar closes < O - 0.5*R (exit executed at next bar open); (b) time exit: the 23:00 bar''s close is the last signal of day D, so the position is sold at the open of the 00:00 UTC bar of day D+1 (flat at midnight); (c) native fixed stop-loss 5% below the entry price (intrabar), added as the engine-required fixed-percentage protection against gaps between the closed-bar exit checks. No cooldown beyond the one-trade-per-day rule, no take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Fixed parameters: 0.6 trigger multiple, 0.5 stop multiple, 0.02 min range ratio, SMA 50 days, entry window 01:00-18:00 UTC. Warm-up: 1300 bars (1200 bars for SMA(50) of daily closes + 24 bars for prior-day range + margin).','2026-11-06T14:09:16.313334+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file research/context/H-043.md (exploration-only summary statistics of other hypotheses) and the validation protocol; BTC, ETH, BNB 1h/15m through 2026-11-06 not inspected.','not approved at validation','Williams-style volatility breakout: day open + 0.6 x prior-day range, 1h, flat at UTC midnight Calibrated exposure: 0.3 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.13983640435463573, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.1577696919878171, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.2385899112825307}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 249, ''ETH/USDT'': 262, ''BNB/USDT'': 292}. [Re-run 2026-11-10: owner-authorised 2026-11-10: the stress-cost drawdown gate was removed after the first decision; same archived code, re-judged on the 9-pair universe, 1000 USDT wallet and current gates] Calibrated exposure: 0.15 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.06584161783735952, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.07655474184212042, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.11814574247125814, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.18471825952174592, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.15522724656466017, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.22340425365863179, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.21017392318472775, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.21068738394833708, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.24554465011791388}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 249, ''ETH/USDT'': 262, ''BNB/USDT'': 292, ''XRP/USDT'': 196, ''ADA/USDT'': 217, ''LTC/USDT'': 247, ''LINK/USDT'': 257, ''DOGE/USDT'': 176, ''SOL/USDT'': 194}. [Frozen for dry-run by the autopilot policy 2026-11-10T15:08:33.639243+00:00, commit fb4dda2d84, strategy sha256 8d56d89aec81; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-044','HeikinAshi4hFlip','Closed candles only; strategy runs on 1h; signals evaluated when a 4h bar completes, order filled at the next 1h open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no cooldown, no other filters. 4h CANDLES: aggregate completed 1h candles into UTC blocks starting 00,04,08,12,16,20 (open=first 1h open, high=max, low=min, close=last 1h close). A 4h bar is complete (and usable) only at the close of its 1h candle starting at hour 03,07,11,15,19,23 UTC; evaluate only on those 1h candles, using only completed 4h bars (no partial bar). HEIKIN ASHI on the 4h bars: haC=(O+H+L+C)/4; haO=(prev haO + prev haC)/2, first bar haO=(O+C)/2; haH=max(H,haO,haC); haL=min(L,haO,haC). A bar is bullish if haC>haO, bearish if haC<haO. ENTRY at completion of 4h bar t when ALL hold: (1) HA bar t bullish; (2) HA bar t-1 bullish; (3) HA bar t-2 bearish (fresh flip); (4) HA bar t has no lower wick: (haO-haL)/haO <= 0.0005; (5) real 4h close(t) > SMA(100) of real 4h closes; (6) no open position. Buy at the next 1h open. EXIT at completion of the first 4h bar (after entry) whose HA candle is bearish (haC<haO), sell at the next 1h open; or by the hard stop. STOP-LOSS: fixed 5% below entry price (native intrabar stop). Parameters: HA recursion as above, wick tolerance 0.05%, SMA 100 4h bars (=400 1h bars). Warm-up: 1200 bars (300 4h bars: SMA(100) needs 400 1h bars and the HA recursion, whose seed influence halves every 4h bar, is fully converged well within 300 4h bars; the HA series must always be computed from the start of the available data so that results do not depend on the start point beyond this warm-up).','2026-11-06T14:57:50.812546+00:00','No market data viewed; only the context file research/context/H-044.md (idea I-030 and the list of tried hypotheses) and the validation protocol. Data universe: BTC, ETH, BNB 1h through 2026-11-06.','rejected at exploration','4h Heikin Ashi fresh bullish flip with no lower wick, SMA(100) 4h filter, built from 1h candles Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.219329257046186, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.16772599473388755, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.23261663662561052}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 432, ''ETH/USDT'': 407, ''BNB/USDT'': 448}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-045','HourlySwingStructureBreak','Closed 1h candles only; signals at bar close, orders at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. SWING PIVOTS: a raw swing high at bar i is high(i) == max(high[i-3..i+3]) (ties: the earliest bar of equal highs counts); a raw swing low at bar i is low(i) == min(low[i-3..i+3]) (ties: earliest). A pivot at i is known only at the close of bar i+3 and is never used earlier. MINIMUM SWING FILTER: a raw pivot is ACCEPTED only if its distance to the most recent accepted pivot of the opposite type is at least 2.0%: for a high H vs accepted low L need (H-L)/L >= 0.02; for a low L vs accepted high H need (H-L)/H >= 0.02. Pivots are processed in order of confirmation time (bar i+3); if no opposite pivot has been accepted yet, the raw pivot is accepted. Rejected pivots are discarded. Latest swing high SH = most recent accepted high; latest swing low SL = most recent accepted low; SL_prev = the accepted low before SL. BULLISH STRUCTURE: SL > SL_prev. ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: structure bullish; close(t) > SH; close(t-1) <= SH as known at t (not already above it); close(t) > SMA(200) of close; no open position; cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when close(t) < SL (latest accepted swing low, as known at t). STOP-LOSS: fixed 4% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 6 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 1500 bars (SMA(200) plus enough history for the pivot sequence to settle; no signal before the bar index 1500).','2026-11-06T15:18:22.942083+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file research/context/H-045.md (hypothesis list and exploration summaries for earlier hypotheses) and the idea I-029 text. BTC, ETH, BNB 1h conceptually through 2026-11-06.','rejected at exploration','Hourly confirmed-swing structure break: higher swing low then close above swing high Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.11854105173330083, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.15770529219886578, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.21905705266546002}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 285, ''ETH/USDT'': 364, ''BNB/USDT'': 362}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-046','LivermorePivotFailFast','Closed 1h candles only; signals evaluated at bar close t, orders filled at the open of bar t+1. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding. Definitions: P(t) = highest high of the prior 240 bars (t-240..t-1, excluding current bar). VolAvg(t) = mean volume of the previous 48 bars (t-48..t-1, excluding current). SMA480(t) = simple mean of close over 480 bars ending at t. ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) close(t) > 1.002 * P(t); (2) volume(t) >= 2.0 * VolAvg(t); (3) close(t) > SMA480(t); (4) no open position; (5) cooldown satisfied. On entry store the pivot level P_entry = P(t) of the signal bar (fixed for the trade). FAIL-FAST EXIT: for the 8 bars after the entry signal bar, i.e. bars t+1..t+8, if any close(k) < P_entry, exit at the open of bar k+1. TRAILING EXIT: from bar t+9 onward (after the 8-bar fail-fast window), exit at the open of the next bar when close(k) < lowest low of the prior 48 bars (k-48..k-1, excluding current bar). Before bar t+9 only the fail-fast exit and the stop apply. STOP-LOSS: fixed 4% below the entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 12 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no other filters. Warm-up: 600 bars (longest lookback SMA480; margin for stability).','2026-11-06T15:50:57.968517+00:00','No price data viewed; only the research context file and validation protocol (exploration results of earlier hypotheses as listed in the context) through 2026-11-06.','not approved at validation','Livermore pivotal-point break with volume expansion and fail-fast exit (1h) Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.12441557026302831, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.13875080566765793, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.24385582279206952}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 130, ''ETH/USDT'': 139, ''BNB/USDT'': 136}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-047','RelativeStrengthRatioRotation','Closed 1h candles only; signal at bar close t, order filled at next bar open. Long only, spot, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit. For traded pair X, Y(t) = geometric mean of the 1h closes of the other two pairs among BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT, BNB/USDT (Y = sqrt(close_A * close_B)); the other two pairs are loaded as informative 1h pairs aligned on the same closed candle timestamp. Ratio R(t) = close_X(t) / Y(t). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) R(t) > SMA(480) of R at t; (2) R(t) is the highest R of the last 120 bars including t (R(t) >= max R over t-119..t); (3) close_X(t) > SMA(480) of close_X at t; (4) no open position; (5) cooldown satisfied. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when R(t) < SMA(48) of R at t, OR close_X(t) < SMA(480) of close_X at t. STOP-LOSS: fixed 6% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 12 candles after any exit. No other filters. All SMAs are simple means of completed bars; no recursive indicators. Warm-up: 480 bars (longest lookback SMA(480); the 120-bar high and SMA(48) are shorter); startup_candle_count = 500. Same rule and numbers for BTC, ETH and BNB.','2026-11-06T16:41:31.617240+00:00','No price data seen; only the context file (exploration results of earlier hypotheses) and the LuxAlgo ratio-chart page, as of 2026-11-06.','not approved at validation','Relative-strength ratio breakout vs the other two pairs, hourly long Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.1434644612173721, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.2029651412394719, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.2095115732784192}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 174, ''ETH/USDT'': 223, ''BNB/USDT'': 211}. [Frozen for dry-run by the autopilot policy 2026-11-06T17:22:42.537097+00:00, commit 283a1ffe59, strategy sha256 6effe0f241cc; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-048','VolumeProfileValueAreaReject','Closed 1h candles only; signals at bar close, orders at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding. PROFILE: at each UTC day D (00:00), use the 168 completed 1h bars ending at 23:00 UTC of day D-1. Let lo = min low, hi = max high of those bars, width = (hi-lo)/50; 50 equal rows, row k covers [lo+k*width, lo+(k+1)*width), top row includes hi. Each bar''s volume is spread equally over every row its [low,high] range overlaps (a bar with high==low goes to the row containing it). POC = row with the largest volume (ties: lowest row); POC price = centre of that row. Value area: start with the POC row, repeatedly compare the summed volume of the next two rows above vs the next two rows below the area (if only one row remains on a side, use it; ties: choose below) and add the heavier pair, until the area holds >= 70% of total volume. VAL = bottom edge of the lowest row in the value area. VAL and POC are frozen for all bars of day D (signal bars 00:00..23:00). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) min(low over bars t-3..t) < VAL; (2) close(t) > VAL; (3) close(t-1) <= VAL OR low(t) < VAL (first reclaim); (4) POC/close(t) - 1 >= 0.015; (5) no open position; (6) no entry already signalled on the same UTC day; (7) cooldown satisfied. At entry record sweep_low = min(low over t-3..t), fixed. EXIT at close of bar t (executed next open) when any: close(t) >= POC (the frozen POC of the current day); 48 bars elapsed since entry; close(t) < sweep_low*0.995. STOP-LOSS: fixed 4% below entry price (native intrabar stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 6 candles after any exit. No take-profit other than the POC exit, no other filters. Warm-up: 200 bars (168-bar profile plus the day alignment; no recursive indicators).','2026-11-06T17:23:16.728438+00:00','Research context file only (hypotheses tried and exploration summaries); no price data, validation or final-test results were viewed. BTC, ETH, BNB 1h scope through 2026-11-06.','dropped: calibrated exposure below the minimum order','Prior-week volume-profile value-area low sweep and reclaim, target point of control Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 324, ''ETH/USDT'': 363, ''BNB/USDT'': 359}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-049','FourHourKAMATrend','Strategy timeframe 1h; closed candles only; long only, spot, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding. INFORMATIVE 4h: build 4h candles from closed 1h bars in UTC blocks starting 00,04,08,12,16,20 (open=first open, high=max high, low=min low, close=last close) and attach them with merge_informative_pair(ffill=True), so a 4h bar''s values become visible only on the 1h candle that completes that block (the 1h candle opening at 03,07,11,15,19,23 UTC). All indicators below are computed on the 4h series, index k = 4h bar. ER(k) = |close(k) - close(k-10)| / sum over j=k-9..k of |close(j) - close(j-1)|; if the denominator is 0, ER = 0. SC(k) = (ER(k)*(2/3 - 2/31) + 2/31)^2. KAMA: seed at the 10th 4h bar of the loaded data (k=9) with the SMA of the first 10 4h closes; then KAMA(k) = KAMA(k-1) + SC(k)*(close(k) - KAMA(k-1)). RISING(k): KAMA(k) > KAMA(k-6). Signals are evaluated only on the 1h candle that completes a 4h block (on other 1h candles enter_long and exit_long are 0); orders fill at the next 1h open. ENTRY when close4h(k) > 1.015 * KAMA(k) AND RISING(k) AND no open position. EXIT when close4h(k) < KAMA(k) (no band). STOP-LOSS: fixed 8% below the entry price, native Freqtrade stoploss = -0.08, triggers intrabar on any 1h candle as soon as price touches it (this replaces the idea''s ''checked on closed 1h bars'' wording, which the engine does not support; level unchanged). No trailing stop, no take-profit (minimal_roi disabled), no time stop, no cooldown, no other filters. The same rule and numbers on BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT, BNB/USDT. Grid: a single cell (no parameter grid is explored). Warm-up: 4000 bars (1000 4h bars; the idea''s ~120 4h-bar lookback is lengthened only so the recursive KAMA, whose slowest constant (2/31)^2 decays with a time constant of about 240 4h bars, passes the recursive-analysis gate; startup_candle_count = 4000).','2026-11-06T17:51:09.785647+00:00','No price data opened; only the context file research/context/H-049.md (exploration-split summary metrics of earlier hypotheses for BTC, ETH, BNB 1h) as of 2026-11-06','rejected at exploration','4h Kaufman adaptive MA trend: close 1.5% above rising KAMA(10,2,30), exit on close below KAMA Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.1779335731203045, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.18995121620117594, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.1919195638590925}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 371, ''ETH/USDT'': 437, ''BNB/USDT'': 426}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-050','VolumeConditionedReversal','Timeframe 15m, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, order filled at the open of bar t+1. Spot, long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks, no other filters. DEFINITIONS (completed bars only): r24(t) = close(t)/close(t-24) - 1 (6-hour return). V6(t) = sum of volume over bars t-23..t (24 bars). Vref(t) = arithmetic mean of V6(t-24*k) for k = 1..56 (56 non-overlapping 6-hour volume sums covering the previous 14 days = 1344 bars, bars t-1367..t-24; the current window is excluded). DAILY REGIME: informative 1d candles merged with merge_informative_pair (ffill, closed daily candles only, so at any 15m bar only the last fully completed UTC day is visible); Dclose = that last completed daily close; DSMA = SMA(100) of daily closes ending at that same completed day; regime holds when Dclose > DSMA. ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) r24(t) <= -0.03; (2) V6(t) >= 1.5 * Vref(t); (3) close(t) > open(t) (the bar just closed is green); (4) daily regime holds; (5) no open position; (6) cooldown satisfied; (7) all inputs defined (no NaN). At signal time store P = close(t-24) (the pre-selloff price, fixed for the trade). EXIT (signal at a bar close, filled at the next open), first of: (a) close(u) >= P for any bar u >= t+1 (full retrace of the 6-hour drop); (b) time exit at the close of bar t+48 (48 bars = 12 hours after the signal bar), filled at the open of bar t+49, so every position is closed within about 12 hours, well under 24 hours. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 3% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 24 candles (6 hours) after any exit. No take-profit other than exit (a). All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid. Warm-up: 1400 bars (15m; longest lookback is Vref, 1368 bars, rounded up; no recursive indicators). The daily SMA(100) additionally needs at least 101 completed daily candles on the informative 1d timeframe, loaded through the informative pair, not through a long 15m lookback.','2026-11-06T18:32:53.636131+00:00','No price data inspected; only research/context/H-050.md exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses (BTC, ETH, BNB) and web sources, as of 2026-11-06','rejected at exploration','15m high-volume 6-hour selloff reversal in a daily uptrend with a 12-hour time exit Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.1693542916632191, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.1869657368005031, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.18965367397135413}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 191, ''ETH/USDT'': 297, ''BNB/USDT'': 212}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-051','HighVolumeSessionMomentum','Closed 1h candles only, UTC clock; signal evaluated at bar close, order filled at the next bar open. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. SESSION of UTC day d = the 8 hourly bars opening at 08:00, 09:00, ..., 15:00 UTC (covering 08:00-16:00). Definitions, all computed at the close of the 15:00 UTC bar of day d: S = close(15:00 bar) / open(08:00 bar) - 1. SV = sum of volume of the 8 session bars. VrefS = arithmetic mean of SV of the previous 20 calendar days (days d-20..d-1, excluding day d; i.e. the SV values at the 15:00 bars 24, 48, ..., 480 bars back). SH = highest high and SL = lowest low of the 8 session bars. P = (close(15:00) - SL) / (SH - SL); if SH = SL, no signal. SMA200 = simple mean of the last 200 1h closes ending at the 15:00 bar (inclusive). ENTRY at the close of the 15:00 UTC bar when ALL hold: (1) S >= 0.015; (2) SV >= 1.5 * VrefS; (3) close(15:00) > SMA200; (4) P >= 0.75; (5) no open position. Buy at the open of the 16:00 UTC bar. If any of the 8 session bars is missing, if fewer than 20 prior SV values exist, or if SMA200 is undefined, no signal that day. EXIT: at the close of the 22:00 UTC bar of the same day (the bar covering 22:00-23:00), sell at the open of the 23:00 UTC bar regardless of price; this is the time exit (7 hourly bars held: 16..22, under 24 hours). STOP-LOSS: one fixed 1.5% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (replaces the scout''s ''closed bar 1.5% below entry'' check, as required by the engine). At most one trade per day per pair by construction (entry only at 16:00 open, position always closed by 23:00 open), so no re-entry the same day; no extra cooldown. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: session 08:00-16:00 UTC (8 bars), session return threshold +1.5%, volume multiple 1.5, volume reference 20 days, close-location threshold 0.75, trend mean 200 bars, exit 23:00 UTC open, stop 1.5%. Warm-up: 500 bars (longest lookback: 20 prior days of session volume = 480 bars plus the 7 earlier session bars = 487; SMA200 is shorter; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count 500, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-06T19:17:45.410784+00:00','No price data opened; only exploration-split summary results of earlier hypotheses in research/context/H-051.md (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h), as of 2026-11-06.','rejected at exploration','High-volume 08-16 UTC session surge carried to the 23:00 UTC close (intraday momentum) Calibrated exposure: 0.5 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.1566378256338753, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.1881117693712634, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.23342327488167533}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 68, ''ETH/USDT'': 72, ''BNB/USDT'': 61}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-052','IntradayNoiseAreaMomentum','Timeframe 1h, closed bars only; a signal at the close of bar t is filled at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position, whole allowed balance, same rule on BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT, BNB/USDT. Day = UTC calendar day; slot h (0..23) = the 1h bar opening at h:00 UTC. O_d = open of the slot-0 bar of day d. DEFINITIONS: move_d(h) = abs(close of slot h on day d / O_d - 1). sigma_d(h) = arithmetic mean of move_k(h) over the 14 previous completed UTC days k = d-1..d-14 (same slot only; i.e. the 14 bars at offsets 24, 48, ..., 336 back from the current bar; the current day is never included). Upper band U_d(h) = O_d * (1 + sigma_d(h)). Daily VWAP_d(h) = sum(TP*volume) / sum(volume) over the bars of day d from slot 0 through slot h inclusive, TP = (high + low + close)/3; it resets at every slot-0 bar. ENTRY: at the close of a bar in slots 1..19 inclusive (slots 0 and 20..23 never enter) when ALL hold: close > U_d(h); close > VWAP_d(h); no position is open; no trade has been entered yet on this UTC day (counting entry fills; at most one entry per pair per UTC day, also after a stop-out). EXIT (evaluated at the close of every bar while in position, starting with the bar in which the entry was filled): if close < max(U_d(h), VWAP_d(h)) of that bar''s slot h, exit at the next open. TIME EXIT: if still in position at the close of the slot-23 bar, exit at the open of the next slot-0 bar (00:00 UTC), so every position lasts at most 23 hours. STOP-LOSS: fixed 3% below the entry price, native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it). No take-profit, no pyramiding, no cooldown beyond the one-entry-per-day rule, no other filters. If fewer than 14 previous complete days exist, sigma is undefined and no entry is taken. Warm-up: 360 bars (336-bar same-slot lookback plus up to 24 bars of the current day).','2026-11-06T19:54:09.630796+00:00','No raw candles viewed; only the exploration-split summary results of earlier hypotheses in research/context/H-052.md (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h), as of 2026-11-06','rejected at exploration','Noise-area intraday momentum: 1h close above the time-of-day noise band from the UTC open, VWAP trailing exit Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 927, ''ETH/USDT'': 1195, ''BNB/USDT'': 1184}. Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.18656931081018774, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.18129122129644673, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.16961942604477315, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.17648402346811137, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.20942512059932436, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.24351281604900166, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.1957543265846715, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.18846765223148232, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.16455210468588266}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 1186, ''ETH/USDT'': 1199, ''BNB/USDT'': 1184, ''XRP/USDT'': 1006, ''ADA/USDT'': 1063, ''LTC/USDT'': 1156, ''LINK/USDT'': 1007, ''DOGE/USDT'': 863, ''SOL/USDT'': 729}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-053','VolumeConditionedReversal','Timeframe 1h, closed bars only; a signal at the close of bar t is filled at the open of bar t+1. Spot, long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks, no other filters; the same rule on BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT, BNB/USDT. DEFINITIONS (completed bars only): r12(t) = close(t)/close(t-12) - 1. s12(t) = sample standard deviation (ddof=1) of the 720 hourly log returns ln(close(i)/close(i-1)) for i = t-720..t-1 (the current bar''s return excluded), multiplied by sqrt(12). V12(t) = sum of volume over bars t-11..t (12 bars). Vmed(t) = median of the 60 non-overlapping 12-bar volume sums V12(t-12), V12(t-24), ..., V12(t-720) (k = 1..60, covering bars t-731..t-12, the prior 30 days; the current window is excluded). ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) r12(t) <= -1.0 * s12(t); (2) r12(t) <= -0.015; (3) V12(t) < Vmed(t) (the drop happened on below-median volume); (4) no open position; (5) all inputs defined (no NaN). At signal time store P = close(t-12) (the pre-drop price, fixed for the trade). EXIT (signal at a bar close, filled at the next open), first of: (a) close(u) >= P at the close of any bar u >= t+1 (the 12-hour drop is fully retraced); (b) time exit: at the close of bar t+12 (the 12th bar after the signal bar, i.e. 12 bars after the entry fill at the open of t+1), exit at the open of bar t+13, so every position lasts at most 12 hours, well under 24 hours. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 5% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it). No cooldown (a new entry may be signalled at the close of the bar on which an exit was signalled only after the position is closed, i.e. from the next bar''s close on), no take-profit other than exit (a), no trend or regime filter. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid. Warm-up: 800 bars (longest lookback: Vmed needs bars back to t-731, s12 needs closes back to t-721; 732 rounded up to 800; no recursive indicators).','2026-11-06T20:45:06.527017+00:00','No price data inspected; only the exploration-split summaries in research/context/H-053.md (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h/15m) were visible.','rejected at exploration','Low-volume 12-hour selloff reversal on 1h: buy drops not backed by volume, exit on full retrace or after 12 bars Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.1483377353404899, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.22320029452464252, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.22869641582327827}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 243, ''ETH/USDT'': 287, ''BNB/USDT'': 401}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-054','RoundNumberStopCascade','Chart: closed 15m candles only; every signal is evaluated at bar close and filled at the next bar''s open. Long only, spot, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding. ROUND GRID: once per UTC day, take P = close of the last 15m bar of the previous UTC day (the 23:45 bar). Step S = the largest number of the form 1, 2.5 or 5 times a power of ten (..., 1, 2.5, 5, 10, 25, 50, 100, 250, 500, 1000, ...) that is <= 0.02*P (e.g. BTC 60000 -> 1000, ETH 3000 -> 50, BNB 600 -> 10). S stays fixed for the whole UTC day. Levels are integer multiples of S. ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) L = floor(close(t)/S)*S, the highest level at or below close(t), and close(t-1) < L (so close(t-1) < L <= close(t); if a bar crosses several levels, L is the highest one crossed); (2) close(t) >= 1.002*L; (3) the level is fresh: the highest high of the 32 bars t-32..t-1 (8 hours, excluding bar t) is < L; (4) close(t) > SMA(96) of 15m closes (24-hour mean, including bar t); (5) no position is open; (6) no earlier entry at the same level L on the same UTC day. Record L and S at signal time; they do not change during the trade. EXIT, whichever comes first: (a) TAKE-PROFIT: limit at L + S (the next round level up), filled intrabar as soon as high >= L + S (at the open if the bar opens above it); (b) STOP: at L - 0.5*S, fixed at entry, triggered intrabar as soon as low touches it (implemented as a custom stop fixed at entry, i.e. a fixed per-trade percentage (fill - (L - 0.5*S))/fill below the fill price; plus a native backstop stoploss of 3% below entry, which the structural stop should always precede); (c) TIME EXIT: market exit at the open of the bar 32 bars (8 hours) after the entry bar (signal at the close of the 32nd bar held, fill at the next open). Every trade closes within 8 hours, well under 24 hours. No cooldown other than condition (6). No other filters. Warm-up: 400 bars (longest lookback SMA(96) plus up to 192 bars to obtain the previous UTC day''s last close, rounded up generously).','2026-11-06T21:15:36.022018+00:00','No candle data opened; only the context file''s exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses (BTC, ETH, BNB) as of 2026-11-06','failed: causality checks','Round-number stop cascade: buy the first 15m close through a fresh round level, target the next level');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-055','HourlyFailedBreakdownReclaim','Chart 15m, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, order filled at the open of bar t+1. Spot, long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks; same rule and numbers on BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT, BNB/USDT. DEFINITIONS: PL(t) = lowest low of the 96 bars with index t-100 through t-5 inclusive (a 24-hour low that excludes the most recent bars t-4..t). SL4(t) = min(low of bars t-3..t). SMA384(t) = simple mean of the 384 closes ending at t (inclusive). ENTRY signal at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) SWEEP: SL4(t) < 0.998*PL(t); (2) DEPTH CAP: SL4(t) >= 0.98*PL(t); (3) RECLAIM: close(t) > PL(t) AND close(t-1) <= PL(t) (PL(t) used on both sides); (4) TREND: close(t) > SMA384(t); (5) no position is open; (6) SPACING: no entry was filled at any of bars t-15..t (at least 16 bars since the previous entry fill; entry-to-entry spacing, not an exit cooldown); (7) all inputs defined. At signal store SWEEP_LOW = SL4(t), fixed for the trade. EXIT, first of: (a) TAKE-PROFIT: limit sell at entry_fill*1.012 (gross price level), filled intrabar as soon as high >= that level (at the open if the bar opens above it); (b) SWEEP-LOW EXIT: if a bar u after the entry fill closes < SWEEP_LOW*0.998, exit at the open of bar u+1 (closed-bar exit signal, not a stop); (c) STOP-LOSS: one fixed native intrabar stop 2.0% below the entry fill (stoploss = -0.02); (d) TIME EXIT: with entry filled at the open of bar e, exit at the open of bar e+48 (signal at the close of bar e+47), i.e. 12 hours, well under 24 hours. No trailing stop, no other filters. Note on the stop: the idea''s stop (SWEEP_LOW*0.998, intrabar) varies per trade; the engine requires one fixed percentage, so the intrabar stop is fixed at 2.0% (the depth cap: the accepted sweep low lies at most 2% below PL, and entry is near or above PL), and the idea''s level is kept as the closed-bar exit (b). Grid: a single cell, no parameters explored. Warm-up: 400 bars (longest lookback SMA(384) of 15m closes; PL needs 101 bars; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count = 400).','2026-11-06T21:33:12.131289+00:00','No price data inspected; only the H-055 context file (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) for BTC, ETH, BNB 15m/1h through 2026-11-06','rejected at exploration','15m stop-sweep of the 24-hour low reclaimed within an hour, 1.2% target, 12-hour time exit Calibrated exposure: 0.3 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.1921807897042881, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.20860509698583923, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.22126062640814065}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 183, ''ETH/USDT'': 177, ''BNB/USDT'': 193}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-056','RoundNumberSupportBounce','Chart: closed 15m candles only; every signal is evaluated at the close of bar t and filled at the open of bar t+1. Spot, long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks; the same rule and numbers on BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT and BNB/USDT. ROUND GRID (fixed per UTC day): P = close of the last 15m bar (the 23:45 bar) of the previous UTC day. Step S = the largest number of the form 1, 2.5 or 5 times a power of ten (..., 1, 2.5, 5, 10, 25, 50, 100, 250, 500, 1000, ...) that is <= 0.02*P (e.g. BTC 60000 -> 1000, ETH 3000 -> 50, BNB 600 -> 10). Levels are integer multiples of S. S stays fixed for the whole UTC day. LEVEL AT BAR t: L = the multiple of S with 0.996*L <= low(t) <= 1.001*L (S is at least 0.8% of P, so at most one level qualifies; if none, no signal). This is the level being touched, i.e. the nearest round level below the recent high that price has come down into. ENTRY signal at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) DECLINE INTO LEVEL: max(high of bars t-32..t-1) >= 1.012*L (the 32 bars = 8 hours before t, excluding t); (2) TOUCH WITHOUT BREAK: 0.996*L <= low(t) <= 1.001*L, AND no bar among t-32..t-1 has close < L; (3) REJECTION: close(t) >= 1.002*L; (4) no position is open; (5) ONE TRADE PER LEVEL PER DAY: no earlier entry signal at the same level L on the same UTC day (UTC day of bar t). Record L at signal time; it is fixed for the trade. EXIT, whichever comes first: (a) TAKE-PROFIT: limit sell at entry_fill*1.010, filled intrabar as soon as high >= that price (at the open if the bar opens above it); (b) LEVEL-BREAK EXIT: if a bar u after the entry fill closes < 0.993*L, exit at the open of bar u+1 (closed-bar exit signal, not a stop); (c) STOP-LOSS: one fixed native intrabar stop 1.5% below the entry fill (stoploss = -0.015), a backstop for gaps and fast moves through the level; (d) TIME EXIT: with the entry filled at the open of bar e, exit at the open of bar e+24 (signal at the close of bar e+23), i.e. 6 hours, well under 24 hours. No cooldown other than condition (5). No trend filter, no other filters. Grid: a single cell, no parameters explored. Warm-up: 200 bars (longest lookback 32 bars plus up to 96 bars to reach the previous UTC day''s 23:45 close, rounded up; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count = 200).','2026-11-06T22:02:46.908031+00:00','No price data inspected; only the exploration-split summaries in research/context/H-056.md (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h/15m exploration results of earlier hypotheses).','dropped: no exposure meets the 25% bootstrap drawdown','Round-number support bounce: buy a 15m rejection of a round level after an 8-hour decline into it Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 1001, ''ETH/USDT'': 691, ''BNB/USDT'': 770}. No exposure on the 5% grid keeps the bootstrap p95 drawdown within 25% on 6 pair(s); calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 1565, ''ETH/USDT'': 1387, ''BNB/USDT'': 1409, ''XRP/USDT'': 1375, ''ADA/USDT'': 1696, ''LTC/USDT'': 1466, ''LINK/USDT'': 1672, ''DOGE/USDT'': 2263, ''SOL/USDT'': 1436}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-057','AbnormalDayContinuation','Timeframe 1h, closed bars only, all times UTC; a signal at a bar close is filled at the next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. DAILY STATISTICS (built from completed 1h bars, no lookahead): for each completed UTC day k, C(k) = close of that day''s 23:00 bar (if that bar is missing, the close of the last bar of that day). Daily return R(k) = C(k)/C(k-1) - 1. For the current UTC day d, m = mean and s = sample standard deviation (ddof=1) of R(k) over the 30 completed days k = d-30 .. d-1 (needs 31 daily closes = 744 bars); m and s are fixed for the whole of day d. INTRADAY: O = open of day d''s 00:00 bar (if missing, the open of the first bar of day d). D(t) = close(t)/O - 1 for every bar t of day d. Threshold T = m + 0.75*s. ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) the open time of bar t is between 01:00 and 18:00 UTC inclusive; (2) D(t) >= T; (3) D(t) >= 0.01; (4) D(t-1) < T, where t-1 is the previous bar of the same UTC day (first crossing); (5) no position is open; (6) no entry has been made earlier in the same UTC day (at most one entry per UTC day). Buy at the next bar open. EXIT, whichever comes first: (a) TIME EXIT: 24 hours after the entry fill, i.e. the exit signal is raised at the close of the 24th bar of the trade (the bar opening 23 hours after the entry bar) and the position is sold at the next open, so no position is held longer than 24 hours; (b) FAILURE EXIT: a bar closes below O, the open of the UTC day on which the entry signal fired (the move has fully failed); sell at the next open. STOP-LOSS: fixed 4% below the entry price, native intrabar stop (a disaster stop only; exit (b) normally triggers first). No cooldown beyond the one-entry-per-UTC-day rule, no take-profit, no trailing, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 800 bars (744 bars for 31 daily closes plus up to 24 bars of the current day, rounded up; no recursive indicators are used).','2026-11-06T22:31:13.747169+00:00','No price data inspected; only research/context/H-057.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) through 2026-11-06','rejected at exploration','Abnormal-day continuation: buy the first intraday crossing of the UTC day''s volatility band, hold at most 24 hours Calibrated exposure: 0.15 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.23612032617965523, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.20964710731691813, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.20545710487214586}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 499, ''ETH/USDT'': 516, ''BNB/USDT'': 516}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-058','USSessionOvernightHold','Timeframe 1h, closed candles only, UTC clock; a signal at a bar close is filled at the next bar open. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters, no trend filter, no informative timeframe. US SESSION of UTC day d = the seven 1h bars opening at 13:00, 14:00, 15:00, 16:00, 17:00, 18:00 and 19:00 UTC of day d. S(d) = close of the 19:00 UTC bar of day d / open of the 13:00 UTC bar of day d - 1. ENTRY: at the close of the 19:00 UTC bar of day d, if the UTC weekday of that bar is Monday to Friday (dayofweek 0-4), S(d) < +0.003, and no position is open, buy at the open of the 20:00 UTC bar of day d. If the 13:00 or the 19:00 bar of day d is missing, no signal that day. At most one entry per day by construction. EXIT (time exit, fixed clock, regardless of price): the exit signal is the close of the 12:00 UTC bar of calendar day d+1, so the position is sold at the open of the 13:00 UTC bar of day d+1, i.e. after 17 hourly bars (20:00..12:00). Friday entries exit at Saturday 13:00 UTC. Backstop: any trade open for 17 hours or more is exited at the next bar open (covers missing bars); no position is ever held more than 24 hours. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 3% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it). This replaces the scout''s ''a 1h bar closes 3% below entry'' check with the intrabar form required by the engine; the 3% level is unchanged. COOLDOWN: none (the next possible entry, 20:00 UTC, is always after the previous 13:00 exit). All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: session 13:00-20:00 UTC (bars 13:00..19:00), threshold +0.3%, entry 20:00 UTC, exit 13:00 UTC next day, stop 3%, weekdays Mon-Fri. Warm-up: 24 bars (longest lookback is 7 bars, from the 13:00 open to the 19:00 close of the same day; 24 bars guarantee a full UTC day; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count 24).','2026-11-06T23:12:06.900787+00:00','No price data inspected; only the exploration-split summaries in research/context/H-058.md (BTC, ETH, BNB 1h) and the web sources cited.','rejected at exploration','US cash-session weakness, overnight hold: buy after a non-rallying US session at 20:00 UTC, sell at 13:00 UTC next day Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 932, ''ETH/USDT'': 777, ''BNB/USDT'': 1054}. Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.1881310749271079, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.20779764364748196, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.15398389791577846, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.2587510596977925, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.27734391906908706, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.17859496922543455, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.17302537889699887, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.2004699224868892, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.1980543546528276}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 1065, ''ETH/USDT'': 1044, ''BNB/USDT'': 1054, ''XRP/USDT'': 891, ''ADA/USDT'': 920, ''LTC/USDT'': 985, ''LINK/USDT'': 804, ''DOGE/USDT'': 803, ''SOL/USDT'': 578}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-059','IntradayJumpContinuation','Chart: 15m, closed bars only, UTC clock; signal at the close of bar t, order at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. DEFINITIONS: r(i) = ln(close(i)/close(i-1)). Local volatility s(t) = sqrt((pi/2) * mean over i = t-96..t-1 of |r(i)|*|r(i-1)|) (bipower variation over the previous 96 bars; the current bar t is excluded; needs closes t-98..t-1). Jump statistic J(t) = r(t)/s(t); if s(t) is 0 or undefined there is no signal. DAILY FILTER: build UTC daily candles from the 15m data (informative 1d via merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily close is visible only after its day has closed). The filter holds when the last completed daily close (the previous UTC day) is strictly above the simple mean of the last 30 completed daily closes (that day included). ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) J(t) >= 4.0; (2) r(t) >= 0.006; (3) bar t opens between 00:00 and 17:45 UTC inclusive; (4) daily filter true; (5) no position open; (6) no trade has already been entered on this UTC day (the day of bar t). Store L = low of the jump bar t at signal time. EXIT, first of: (a) on any 15m bar u >= t+1 (the entry bar included) whose close < L, sell at the open of bar u+1; (b) time exit: at the close of the 23:45 UTC bar of the signal day, sell at the open of the 00:00 UTC bar of the next day, so every position is closed within 24 hours. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 3% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (a catastrophic backstop; exit (a) is the designed loss exit). COOLDOWN: none beyond the one-trade-per-UTC-day rule. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: return window 1 bar, bipower window 96 bars, jump threshold 4.0, minimum bar return 0.006 log, entry window 00:00-17:45 UTC, daily mean 30 days, time exit 23:45 bar close, stop 3%. Warm-up: 3072 bars (30 completed daily closes need up to 31 UTC days = 2976 15m bars; the bipower window needs 98 bars; 3072 = 32 days gives margin; no recursive indicators; under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-06T23:54:31.238055+00:00','No price data opened; only the context file research/context/H-059.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses for BTC, ETH, BNB 1h) and the web sources listed, through 2026-11-06.','rejected at exploration','Intraday positive-jump continuation: buy a 15m bipower-scaled jump, hold to the UTC day close Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17210147269514461, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.15066120614650888, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.17409235028559686, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.30268006283392457, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.2464124890385785, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.24393045868328278, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.21774358911770125, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.40268046595917845, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.1849513334862245}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 304, ''ETH/USDT'': 298, ''BNB/USDT'': 269, ''XRP/USDT'': 253, ''ADA/USDT'': 209, ''LTC/USDT'': 290, ''LINK/USDT'': 189, ''DOGE/USDT'': 205, ''SOL/USDT'': 147}. Breadth: candidate on 2 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-060','SameSlotPeriodicity','Chart 1h, closed bars only, all times UTC; a signal at a bar close fills at the next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. BLOCKS: each UTC day is split into six 4-hour blocks b in {0,1,2,3,4,5} starting at 00:00, 04:00, 08:00, 12:00, 16:00, 20:00 UTC; each block has four 1h bars (open times hh, hh+1, hh+2, hh+3). BLOCK RETURN R(d,b) = close of the bar opening at hh+3 on day d / open of the bar opening at hh on day d - 1; it is defined only if all four bars of that block exist, otherwise it is missing. DAILY SELECTION (once per day, fixed for the whole of day d): at the close of the 23:00 bar of day d-1, for each block b compute M(b) = arithmetic mean of R(d-k,b) for k = 1..28 (the 28 completed days d-1 ... d-28, i.e. 672 bars back) and H(b) = count of those 28 returns that are > 0, divided by 28. If any of the 28 returns for a block is missing, that block is not eligible that day. b* = the eligible block with the largest M(b); ties go to the earliest block in the day. ENTRY: if M(b*) >= 0.0040 AND H(b*) >= 16/28 (0.5714), buy at the open of the first bar of block b* on day d (in practice: entry signal at the close of the bar opening at hh-1, i.e. the 23:00 bar of day d-1 for block 0, filled at the next open). If no block passes, no trade that day. At most one entry per pair per UTC day. EXIT (time exit): sell at the close of the 4th bar of block b* (the bar opening at hh+3), filled at the next bar open, so the hold is exactly 4 bars (4 hours); this is far inside the 24-hour limit. STOP-LOSS: fixed 3% below the entry price, native intrabar stop. No take-profit, no trailing stop, no cooldown beyond the one-entry-per-day limit, no other filters, no daily indicators. Same rule and parameters on all nine pairs. Warm-up: 720 bars (672 bars for the 28-day window plus up to 24 bars to align to the UTC day boundary, rounded up).','2026-11-07T12:31:07.205010+00:00','No price data inspected; only research/context/H-060.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses on BTC, ETH, BNB 1h) and the validation protocol.','rejected at exploration','Same-time-of-day periodicity: hold the UTC 4-hour block with the strongest trailing 28-day same-block return Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 644, ''ETH/USDT'': 813, ''BNB/USDT'': 970, ''XRP/USDT'': 928, ''ADA/USDT'': 984, ''LTC/USDT'': 665, ''LINK/USDT'': 870, ''DOGE/USDT'': 596, ''SOL/USDT'': 763}. Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.11749238276634741, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.17385339197659444, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.1452193390980254, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.12559953315124767, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.1496088525188981, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.1873618307023489, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.1866145816079706, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.1357432476809834, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.13901985164414624}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 644, ''ETH/USDT'': 813, ''BNB/USDT'': 970, ''XRP/USDT'': 928, ''ADA/USDT'': 984, ''LTC/USDT'': 820, ''LINK/USDT'': 1021, ''DOGE/USDT'': 596, ''SOL/USDT'': 763}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-061','DailyPivotS1Reclaim','Chart 15m, closed bars only, all times UTC; a signal at bar close fills at the next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. DAILY LEVELS: from the previous completed UTC day (its 96 15m bars, 00:00-23:45; equivalently the closed 1d candle via merge_informative_pair, shifted so only the completed prior day is used) take high H, low L, close C. P=(H+L+C)/3, S1=2*P-H, S2=P-(H-L). These levels are constant for the whole current UTC day. ARMING: the day is armed only if (P-S1)/S1 >= 0.008. ENTRY at the close of bar t (open time 00:00 to 19:45 UTC inclusive) of an armed day when ALL hold: (1) min(low over bars t-3..t) < S1 (today''s S1); (2) close(t) > S1 AND (close(t-1) <= S1 OR low(t) < S1); (3) no bar of the current UTC day from 00:00 through t has low <= S2; (4) no open position and no entry signal has already been taken earlier in the current UTC day (max one trade per UTC day). At entry record SweepLow = min(low over bars t-3..t) and the day''s P. EXIT (signal at bar close, fill at next open) at the first of: (a) TARGET close >= P; (b) STRUCTURE STOP close < SweepLow; (c) TIME EXIT at the close of the 23:45 UTC bar of the entry day (fills at 00:00 open; maximum holding under 24 hours). STOP-LOSS: native fixed stop 3% below entry price (intrabar, catastrophic backstop only). No cooldown beyond the one-trade-per-day rule, no take-profit other than (a), no trailing, no pyramiding, no other filters. Lookback: 96 bars for the prior day plus 4 bars for the sweep window = 100 bars. Warm-up: 200 bars (two full UTC days plus the 4-bar window, so the first complete prior day is always available; no recursive indicators are used).','2026-11-07T12:53:11.905314+00:00','No price data inspected; only research/context/H-061.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the cited web page, as of 2026-11-07.','rejected at exploration','Daily floor-pivot S1 reclaim on 15m: buy the close back above S1, target the pivot, flat by UTC day end Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 554, ''ETH/USDT'': 753, ''BNB/USDT'': 709, ''XRP/USDT'': 691, ''ADA/USDT'': 726, ''LTC/USDT'': 751, ''LINK/USDT'': 519, ''DOGE/USDT'': 549, ''SOL/USDT'': 451}. Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.174934060268072, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.14851456319705855, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.16987109234265574, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.13599623566010605, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.1629536313961083, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.14487608649866546, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.1862280512744616, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.10447329450718072, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.12927386154691586}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 665, ''ETH/USDT'': 753, ''BNB/USDT'': 721, ''XRP/USDT'': 691, ''ADA/USDT'': 726, ''LTC/USDT'': 751, ''LINK/USDT'': 629, ''DOGE/USDT'': 549, ''SOL/USDT'': 451}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-062','VolumeSpikeCrashRebound','Chart 15m, closed candles only; signal at the close of bar t, order filled at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks, no trend/daily or other filters. Definitions (completed bars only): r(i) = close(i)/close(i-1) - 1. sigma(t) = sample standard deviation (ddof=1) of r over the 672 bars t-672..t-1 (7 days; current bar excluded). Vmed(t) = median volume of the 96 bars t-96..t-1 (1 day; current bar excluded). Shock bar return b(t) = close(t)/open(t) - 1. ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) b(t) <= -max(0.008, 3.0*sigma(t)); (2) volume(t) >= 3.0*Vmed(t); (3) no open position; (4) cooldown satisfied (at least 8 bars since the last exit); (5) all inputs defined (no NaN). At signal time store TARGET = open(t) and FLOOR = 0.99*low(t) of the shock bar (both fixed for the trade). EXIT (signal at a bar close, filled at the next bar open), first of: (a) full retrace: close(u) >= TARGET at the close of any bar u >= t+1 (the entry bar is the first bar checked); (b) breakdown exit: close(u) < FLOOR at the close of any bar u >= t+1; (c) time exit: at the close of bar t+16 (the 16th bar after entry, 4 hours), filled at the open of bar t+17. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 3% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (a catastrophe backstop; the scout''s closed-bar condition (b) is kept as an exit signal, not as the stop). COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 8 candles after any exit. No take-profit other than exit (a). Every position closes within 17 bars (4.25 hours) of the signal, well under 24 hours. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: 672-bar volatility window, 3.0 sigma, 0.8% minimum drop, 96-bar median volume window, volume multiple 3.0, floor 0.99 x shock-bar low, time exit 16 bars, stop 3%, cooldown 8. Warm-up: 700 bars (longest lookback is 673 closes for 672 returns; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count 700, under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-07T13:18:03.698974+00:00','No candle data read; only the context file research/context/H-062.md (exploration-split summary results of earlier hypotheses) and the paper abstract page.','rejected at exploration','15m aggressive-selling bar reversal: volume-confirmed 3-sigma red bar, exit on full retrace or 4 hours Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 605, ''ETH/USDT'': 453, ''BNB/USDT'': 877, ''XRP/USDT'': 881, ''ADA/USDT'': 788, ''LTC/USDT'': 881, ''LINK/USDT'': 789, ''DOGE/USDT'': 765, ''SOL/USDT'': 553}. Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.2213770293559952, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.2519308941934251, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.1697920829990641, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.16334986018129374, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.1785184005067088, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.18537989842260813, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.11888087062919761, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.17281157977407868, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.10090760603183933}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 955, ''ETH/USDT'': 1040, ''BNB/USDT'': 877, ''XRP/USDT'': 881, ''ADA/USDT'': 951, ''LTC/USDT'': 1037, ''LINK/USDT'': 789, ''DOGE/USDT'': 765, ''SOL/USDT'': 553}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-063','VarianceRatioRegimeBreakout','Chart 15m, closed candles only; a signal at the close of bar t is executed at the open of bar t+1. Long only, one position at a time, whole balance, same rule and parameters on every pair. DEFINITIONS: r(i) = ln(close(i)/close(i-1)). VARIANCE RATIO VR(t) over the 384-bar window of returns r(t-383..t): q(i) = r(i-3)+r(i-2)+r(i-1)+r(i) (overlapping 4-bar sums), taken for i = t-380..t so all its returns lie inside the window (381 values); VR(t) = sample variance (ddof=1) of those q(i) / (4 * sample variance (ddof=1) of r(t-383..t)). In pandas: q = r.rolling(4).sum(); VR = q.rolling(381).var() / (4 * r.rolling(384).var()). HTF FILTER: build 4h candles from the 15m data in UTC blocks starting 00,04,08,12,16,20 (informative 4h via merge_informative_pair, ffill, so only COMPLETED 4h candles are visible); the filter is true when the last completed 4h close > simple mean of the last 50 completed 4h closes (that close included). ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) close(t) > highest high of bars t-96..t-1 (prior 24 hours, current bar excluded); (2) VR(t) >= 1.10; (3) HTF filter true; (4) no open position. No cooldown. EXIT, the first of: (a) at the close of any bar after the entry bar, close < lowest low of the prior 16 bars (current bar excluded) -> sell at the next open; (b) TIME EXIT: at the close of the 96th 15m bar counted from the entry bar (the bar whose open was the fill), sell at the next open, so no position lasts more than 24 hours; (c) STOP-LOSS: fixed 5% below the entry price, native intrabar stop (protective only; exits (a) and (b) are the intended exits). No take-profit, no trailing stop, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 900 bars (4h SMA50 = 800 bars of 15m plus up to 15 bars of 4h-block alignment, rounded up; the VR window needs 385). startup_candle_count = 900.','2026-11-07T13:47:53.930488+00:00','No price data viewed; only the research context file research/context/H-063.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the validation protocol, through 2026-11-07.','rejected at exploration','Variance-ratio regime gate: 15m 24-hour-high breakout only when short-horizon returns trend Calibrated exposure: 0.25 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.2083995156129031, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.1600273834410105, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.21927482494160855, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.22806184570777602, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.25150152576289986, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.1719949926272899, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.24105051641766553, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.19258612886804072, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.1736083982627351}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 92, ''ETH/USDT'': 132, ''BNB/USDT'': 74, ''XRP/USDT'': 72, ''ADA/USDT'': 66, ''LTC/USDT'': 97, ''LINK/USDT'': 71, ''DOGE/USDT'': 41, ''SOL/USDT'': 70}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-064','SameSlotPeriodicity','Chart 1h, closed bars only, all times UTC; a signal at a bar close fills at the next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, same rule and parameters on all nine pairs. SLOTS: each UTC day is split into six 4-hour blocks b in {0..5} starting at 00:00, 04:00, 08:00, 12:00, 16:00, 20:00 UTC; each block has four 1h bars (open times hh, hh+1, hh+2, hh+3). A slot is (UTC weekday, block), 42 slots per week. SLOT RETURN R(d,b) = close of the bar opening at hh+3 on day d / open of the bar opening at hh on day d - 1; missing if any of the four bars is missing. DAILY SELECTION (once per day d, fixed for all of day d): at the close of the 23:00 bar of day d-1, for each block b of day d use the 26 observations R(d-7k, b), k = 1..26 (same weekday and block in the previous 26 weeks, up to 4368 bars back). Compute mean m(b), sample std s(b) with ddof=1, and t(b) = m(b) / (s(b) / sqrt(26)). A block is ineligible if any of its 26 observations is missing or s(b) = 0. b* = the eligible block with the largest t(b); ties go to the earliest block of the day. ENTRY: only if m(b*) >= 0.0040 AND t(b*) >= 1.5, buy at the open of the first bar of block b* on day d (entry signal at the close of the bar opening at hh-1; for block 0 that is the 23:00 bar of day d-1). If b* fails either threshold, no trade that day (no fallback to another block). At most one entry per pair per UTC day; if a position is still open when the entry signal fires, skip that entry. EXIT (time exit): exit signal at the close of the 4th bar of block b* (bar opening at hh+3), filled at the next bar open, so the hold is 4 bars (4 hours), far inside the 24-hour limit. STOP-LOSS: fixed 3% below the entry price, native intrabar stop. No take-profit, no trailing stop, no cooldown beyond the one-entry-per-day limit, no other filters. Warm-up: 4400 bars (4368 bars for 26 weeks of same-slot history plus up to 24 bars to align to the UTC day boundary, 4392, rounded up).','2026-11-07T14:46:41.023208+00:00','No price data opened; only research/context/H-064.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the source paper abstract page.','rejected at exploration','Hour-of-week periodicity: trade the weekday 4-hour block with a persistent 26-week same-slot drift Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.20368100165296107, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.2814581210381689, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.20945877143552602, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.2314073317848625, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.277642564015649, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.2304191742053566, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.2818435725299387, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.22096306815754718, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.20077470078744347}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 603, ''ETH/USDT'': 866, ''BNB/USDT'': 856, ''XRP/USDT'': 780, ''ADA/USDT'': 828, ''LTC/USDT'': 767, ''LINK/USDT'': 821, ''DOGE/USDT'': 612, ''SOL/USDT'': 540}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-065','ADXRegimeSwitch','Chart 1h, closed bars only; every signal is evaluated at the close of bar t and filled at the open of bar t+1. Spot, long only, one position at a time, whole balance. Indicators on 1h close/high/low: ADX(14), +DI(14), -DI(14) with Wilder smoothing; ATR(14) with Wilder smoothing; ATRp(t) = ATR14(t)/close(t); MED(t) = median of ATRp over the 720 bars t-720..t-1 (excluding the current bar); EMA(10) and EMA(30) of close; RSI(14) of close with Wilder smoothing. TREND regime at t: ADX(t) >= 25 AND +DI(t) > -DI(t) AND ATRp(t) >= MED(t). RANGE regime at t: ADX(t) < 20 (the two regimes are mutually exclusive; ADX in [20,25) is neither, no entry). TREND ENTRY (tag ''trend''): TREND regime at t AND EMA10(t) > 1.002*EMA30(t) AND EMA10(t-1) <= 1.002*EMA30(t-1). RANGE ENTRY (tag ''range''): RANGE regime at t AND RSI14(t) < 30. If both were ever true on the same bar, the trend entry takes precedence. Entries require no open position and the cooldown satisfied. EXITS depend on the tag set at entry, whatever the current regime: a ''trend'' trade exits at the first close with EMA10(t) < EMA30(t); a ''range'' trade exits at the first close with RSI14(t) >= 50. TIME EXIT for both: if the trade is still open at the close of the 24th 1h bar counted from the entry bar (the entry fill bar is bar 1), exit at the next open, i.e. at most 24 hours after entry. STOP-LOSS for both: fixed 3% below the entry price, native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it). COOLDOWN: no new entry for 4 candles after any exit. No take-profit, no trailing stop, no pyramiding, no other filters. Longest lookback: 720-bar median of ATRp plus 14-bar ATR = 734 bars; Warm-up: 1000 bars (extra margin for the recursive Wilder/EMA indicators; startup_candle_count = 1000).','2026-11-07T15:26:42.548191+00:00','No price data inspected; only the research context file research/context/H-065.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the cited forum page, as of 2026-11-07.','rejected at exploration','ADX/volatility regime switch on 1h: EMA cross entries in trending high-vol regime, RSI dips in quiet range, 24h cap Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.18859519094023158, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.16407196890417977, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.19822545208762857, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.2158574104337331, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.21313795802137614, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.16440780660731152, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.1364750216836138, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.17258135893352522, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.12401137265557007}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 211, ''ETH/USDT'': 193, ''BNB/USDT'': 168, ''XRP/USDT'': 182, ''ADA/USDT'': 160, ''LTC/USDT'': 173, ''LINK/USDT'': 139, ''DOGE/USDT'': 130, ''SOL/USDT'': 102}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-066','HourlyKeltnerMTFBreakout','Chart 1h, closed bars only; a signal at the close of bar t is filled at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position at a time, whole balance. 1h indicators: EMA50 = EMA(50) of close; ATR50, ATR30, ATR20 = ATR with Wilder smoothing over 50, 30 and 20 bars; upper band U = EMA50 + 2.5*ATR50; RSI40 = RSI(40, Wilder) computed on the typical price (high+low+close)/3. 4h filter: 4h candles resampled from completed 1h bars in UTC blocks starting 00,04,08,12,16,20, merged with merge_informative_pair so that a 4h candle is visible only after its last 1h bar has closed. EMA4h = EMA(50) of 4h close. Filter holds at bar t if the last completed 4h close > EMA4h of that bar AND EMA4h of that bar > EMA4h of the completed 4h bar 6 bars earlier. ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: close(t) > U(t); close(t-1) <= U(t-1) (fresh close above the band); RSI40(t) > 50; the 4h filter holds; no open position. No cooldown. Let P = fill price (open of t+1), and freeze ATR20(t) and ATR30(t) of the signal bar. STOP-LOSS: native intrabar stop at P - 1.6*ATR20(t), i.e. a fixed percentage 1.6*ATR20(t)/P below the entry price set once at entry and never moved (custom_stoploss returning that constant). TARGET: sell when a bar''s high touches P + 4.5*ATR30(t), filled at the target price (at the bar open if it gaps above). If stop and target are both touched in the same bar, assume the stop filled first. TIME EXIT: if neither is hit, exit signal at the close of the 16th bar held (bar t+16), filled at the open of bar t+17, so no position lasts more than 16 hours. No other filters, no pyramiding, no trailing. Same rule and parameters on all nine pairs. Warm-up: 1000 bars (longest raw lookback is the 4h EMA50 plus a 6-bar 4h slope = 56 4h bars = 224 1h bars; 1000 bars, about 250 4h bars, is set so recursive EMA/Wilder values converge).','2026-11-07T16:13:44.250535+00:00','No price data inspected; only research/context/H-066.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the validation protocol, as of 2026-11-07.','failed: causality checks','1h Keltner 2.5-ATR breakout gated by a rising 4h EMA50, ATR stop and target, 16-bar time exit');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-067','AsianRangeLondonBreakout','Chart 15m, closed bars only, UTC clock; a signal at a bar close is filled at the next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding. Runs every calendar day, weekends included. ASIAN RANGE for UTC day D: AH = highest high and AL = lowest low of the 28 bars of day D opening 00:00, 00:15, ..., 06:45 UTC. If any of these 28 bars is missing, day D is not armed. DAILY FILTER: ATR14 = ATR(14) with Wilder smoothing (RMA, alpha 1/14) of true range, computed on closed UTC daily candles (informative 1d via merge_informative_pair, only completed days, so the value used on day D is the one at the close of day D-1). Day D is ARMED only if 0.25 <= (AH - AL) / ATR14 <= 0.80. ENTRY WINDOW: the 12 bars of day D opening 07:00 through 09:45 UTC. Scan these bars in time order on their closes: if a bar closes below AL before any bar has closed above AH, there is no trade on day D (first break is downward). Otherwise, at the first bar in the window whose close > AH, buy at the next bar open (latest possible fill: the 10:00 open). At most one trade per UTC day; no re-entry that day after any exit. STOP: a price stop at AL, intrabar (fills as soon as the low touches AL; if a bar opens below AL, fill at the open), implemented with custom_stoploss as a fixed price level for the trade. Native fixed backstop stop-loss: 8% below entry price (intrabar), only a safety net since AL is always closer given the width filter on these pairs. TARGET: T = entry + (entry - AL), entry = actual fill price (1R); exit as a limit when a bar high reaches T, filled at T (if a bar opens at or above T, fill at that open). TIME EXIT: if neither stop nor target is hit, sell at the open of the 12:00 UTC bar of day D (exit signal on the close of the 11:45 bar). Longest hold about 5 hours, always under 24 hours. No cooldown beyond one trade per day. No other filters. Warm-up: 4320 bars (45 daily candles x 96 bars, generous for the recursive Wilder ATR(14); the intraday range needs at most 40 bars).','2026-11-07T16:30:37.469787+00:00','No price data inspected; only the context file research/context/H-067.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses on BTC, ETH, BNB) and the cited web pages, as of 2026-11-07.','failed: causality checks','Asian-session (00-07 UTC) range breakout at the European open on 15m, 1R target, flat by 12:00 UTC');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-068','SeasonalVolumeSurprise','Chart 1h, closed bars only, UTC clock; a signal at the close of bar t is filled at the open of bar t+1. Spot, long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks; the same rule and numbers on all nine pairs. DEFINITIONS (completed bars only): EXPECTED VOLUME Vexp(t) = arithmetic mean of volume at bars t-24, t-48, ..., t-480 (the 20 bars at the same UTC hour on the 20 previous days; the current day and bar t are excluded). In pandas: mean of volume.shift(24*k) for k = 1..20; if any of the 20 values is missing (NaN) or Vexp(t) = 0, no signal. VOLUME SURPRISE VS(t) = volume(t) / Vexp(t). BAR RETURN B(t) = close(t)/open(t) - 1. CLOSE LOCATION CL(t) = (close(t) - low(t)) / (high(t) - low(t)); if high(t) == low(t) there is no signal. ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) VS(t) >= 2.0; (2) B(t) >= 0.006; (3) CL(t) >= 0.7; (4) no position is open. Buy at the open of bar t+1. At signal time store LOWSIG = low(t), fixed for the trade. EXITS, the first of: (a) TIME EXIT: the exit signal is raised at the close of bar t+12 (the 12th bar held, counting the entry-fill bar t+1 as the first) and the position is sold at the open of bar t+13, i.e. after 12 full bars; no position lasts more than 12 hours, well under 24 hours. (b) SIGNAL-BAR-LOW EXIT: if any bar u >= t+1 (the entry-fill bar included) closes below LOWSIG, sell at the open of bar u+1. (c) STOP-LOSS: one fixed native intrabar stop 2.0% below the entry price (stoploss = -0.02), triggered as soon as price touches it. Note on the stop: the idea''s stop is the low of bar t checked intrabar, which varies per trade; the engine requires one fixed percentage, so the intrabar stop is fixed at 2.0% (an up bar of at least 0.6% that closes in its top 30% usually has its low roughly 0.7-2% below the close) and the idea''s level is kept as the closed-bar exit (b). No take-profit, no trailing stop, no trend, daily or other filter, no cooldown other than one position at a time (a new entry can be signalled only on a bar close after the previous position has been closed). Single cell, no grid explored. Warm-up: 500 bars (longest lookback is the same-hour volume 480 bars back; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count = 500).','2026-11-07T16:46:43.043045+00:00','No price data opened; only the exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses in research/context/H-068.md (nine pairs, 1h and 15m) and the Quantpedia page.','rejected at exploration','Time-of-day-adjusted volume surprise on a strong 1h up bar, 12-hour continuation hold Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 890, ''ETH/USDT'': 975, ''BNB/USDT'': 228, ''XRP/USDT'': 594, ''ADA/USDT'': 721, ''LTC/USDT'': 579, ''LINK/USDT'': 773, ''DOGE/USDT'': 718, ''SOL/USDT'': 699}. Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.16662426874626077, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.19109957752321513, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.2532173545198958, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.23350475116219868, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.190234758011071, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.2449035012265253, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.2203647895403671, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.15837050806168665, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.17151941859103964}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 890, ''ETH/USDT'': 1033, ''BNB/USDT'': 965, ''XRP/USDT'': 860, ''ADA/USDT'': 990, ''LTC/USDT'': 988, ''LINK/USDT'': 925, ''DOGE/USDT'': 718, ''SOL/USDT'': 699}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-069','SessionOpeningRangeBreakout','Chart 15m, closed bars only; a signal at a bar close is filled at the next bar open. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters (no 1h/4h/1d filter). CLOCK: every time is New York local time (IANA zone America/New_York, DST handled per date), converted from each candle''s UTC open time; 09:30 ET = 13:30 UTC in US daylight time and 14:30 UTC in standard time. Trade only when the New York date is Monday to Friday (no holiday calendar). OPENING RANGE: the single 15m bar whose open time is 09:30 ET on that New York date; ORH = its high, ORL = its low. If that bar is missing, no trade that day. The day is ARMED only if 0.003 <= (ORH - ORL) / ORL <= 0.025. ENTRY: on an armed day, the FIRST 15m bar of that New York date whose open time is between 09:45 ET and 14:30 ET inclusive and whose close > ORH gives the entry signal (buy at the next bar open); later bars of the same day never give a signal, so at most one trade per day and no re-entry after an exit. EXIT (exit signal at bar close, filled at the next open), first of: (a) a 15m bar of the entry day closes below ORL (closed-bar replacement of the idea''s ORL stop); (b) TIME EXIT: the bar opening at 15:45 ET of the entry day closes, so the position is sold at the 16:00 ET open; as a safety for missing bars, any bar with open time >= 15:45 ET on the entry date, or on any later date, also triggers the exit. Holding is always under 7 hours, far below 24 hours. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 3.0% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (since ORL is at most 2.5% below ORH, this is a catastrophe net just beyond the widest possible ORL distance). Cooldown: none beyond the one-trade-per-day rule. ORH/ORL are frozen from the 09:30 ET bar and never updated during the day. Warm-up: 96 bars (no indicator; the furthest look-back is the 09:30 ET bar, at most 20 bars before a 14:30 ET signal bar; 96 bars = one full day of 15m bars for margin).','2026-11-07T17:13:48.368078+00:00','No price data opened; only research/context/H-069.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses on BTC, ETH, BNB 1h) and the two web sources, as of 2026-11-07.','rejected at exploration','US cash-open 15m opening-range breakout, New York time with DST, flat at the 16:00 ET close Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 919, ''ETH/USDT'': 1022, ''BNB/USDT'': 741, ''XRP/USDT'': 940, ''ADA/USDT'': 1012, ''LTC/USDT'': 892, ''LINK/USDT'': 897, ''DOGE/USDT'': 701, ''SOL/USDT'': 610}. Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.13550340562925448, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.12744009868363282, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.21304213538357242, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.12813705018195146, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.17014148017067254, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.19378910396676502, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.17405639006783608, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.14712261245810762, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.09891458423394552}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 919, ''ETH/USDT'': 1022, ''BNB/USDT'': 988, ''XRP/USDT'': 940, ''ADA/USDT'': 1012, ''LTC/USDT'': 1019, ''LINK/USDT'': 897, ''DOGE/USDT'': 701, ''SOL/USDT'': 610}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-070','RealizedSkewnessDay','Chart: 15m, closed bars only, UTC clock, bars labelled by open time. A signal at a bar close is filled at the next bar open. Long only, spot, one position, whole balance. DAILY STATISTIC, computed once at the close of the 23:45 UTC bar of day d: for each of the 96 15m bars of day d (open times 00:00 to 23:45), r_i = ln(close_i / close_{i-1}), where the first return uses the close of the 23:45 bar of day d-1 (97 closes in total). RV = sum of r_i^2 over the 96 returns. RSK = sqrt(96) * (sum of r_i^3) / RV^1.5 (Amaya et al. realized skewness). If any of the 97 required bars is missing (fewer than 97 consecutive 15m bars spanning 23:45 of d-1 to 23:45 of d) or RV = 0, there is no signal for day d+1. ENTRY: at the close of the 23:45 UTC bar of day d, if RSK <= -0.25 and no position is open, emit a buy signal; it fills at the open of the 00:00 UTC bar of day d+1. EXIT (time exit): at the close of the 23:30 UTC bar of day d+1, emit a sell signal; it fills at the open of the 23:45 UTC bar of day d+1 (95 bars, 23h45m after entry; equivalently, exit once the trade has been open 95 bars). The time exit is the only exit. Stop-loss: none by design (implement as a native stoploss of -0.99, i.e. 99% below entry, which is never meant to bind). No take-profit, no trailing stop, no trend filter, no cooldown (entries happen only at 00:00 UTC, so positions cannot overlap or chain; the exit at 23:45 leaves the 00:00 bar free for the next signal). Same rule and parameters on all nine pairs. Warm-up: 192 bars (longest lookback is 97 bars; 192 = two full UTC days so a complete prior day is always available).','2026-11-07T17:48:03.986906+00:00','No price data inspected; only the research context file H-070.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the validation protocol.','dropped: calibrated exposure below the minimum order','Negative realized skewness of the prior UTC day (96 x 15m returns): buy 00:00 UTC, exit at 23:45 UTC Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 1030, ''ETH/USDT'': 1012, ''BNB/USDT'': 975, ''XRP/USDT'': 960, ''ADA/USDT'': 888, ''LTC/USDT'': 966, ''LINK/USDT'': 120, ''DOGE/USDT'': 652, ''SOL/USDT'': 540}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-071','ATRTrailMomentum','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, filled at the open of bar t+1. Long only, one position, whole balance, same rule and parameters on every pair. Definitions: M(t) = close(t)/close(t-24) - 1 (24-bar momentum). S(t) = sample standard deviation (ddof=1) of the 720 values M(t-720), ..., M(t-1) (rolling 720-bar std of M, shifted by one bar so the current bar is excluded). ATR(t) = Wilder ATR with period 14 on 1h bars (true range smoothed with alpha = 1/14). ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) M(t) >= 1.5 * S(t); (2) M(t) >= 0.02; (3) close(t) > close(t-1); (4) no open position; (5) cooldown satisfied: no entry for 6 candles after any exit (at least 6 bars since the last exit). TRAILING EXIT (close-based, an exit signal, not the native stop): let e be the entry bar (the bar whose open is the fill) and P the fill price. Initial trail level T = P - 2.5 * ATR(t), with t the signal bar. At the close of every bar j >= e: if close(j) < T, exit at the open of bar j+1; otherwise update T = max(T, close(j) - 2.5 * ATR(j)), so T only moves up. TIME EXIT: if still open, exit at the close of bar e+23 (the 24th bar of the trade, filled at the open of bar e+24), so every position is closed within 24 hours. Whichever of the trailing exit and the time exit comes first applies. STOP-LOSS: native fixed stop 8% below the entry price (intrabar, triggers on touch); it is a catastrophic backstop only, since the 2.5-ATR trail normally sits much closer. No take-profit, no ROI table, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 1000 bars (longest lookback 744 = 720-bar std of a 24-bar return, plus margin so Wilder ATR(14) is stable for the recursive check).','2026-11-07T18:12:09.263547+00:00','No price data inspected; only research/context/H-071.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the cited paper.','dropped: calibrated exposure below the minimum order','Volatility-scaled 24-hour momentum on 1h with a ratcheting 2.5-ATR trailing stop and a 24-hour time exit Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 363, ''ETH/USDT'': 418, ''BNB/USDT'': 418, ''XRP/USDT'': 326, ''ADA/USDT'': 386, ''LTC/USDT'': 370, ''LINK/USDT'': 372, ''DOGE/USDT'': 274, ''SOL/USDT'': 257}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-072','IdiosyncraticResidualReversal','Chart 1h, closed bars only. Signal at the close of bar t, order filled at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks. Reference series B: BTC/USDT for every traded pair; for BTC/USDT itself B = ETH/USDT. B is an informative 1h pair (merge_informative_pair, closed bars, aligned on the same candle timestamp); if B''s bar is missing at any timestamp needed, no signal. Definitions: x(i) = ln(C(i)/C(i-1)) of the traded pair, b(i) = ln(CB(i)/CB(i-1)) of B. beta(t) = sample cov(x,b) / sample var(b) over the 720 bars t-720..t-1 (excludes bar t); if var(b) = 0 or any input is NaN, no signal. rB6(t) = ln(CB(t)/CB(t-6)). Residual e6(t) = ln(C(t)/C(t-6)) - beta(t)*rB6(t), where each e6(i) uses its own beta(i). s(t) = sample std (ddof=1) of e6 over the 720 bars t-720..t-1 (excludes bar t). ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) e6(t) <= -2.5*s(t); (2) e6(t) <= -0.02; (3) |rB6(t)| <= 0.01; (4) no open position; (5) all inputs defined. At entry store beta_e = beta(t), E = |e6(t)|, B0 = CB(t) (reference close at the signal bar) and P0 = the entry fill price. EXIT (signals checked at the close of every bar u from the entry bar on, filled at the open of bar u+1): (a) TARGET: ln(C(u)/P0) - beta_e*ln(CB(u)/B0) >= 0.6*E; (b) TIME: if the entry fills at the open of bar e, exit signal at the close of bar e+11, filled at the open of bar e+12 (12 hours held, well under 24 h); whichever comes first. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 4% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it; replaces the idea''s closed-bar check). No cooldown beyond one position at a time. No take-profit other than (a), no other filters. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: 720-bar beta window, 6-bar residual horizon, 720-bar residual std window, 2.5 sigma, 2% minimum residual drop, 1% reference flat band, 60% gap closure, 12-bar time exit, 4% stop. Warm-up: 1500 bars (e6 at t-720 needs beta from bars t-1440..t-721 plus 6 bars, i.e. about 1447 bars; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count 1500, under 4500).','2026-11-07T18:42:04.758944+00:00','No candle data viewed; only the exploration-split summaries in research/context/H-072.md (through 2026-11-07) and the two web sources.','rejected at exploration','Idiosyncratic 6-hour drop versus a flat BTC: buy the beta-adjusted residual dislocation, 12-hour cap Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.0780276083871384, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.17610276412012305, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.24649214042108372, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.28942336255951273, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.22617795166319904, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.159751532398926, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.2254054772222004, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.1832221005325229, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.18409886222661742}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 40, ''ETH/USDT'': 65, ''BNB/USDT'': 102, ''XRP/USDT'': 113, ''ADA/USDT'': 110, ''LTC/USDT'': 90, ''LINK/USDT'': 76, ''DOGE/USDT'': 91, ''SOL/USDT'': 67}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-073','BreadthThrustIntraday','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, order filled at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position per traded pair, whole balance, no pyramiding. All nine pairs (BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP, ADA, LTC, LINK, DOGE, SOL against USDT) are loaded as informative 1h pairs and aligned on the same candle timestamp as the traded pair. BREADTH: at each bar t, A(t) = number of the nine pairs with close(t) > close(t-1); D(t) = number with close(t) < close(t-1); pairs with close(t) = close(t-1), or with no candle at t or t-1, are left out of both counts. B(t) = A(t)/(A(t)+D(t)), or 0.5 if A(t)+D(t) = 0. E(t) = exponential moving average of B with span 10 (alpha = 2/11, recursive, adjust=False). THRUST(t) is true when E(t) > 0.615 AND min(E(t-10), ..., E(t-1)) < 0.40 (the 10 bars before t, excluding t). ENTRY on traded pair X at the close of bar t when all hold: (1) THRUST(t) is true and THRUST(t-1) is false (rising edge only); (2) close_X(t) > close_X(t-10); (3) X has no open position. EXIT at the first of: (a) TIME: at the close of bar t+24 (the 24th closed bar after the signal bar t), filled at the open of t+25, so every trade lasts 24 hours from the fill; (b) STOP: native fixed stop-loss 3% below the entry price, triggered intrabar as soon as price touches it; (c) BREADTH COLLAPSE: at the close of any bar after the fill bar where E < 0.40, filled at the next open. No take-profit, no trailing stop, no cooldown, no other filters. Longest lookback: 10 bars for E and close(t-10), 24 bars for the time exit; E is recursive, so the warm-up is sized for EMA convergence. Warm-up: 200 bars.','2026-11-07T19:30:32.119238+00:00','No price data viewed; only the H-073 context file (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the LuxAlgo breadth-thrust page, as of 2026-11-07','rejected at exploration','Nine-pair hourly breadth thrust: buy when the EMA share of rising pairs surges from below 0.40 to above 0.615 Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.23334066929980096, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.23960762410110573, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.20865180888291643, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.350602532170846, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.3495460520648275, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.3354040335657151, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.17969125579803524, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.22991267720156422, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.24307815406880978}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 932, ''ETH/USDT'': 956, ''BNB/USDT'': 896, ''XRP/USDT'': 742, ''ADA/USDT'': 834, ''LTC/USDT'': 885, ''LINK/USDT'': 733, ''DOGE/USDT'': 660, ''SOL/USDT'': 555}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-074','FeedbackVolRegimeSwitch','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, order filled at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one open position at a time, whole balance. Definitions: r(i) = ln(close(i)/close(i-1)). sig(t) = sample standard deviation (ddof=1) of r over the 24 bars t-23..t (current bar included). M(t) = median of sig over the 720 bars t-720..t-1 (30 days, current bar excluded). R6(t) = close(t)/close(t-6) - 1. CALM regime: sig(t) < M(t). VOLATILE regime: sig(t) >= 1.5*M(t). If M(t) <= sig(t) < 1.5*M(t) there is no entry. ENTRY A (continuation, CALM only): R6(t) >= 2.0*sig(t)*sqrt(6) AND R6(t) >= 0.012. ENTRY B (reversal, VOLATILE only): R6(t) <= -2.0*sig(t)*sqrt(6) AND R6(t) <= -0.025. Enter long if ENTRY A or ENTRY B holds, no position is open, and the cooldown is satisfied. EXIT (both entries): the first of (1) the native stop-loss, a fixed 3% below the entry price, triggered intrabar as soon as price touches it; or (2) time exit: at the close of the 12th bar after the entry bar (the entry bar is the bar whose open filled the order), exit signalled and filled at the next open, so every position is closed within 13 hours (well under 24 hours). No take-profit, no trailing stop, no trend filter, no pyramiding, no other filters. COOLDOWN: after any exit, no new entry for 6 candles. If any input (sig, M, R6) is undefined because of insufficient history, no entry. Same rule and parameters on all nine pairs. Warm-up: 800 bars (minimum needed 745 = 720 bars of sig history + 24 returns + 1 close; rounded up; no recursive indicators).','2026-11-07T20:26:08.944368+00:00','No price data opened; only the exploration-split summaries in research/context/H-074.md (BTC, ETH, BNB and earlier hypotheses), through 2026-11-07','rejected at exploration','Feedback-trading volatility switch on 1h: follow 6-hour surges when calm, fade 6-hour drops when volatile Calibrated exposure: 0.15 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17721211804248813, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.22502024674573765, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.16043021252020728, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.274342916561095, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.28384435328503205, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.20274335812399005, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.16309302934293657, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.13872183327159393, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.2412116828272854}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 383, ''ETH/USDT'': 401, ''BNB/USDT'': 374, ''XRP/USDT'': 285, ''ADA/USDT'': 320, ''LTC/USDT'': 368, ''LINK/USDT'': 295, ''DOGE/USDT'': 216, ''SOL/USDT'': 211}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-075','HourlyBullFlagBreak','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, order filled at the open of bar e = t+1. Long only, one position, whole balance. POLE CANDIDATES: for each p with t-9 <= p <= t-3 (flag of 2 to 8 bars), require high(p) = highest high of bars p..t-1. PL(p) = lowest low of bars p-5..p (6 bars); H(p) = high(p) - PL(p); require high(p)/PL(p) - 1 >= 0.025. FLAG = bars p+1..t-1. FL = lowest low of the flag, FH = highest high of the flag. Conditions: (1) depth: FL >= high(p) - 0.5*H; (2) tightness: FH - FL <= 0.5*H; (3) volume: mean volume of the flag bars <= 0.7 * mean volume of bars p-5..p; (4) trend: close(t) > SMA(168) of 1h closes at t. If several p satisfy all of (pole, 1-3), use the most recent p (largest p). ENTRY at the close of t when close(t) > high(p) for that p AND condition (4) AND no open position AND that pole (identified by the timestamp of bar p) has not already been traded (store it in the entry tag; reject a new entry with the same pole timestamp). Store FL and TARGET = FL + H in the entry tag, fixed at entry. EXITS, first of: (a) TARGET: limit-style take-profit at price FL + H, filled intrabar when high touches it (custom_roi), or at the open if a bar opens at or above it; (b) STRUCTURAL STOP: a closed bar u after the fill with close(u) < FL -> exit at the open of u+1; (c) NATIVE STOP: fixed 4% below the entry fill price, intrabar (stoploss = -0.04), as the engine-compatible stand-in for the flag-low stop of the idea; (d) TIME EXIT: at the open of bar e+24 (signal at the close of bar e+23, i.e. the close of the 24th bar after the signal bar t), so every position lasts at most 24 hours. No cooldown beyond the one-trade-per-pole rule, no pyramiding, no trailing stop, no other filters. Warm-up: 200 bars (SMA 168 plus the 15-bar pole/flag window, rounded up; no recursive indicators).','2026-11-07T21:04:06.086911+00:00','No price data or results viewed; only the context file research/context/H-075.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and archived strategy code.','rejected at exploration','Hourly bull flag: steep 6-bar pole, tight low-volume 2-8 bar flag, buy the close above the pole high Calibrated exposure: 0.25 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.17042354514283437, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.23585651829128185, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.21835351384178636, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.2853488299088446, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.15998215240928082, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.23151149637352123, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.22075727413662394, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.18487975849403304, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.18710211821913936}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 107, ''ETH/USDT'': 135, ''BNB/USDT'': 126, ''XRP/USDT'': 102, ''ADA/USDT'': 115, ''LTC/USDT'': 128, ''LINK/USDT'': 112, ''DOGE/USDT'': 91, ''SOL/USDT'': 82}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-076','VSAStopTestConfirm','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signals are evaluated at bar close and filled at the next bar''s open. Long only, one position at a time, whole balance, no pyramiding, no trend filter, no cooldown. Warm-up: 64 bars (no recursive indicators). DEFINITIONS: Vmed(s) = median volume of bars s-48..s-1 (48 bars, excluding s). Pos(i) = (close(i)-low(i))/(high(i)-low(i)); if high(i) = low(i) the bar cannot be a stopping, test or confirmation bar. STOPPING BAR s, all must hold: low(s) = lowest low of bars s-47..s (48 bars including s); volume(s) >= 2.5*Vmed(s); Pos(s) >= 0.5; close(s) < close(s-6). The most recent stopping bar is the only active setup; a new stopping bar replaces any older one, and a stopping bar that has produced an entry is used up. VOID: if any bar after s, before entry, closes below low(s), the setup is cancelled. TEST BAR t, any bar in s+1..s+12 with: low(t) < low(t-1) AND low(t) >= low(s) AND volume(t) <= 0.6*Vmed(s) (Vmed of the stopping bar) AND Pos(t) >= 0.5. CONFIRMATION: bar c in t+1..t+3 (c <= s+15) with close(c) > high(t) AND volume(c) > volume(t). If several valid test bars have open confirmation windows, use the most recent test bar t. ENTRY signal at the close of the first confirming bar c when no position is open; fill at open of c+1 (entry price E). STOP: price low(t), fixed at entry and never moved, triggered intrabar when price touches it (custom stoploss from the stored low(t)); native safety stop -10% below E, so the effective stop is max(low(t), 0.90*E). If E <= low(t) the trade exits at the stop immediately. TARGET: limit exit at E + 2*(E - low(t)), filled at that price as soon as a bar''s high reaches it. If stop and target are both touched in the same bar, assume the stop. TIME EXIT: signal at the close of bar c+24, filled at the open of c+25 (24 hours after entry). No other exits.','2026-11-07T21:44:29.004383+00:00','No price data inspected; only research/context/H-076.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the LuxAlgo VSA Test Bar page, as of 2026-11-07.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','VSA stopping volume, then low-volume test, then confirmed up bar: buy the retest of an absorbed hourly low DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 26, ''ETH/USDT'': 19, ''BNB/USDT'': 26, ''XRP/USDT'': 19, ''ADA/USDT'': 30, ''LTC/USDT'': 33, ''LINK/USDT'': 23, ''DOGE/USDT'': 23, ''SOL/USDT'': 16} (30 or more on 2 pair(s), 6 needed); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-077','CrossSectionalDailyMomentum','Chart 1h, closed bars only, all times UTC. Signal at the close of bar t, order filled at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position per traded pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks. Universe: the nine pairs BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT, BNB/USDT, XRP/USDT, ADA/USDT, LTC/USDT, LINK/USDT, DOGE/USDT, SOL/USDT; every pair other than the traded one is loaded as an informative 1h pair (merge_informative_pair, closed bars, aligned on the same candle timestamp). RANKING (once per day): at the close of the 23:00 UTC bar of day d-1, for each of the nine pairs compute R = close(23:00 bar of day d-1) / close(23:00 bar of day d-2) - 1 (the 24-bar return). A pair is dropped from that day''s ranking if any of its 25 hourly closes from the 23:00 bar of d-2 through the 23:00 bar of d-1 is missing. Rank the remaining pairs by R, highest first; exact ties are broken by pair name in ascending alphabetical order (the alphabetically earlier name ranks higher). ENTRY: the entry signal is raised only on the 23:00 UTC bar, and only if the traded pair is in the ranking and its rank is 1, 2, 3 or 4 (top 4); the order fills at the open of the 00:00 UTC bar of day d. No entry signal on any other bar. EXIT: time exit; exit signal at the close of the 22:00 UTC bar of day d, filled at the open of the 23:00 UTC bar (every trade lasts 23 hours, under 24 hours). STOP-LOSS: one fixed 5% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (triggers as soon as price touches it). After a stop-out, no re-entry until the next daily decision at the 23:00 bar. Each day is a fresh decision; a pair in the top 4 on consecutive days is closed at 23:00 and re-bought at 00:00 (no carry-over). No trend filter, no cooldown other than the above, no other conditions. Warm-up: 50 bars (longest lookback is 25 closes / 24-bar return; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count = 50 covers informative alignment).','2026-11-07T22:14:11.557886+00:00','No price data opened; only the exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses in research/context/H-077.md (through 2026-11-07).','dropped: calibrated exposure below the minimum order','Large-coin daily cross-sectional momentum: hold the top-4 of nine pairs by prior UTC-day return for 23 hours Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 1519, ''ETH/USDT'': 418, ''BNB/USDT'': 1133, ''XRP/USDT'': 994, ''ADA/USDT'': 584, ''LTC/USDT'': 278, ''LINK/USDT'': 655, ''DOGE/USDT'': 752, ''SOL/USDT'': 336}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-078','CrossSectionalLowVolReversal','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, order filled at the open of bar t+1. Spot, long only, one position per traded pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks. Universe: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP, ADA, LTC, LINK, DOGE, SOL against USDT; every pair other than the traded pair X is loaded as an informative 1h pair (merge_informative_pair, closed bars, aligned on the same candle timestamp). DEFINITIONS for each pair at bar t: r4(t) = close(t)/close(t-4) - 1. V4(t) = sum of volume over bars t-3..t (4 bars). VN(t) = arithmetic mean of V4(t-24k) for k = 1..14 (the same 4-hour clock window on each of the 14 previous days; uses bars back to t-339). A pair counts in the cross-section at bar t only if its r4(t) is defined (closes at t and t-4 present). M(t) = median of r4(t) over the pairs that count (with an even count, the mean of the two middle values). If fewer than 5 pairs count, or X does not count, there is no signal. ENTRY for X at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) r4_X(t) <= r4_Y(t) for every other counting pair Y (X is the lowest; ties allowed); (2) r4_X(t) <= -0.02; (3) r4_X(t) <= M(t) - 0.015; (4) V4_X(t) <= 1.0 * VN_X(t), with all 14 V4 terms defined and VN_X(t) > 0; (5) no open position in X; (6) cooldown satisfied. At signal store P = close_X(t-4) (pre-drop price, fixed for the trade). EXIT, first of: (a) TARGET: at the close of any bar u from the entry fill bar e = t+1 onward with close(u) >= P, exit at the open of u+1; (b) TIME: exit signal at the close of bar e+11, filled at the open of bar e+12 (12 hours held, well under 24 h); (c) STOP-LOSS: one fixed 4% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (stoploss = -0.04, triggers as soon as price touches it; replaces the idea''s close-checked stop). COOLDOWN: no new entry on X for 4 candles after any exit. No take-profit other than (a), no trailing stop, no trend filter, no other filters. All numbers fixed ex ante, single grid cell. Warm-up: 400 bars (longest lookback: VN needs bars t-339..t, i.e. 340 bars; no recursive indicators; rounded up to 400 for informative alignment).','2026-11-07T22:36:27.479350+00:00','No price data inspected; only the exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses in research/context/H-078.md (nine pairs, 1h) through 2026-11-07.','rejected at exploration','Low-volume cross-sectional loser reversal on 1h: buy the worst of nine pairs when its 4h drop is not backed by volume Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BNB/USDT'': 0.04068614386496832, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.10710926176711995, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.15608879518437346, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.06686236581195948, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.23316736447202474, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.13867146711135495, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.29525352216295986}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 10, ''ETH/USDT'': 22, ''BNB/USDT'': 126, ''XRP/USDT'': 117, ''ADA/USDT'': 153, ''LTC/USDT'': 77, ''LINK/USDT'': 372, ''DOGE/USDT'': 180, ''SOL/USDT'': 458}. Breadth: candidate on 1 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-079','MoneyFlowBreakout','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one open position, whole balance. Definitions: MFM(i) = ((close(i)-low(i)) - (high(i)-close(i))) / (high(i)-low(i)), set to 0 when high(i) = low(i). MFV(i) = MFM(i) * volume(i). CMF20(t) = sum of MFV over bars t-19..t divided by sum of volume over bars t-19..t (set CMF20 to 0 if the volume sum is 0). H24(t) = highest high of bars t-24..t-1 (24 bars, current bar excluded). L24(t) = lowest low of bars t-24..t-1. L6(t) = lowest low of bars t-6..t-1 (6 bars, current bar excluded). ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) close(t) > H24(t); (2) CMF20(t) >= 0.05; (3) CMF20(t) > CMF20(t-6); (4) (H24(t) - L24(t)) / close(t) >= 0.02; (5) no open position; (6) cooldown: at least 6 bars since the last exit (no re-entry for 6 candles after any exit). EXIT (signal at a bar close, fill at next open) at the first bar t after entry where any holds: (a) CMF20(t) <= -0.05; (b) close(t) < L6(t); (c) time exit: the trade has been open 24 bars (exit at the close of the 24th bar after the entry fill, so every position is closed within 24 hours). STOP-LOSS: fixed 2.5% below the entry price, engine-native, triggers intrabar. No take-profit, no trailing stop, no pyramiding, no other filters. CMF and rolling high/low are non-recursive; longest lookback is CMF20 at t-6 (26 bars). Warm-up: 30 bars.','2026-11-07T23:18:50.833746+00:00','No price data inspected; only the research context file research/context/H-079.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the cited web page.','dropped: calibrated exposure below the minimum order','Chaikin Money Flow confirmed 1h breakout of the 24-hour high, exit on distribution or after 24 hours Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 683, ''ETH/USDT'': 746, ''BNB/USDT'': 781, ''XRP/USDT'': 615, ''ADA/USDT'': 707, ''LTC/USDT'': 681, ''LINK/USDT'': 669, ''DOGE/USDT'': 457, ''SOL/USDT'': 491}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-080','CrossPairCatchUp','Chart 15m, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position, whole balance. Leader L = BTC/USDT for every traded pair except BTC/USDT, whose leader is ETH/USDT; L is merged as an informative 15m pair on the same timestamp (closed bars only). Definitions: b(t) = close_L(t)/close_L(t-1) - 1. sL(t) = sample standard deviation (ddof=1) of b over bars t-672..t-1 (672 bars = 7 days, current bar excluded). VL(t) = volume_L(t) / median(volume_L over bars t-96..t-1) (current bar excluded). x(t) = close_X(t)/close_X(t-1) - 1 for the traded pair X. SMA96_L(t) = simple mean of close_L over bars t-95..t (96 bars). ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) b(t) >= max(0.006, 2.5*sL(t)); (2) VL(t) >= 2.0; (3) x(t) <= 0.4*b(t); (4) close_L(t) > SMA96_L(t); (5) no open position. At entry, store from the signal bar t: target T = close_X(t) * (1 + b(t) - x(t)) and, with the actual fill price E, exit level S = E * (1 - 1.5*b(t)). EXIT (signal at a bar close, fill at the next open), first of: (a) close_X >= T; (b) close_X <= S; (c) time exit: at the close of the 16th 15m bar counted from the entry bar (inclusive), i.e. the position is closed about 4 hours after entry and never later than 24 hours. STOP-LOSS: native fixed stop 3% below entry price, triggered intrabar (catastrophe cap; the 1.5*b close exit (b) normally acts first). No cooldown, no take-profit other than T, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 700 bars (longest lookback 672 returns plus 1 bar for the return, rounded up; recursive-free indicators).','2026-11-07T23:40:21.267929+00:00','No price data inspected; only the research context file research/context/H-080.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the source paper''s abstract.','rejected at exploration','BTC-led 15m catch-up: buy a pair lagging a volume-backed leader surge bar, 4-hour time cap Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.32161096988107585, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.11610638560152799, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.22657138619767134, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.24966023979873828, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.17606207615246544, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.12106407827082832, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.2272955423196407, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.15214120310040533, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.22139653215204852}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 541, ''ETH/USDT'': 196, ''BNB/USDT'': 396, ''XRP/USDT'': 372, ''ADA/USDT'': 309, ''LTC/USDT'': 239, ''LINK/USDT'': 316, ''DOGE/USDT'': 271, ''SOL/USDT'': 200}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-081','VolatilitySqueezeBreakout','Chart 15m, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position, whole balance. INDICATORS (15m): SMA20 = 20-bar simple mean of close. Population std20 = 20-bar standard deviation of close with ddof=0. Bollinger: BBU = SMA20 + 2.0*std20, BBL = SMA20 - 2.0*std20. ATR20 = Wilder ATR of 20 bars (true range smoothed with alpha 1/20). Keltner: KCU = SMA20 + 1.5*ATR20, KCL = SMA20 - 1.5*ATR20. SQUEEZE_ON(t) = BBU(t) < KCU(t) AND BBL(t) > KCL(t). Mid(t) = ((highest high of bars t-19..t + lowest low of bars t-19..t)/2 + SMA20(t))/2. MOM(t) = fitted value at the last point (bar t) of an ordinary least-squares line of (close - Mid) over bars t-19..t against x = 0..19 (i.e. linreg(close-Mid, 20, 0)). 4h FILTER: 4h candles resampled from 15m/1h data in UTC blocks starting 00,04,08,12,16,20, merged with merge_informative_pair so a 4h bar is visible only after it closes. EMA50_4h = 50-period EMA of 4h close (adjust=False). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) SQUEEZE_ON for every bar t-6..t-1 (6 bars) AND SQUEEZE_ON(t) is false (the fire); (2) MOM(t) > 0 AND MOM(t) > MOM(t-1); (3) close(t) > KCU(t); (4) last closed 4h close > EMA50_4h of that bar AND EMA50_4h of that bar > EMA50_4h of the previous 4h bar; (5) no open position. EXIT at the close of the first bar after entry where any holds: (a) MOM fell on 2 consecutive bars (MOM(t) < MOM(t-1) AND MOM(t-1) < MOM(t-2)); (b) close(t) < SMA20(t); (c) 32 bars (8 hours) have elapsed since entry (time exit, closed at that bar''s close / next open). STOP-LOSS: fixed 1.5% below entry price, engine native intrabar stop (this replaces the idea''s ''lowest low of t-6..t'' structural stop, which the engine cannot express as one fixed percentage; 1.5% is the round value chosen ex ante as roughly the width of a 7-bar 15m coil plus slippage). No cooldown, no take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Longest lookback: 4h EMA50 with 1-bar slope = 51 4h bars = 816 15m bars; for EMA convergence (recursive gate) Warm-up: 2400 bars (150 4h bars).','2026-11-08T00:34:13.883591+00:00','No price data inspected; only research/context/H-081.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses on BTC, ETH, BNB) as of 2026-11-07.','failed: causality checks','15m TTM squeeze fire with rising positive momentum and closed-4h EMA50 uptrend filter, 8-hour time exit');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-082','HourlyTenDayExtreme','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signals are evaluated at the close of bar t and filled at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position at a time, whole balance, identical numbers on every pair, no per-pair tuning. Definitions (current bar excluded): MAX240(t) = highest close of bars t-240..t-1; MIN240(t) = lowest close of bars t-240..t-1 (240 hourly bars = 10 days). AT_MAX(t): close(t) > MAX240(t). AT_MIN(t): close(t) < MIN240(t). The two states cannot hold together. ENTRY: at the close of bar t when (AT_MAX(t) OR AT_MIN(t)) is true and no position is open; buy at the open of bar t+1. Both legs use the same entry and exit; there is no other filter (no trend, volume or volatility filter). EXIT: time exit only. Sell at the open of bar t+25, i.e. exactly 24 hours after the entry fill at the open of t+1 (equivalently: exit signal at the close of the 24th 1h bar after the entry signal bar, or exit when the trade has been open for >= 24 hours). No take-profit, no indicator exit, no trailing stop. STOP-LOSS: none in the rule; the engine''s mandatory native stop is set to 99% below entry (stoploss = -0.99) so it never acts in practice. COOLDOWN: none (0 bars); after an exit, a new entry is allowed on the next signal, including a fresh AT_MAX or AT_MIN on the bar whose close produced the exit if the engine allows it, otherwise on the next bar. No pyramiding, no position adjustment. Warm-up: 240 bars (the 240-bar closing max/min excluding the current bar; no recursive indicators are used; the developer may set startup_candle_count to 240 or a slightly larger round value such as 300).','2026-11-08T00:58:19.851770+00:00','No price data inspected; only research/context/H-082.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the Quantpedia article, as of 2026-11-07.','dropped: calibrated exposure below the minimum order','Hourly 10-day closing extreme: buy a 1h close above its 240-bar closing high or below its 240-bar closing low, hold 24h Calibrated exposure: 0.05 gives a stake of 5 on the 100 wallet, below the 10 minimum order; the drawdown control needs a smaller stake than the exchange accepts. Calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 645, ''ETH/USDT'': 599, ''BNB/USDT'': 591, ''XRP/USDT'': 462, ''ADA/USDT'': 528, ''LTC/USDT'': 580, ''LINK/USDT'': 92, ''DOGE/USDT'': 369, ''SOL/USDT'': 367}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-083','SupertrendMTFIntraday','Chart: 15m, closed bars only; every signal is evaluated at the close of a 15m bar and filled at the next 15m bar open. Long only, spot, one position at a time, whole balance. 15m indicators: ATR10 = Wilder ATR(10) of 15m bars. hl2 = (high+low)/2. Basic upper band BU = hl2 + 3*ATR10; basic lower band BL = hl2 - 3*ATR10. Final upper band FU(t) = BU(t) if BU(t) < FU(t-1) or close(t-1) > FU(t-1), else FU(t-1). Final lower band FL(t) = BL(t) if BL(t) > FL(t-1) or close(t-1) < FL(t-1), else FL(t-1). Direction: direction(t) = UP if close(t) > FU(t-1); DOWN if close(t) < FL(t-1); otherwise direction(t) = direction(t-1). Supertrend line ST(t) = FL(t) when direction(t) = UP. 1h filter: EMA200 = EMA(200) of 1h closes from an informative 1h timeframe merged with merge_informative_pair so that a 15m bar only sees the last COMPLETED 1h bar. ENTRY signal at close of 15m bar t when: direction(t-1) = DOWN AND direction(t) = UP AND close(t) > EMA200_1h AND no open position. At signal store S = ST(t), the fixed stop price for the whole trade. At fill (next open, price P): R = P - S; reject the entry (e.g. in confirm_trade_entry) if R/P < 0.004. EXITS, first hit wins: (1) Stop: fixed price S, intrabar (sell as soon as price touches S), implemented as a per-trade fixed stop price via custom_stoploss/stoploss_from_absolute; native stoploss backstop -10% from entry, so the effective stop is the higher of S and 0.90*P. (2) Take-profit: price P + 2R, filled at that price as soon as a 15m bar''s high reaches it. (3) Trend flip: at the close of a 15m bar where direction turns DOWN, exit at the next open. (4) Time exit: at the close of the 96th 15m bar after entry (24 hours after the fill). No cooldown, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 3200 bars (15m; = 800 completed 1h bars, 4x the EMA200 length so the recursive EMA and Wilder ATR are converged; within the 4500 limit).','2026-11-08T01:18:40.580461+00:00','No price data opened; only research/context/H-083.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses on BTC, ETH, BNB and the enabled pairs) and the validation protocol, as of 2026-11-07.','failed: causality checks','15m Supertrend(10,3) up-flip above closed-1h EMA200, Supertrend-line stop, 2R target, 24h time exit');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-084','HourlyIchimokuTrend','Chart 1h, closed bars only; every signal is evaluated at the close of bar t and filled at the open of bar t+1. Spot, long only, one position at a time, whole balance. No higher-timeframe filter. INDICATORS (all windows include the current closed bar t): Tenkan T(t) = (max high of bars t-19..t + min low of bars t-19..t)/2 (20 bars). Kijun K(t) = same over bars t-59..t (60 bars). SpanA_raw(t) = (T(t)+K(t))/2. SpanB_raw(t) = (max high + min low of bars t-119..t)/2 (120 bars). Displacement 30: the cloud at bar t is SpanA(t) = SpanA_raw(t-30) and SpanB(t) = SpanB_raw(t-30); CloudTop(t) = max(SpanA(t), SpanB(t)). Lagging-line confirmation: close(t) > close(t-30). ENTRY at close of bar t when flat and all of: close(t) > CloudTop(t) AND close(t) > close(t-30) AND at least one of (A) TK cross: T(t-1) <= K(t-1) and T(t) > K(t); or (B) cloud break: close(t-1) <= CloudTop(t-1) and T(t) > K(t). Buy at open of bar t+1. EXITS, whichever comes first: (1) native hard stop-loss 3% below the entry fill price, triggered intrabar as soon as price touches it (stoploss = -0.03); (2) Kijun exit: a closed 1h bar with close < K of that bar, sold at the next bar open; (3) time exit: when the trade has been open 24 hours (i.e. at the close of the 24th 1h bar counted from the entry bar, the entry bar being bar 1), sold at the next open, so no position is held more than 24 hours. No take-profit, no trailing stop, no cooldown, no pyramiding; a new entry may be taken on any later bar that meets the entry condition. Warm-up: 150 bars (120-bar SpanB plus 30-bar displacement; all indicators are rolling max/min, non-recursive).','2026-11-08T01:36:24.139419+00:00','No price data inspected; only the exploration-split summaries in research/context/H-084.md (BTC, ETH, BNB results of earlier hypotheses), as of 2026-11-07','rejected at exploration','Hourly Ichimoku 20/60/120/30: TK cross or cloud break above the cloud, Kijun exit, 3% stop, 24h cap Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.12583593588729028, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.08231856996969776, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.1947704244666839, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.2232429336516839, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.18177109605666486, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.14511538693079928, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.1723622787357868, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.23487065579773275, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.17778452785703724}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 512, ''ETH/USDT'': 525, ''BNB/USDT'': 562, ''XRP/USDT'': 509, ''ADA/USDT'': 491, ''LTC/USDT'': 508, ''LINK/USDT'': 461, ''DOGE/USDT'': 389, ''SOL/USDT'': 319}. Breadth: candidate on 1 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-085','RSIOverboughtMomentum','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at bar close, fill at the next 1h bar open. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, same numbers on all nine pairs. No informative timeframe. INDICATOR: RSI14 = Wilder RSI of length 14 on 1h closes (standard talib/ta-lib RSI, Wilder smoothing alpha = 1/14). ENTRY at the close of 1h bar t when RSI14(t-1) <= 70 AND RSI14(t) > 70 (fresh cross into the overbought zone) AND no position is open; buy at the open of bar t+1. A new entry requires a new cross from at or below 70 (a bar where RSI14 stays above 70 is never an entry). EXITS, whichever comes first: (a) TAKE-PROFIT: a limit at entry fill price * 1.03 (+3.0%), filled intrabar as soon as the high touches it (implement via minimal_roi = {"0": 0.03}); (b) RSI EXIT: a 1h bar closes with RSI14 < 55, sell at the next 1h open; (c) TIME EXIT: at the close of the 24th 1h bar after the entry bar (trade age >= 24 hours), sell at the next 1h open, so no position is held past about 25 hours from the signal and every position is closed within 24 hours of fill plus one bar of execution. If both (b) and (c) are true on the same bar, one exit order is sent. STOP-LOSS: none in the published rule; the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, a non-binding stop that is never intended to trigger (the RSI-55 and 24-hour exits bound the loss). No trailing stop, no cooldown, no trend filter, no volume filter, no other condition. All numbers fixed ex ante from the source rule (moved from 4h to 1h with the target scaled from 6% to 3%), no grid: RSI length 14, entry level 70, exit level 55, take-profit 3%, time exit 24 bars. Warm-up: 300 bars (RSI(14) needs 15 bars; 300 are taken so the recursive Wilder smoothing has converged and the recursive-indicator gate passes; startup_candle_count = 300, far under the 4500 limit).','2026-11-08T02:19:29.359039+00:00','No price data viewed; only the exploration-split summary results listed in research/context/H-085.md (BTC, ETH, BNB and others) and the source web page.','rejected at exploration','Overbought-is-strength: buy the 1h RSI(14) cross above 70, exit at +3%, RSI below 55, or after 24 hours Calibrated exposure: 0.15 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.08253710998695182, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.21314122795372012, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.1359293360966816, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.4036027854098343, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.18240628126954841, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.3114418616065458, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.1932959082488772, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.16811957599552466, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.20988297815871504}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 554, ''ETH/USDT'': 610, ''BNB/USDT'': 555, ''XRP/USDT'': 471, ''ADA/USDT'': 472, ''LTC/USDT'': 501, ''LINK/USDT'': 458, ''DOGE/USDT'': 355, ''SOL/USDT'': 346}. Breadth: candidate on 3 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-086','SessionVWAPBandFade','Chart 15m, closed bars only, all times UTC. A signal at the close of bar t fills at the open of bar t+1. Warm-up: 192 bars. SESSION: each UTC day; it resets at 00:00 UTC. For every bar, typical price tp=(high+low+close)/3. VWAP(t)=sum(tp*volume)/sum(volume) over the session''s bars from 00:00 up to and including t. SD(t)=sqrt(sum(volume*(tp-VWAP(t))^2)/sum(volume)) over the same bars. LB(t)=VWAP(t)-2.0*SD(t). SIGNAL WINDOW: only bars opening from 02:00 to 19:45 UTC inclusive can be a tag bar or an entry bar (bars opening 00:00-01:45 and 20:00-23:45 give no tags and no entries). TREND-DAY FILTER: at least one earlier bar of the same session closed above its own VWAP before the tag bar. TAG: a bar k in the signal window with low(k) <= LB(k) that passes the trend-day filter. ENTRY (long) at the close of the first bar t with k+1 <= t <= k+8 (k = the most recent tag, same session) such that close(t) > LB(t) AND close(t) < VWAP(t) AND (VWAP(t)-close(t))/close(t) >= 0.008, and no position is open. Each tag can produce at most one entry; after an exit, a new entry requires a new tag bar after the exit bar. At most 2 entries per session per pair. STOP-LOSS: native fixed stop 1.0% below the entry price, triggered intrabar (this fixed percentage replaces the source''s ''lowest low from tag to entry'' stop, as the engine requires one fixed percentage). TARGET EXIT: exit signal at the close of the first bar after entry whose close >= VWAP of that bar (current session VWAP), filled at the next open. TIME EXIT: exit at the close of the 23:45 UTC bar (fill at the 00:00 open, before the VWAP reset), and in any case after 48 bars (12 hours) in the trade, whichever comes first. No leverage, spot, long only, one position per pair, whole stake per trade.','2026-11-08T16:29:48.314938+00:00','No price data inspected; only research/context/H-086.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the cited web page, as of 2026-11-08.','dropped: no exposure meets the 25% bootstrap drawdown','UTC-session VWAP 2-sigma lower-band fade on 15m: close back inside the band, exit at VWAP, flat by day end No exposure on the 5% grid keeps the bootstrap p95 drawdown within 25% on 6 pair(s); calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 1458, ''ETH/USDT'': 1323, ''BNB/USDT'': 1353, ''XRP/USDT'': 1384, ''ADA/USDT'': 1356, ''LTC/USDT'': 1459, ''LINK/USDT'': 1299, ''DOGE/USDT'': 1708, ''SOL/USDT'': 1318}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-087','IntradayReturnAcceleration','Chart 15m, closed bars only; a signal at the close of bar t is filled at the open of bar t+1. No informative timeframe. Definitions: R1(t) = close(t)/close(t-16) - 1 (last 4 hours); R0(t) = close(t-16)/close(t-32) - 1 (previous 4 hours); A(t) = R1(t) - R0(t). mu(t) = mean of A over bars t-2880..t-1 and sd(t) = sample standard deviation (ddof=1) of A over the same 2880 bars (30 days; current bar excluded, i.e. rolling(2880) of A shifted by 1). Z(t) = (A(t) - mu(t)) / sd(t); if sd(t) is 0 or NaN, no signal. ENTRY (long, only when flat): Z(t) >= 2.0 AND Z(t-1) < 2.0 (fresh cross) AND R1(t) >= 0.01 AND close(t) > open(t). EXIT SIGNAL: at the close of the first bar after entry where Z < 0, exit at the next open. TIME EXIT: close the position at the open of the 33rd bar after the entry bar, i.e. after 32 bars = 8 hours held (implement as exit when trade age >= 480 minutes, checked at bar open/close; no position may stay open more than 8h15m). STOP-LOSS: fixed native stop 2.0% below the entry price, triggered intrabar (stoploss = -0.02). This replaces the idea''s variable ''lowest low of last 4 bars minus 0.2%, capped at 3%'' stop, because the engine supports only one fixed percentage; 2% is the round midpoint-level value inside that cap, chosen ex ante. No take-profit, no trailing stop, no higher-timeframe filter, no cooldown beyond the flat requirement. One open trade at a time per pair, whole balance per trade. Warm-up: 3000 bars (longest need is 2880-bar Z window + 32-bar return lag + 1 bar for Z(t-1) = 2913, rounded up to 3000).','2026-11-08T17:10:06.374732+00:00','No price data inspected; only research/context/H-087.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the cited web page, as of 2026-11-08.','rejected at exploration','Intraday return acceleration on 15m: buy a 2-sigma jump of the last-4h return over the prior 4h, max 8h hold Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.16626246392577004, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.2202057901390341, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.2098804615135078, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.2352849463715052, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.21857170627058634, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.23195676954146577, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.2202165554533004, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.19888422009868523, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.13331025518583162}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 814, ''ETH/USDT'': 935, ''BNB/USDT'': 971, ''XRP/USDT'': 829, ''ADA/USDT'': 986, ''LTC/USDT'': 939, ''LINK/USDT'': 889, ''DOGE/USDT'': 707, ''SOL/USDT'': 599}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-088','ElderTripleScreen','Chart 1h, closed bars only; a signal at a bar close is filled at the next bar open; spot, long only, one position at a time, whole balance. SCREEN 1 (tide, 4h): build 4h candles from completed 1h bars in UTC blocks starting 00,04,08,12,16,20 (informative 4h via merge_informative_pair, a 4h bar visible only after its last 1h bar has closed). On 4h closes: EMA13 = EMA(13); MACD line = EMA(12) - EMA(26); signal = EMA(9) of the MACD line; histogram H = MACD line - signal. TIDE UP when, on the last completed 4h bar k, EMA13(k) > EMA13(k-1) AND H(k) > H(k-1). SCREEN 2 (wave, 1h): FI(t) = (close(t) - close(t-1)) * volume(t); FI2 = EMA(2) of FI. A SETUP exists at bar s when TIDE UP at s and FI2(s) < 0. A setup lives for one bar only; every bar with FI2 < 0 under TIDE UP is a new setup. SCREEN 3 (trigger): entry signal at the close of bar s+1 if close(s+1) > high(s) AND TIDE UP at s+1 AND no open position; fill at open of bar s+2 (entry price P). Stop level L = min(low(s), low(s+1)); risk R = P - L. Skip the entry if R / P < 0.004 (includes R <= 0). STOP: fixed at entry as a percentage stop of (P - L)/P below P, never moved, triggered intrabar (custom_stoploss returning that fixed distance); native backstop stoploss -10%. EXITS, first hit: (a) stop at L intrabar; (b) take-profit limit at P + 2R, filled at that price when a bar''s high reaches it; (c) tide turns down: at a 1h close where the last completed 4h bar has EMA13(k) < EMA13(k-1), exit at the next open; (d) time exit at the close of the 12th 1h bar counted from the entry bar (12 hours after the fill). No cooldown beyond one position at a time. No ROI table other than the rule above. Warm-up: 1000 bars (1h; = 250 4h bars, generous for the recursive EMA26+EMA9 MACD and EMA13 on 4h; longest raw lookback 4h EMA26+EMA9 = 35 4h bars = 140 1h bars).','2026-11-08T18:11:26.435557+00:00','No price data viewed; only the context file research/context/H-088.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) through 2026-11-08','failed: causality checks','Elder Triple Screen intraday: rising 4h tide, negative 1h Force Index wave, break of setup-bar high, 2R target');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-089','WeeklyBreakoutRegime','Chart 1h, closed candles only; signals evaluated at the close of bar t, orders filled at the open of bar t+1. Spot, long only, one position per pair, no pyramiding, no DCA. All times UTC; a bar''s time is its open time. REGIME(t): SMA(60)(t) > SMA(180)(t) AND close(t) > SMA(60)(t), SMAs of close. ENTRY signal at close of bar t when ALL hold: REGIME(t); close(t) > max(high over bars t-14..t-1) (prior 14 bars, current bar excluded); no open position; bar t opens between 00:00 and 15:00 inclusive (so every entry fill is at an open from 01:00 to 16:00); fewer than 2 entries already filled on this pair on the same UTC date; cooldown satisfied. COOLDOWN: no re-entry for 2 candles after any exit (Freqtrade CooldownPeriod, stop_duration_candles = 2). EXIT signal at close of bar t (filled at next open) when close(t) < min(low over bars t-6..t-1) (prior 6 bars, current excluded) OR close(t) < SMA(60)(t). STOP-LOSS: fixed 2% below the entry price, native intrabar stop (stoploss = -0.02), no trailing. No take-profit (minimal_roi disabled). TIME EXIT (mandatory): the position is sold at the open of the bar opening at 23:00, or at the open of the 12th bar after the entry bar (entry fill time + 12 hours), whichever comes first; equivalently an exit signal at the close of the bar opening 22:00, or at the close of the 11th bar after the entry bar. No position is ever held past 23:00 or longer than 12 hours. The first of stop, signal exit and time exit to trigger closes the trade. No other filters. Warm-up: 200 bars (longest lookback SMA(180) plus a 20-bar margin; all indicators are non-recursive). Single-cell grid: no other parameter values are run. EXPOSURE: fixed share of the account by the lab rule (largest 5% grid value whose seeded block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown is <= 25% on all pairs, from this rule''s own exploration trades at base cost and full exposure; fewer than 30 trades on a pair drops the hypothesis, no retuning).','2026-11-09T22:33:48.218366+00:00','No price data opened. Only the exploration-split summaries in research/context/H-089.md (BTC, ETH, BNB per-hypothesis results and the H-009 audit); no validation or final-test data.','failed: exploration','Fast 14-hour breakout in a 60h/180h SMA uptrend, forced flat within the UTC day (1h)');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-090','RelativeStrengthRatioRotation','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at close of bar t, order filled at open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position per pair, no pyramiding, no take-profit. BASKET: for traded pair X, Y(t) = geometric mean of the 1h closes of BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT, BNB/USDT excluding X: if X is BTC, ETH or BNB, Y = sqrt(close_A*close_B) of the other two; for every other pair, Y = cbrt(close_BTC*close_ETH*close_BNB). Basket pairs loaded as informative 1h pairs aligned on the same closed-candle timestamp. R(t) = close_X(t)/Y(t). ENTRY signal at close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) R(t) > SMA(40) of R at t; (2) R(t) >= max(R over t-9..t), i.e. highest R of the last 10 bars including t; (3) close_X(t) > SMA(40) of close_X at t; (4) no open position; (5) cooldown: no re-entry for 1 candle after any exit; (6) session: bar t opens between 00:00 and 15:00 UTC inclusive (so fills happen at opens 01:00-16:00 UTC); (7) day limit: fewer than 2 entries already filled for this pair on the current UTC calendar day (counted by entry fill time). EXIT signal at close of bar t (filled at next open) when R(t) < SMA(4) of R at t, OR close_X(t) < SMA(40) of close_X at t. TIME EXIT (mandatory): sell at the open of the 23:00 UTC bar, i.e. exit signal at the close of the bar opening 22:00 UTC, OR sell at the open of the bar 12 hours after the entry fill (exit signal at the close of a bar when that close time minus entry fill time >= 12 hours), whichever comes first; never held overnight, maximum hold 12 hours. STOP-LOSS: fixed 2% below entry price (native intrabar stop, triggers on touch). All SMAs are simple means of completed bars; no recursive indicators, no other filters. Warm-up: 40 bars (longest lookback SMA(40) of R and of close; the 10-bar max and SMA(4) are shorter); startup_candle_count = 50. Same rule and numbers on all nine pairs.','2026-11-09T22:50:16.190709+00:00','No price data inspected; only the research context file H-090.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses, including H-047 exploration on BTC, ETH, BNB 1h) as of 2026-11-09.','dropped: no exposure meets the 25% bootstrap drawdown','Fast 1h relative-strength ratio breakout vs BTC/ETH/BNB basket, flat within the UTC day No exposure on the 5% grid keeps the bootstrap p95 drawdown within 25% on 6 pair(s); calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 1305, ''ETH/USDT'': 1601, ''BNB/USDT'': 1603, ''XRP/USDT'': 1131, ''ADA/USDT'': 1438, ''LTC/USDT'': 1536, ''LINK/USDT'': 1445, ''DOGE/USDT'': 1011, ''SOL/USDT'': 1102}.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-091','DailyRSI2Dip','Chart: 1h, spot, long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding. Signal frame: informative 2h candles aligned to UTC blocks 00,02,...,22, merged with merge_informative_pair (ffill), so a 2h candle is visible only after both its 1h bars have closed. The 2h close is the close of the block''s second 1h bar. Indicators on 2h closes: RSI2 = Wilder RSI(2) (alpha 1/2, seeded with the simple average of the first 2 changes); SMA200 = SMA(200); SMA5 = SMA(5). Signals are checked only on the 1h bar that completes a 2h block (1h bars opening at 01,03,...,23 UTC); orders fill at the next 1h open. ENTRY when a 2h candle closes with close > SMA200 AND RSI2 < 10 AND no open position AND the fill bar opens between 00:00 and 16:00 UTC inclusive AND fewer than 2 entries have already filled on this pair in this UTC day (counted by fill date). EXIT SIGNAL when a 2h candle closes with close > SMA5 OR close < SMA200: sell at the next 1h open. STOP-LOSS: native fixed stop 2% below the entry price (stoploss = -0.02), triggers intrabar as soon as price touches it. TIME EXIT (mandatory): sell at the open of the 23:00 UTC 1h bar, or at the open of the 12th 1h bar after the entry bar (entry at the open of bar E means sale at the open of bar E+12, max hold 12 hours), whichever comes first; implement by raising the exit at the close of the 22:00 bar or of bar E+11. First exit hit wins (stop, signal, time). No take-profit, no trailing, no cooldown (after any exit a new entry is allowed at the next qualifying 2h close if the daily limit allows). No other filters, no sizing hooks. All numbers fixed ex ante from the parent rule (RSI 2, threshold 10, SMA 5 and 200) plus the lab''s common day-trade frame (2% stop, 00:00-16:00 entry window, 2 entries per day, 23:00 UTC / 12-bar exit); no grid. Warm-up: 800 bars (1h; = 400 closed 2h candles: 200 for SMA(200) plus 200 for the Wilder RSI to converge; within the 4500 limit).','2026-11-09T23:28:48.456444+00:00','No candle data opened; only the exploration-split summaries in research/context/H-091.md (BTC, ETH, BNB and other enabled pairs, 1h/15m) as provided on 2026-11-09, and the therighttrader.com RSI(2) page.','rejected at exploration','Fast RSI(2) dip above the 200-candle mean on closed 2-hour candles, flat within the day Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.21377038135728166, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.24452578383613152, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.22410968261597392, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.15268166397643476, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.17613286580002074, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.17324432432154782, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.15906160243636738, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.18464472875917307, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.18836294849666713}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 590, ''ETH/USDT'': 626, ''BNB/USDT'': 691, ''XRP/USDT'': 479, ''ADA/USDT'': 559, ''LTC/USDT'': 541, ''LINK/USDT'': 546, ''DOGE/USDT'': 404, ''SOL/USDT'': 420}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-092','SessionOpeningRangeBreakout','Chart 15m, closed bars only, UTC clock (fixed UTC, no DST conversion). A signal at a bar close is filled at the next bar open. Spot, long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks, no other filters (no 1h/4h/1d filter). DAYS: trade only when the UTC date is Monday to Friday. OPENING RANGE of a UTC day: the two 15m bars opening at 13:30 and 13:45 UTC. RH = max of their highs, RL = min of their lows, M = (RH + RL) / 2. If either bar is missing or has zero volume, the day is not armed. RH, RL and M are frozen for the day. ARMED: the day is armed only if (RH - RL) / RL >= 0.02. ENTRY: on an armed day, the FIRST 15m bar whose open time is between 14:00 and 17:45 UTC inclusive and whose close > RH gives the entry signal; buy at the next bar open (latest fill 18:00 UTC). Later bars of the same day never signal, so there is at most one entry per day per pair and no new entry that day after any exit. STOP (per-trade, intrabar): at entry, the stop price is fixed at M and is never moved. This is a constant fraction s = (fill - M) / fill below the fill price for that trade (s >= about 1% because RH - M >= 1% of RL). It triggers intrabar as soon as the price touches M or lower, filled at M (or at the bar open if the bar opens below M). If fill <= M, exit at once. Safety net: the engine''s native fixed stoploss is -10% below entry, used only if M cannot be read. TAKE PROFIT (intrabar): T = fill + 2.0 x (fill - M). Exit as soon as the price touches T, filled at T. TIME EXIT: the close of the 15m bar opening at 19:45 UTC on the entry day gives an exit signal, sold at the 20:00 UTC open whatever happens. As a safety against missing bars, any bar with open time >= 19:45 UTC on the entry date, or on a later date, also triggers the exit. Holding is at most 5h45m (entry 14:15 at the earliest, exit 20:00), under the 12-hour limit. If stop and target are touched in the same bar, the stop counts first. Cooldown: none beyond the one-entry-per-day rule. No indicators. Longest lookback is the 13:30 bar, 17 bars before a 17:45 signal bar. Warm-up: 96 bars.','2026-11-10T00:35:19.399488+00:00','No candle data was inspected. Only research/context/H-092.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses), the validation protocol, and the archived strategy H067 code were read.','rejected at exploration','US-open 30-minute opening-range bracket on 15m: midpoint stop, 2R target, flat at 20:00 UTC, ranges >= 2% only Calibrated exposure: 0.15 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.10359691136033444, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.19719315554178973, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.20445093673542414, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.17389418821184266, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.16404512119739112, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.15826564117568714, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.21833970084218024, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.1549577384017371, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.24139924409310543}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 63, ''ETH/USDT'': 119, ''BNB/USDT'': 119, ''XRP/USDT'': 100, ''ADA/USDT'': 124, ''LTC/USDT'': 140, ''LINK/USDT'': 173, ''DOGE/USDT'': 100, ''SOL/USDT'': 179}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-093','TDSetupExhaustion','Chart 15m, closed bars only. A signal at a bar close fills at the next bar''s open. Each pair is traded on its own. No indicators. Warm-up: 100 bars (the longest lookback is about 21 bars: 5 before the flip plus up to 15 after it; 100 bars is a safe margin).
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-094','HolyGrailADXPullback','Chart 15m, closed bars only, UTC clock; a signal at the close of bar t is filled at the open of bar t+1. Spot, long only, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks, no higher-timeframe filter. Same rule and numbers on all nine pairs. INDICATORS (15m): ADX(14), +DI(14), -DI(14) with Wilder smoothing (alpha 1/14); EMA20 = EMA(20) of close (adjust=False). TOUCH BAR s (all must hold): ADX(s-1) > 30; ADX(s-1) > ADX(s-5); +DI(s-1) > -DI(s-1); EMA20(s) > EMA20(s-4); close(s-1) > EMA20(s-1); low(s) <= EMA20(s). TRIGGER at bar t: there is a touch bar s with t-3 <= s <= t-1 that is not consumed, AND close(t) > high(t-1) AND close(t) > EMA20(t). If several unconsumed touch bars lie in t-3..t-1, use the earliest one as s. LL = lowest low of bars s..t (both included). SKIP: if LL < 0.975*close(t), no trade; this setup and all touch bars <= t are consumed. ENTRY: on a valid trigger, if no position is open and fewer than 3 entries have been signalled on this pair on the UTC date of bar t, buy at the open of t+1 (fill price P); all touch bars <= t are then consumed (a setup is used once). STOP: SP = min(LL, 0.99*P); stop distance d = (P - SP)/P (always >= 1%), computed once at the fill and frozen for the trade: a fixed percentage d below the entry price, intrabar (custom_stoploss returning the constant d; triggers as soon as price touches SP). Native stoploss = -0.03 as a backstop (binds only if a gap makes d > 3%). TAKE-PROFIT: TP = P + 1.5*(P - SP); exit as a limit when a bar''s high reaches TP, filled at TP (at the open if a bar opens above TP). If stop and TP are touched in the same bar, assume the stop filled. TIME EXIT: with the fill bar counted as bar 1, the exit signal is raised at the close of bar 32 and filled at the next open (8 hours held). No trailing, no cooldown beyond the setup consumption and the 3-entries-per-UTC-day cap. Single cell, no grid. Warm-up: 500 bars (longest raw lookback is ADX(14) at s-5, about 33 bars; 500 bars lets the recursive Wilder ADX/DI and EMA20 converge for the recursive check).','2026-11-10T04:29:56.863595+00:00','No price data inspected; only the exploration-split summary results of earlier hypotheses listed in research/context/H-094.md (nine pairs, 15m/1h), as of 2026-11-10.','failed: exploration','Raschke Holy Grail on 15m: ADX above 30 and rising, first pullback to EMA20, buy the break of the prior bar high');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-095','SessionVWAPFirstPullback','Chart 15m, closed bars, UTC; a bar''s time is its open time; a signal at a bar close fills at the next bar open. Spot, long only, one position per pair, no sizing hooks, no higher-timeframe filter, same numbers on all pairs. SESSIONS (every UTC day): A = bars 00:00-07:45 (32 bars), E = 08:00-13:15 (22 bars), U = 13:30-23:45 (42 bars). Bar i = i-th bar of its session (i=1 is the session open). O = open of bar 1. tp=(high+low+close)/3; VWAP(t)=sum(tp*volume)/sum(volume) over the session''s bars 1..t (bar t included). DRIVE, known after bar 8 closes: D = summed volume of bars 1-8. The session is a drive session if max(high of bars 1-8) >= 1.012*O AND D >= 1.5 * mean of D of the same session (A, E or U) on the 14 previous UTC dates (all 14 must exist, else no drive). TEST: in a drive session, s = the first bar with i >= 9 and low(s) <= VWAP(s). The session is void (no trade) if close(s) < VWAP(s) OR volume(s) > mean volume of the session''s bars 1..s-1. No test bar: no trade. TRIGGER: t = s+1 if close(s+1) > high(s); else t = s+2 if close(s+2) > high(s); both must lie inside the session; otherwise no trade. H = max high of the session''s bars 1..t. The signal is valid only if H >= 1.01*close(t) AND bar t+1 opens at least 4 bars before session end (A: t+1 opens <= 07:00, E: <= 12:15, U: <= 22:45) AND no position is open. Buy at the open of t+1 (fill price P). FILL CHECKS (confirm_trade_entry with P = fill rate): skip if low(s) < 0.975*P, or if P >= H. STOP: SP = min(low(s), 0.99*P); d = (P-SP)/P (between 1% and 2.5%) is computed once at the fill and frozen: a fixed percentage d below the entry price, triggered intrabar (custom_stoploss returning the constant d). Native stoploss -0.03 is only a backstop. TAKE-PROFIT: limit at H, filled at H when a bar''s high reaches it (at the open if a bar opens above H). If stop and H are touched in the same bar, the stop counts first. TIME EXIT: counting the fill bar as held bar 1, an exit signal at the close of held bar 12 (3 hours), or at the close of the session''s last bar (07:45, 13:15 or 23:45), whichever comes first, filled at the next open. Only the first VWAP test of a session counts, so at most one trade per session (max 3 per day per pair). No cooldown, no trailing, no grid (single cell). Warm-up: 1440 bars (14 previous days of same-session drive volume = 1344 bars plus up to one current day of 96 bars; VWAP is non-recursive).','2026-11-10T05:25:00.408809+00:00','No price data inspected; only the context file research/context/H-095.md (exploration summaries of earlier hypotheses) and existing strategy code. Timeframe kept at 15m as in idea I-089 because the rule''s 8-bar drive and 12-bar exit are defined on 15m bars.','dropped: fewer than 30 trades','First pullback to session VWAP after a high-volume opening drive, three UTC sessions, 15m DROPPED by the pre-registered rule: calibration trades {''BTC/USDT'': 6, ''ETH/USDT'': 16, ''BNB/USDT'': 12, ''XRP/USDT'': 13, ''ADA/USDT'': 34, ''LTC/USDT'': 25, ''LINK/USDT'': 15, ''DOGE/USDT'': 12, ''SOL/USDT'': 15} (30 or more on 1 pair(s), 6 needed); not retuned.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-096','SessionRangeJudasSweep','Chart 15m, closed bars, UTC, bar time = open time; a signal at a bar close fills at the next bar open. Spot, long only, one position per pair, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks, no other filters, every calendar day, same numbers on all pairs. Two setups per UTC day. A (Asia->London): range bars 00:00-06:45 (28 bars), sweep window 07:00-10:45 (16 bars), exit bar 14:45. L (London->US): range bars 07:00-13:15 (26 bars), window 13:30-16:45 (14 bars), exit bar 20:45. Per setup: RH = max high, RL = min low of its range bars; if any range bar is missing the setup is off. ARMED only if (RH-RL)/RL >= 0.012. SWEEP: a window bar with low < 0.999*RL; the first such bar activates the setup. From then on SL(t) = lowest low of the window bars from window start through t, and K(t) = the latest bar at or before t whose low equals SL(t). DEAD: any window bar t after the first sweep bar with close(t) < 0.995*SL(t-1) kills the setup (no trade). RECLAIM: the first window bar t, at or after the first sweep bar, setup not dead, with t-K(t) <= 4 bars AND close(t) > RL AND high(t) > low(t) AND (close(t)-low(t))/(high(t)-low(t)) >= 0.5. Signal at close of t; buy at the open of t+1 (fill P) only if no position is open; otherwise the setup is consumed with no trade. The first reclaim consumes the setup (one trade per setup, at most 2 per day). FILL CHECKS (confirm_trade_entry, P = fill rate, SL = SL(t)): skip if 0.998*SL < 0.97*P (stop more than 3% away), or if RH < 1.01*P. STOP: SP = min(0.998*SL, 0.99*P); d = (P-SP)/P (between 1% and 3%) is computed once at the fill and frozen: a fixed percentage below the entry price, intrabar (custom_stoploss returning d; triggers as soon as price touches SP). Native stoploss -0.03 as backstop only. TAKE-PROFIT: limit at RH, filled at RH when a bar high reaches it (at the open if a bar opens above RH). If stop and RH are touched in the same bar, the stop counts first. TIME EXIT: exit signal at the close of the setup''s exit bar on the entry date (A: 14:45, L: 20:45), sold at the next open (15:00 / 21:00); any later bar also triggers it. Max hold: A fills 07:15-11:00 and exits by 15:00; L fills 13:45-17:00 and exits by 21:00, so at most 7h45m. No trailing, no cooldown beyond one trade per setup, single cell, no grid. Warm-up: 96 bars (longest lookback 44 bars, 00:00 to 10:45; no recursive indicators).','2026-11-10T05:49:40.618840+00:00','No candle data viewed; only exploration-split summary metrics of earlier hypotheses in research/context/H-096.md (through 2026-11-10).','rejected at exploration','Judas sweep: buy the quick reclaim of a pre-open range low swept at the London or US open, target the range high Calibrated exposure: 0.05 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.15025246796227443, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.15961742729958864, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.16847625184889292, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.16954005365510216, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.20566250076666773, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.20618110472994772, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.17751288071641222, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.149519520336306, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.1426272105728611}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 786, ''ETH/USDT'': 889, ''BNB/USDT'': 881, ''XRP/USDT'': 877, ''ADA/USDT'': 961, ''LTC/USDT'': 998, ''LINK/USDT'': 905, ''DOGE/USDT'': 698, ''SOL/USDT'': 634}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-097','RSIBullDivergence','Chart 15m, closed bars only, each pair alone, one position at a time. A signal at the close of bar t fills at the open of t+1. RSI14 = Wilder RSI(14) of 15m closes. H1RSI = Wilder RSI(14) of 1h closes (informative 1h via merge_informative_pair, last completed hour only). PIVOT LOW at bar i: low(i) < low(j) for j=i-3..i-1 and low(i) <= low(j) for j=i+1..i+3. A pivot is known only at the close of i+3. DIVERGENCE: i2 = a newly confirmed pivot low, i1 = the confirmed pivot low just before it. It holds if 6 <= i2-i1 <= 25, low(i2) < low(i1), RSI14(i2) > RSI14(i1) and RSI14(i1) < 40. ENTRY: the first bar t in i2+3..i2+8 with close(t) > max(high of bars i2..t-1) AND H1RSI(t) < 40 AND flat. If no bar triggers, the divergence expires. At most one trade per divergence. STOP: at the signal bar R = 1 - low(i2)*0.998/close(t). Skip if R > 0.03. Otherwise D = max(0.01, R). The stop is a fixed percentage D below the entry fill for that trade (custom_stoploss returns -D from the open rate). It triggers intrabar on touch. The native stoploss is -0.03 as a hard cap. EXITS, first of: (a) the stop; (b) the first bar close >= entry*(1+2D) exits at the next open; (c) the first bar where RSI14 closes >= 70 exits at the next open; (d) time exit: still open at the close of the 48th 15m bar after entry, so exit at the next open (at most 12 hours). No cooldown and no other filters. Same numbers on all nine pairs. Warm-up: 1200 bars (15m). The raw lookback is about 40 bars; the margin is for the recursive Wilder RSI on 1h (300 hours) and on 15m to converge. EXPOSURE: the lab''s standard calibration (largest 5% grid share with block-bootstrap p95 closed-trade drawdown <= 25% from this rule''s exploration trades at base cost). Fewer than 30 trades on a pair means it is dropped, with no retuning. Parameters come from the source and the scout''s idea, fixed before any result.','2026-11-10T07:30:25.289989+00:00','No price data viewed. Only research/context/H-097.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses, as of 2026-11-10), the validation protocol, and the cited web pages.','rejected at exploration','15m RSI bullish divergence at confirmed pivot lows, hourly RSI below 40, structure-break entry, 2R target, 12h time exit Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.25665071222710034, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.23914111418490774, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.22011976814114267, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.12612477028675229, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.2434230755371043, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.1693544573882727, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.20882562393802578, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.21335753986673597, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.16424941880990754}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 209, ''ETH/USDT'': 216, ''BNB/USDT'': 211, ''XRP/USDT'': 181, ''ADA/USDT'': 209, ''LTC/USDT'': 200, ''LINK/USDT'': 192, ''DOGE/USDT'': 146, ''SOL/USDT'': 121}. Breadth: candidate on 0 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-098','HourlyFailedBreakdownReclaim','Chart 15m, closed bars only, UTC, bar time = open time. Spot, long only, one position per pair, no pyramiding, no sizing hooks, same numbers on all nine pairs, no other filters. 4H BLOCKS: built from closed 15m bars in UTC blocks starting 00:00, 04:00, 08:00, 12:00, 16:00, 20:00 (16 bars each: open = open of first bar, high = max high, low = min low, close = close of the 16th bar). A block is usable only after its 16th bar has closed; if any of its 16 bars is missing the block is unusable. At the close of the 16th bar of block C2 (the block just completed), let C1 = the block immediately before C2: H1 = high(C1), L1 = low(C1), R1 = H1-L1, M1 = L1 + R1/2. SETUP, all required: (1) R1/L1 >= 0.015; (2) low(C2) < L1; (3) high(C2) <= H1; (4) close(C2) > L1; (5) close(C2) < M1; (6) low(C2) >= 0.97*close(C2) (swept low no more than 3% below close; otherwise skip). ENTRY: signal at the close of C2''s 16th bar, buy at the open of the next bar (first 15m bar of the next block), fill P, only if no position is open; otherwise the setup is dropped (no queue). At most one entry per 4h block. Fill checks: skip if P >= H1 or P <= SP. STOP: SP = min(low(C2), 0.992*close(C2)); d = (P-SP)/P computed once at the fill and frozen, i.e. a fixed percentage below the entry price for that trade, intrabar (custom_stoploss returning d, triggers as soon as price touches SP). Native stoploss -0.04 as backstop only. TAKE-PROFIT: limit sell at H1, filled intrabar when a bar high reaches H1 (at the open if a bar opens above H1). If stop and target are touched in the same bar, the stop counts. TIME EXIT: with entry filled at the open of bar e, exit signal at the close of bar e+47, sold at the open of bar e+48 (12 hours). No trailing stop, no cooldown beyond the one-position rule. Single cell, no grid. Warm-up: 64 bars (longest lookback 32 bars for C1+C2 plus up to 15 bars of block alignment = 47; no recursive indicators; startup_candle_count = 64).','2026-11-10T08:49:23.556944+00:00','No price data inspected; only research/context/H-098.md (exploration-split summaries of earlier hypotheses) and the web sources listed, as of 2026-11-10.','implemented','CRT on 4h UTC blocks: next 4h candle sweeps only the low, closes inside below mid, target far high');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-099','TimeSeriesMomentum','Chart: 1h, closed candles only; every signal is computed at the close of bar t and filled at the open of bar t+1. Spot, long only, one open position per pair, whole allowed balance per trade, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no other filters. Definitions on bar t: MOM(t) = close(t) / close(t-60) - 1 (close of the bar 60 bars earlier). ENTRY signal at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) close(t) > close(t-60); (2) close(t) > close(t-1); (3) no open position on the pair; (4) cooldown satisfied: at least 2 candles have elapsed since the last exit on the pair (Freqtrade CooldownPeriod, stop_duration_candles = 2); (5) session window: the FILL bar t+1 opens at 00:00, 01:00, ..., 16:00 UTC inclusive (equivalently the signal bar t opens at 23:00 UTC or at 00:00-15:00 UTC); (6) day cap: fewer than 2 entries have been filled on this pair with a fill time on the same UTC calendar day as bar t+1 (count by entry fill date; reject the third and later entries in confirm_trade_entry). EXIT (first one that occurs): (a) momentum exit: at the close of bar t, close(t) <= close(t-60) -> sell at the open of t+1; (b) stop-loss: fixed 2% below the entry fill price, native Freqtrade stoploss = -0.02, triggered intrabar as soon as price touches it; (c) evening exit: any position still open is sold at the open of the 23:00 UTC bar (signal raised at the close of the 22:00 UTC bar); (d) time exit: any position still open is sold at the open of the bar that starts 12 hours after the entry fill (i.e. 12 bars after the purchase), whichever of (c) and (d) comes first. Because the last allowed fill is 16:00 UTC, every position is closed the same UTC day, and no position is held more than 12 hours. The momentum lookback is fixed at 60 bars and the trigger at 1 bar; no parameter grid is run (single configuration). No recursive indicators are used. Warm-up: 100 bars (60-bar lookback plus 1-bar lag, rounded up to 100 for safety; startup_candle_count = 100).','2026-11-10T12:18:38.154324+00:00','No candle data opened; only the exploration-split summaries in research/context/H-099.md (through 2026-11-10) for the nine enabled pairs; no validation or final-test results.','implemented','Sixty-hour momentum sign with a rising-bar trigger, intraday entries 00:00-16:00 UTC, flat by 23:00 UTC or 12 bars');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-100','RSIOverboughtMomentumRVol','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at bar close, fill at the next 1h bar open. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, same numbers on all nine pairs. No informative timeframe. INDICATOR: RSI14 = Wilder RSI of length 14 on 1h closes (standard talib/ta-lib RSI, Wilder smoothing alpha = 1/14). ENTRY at the close of 1h bar t when RSI14(t-1) <= 70 AND RSI14(t) > 70 (fresh cross into the overbought zone) AND no position is open; buy at the open of bar t+1. A new entry requires a new cross from at or below 70 (a bar where RSI14 stays above 70 is never an entry). EXITS, whichever comes first: (a) TAKE-PROFIT: a limit at entry fill price * 1.03 (+3.0%), filled intrabar as soon as the high touches it (implement via minimal_roi = {"0": 0.03}); (b) RSI EXIT: a 1h bar closes with RSI14 < 55, sell at the next 1h open; (c) TIME EXIT: at the close of the 24th 1h bar after the entry bar (trade age >= 24 hours), sell at the next 1h open, so no position is held past about 25 hours from the signal and every position is closed within 24 hours of fill plus one bar of execution. If both (b) and (c) are true on the same bar, one exit order is sent. STOP-LOSS: none in the published rule; the strategy sets stoploss = -0.99 only to satisfy the engine contract, a non-binding stop that is never intended to trigger (the RSI-55 and 24-hour exits bound the loss). No trailing stop, no cooldown, no trend filter, no volume filter, no other condition. All numbers fixed ex ante from the source rule (moved from 4h to 1h with the target scaled from 6% to 3%), no grid: RSI length 14, entry level 70, exit level 55, take-profit 3%, time exit 24 bars. Warm-up: 300 bars (RSI(14) needs 15 bars; 300 are taken so the recursive Wilder smoothing has converged and the recursive-indicator gate passes; startup_candle_count = 300, far under the 4500 limit). ADDED RULE (the only change from H-085): the ENTRY also requires relative volume RV(t) >= 2.0 at the signal bar t, where RV(t) = volume(t) / mean(volume(t-120..t-1)) (the previous 120 closed 1h bars, the current bar excluded); no other change: exits, stops, timing, windows and the 24-hour/day limits are exactly those of H-085. The 2.0 and the 120 are fixed ex ante (twice the 5-day mean volume), no grid.','2026-11-10T17:00:16.976957+00:00','Exploration-split trade statistics of H-085 only (research/learnings digest and its backtest artifacts). Validation and holdout data were not opened.','rejected at exploration','Overbought-is-strength with a relative-volume confirmation: 1h RSI(14) cross above 70 on at least twice the usual volume [v2 of H-085, owner request 2026-11-10] Calibrated exposure: 0.2 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.11799910238926302, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.10064859857085154, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.12847661333051164, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.4357217991170981, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.23527074936767342, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.2592307579899406, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.17240342388262866, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.21000405383239076, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.1644136615558383}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 321, ''ETH/USDT'': 344, ''BNB/USDT'': 297, ''XRP/USDT'': 306, ''ADA/USDT'': 295, ''LTC/USDT'': 325, ''LINK/USDT'': 285, ''DOGE/USDT'': 264, ''SOL/USDT'': 206}. Breadth: candidate on 4 of 9 pairs, 6 needed. [Frozen for dry-run by the autopilot policy 2026-11-10T21:42:56.038015+00:00, commit 3c6c267cfe, strategy sha256 07e59ea26153; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-101','HourlyIchimokuTrendRVol','Chart 1h, closed bars only; every signal is evaluated at the close of bar t and filled at the open of bar t+1. Spot, long only, one position at a time, whole balance. No higher-timeframe filter. INDICATORS (all windows include the current closed bar t): Tenkan T(t) = (max high of bars t-19..t + min low of bars t-19..t)/2 (20 bars). Kijun K(t) = same over bars t-59..t (60 bars). SpanA_raw(t) = (T(t)+K(t))/2. SpanB_raw(t) = (max high + min low of bars t-119..t)/2 (120 bars). Displacement 30: the cloud at bar t is SpanA(t) = SpanA_raw(t-30) and SpanB(t) = SpanB_raw(t-30); CloudTop(t) = max(SpanA(t), SpanB(t)). Lagging-line confirmation: close(t) > close(t-30). ENTRY at close of bar t when flat and all of: close(t) > CloudTop(t) AND close(t) > close(t-30) AND at least one of (A) TK cross: T(t-1) <= K(t-1) and T(t) > K(t); or (B) cloud break: close(t-1) <= CloudTop(t-1) and T(t) > K(t). Buy at open of bar t+1. EXITS, whichever comes first: (1) native hard stop-loss 3% below the entry fill price, triggered intrabar as soon as price touches it (stoploss = -0.03); (2) Kijun exit: a closed 1h bar with close < K of that bar, sold at the next bar open; (3) time exit: when the trade has been open 24 hours (i.e. at the close of the 24th 1h bar counted from the entry bar, the entry bar being bar 1), sold at the next open, so no position is held more than 24 hours. No take-profit, no trailing stop, no cooldown, no pyramiding; a new entry may be taken on any later bar that meets the entry condition. Warm-up: 150 bars (120-bar SpanB plus 30-bar displacement; all indicators are rolling max/min, non-recursive). ADDED RULE (the only change from H-084): the ENTRY also requires relative volume RV(t) >= 2.0 at the signal bar t, where RV(t) = volume(t) / mean(volume(t-120..t-1)) (the previous 120 closed 1h bars, the current bar excluded); no other change: exits, stops, timing, windows and the 24-hour/day limits are exactly those of H-084. The 2.0 and the 120 are fixed ex ante (twice the 5-day mean volume), no grid.','2026-11-10T17:00:16.988763+00:00','Exploration-split trade statistics of H-084 only (research/learnings digest and its backtest artifacts). Validation and holdout data were not opened.','rejected at exploration','Hourly Ichimoku 20/60/120/30 trend entry confirmed by at least twice the usual volume [v2 of H-084, owner request 2026-11-10] Calibrated exposure: 0.3 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.13363605961724476, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.09306199073038363, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.23131650064396087, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.24962585754195793, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.18661407630742, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.22058148584336512, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.12934000471718607, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.3623175844546698, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.2511848408222351}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 109, ''ETH/USDT'': 124, ''BNB/USDT'': 131, ''XRP/USDT'': 135, ''ADA/USDT'': 121, ''LTC/USDT'': 148, ''LINK/USDT'': 128, ''DOGE/USDT'': 124, ''SOL/USDT'': 83}. Breadth: candidate on 4 of 9 pairs, 6 needed. [Frozen for dry-run by the autopilot policy 2026-11-10T21:42:59.114751+00:00, commit 14c4468ed7, strategy sha256 43918f9c7835; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-102','IntradayJumpContinuationStrong','Chart: 15m, closed bars only, UTC clock; signal at the close of bar t, order at the open of bar t+1. Long only, spot, one position per pair, whole allowed balance, no pyramiding, no take-profit, no sizing hooks, no other filters. DEFINITIONS: r(i) = ln(close(i)/close(i-1)). Local volatility s(t) = sqrt((pi/2) * mean over i = t-96..t-1 of |r(i)|*|r(i-1)|) (bipower variation over the previous 96 bars; the current bar t is excluded; needs closes t-98..t-1). Jump statistic J(t) = r(t)/s(t); if s(t) is 0 or undefined there is no signal. DAILY FILTER: build UTC daily candles from the 15m data (informative 1d via merge_informative_pair, forward-filled, so a daily close is visible only after its day has closed). The filter holds when the last completed daily close (the previous UTC day) is strictly above the simple mean of the last 30 completed daily closes (that day included). ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) J(t) >= 4.0; (2) r(t) >= 0.006; (3) bar t opens between 00:00 and 17:45 UTC inclusive; (4) daily filter true; (5) no position open; (6) no trade has already been entered on this UTC day (the day of bar t). Store L = low of the jump bar t at signal time. EXIT, first of: (a) on any 15m bar u >= t+1 (the entry bar included) whose close < L, sell at the open of bar u+1; (b) time exit: at the close of the 23:45 UTC bar of the signal day, sell at the open of the 00:00 UTC bar of the next day, so every position is closed within 24 hours. STOP-LOSS: one fixed 3% below the entry price, the engine''s native intrabar stop (a catastrophic backstop; exit (a) is the designed loss exit). COOLDOWN: none beyond the one-trade-per-UTC-day rule. All numbers fixed ex ante, no grid: return window 1 bar, bipower window 96 bars, jump threshold 4.0, minimum bar return 0.006 log, entry window 00:00-17:45 UTC, daily mean 30 days, time exit 23:45 bar close, stop 3%. Warm-up: 3072 bars (30 completed daily closes need up to 31 UTC days = 2976 15m bars; the bipower window needs 98 bars; 3072 = 32 days gives margin; no recursive indicators; under the 4500 limit). CHANGED NUMBER (the only change from H-059): the jump statistic threshold is J(t) >= 6.0 instead of 4.0; everything else is exactly as in H-059.','2026-11-10T17:00:16.998428+00:00','Exploration-split trade statistics of H-059 only (research/learnings digest and its backtest artifacts). Validation and holdout data were not opened.','rejected at exploration','Intraday positive-jump continuation on 15m with a stronger jump (statistic at least 6.0 instead of 4.0) [v2 of H-059, owner request 2026-11-10] Calibrated exposure: 0.5 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.21688380836794555, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.13606684708332284, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.15396229041533718, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.40540794980332795, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.18816350690662292, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.2887582250968916, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.2425163523778268, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.600334776134883, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.16079942265286398}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 115, ''ETH/USDT'': 92, ''BNB/USDT'': 91, ''XRP/USDT'': 105, ''ADA/USDT'': 62, ''LTC/USDT'': 103, ''LINK/USDT'': 46, ''DOGE/USDT'': 88, ''SOL/USDT'': 43}. Breadth: candidate on 5 of 9 pairs, 6 needed. [Frozen for dry-run by the autopilot policy 2026-11-10T21:43:02.862919+00:00, commit 5f0d2bb2b8, strategy sha256 afdda7a789e9; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-103','AbnormalDayContinuationRVol','Timeframe 1h, closed bars only, all times UTC; a signal at a bar close is filled at the next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. DAILY STATISTICS (built from completed 1h bars, no lookahead): for each completed UTC day k, C(k) = close of that day''s 23:00 bar (if that bar is missing, the close of the last bar of that day). Daily return R(k) = C(k)/C(k-1) - 1. For the current UTC day d, m = mean and s = sample standard deviation (ddof=1) of R(k) over the 30 completed days k = d-30 .. d-1 (needs 31 daily closes = 744 bars); m and s are fixed for the whole of day d. INTRADAY: O = open of day d''s 00:00 bar (if missing, the open of the first bar of day d). D(t) = close(t)/O - 1 for every bar t of day d. Threshold T = m + 0.75*s. ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) the open time of bar t is between 01:00 and 18:00 UTC inclusive; (2) D(t) >= T; (3) D(t) >= 0.01; (4) D(t-1) < T, where t-1 is the previous bar of the same UTC day (first crossing); (5) no position is open; (6) no entry has been made earlier in the same UTC day (at most one entry per UTC day). Buy at the next bar open. EXIT, whichever comes first: (a) TIME EXIT: 24 hours after the entry fill, i.e. the exit signal is raised at the close of the 24th bar of the trade (the bar opening 23 hours after the entry bar) and the position is sold at the next open, so no position is held longer than 24 hours; (b) FAILURE EXIT: a bar closes below O, the open of the UTC day on which the entry signal fired (the move has fully failed); sell at the next open. STOP-LOSS: fixed 4% below the entry price, native intrabar stop (a disaster stop only; exit (b) normally triggers first). No cooldown beyond the one-entry-per-UTC-day rule, no take-profit, no trailing, no pyramiding, no other filters. Warm-up: 800 bars (744 bars for 31 daily closes plus up to 24 bars of the current day, rounded up; no recursive indicators are used). ADDED RULE (the only change from H-057): the ENTRY also requires relative volume RV(t) >= 2.0 at the signal bar t, where RV(t) = volume(t) / mean(volume(t-120..t-1)) (the previous 120 closed 1h bars, the current bar excluded); no other change: exits, stops, timing, windows and the 24-hour/day limits are exactly those of H-057. The 2.0 and the 120 are fixed ex ante (twice the 5-day mean volume), no grid.','2026-11-10T17:00:17.008317+00:00','Exploration-split trade statistics of H-057 only (research/learnings digest and its backtest artifacts). Validation and holdout data were not opened.','rejected at exploration','Abnormal-day continuation: first intraday crossing of the volatility band, only on at least twice the usual volume [v2 of H-057, owner request 2026-11-10] Calibrated exposure: 0.1 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.06036521175315332, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.07096326847092208, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.11140879545648537, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.17424302126359825, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.13918625577314894, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.17802207746827658, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.1825401260310432, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.24048463724918237, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.15259308760268295}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 266, ''ETH/USDT'': 288, ''BNB/USDT'': 253, ''XRP/USDT'': 234, ''ADA/USDT'': 248, ''LTC/USDT'': 301, ''LINK/USDT'': 245, ''DOGE/USDT'': 220, ''SOL/USDT'': 175}. Breadth: candidate on 3 of 9 pairs, 6 needed. [Frozen for dry-run by the autopilot policy 2026-11-10T21:43:20.182891+00:00, commit 9d27921173, strategy sha256 cfe1efe601ce; Dry-run como coleta de evidência: NÃO validada; sem evidência prospectiva; não é aprovação, não é holdout e não consome a leitura da validação.]');
INSERT INTO "hypotheses" VALUES('H-104','HourlyWilliamsVolBreakoutRVol','Closed 1h candles only; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. Long only, one position, whole allowed balance. UTC days built from 1h bars. For UTC day D: O = open of the 00:00 bar of D; R = (highest high - lowest low) of the 24 bars of day D-1; level = O + 0.6*R; TrendDay = close of the last bar (23:00) of day D-1 > SMA(50) of daily closes, where the daily closes are the 23:00-bar closes of the last 50 completed UTC days up to and including D-1 (equivalent to a 1h series of 1200 bars sampled at day ends; all use completed days only). ENTRY at the close of a 1h bar whose open time is between 01:00 and 18:00 UTC inclusive on day D when ALL hold: close > level; R/O >= 0.02; TrendDay true; no open position; no trade already entered on day D. The buy fills at the next bar open. At most one entry per day, no re-entry on the same day after an exit. EXIT, whichever first: (a) a 1h bar closes < O - 0.5*R (exit executed at next bar open); (b) time exit: the 23:00 bar''s close is the last signal of day D, so the position is sold at the open of the 00:00 UTC bar of day D+1 (flat at midnight); (c) native fixed stop-loss 5% below the entry price (intrabar), added as the engine-required fixed-percentage protection against gaps between the closed-bar exit checks. No cooldown beyond the one-trade-per-day rule, no take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters. Fixed parameters: 0.6 trigger multiple, 0.5 stop multiple, 0.02 min range ratio, SMA 50 days, entry window 01:00-18:00 UTC. Warm-up: 1300 bars (1200 bars for SMA(50) of daily closes + 24 bars for prior-day range + margin). ADDED RULE (the only change from H-043): the ENTRY also requires relative volume RV(t) >= 2.0 at the signal bar t, where RV(t) = volume(t) / mean(volume(t-120..t-1)) (the previous 120 closed 1h bars, the current bar excluded); no other change: exits, stops, timing, windows and the 24-hour/day limits are exactly those of H-043. The 2.0 and the 120 are fixed ex ante (twice the 5-day mean volume), no grid.','2026-11-10T17:00:17.020025+00:00','Exploration-split trade statistics of H-043 only (research/learnings digest and its backtest artifacts). Validation and holdout data were not opened.','rejected at exploration','Williams-style volatility breakout (day open + 0.6 x prior range) taken only on at least twice the usual volume [v2 of H-043, owner request 2026-11-10] Calibrated exposure: 0.25 (p95 by pair {''BTC/USDT'': 0.09110265879071806, ''ETH/USDT'': 0.101393472645356, ''BNB/USDT'': 0.12173869054106216, ''XRP/USDT'': 0.24814400516936824, ''ADA/USDT'': 0.19360101484535566, ''LTC/USDT'': 0.23094998594797478, ''LINK/USDT'': 0.24966438322021986, ''DOGE/USDT'': 0.29225979527598606, ''SOL/USDT'': 0.30298252537680637}). Calibration trades: {''BTC/USDT'': 166, ''ETH/USDT'': 182, ''BNB/USDT'': 186, ''XRP/USDT'': 146, ''ADA/USDT'': 161, ''LTC/USDT'': 181, ''LINK/USDT'': 180, ''DOGE/USDT'': 140, ''SOL/USDT'': 136}. Breadth: candidate on 5 of 9 pairs, 6 needed.');
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-001','S20261104T205946Z','Daily RSI(2) oversold dip buy in 200-day uptrend, exit above 5-day SMA','blog','https://therighttrader.com/learn/trading-strategies/rsi-2-strategy','RSI 2 Strategy (therighttrader.com)','unknown','Signals from closed DAILY candles built from the 1h data, executed at the next 1h open. RSI(2) uses Wilder smoothing on daily closes. ENTRY: daily close > SMA(200 days) of daily close AND RSI(2) < 10 AND no open position. EXIT: first daily close above SMA(5 days) of daily close, OR daily close below SMA(200 days). No profit target, no pyramiding. Optional protective stop (not part of the published exit): none in the base rule; a developer may add a fixed percentage stop below entry. Free numbers: RSI length 2, threshold 10, exit average 5, trend average 200.','Very short-term sell-offs inside an established uptrend are often forced or impatient selling (liquidations, panic sellers) that overshoots; liquidity takers pay a concession to dip buyers, and price snaps back toward its short mean. The source gives only a brief rationale (extreme readings flag dips; the 200-day filter avoids downtrends); the liquidity-overshoot story is the closest honest mechanism.','1d',200,4,1,9.0,'DailyRSI2Dip','89cdd0d318c9fa83fc961babbf54823dd6a77b3395b6d4a6aca0d21b74512381','registered','formalised as H-019',2.9379,'H-019','2026-11-04T21:00:41.983635+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-002','S20261105T154404Z','Daily Double 7: buy a 7-day closing low above the 200-day mean, sell a 7-day closing high','blog','https://strategyquant.com/blog/larry-connors-double-7-strategy-tested-on-spy-and-8-other-markets/','Larry Connors'' Double 7 Strategy: Tested on SPY and 8 Other Markets','unknown','Daily signals from closed daily candles built from the 1h data; orders executed at the next 1h open. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance. ENTRY when a daily close is above the 200-day simple moving average of daily closes AND that close is less than or equal to the lowest daily close of the last 7 days (including the current day) AND no position is open. EXIT when a daily close is greater than or equal to the highest daily close of the last 7 days (including the current day). No stop, no profit target, no time exit. Lookbacks: 7 days for entry channel, 7 days for exit channel, 200 days for the trend filter.','Counterparty: short-horizon sellers who capitulate or de-risk after a few down days inside a long-term uptrend, pushing price below fair value for a short time; liquidity-demanding panic sellers pay a premium to exit. Short-term reversal after a pullback is paid to the buyer who supplies liquidity. The source gives no mechanism beyond the stock-index mean reversion observation; this is the closest honest one.','1d',200,3,1,9.0,'Double7ChannelDip','f0f19b8980a768896d77b527e47b9400160e7b68404b216f53ba76ccf5891bcf','registered','formalised as H-020',3.3251,'H-020','2026-11-05T15:44:47.191227+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-003','S20261105T172127Z','Daily internal bar strength dip buy in 200-day uptrend','repo','https://doc.stocksharp.com/en/api-examples/0927_Internal_Bar_Strength_IBS','Internal Bar Strength IBS Strategy (StockSharp docs)','unknown','Daily signals from closed UTC daily candles built from 1h data, executed at the next 1h open. IBS = (close - low) / (high - low) of the daily candle; skip days with zero range. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with IBS < 0.2 AND daily close > SMA(200 days) AND no open position. EXIT when a later daily candle closes with IBS >= 0.8. Safety exit: daily close below the 200-day SMA. Optional hard stop 12% below entry. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance. The source uses 0.2 and 0.8 thresholds on 4h bars with no trend filter; the 200-day filter and daily frame are my adaptation.','A close near the day''s low in an uptrend often reflects forced selling or liquidity-driven pressure at the end of the day. Dip buyers who provide liquidity are paid when price reverts the next sessions. The source gives no mechanism; this is the usual short-term reversal / liquidity-provision explanation.','1d',200,4,1,14.0,'DailyIBSDip','665ca9337a26f817ae3886f1d35a3643611d21f22d9a804bd196a0b8eec4e1be','registered','formalised as H-021',3.1905,'H-021','2026-11-05T17:22:20.894055+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-004','S20261105T172127Z','Connors 3-day lower highs and lows pullback in 200-day uptrend','blog','https://www.tradingview.com/script/2DMs2jT9','Larry Connors 3-day high/low method (TradingView open-source script)','unknown','Daily signals from closed UTC daily candles built from 1h data, executed at the next 1h open. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close > SMA(200 days); close < SMA(5 days); and three consecutive days of falling range, meaning each of the last three daily candles has both a lower high and a lower low than the candle before it (today vs yesterday, yesterday vs two days ago, two days ago vs three days ago); and no open position. EXIT when a daily close is above SMA(5 days). Safety exit: daily close below SMA(200 days) or 12% below entry. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance, no add-ons (the source''s optional add-on is excluded).','Three successive days of lower highs and lows inside a long-term uptrend is a short-lived selling streak. Impatient sellers and stop-triggered holders push price below its short mean, and buyers who provide liquidity are paid when price snaps back to the 5-day mean. The source states no mechanism; this is the standard short-term reversal explanation.','1d',200,4,1,8.0,'ThreeDayLowerRangeDip','57b1f8d970a707f77122887507d9d8c89b89aa3f4c65bdc7c1faea6abfa43a1f','registered','formalised as H-022',2.5137,'H-022','2026-11-05T17:22:20.900770+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-005','S20261105T183908Z','Daily R3: three falling RSI(2) readings ending below 10, in 200-day uptrend','repo','https://in.tradingview.com/script/5CDSns2I-R3-ETF-Strategy','R3 ETF Strategy (TradingView open-source script, after Connors and Alvarez)','unknown','All signals from closed daily candles (UTC) built from 1h data, executed at next 1h open. Compute RSI(2) on daily closes and SMA(200 days) of daily close. ENTRY when a daily candle closes with: close > SMA200 AND RSI(2) has fallen on each of the last three days (RSI today < RSI yesterday < RSI two days ago < RSI three days ago) AND RSI(2) three days ago was below 60 AND RSI(2) today is below 10, with no open position. EXIT when a daily close has RSI(2) above 70. No stop, no profit target. One position per pair, whole balance.','A multi-day one-way slide that ends in extreme short-term oversold inside a long-term uptrend is typically forced or panicked selling (liquidations, stop runs). Liquidity providers and dip buyers on the other side collect the usual partial snap-back. The source gives no mechanism beyond the ETF mean-reversion claim; this is the closest honest one.','1d',200,5,1,7.0,'DailyR3Streak','ab7bf7d7a72fee656de5e0d908a5b8774dca7b80618d1c014fb646352f63974c','registered','formalised as H-023',2.2501,'H-023','2026-11-05T18:39:53.248450+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-006','S20261105T191024Z','Late-evening UTC two-hour window long in daily uptrend and high-volatility regime','blog','https://quantpedia.com/the-seasonality-of-bitcoin/','The Seasonality of Bitcoin (Quantpedia)','none','Hourly candles, UTC. Regime is read from daily data at 00:00 UTC and holds for that whole UTC day. Uptrend: the last closed daily close is above the 50-day SMA of daily closes. High volatility: the 30-day standard deviation of hourly returns is above the median of that same measure over the previous 180 days (shortened from the source''s 365 to fit the lab''s lookback limit). ENTRY: on days when both hold, buy at the open of the 21:00 UTC hourly candle. EXIT: sell at the open of the 23:00 UTC candle (two hour hold, no stop). One position, whole balance, no other filters.','The source offers no firm mechanism. The closest honest story: liquidity thins and US-evening order flow, plus retail and derivative-hedging flows near the daily roll, push prices up late in the UTC day; they pay for immediacy. The effect is likely strongest when volatility is high and the trend is up. Academic work finds time-of-day effects unstable across periods, and a 2-hour hold may not clear 0.35% costs.','1h',4320,4,1,120.0,'IntradayUTCWindow','32c57879124fbc9ba3d87a70c4043fc0a304753b05369faa13300a0749af269f','dropped','forbidden by the lab: derivatives',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-05T19:11:12.743800+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-007','S20261105T191114Z','Daily lottery-jump (MAX) persistence gate with 20-day mean exit','paper','https://research.birmingham.ac.uk/en/publications/max-momentum-in-cryptocurrency-markets/','MAX momentum in cryptocurrency markets','none','Daily signals from closed UTC daily candles, executed at next 1h open. MAX(t) = largest daily close-to-close return among the last 30 daily closes including the just-closed day. Jump-regime is on when MAX(t) is at or above the median of MAX over the previous 150 days (excluding today). ENTRY: jump-regime on AND daily close > SMA(50 days) AND daily close > highest daily close of the prior 10 days AND no open position. EXIT: daily close < SMA(20 days). Hard stop 12% below entry, checked on closed bars. No re-entry for 3 days after exit. Long only, one position, whole balance. Single-asset time-series adaptation of the cross-sectional MAX momentum finding (the paper sorts coins; this is my own adaptation).','The source says crypto has lottery-like, positively skewed payoffs and that coins with large recent maximum daily returns keep earning higher returns (attention and speculative demand persist). The other side is late sellers and contrarians who treat a spike as an overreaction and sell into continuing attention-driven demand. The source gives no single-asset version; this is the closest honest reading.','1d',180,6,0,7.0,'DailyMaxJumpMomentum','26d6ec0a3d544ee41d461c309ade4f0676306baf5b0da78dbf251d86adb11fc9','registered','formalised as H-024',1.9705,'H-024','2026-11-05T19:12:04.019476+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-008','S20261105T193815Z','Daily nearness-to-26-week-high momentum gate with hysteresis exit','paper','https://wp.ffu.vse.cz/artkey/wps-202301-0003_impact-of-size-and-volume-on-cryptocurrency-momentum-and-reversal.php','Impact of size and volume on cryptocurrency momentum and reversal (FFA Working Papers)','unknown','Daily signals from closed daily candles, executed at the next 1h open. Define H(d) = highest daily high of the 182 days ending at day d (including d). Nearness N(d) = close(d)/H(d). ENTRY when a daily candle closes with N(d) >= 0.95 and no position is open. EXIT when a daily candle closes with N(d) < 0.85. Between 0.85 and 0.95 hold the current state (hysteresis). No other filters, no take-profit, no leverage, one position per pair. Parameters: window 182 days, entry 0.95, exit 0.85.','Investors anchor on recent highs and are reluctant to bid prices up to and through them, so good news is underreacted to near the high (George-Hwang anchoring). Sellers who sell near the high give away the slow drift. The paper gives distance from the k-week high as a predictor for large liquid coins, which BTC, ETH and BNB are; the exact trading rule here is my own adaptation.','1d',182,3,0,6.0,'NearHighAnchorGate','e5a3bef73e8f4111682b78c32bd30b6f2c625add057bfa8a7203a9db45368706','registered','formalised as H-026',2.3001,'H-026','2026-11-05T19:39:11.958565+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-009','S20261105T193815Z','Daily Keltner upper-band close breakout in uptrend, exit at EMA20','repo','https://doc.stocksharp.com/en/api-examples/0955_Keltner_Channel','Keltner Channel Strategy (StockSharp API examples)','unknown','Daily signals from closed daily candles, executed at the next 1h open. Keltner mid = EMA(20) of daily close; ATR(20) simple/Wilder average of daily true range; upper band = mid + 1.5*ATR(20). ENTRY when a daily close is above the upper band, the previous daily close was at or below the previous upper band (fresh cross), daily close > SMA(100), and no position is open. EXIT when a daily close falls below EMA(20), or close is 2.0*ATR(20) (at entry) below the entry price (stop checked on daily closes). Source uses 1.5 band multiplier and 20-length; I adapted the lower-band reversion idea into a trend breakout on the upside, so the rule is my own.','A close beyond 1.5 ATR above the 20-day mean marks a volatility expansion; slower participants and stop-driven sellers/short covers chase it over following days, so the move tends to continue until price falls back to the mean. Source gives no mechanism for the breakout direction; this is the closest honest one.','1d',100,5,1,8.0,'DailyKeltnerBreakout','cccd11193f5e4e567ef17ac9e808e506c771be7bbd02d52d0f77d0938103ead2','registered','formalised as H-025',2.7201,'H-025','2026-11-05T19:39:11.965980+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-010','S20261105T202520Z','Daily Supertrend (ATR 10, x3) long-only flip trend follower','repo','https://stocksharp.com/store/strategies.0010_super_trend/','Super Trend (C#) - StockSharp strategy store','unknown','Daily signals from closed daily candles built from the 1h data, executed at the next 1h open. Compute ATR(10) on daily candles (Wilder smoothing). Basic bands: hl2 +/- 3.0 * ATR. Final lower band only ratchets up while the close stays above it and resets when price closes below it; the Supertrend line is the final lower band in an uptrend and the final upper band in a downtrend. ENTRY: the daily close crosses from below to above the Supertrend line (trend flips to up) and no position is open. EXIT: the daily close crosses below the Supertrend line (trend flips to down); the line itself acts as a trailing stop. No other filters, no take-profit, no fixed stop. Long only, whole balance, one position per pair.','Trend followers who trade a volatility-scaled trailing stop profit from slow information diffusion and herding in crypto: large moves tend to continue, while the ATR-scaled trail cuts losers. The other side is late mean-reversion sellers and traders who fade breakouts. The source gives no mechanism beyond the technical description, so this is the closest honest one.','1d',60,2,1,7.0,'DailySupertrendFlip','3034b0e2ca74659971519f5b023859a531eef36ea6ab6d85dac6a37a8605ba0f','registered','formalised as H-027',2.9843,'H-027','2026-11-05T20:26:17.530457+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-011','S20261105T225949Z','Intraday momentum: strong early-UTC-day move predicts late-day continuation','paper','https://research.birmingham.ac.uk/en/publications/bitcoin-intraday-time-series-momentum/','Bitcoin intraday time series momentum','unknown','Hourly candles, UTC clock. At the close of the 03:00 UTC bar (the bar covering 03:00-04:00), compute r = that close / open of the 00:00 UTC bar of the same day - 1. If r >= +1.0% and no position is open, buy at the open of the next bar (04:00 UTC). Exit at the close of the 15:00 UTC bar (executed at the 16:00 open) regardless of price. Stop: exit if a closed 1h bar is 2.5% below entry. At most one trade per day per pair. No other filters. All signals hourly.','The source reports that the early-session return positively predicts a later-session return and attributes it to liquidity provision (dealers laying off inventory gradually), not late news. The other side is those who sell into the early move too cheaply and must re-buy later. The source defines sessions by volume, not UTC clock, so fixed UTC windows are an adaptation. The gross move after a >=1% early move must exceed 0.35% to pay; this is not guaranteed.','1h',5,5,0,40.0,'IntradayEarlySessionMomentum','82f6d343e7210d1c657bf042cd0bc1e35d194a13a08ee40455ed704391044fe1','registered','formalised as H-028',2.7647,'H-028','2026-11-05T23:01:23.137342+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-012','S20261105T225949Z','Monday-session long in daily uptrend, flat by Monday close','blog','https://quantpedia.com/are-there-any-simple-calendar-effects-in-bitcoin-market/','Are There Any Simple Calendar Effects in Bitcoin Market?','unknown','Signals from closed daily candles plus the hourly clock. Condition: the last closed daily close is above its 50-day SMA of daily closes. Entry: buy at the 00:00 UTC bar open on Monday if the condition holds and no position is open. Exit: sell at the open of the Tuesday 00:00 UTC bar (i.e. hold exactly 24 hours), or earlier on a close-based stop when a closed 1h bar is 3% below entry. One trade per week per pair. Daily filter is daily; entry and exit are on the hourly chart.','The source documents a higher Monday return and lower weekend volume in Bitcoin, likening it to currency markets, and suggests retail dominance causes inefficiency. It also found the effect inconsistent over time and concludes there is no reliable exploitable pattern. Closest honest mechanism: weekend thin liquidity lets sellers push price down and Monday''s return of institutional flow restores it. A 24h Monday move must exceed 0.35% to pay, which is doubtful; this is a low-confidence diversifier.','1h',1200,4,0,35.0,'MondayEffectLong','29a7320f6352081aa6b1be72d265119cc87dc73411ae768f29af67a5f4f48398','registered','formalised as H-029',2.2742,'H-029','2026-11-05T23:01:23.141965+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-013','S20261105T225949Z','Thin-liquidity overnight drop reversal: buy 08:00 UTC after sharp 00-08 UTC fall','blog','https://quantpedia.com/are-there-any-simple-calendar-effects-in-bitcoin-market/','Are There Any Simple Calendar Effects in Bitcoin Market?','unknown','Hourly candles, UTC clock. At the close of the 07:00-08:00 UTC bar compute d = close/open(00:00 UTC bar of the same day) - 1 (the overnight return over 8 bars). If d <= -1.5% and the last closed daily close is above the 100-day SMA of daily closes and no position is open, buy at the next bar open. Exit at the open of the 16:00 UTC bar the same day (when US hours are active), or earlier if a closed 1h bar is 3% below entry. One trade per day per pair. Daily trend filter is daily; others hourly.','The source notes volume is lowest overnight and higher while US markets are open. Moves made in thin hours are less backed by real flow, so sellers who pushed price down through an empty book may be partly reversed when liquidity returns. This mechanism is the closest honest one, not stated by the source. The 0.35% round-trip cost needs a rebound well above that after a 1.5% drop, which fits only if reversals are sizeable. This is the opposite sign of idea 1, so it is a distinct test.','1h',2400,5,0,25.0,'OvernightDropReversal','768a26ce45c88544d9c469feda4abfe9b762d981308a5aab5408e14b53ebfc08','registered','formalised as H-030',2.1333,'H-030','2026-11-05T23:01:23.146453+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-014','S20261106T002034Z','UTC-day opening-range breakout on 15m, wide ranges only, midpoint stop and time exit','blog','https://www.altrady.com/blog/crypto-trading-strategies/orb-trading-strategy','ORB Trading Strategy (Altrady)','unknown','15m closed candles, UTC clock; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. Each UTC day, the opening range is the highest high and lowest low of the four 15m bars from 00:00 to 01:00 UTC. The day is armed only if (range high - range low)/range low >= 0.8%. ENTRY: between 01:00 and 12:00 UTC, the first 15m close above the range high, if flat and no trade yet today (one trade per day per pair). EXIT, first of: 15m close below the range midpoint; 15m close >= range high + 1.5 x range height (profit target); 20:00 UTC bar close (time exit). No re-entry the same day. No trend filter.','Overnight/early-session range compression is followed by a directional move when the first participants of the Asian-to-Europe handover (stops, breakout buyers, momentum chasers) hit the book; late sellers who fade the range are forced to cover or chase. The width filter keeps the range at 0.8% or more, so a 1.5x range-height target is a move well above the 0.35% round-trip cost; the midpoint stop caps the loss at about half a range. Source gives the generic ORB rule and no crypto mechanism; this is the closest honest one.','15m',4,5,0,90.0,'SessionOpeningRangeBreakout','09c197ba5057f885ffac40f9c143bbe0e6ff07497c00a7435c0227ff0818cfb3','registered','formalised as H-034',2.2442,'H-034','2026-11-06T00:21:23.846236+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-015','S20261106T002034Z','Cross-pair catch-up: buy the laggard after the other two pairs jump on 1h','paper','https://irep.iium.edu.my/73405/','Lead-lag relationship between Bitcoin and Ethereum: evidence from hourly and daily data','unknown','1h closed candles of the three pairs; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. For pair X at bar t, let L(t) = mean of the 2-bar returns (close(t)/close(t-2) - 1) of the other two pairs, and r(t) = X''s own 2-bar return. ENTRY when L(t) >= 1.5%, r(t) <= L(t) - 1.0% (X has not followed), and no position in X. EXIT at the close of the 4th bar after entry (time exit), or earlier if X closes below its entry price by 1.5% (stop checked on closed bars). Cooldown 4 bars after exit. No other filters.','Price discovery is not instant across pairs: the source finds causality running between BTC and ETH on hourly data (mixed, and it warns that profit is hard). Smaller or less liquid pairs absorb a large move in the others with a delay because market makers and arbitrageurs re-quote them in steps, so the laggard catches up. Only large jumps (1.5% or more with a gap of 1% or more) are used, so that a catch-up of a fraction of the gap can exceed the 0.35% cost. The source gives no tradable rule; the edge is doubtful and is left for the gates to judge.','1h',2,5,0,25.0,'CrossPairCatchUp','d9766f4169b7f060f3429359bcb13c51cb28245e0aa47dbef544a532be4171e5','registered','formalised as H-031',2.8095,'H-031','2026-11-06T00:21:23.854941+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-016','S20261106T092700Z','Hourly negative-shock overreaction: buy 4h crash close, 24h hold','paper','https://ideas.repec.org/a/taf/recsxx/v25y2022i1p1294-1313.html','Intraday Bitcoin price shocks: when bad news is good news','unknown','Closed 1h candles only; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance. r4(t) = close(t)/close(t-4) - 1. ENTRY at close of bar t when r4(t) <= -4.0% AND close(t) > SMA(1200 bars) of close (not a long-term downtrend) AND no open position. EXIT at the close of bar t+24 (executed next open), or earlier at close if close >= close(t-4) (the pre-drop price); hard stop: close 5% below entry price, checked on closed bars. No re-entry within 12 bars of an exit. All thresholds are fixed in advance, not tuned.','Forced sellers (liquidations, stop cascades, panic market orders) push price below fair value within hours; liquidity providers and patient buyers are paid to absorb the flow as price relaxes back over 6-24 hours. The cited paper reports overreaction after negative hourly shocks that grows over 6-24 hours; it gives no explicit rule, so thresholds here are my own. A 4% drop with partial recovery to the pre-drop price targets a move well above the 0.35% cost.','1h',1200,5,1,12.0,'HourlyShockOverreaction','7f6565fe76bbcacb50b420c8f0d88a0de60a9ef0cec4428a7a715efba7807e7c','registered','formalised as H-033',3.7179,'H-033','2026-11-06T09:29:52.111753+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-017','S20261106T092700Z','Volatility-scaled hourly crash with volume spike, rebound to crash-bar open','paper','https://ideas.repec.org/a/taf/recsxx/v25y2022i1p1294-1313.html','Intraday Bitcoin price shocks: when bad news is good news','unknown','Closed 1h candles only; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. Long only, one position per pair, whole balance. r1(t) = close(t)/close(t-1) - 1. S(t) = standard deviation of r1 over the 720 bars ending at t-1. V(t) = volume(t) divided by the mean volume of the 168 bars ending at t-1. ENTRY at close of bar t when r1(t) <= -3.0*S(t) AND r1(t) <= -1.5% AND V(t) >= 3 AND (close(t)-low(t))/(high(t)-low(t)) >= 0.5 (bar closes in its upper half, rejecting the low) AND no open position. EXIT at the close of the first bar with close >= open of the crash bar t (executed next open), or at the close of bar t+18, whichever is first. Stop: close 4% below entry on closed bars. Cooldown 6 bars after exit.','A volume-spiking crash bar that closes off its low shows forced or panic selling being absorbed; the cited paper finds overreaction after negative hourly shocks that keeps reversing for 6-24 hours. Sellers who dumped at the low pay the rebound to patient buyers. The paper gives no explicit rule; the volume spike and range-position confirmation are my own additions. The target (crash-bar open) is at least 1.5% above the signal close, above the 0.35% cost.','1h',720,6,1,15.0,'VolumeSpikeCrashRebound','1a0cac8402259fbca65a082c11d117296894ee7373c0d3fb20d31d7c1734c3f1','registered','formalised as H-032',3.7568,'H-032','2026-11-06T09:29:52.120194+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-018','S20261106T102744Z','Hourly range-expansion bar closing at its high, continuation hold in uptrend','blog','https://www.altrady.com/blog/crypto-trading-strategies/orb-trading-strategy','Opening range breakout (ORB) trading strategy - Altrady','unknown','Closed 1h candles, UTC. Range(t)=high-low of bar t; ATR(t)=mean true range of the 24 bars before t. Pos(t)=(close-low)/(high-low). ENTRY at close of bar t when ALL hold: Range(t) >= 3.0*ATR(t); Pos(t) >= 0.8; close(t) > open(t); close(t) > SMA(480) of 1h closes; no open position. Buy at next bar open. EXIT at the first of: a bar close below the low of the entry-signal bar (stop, executed next open); or 24 bars after entry (time exit at that bar''s open). No re-entry for 6 bars after an exit. No pyramiding, no take-profit.','The source only suggests taking breakouts whose candle is large versus recent candles and closes near its extreme; it gives no mechanism. Closest honest one: an abnormally large bar closing at its high marks forced or stop-driven buying (short covering, breakout stops) that clears liquidity; slower participants and algos chase over the following hours, so drift continues. A 3x-ATR shock bar makes a mean gross move above 0.35% plausible.','1h',480,6,0,40.0,'HourlyRangeExpansionDrift','3838cff88335c796f414b597ad4caab313c2ce75a6ecf042c7e40f9cddd542f2','registered','formalised as H-035',2.2692,'H-035','2026-11-06T10:28:34.973008+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-019','S20261106T105207Z','US-session volume-surge continuation: 1h bar at US open, 4-hour hold','blog','https://quantpedia.com/Blog/Details/are-there-any-simple-calendar-effects-in-bitcoin-market','Are There Any Simple Calendar Effects in Bitcoin Market?','none','Closed 1h candles, UTC clock. Signal bar is the 1h bar opening at 14:00 UTC (covers 14:00-15:00, just after the US cash open). Let V = its volume and Vref = mean volume of the 14:00 bars of the previous 20 days. ENTRY at the close of that bar if V >= 2.0 * Vref AND close > open AND (close/open - 1) >= 0.007 AND close > SMA(200 bars) of 1h closes AND no open position; buy at the next bar open (15:00). EXIT at the close of the 18:00 bar (executed at next open, i.e. 4 bars held), or earlier if a closed bar is more than 1.5% below the entry price. At most one trade per day per pair. No other filters.','Bitcoin activity is highest while US markets are open and thin overnight. A volume-confirmed up move at the US open is likely information-driven flow from institutional and ETF-linked participants who execute in slices over several hours, so price keeps drifting as the remaining orders arrive. The other side is slower liquidity providers and sellers who anchor on the pre-open price. The source describes only the time-of-day volume pattern, not a rule; the rule is my own construction. Whether the continuation exceeds the 0.35% cost is uncertain, which is why the filter demands a large volume and price shock.','1h',480,6,0,40.0,'USOpenVolumeContinuation','9d7cd866ab7fe3e1b0e18515ce1e35fc46e82c0cef21ef108f2bfc238a5db84d','registered','formalised as H-036',2.1667,'H-036','2026-11-06T10:53:14.326360+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-020','S20261106T105207Z','Weekend thin-liquidity drop reversal: buy Sunday-morning dip, exit Sunday close','blog','https://quantpedia.com/Blog/Details/are-there-any-simple-calendar-effects-in-bitcoin-market','Are There Any Simple Calendar Effects in Bitcoin Market?','none','Closed 1h candles, UTC clock, Saturday and Sunday only. Define D = close of the current bar / highest close of the prior 24 bars - 1. ENTRY at the close of any bar whose open time is Saturday 00:00 UTC through Sunday 15:00 UTC when D <= -0.03 (price at least 3% below its 24-hour high close), the bar''s close is above its open (first green bar after the drop), close > SMA(1200 bars) of 1h closes, and no position is open; buy at the next bar open. EXIT when close >= the highest close of the prior 24 bars measured at entry signal time minus half the drop (i.e. half the drop recovered), or at the close of the Sunday 23:00 UTC bar, or on a closed bar 2.5% below entry. One position per pair, at most one trade per weekend per pair.','Weekend volume is lower, so order books are thinner and forced sellers (stop cascades, liquidations of leveraged holders felt on spot) move price further than information justifies. Market makers widen spreads and refill depth only slowly; the buyers who step in when depth returns collect the recovery. The source documents lower weekend volume but no rule, so this is my own construction. A 3% drop with half recovered gives a gross target near 1.5%, above the 0.35% cost, but the trade count is modest and the edge is unproven.','1h',1200,5,0,15.0,'WeekendThinDropReversal','2b0b509bea42ab4b0bfdf90e744397949b0c2ab8a8376ee36068d2015d5d9cd9','dropped','forbidden by the lab: leverage or margin',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-06T10:53:14.333997+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-021','S20261106T112143Z','Hourly MACD cross-up gated by daily MACD uptrend, exit on hourly cross-down','blog','https://quantpedia.com/how-to-design-a-simple-multi-timeframe-trend-strategy-on-bitcoin/','How to Design a Simple Multi-Timeframe Trend Strategy on Bitcoin','unknown','Hourly signals from closed 1h candles, daily trend from closed daily candles built from the 1h data (visible only after the daily close). Daily trend is up when the daily MACD line (EMA12 - EMA26 of daily closes) is above its 9-day EMA signal line. ENTRY at the close of an hourly bar when the hourly MACD line (EMA12 - EMA26 of hourly closes, signal EMA9) crosses from at-or-below to above its signal line, the daily trend is up, and no position is open; buy at next bar open. EXIT at the close of the first hourly bar where the hourly MACD line crosses below its signal line; sell at next open. Also exit if the daily trend turns down at a daily close. Hard stop 5% below entry. No other filters, no pyramiding. All MACD periods are the textbook 12/26/9.','Counterparties are slower participants who react to a daily trend with a delay: when the daily momentum is positive, an hourly momentum re-acceleration marks the continuation leg of the larger move, while the daily gate avoids buying hourly crosses inside downtrends where they are mostly noise. Holding until the hourly cross-down (not one bar) lets winners run to a few percent so the average move can exceed the 0.35% round trip; the source gives only a loose rationale (trade with the higher-timeframe trend), so this is a stated hypothesis, not proven.','1h',1000,3,1,120.0,'MultiTimeframeMACDTrend','25788274e13cef3a70811dad952aabd9116e57accba52bf1145f5457b8145a6a','registered','formalised as H-037',3.8,'H-037','2026-11-06T11:22:31.855464+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-022','S20261106T114433Z','Daily NR7 compression day, next-day upside breakout on 1h in 50-day uptrend','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/nr4-nr7-narrow-range-bars.md','NR4/NR7 Narrow-range Bars','Free to use with attribution (LuxAlgo Library)','Daily signals from closed UTC daily candles built from 1h data; execution on 1h. A day D is NR7 when its high-low range is strictly smaller than the high-low range of each of the 6 days before it. The day after D (UTC), if the last closed daily close is above the SMA(50) of daily closes, ENTRY on the first 1h bar whose close is above the NR7 day''s high (order at next 1h open), only if that bar closes before 20:00 UTC. At most one entry per NR7 day. EXIT at a 1h close below the NR7 day''s low, or after 48 1h bars from entry (time exit), whichever comes first. Hard stop at the NR7 day''s low (checked on closed bars). Enter nothing on days that are not the day after an NR7 day. No take-profit, no pyramiding.','A very narrow day means participants agreed on price and resting stop orders and breakout orders stack just beyond the range. When price clears the high, short covering and momentum buyers must buy at once, so the following move tends to exceed the narrow range. The sellers who give the money away are those who faded the range and are stopped out. The source gives no mechanism beyond compression-then-expansion; this is the closest honest one. Cost risk: the stop is the narrow range, so the target must be larger than 0.35%.','1d',50,4,1,18.0,'DailyNR7Breakout','6afa0c70e0e2c487300424849b3ea5439c4ef1d206a1c53eebdde9763589356c','registered','formalised as H-040',3.1111,'H-040','2026-11-06T11:45:55.401141+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-023','S20261106T114433Z','Turtle Soup on 1h: failed 20-day-low sweep reclaimed within 3 bars, buy the stop run','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/turtle-soup.md','Turtle Soup','Free to use with attribution (LuxAlgo Library)','Closed 1h candles only, signals at bar close, order at next bar open. Let PL = lowest low of the 480 bars (20 days) before bar t-3, and require that this low was set at least 96 bars (4 days) before bar t. SWEEP: within bars t-3..t, at least one bar low is below PL. RECLAIM: close(t) > PL and close(t-1) <= PL or the sweep occurred on bar t itself with close(t) > PL (first reclaim close only). ENTRY at close of t when sweep and reclaim hold and no position is open. Let S = the lowest low over bars t-3..t. EXIT at the first close >= the highest high of the 24 bars ending at t (target), or after 48 bars from entry, or at a close below S (stop, checked on closed bars). One entry per sweep; no re-entry for 24 bars after exit.','Stop orders of longs and breakout sellers cluster just under a well-known 20-day low. Price is pushed through, the stops trigger forced selling, and once that supply is gone and price closes back above the level, there is no follow-through, so the move snaps back. The other side is the breakout seller who sold the failed break. The source gives no evidence or mechanism beyond the pattern description; this is the closest honest one. The rebound toward the 24h high is typically several percent, above the 0.35% cost.','1h',480,5,1,25.0,'HourlyFailedBreakdownReclaim','0b1153f5e74986d152492438e675b0502c9ffd7ef546b154b6060e845264dc11','registered','formalised as H-038',3.2561,'H-038','2026-11-06T11:45:55.407803+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-024','S20261106T114433Z','Weekend daytime session long (Sat/Sun 13:00-21:00 UTC) when NYSE is closed, in 50-day uptrend','blog','https://quantpedia.com/are-there-seasonal-intraday-or-overnight-anomalies-in-bitcoin/','Are There Seasonal Intraday or Overnight Anomalies in Bitcoin?','unknown','UTC clock, closed 1h candles. On Saturday and Sunday only: if the last closed daily candle''s close is above the SMA(50) of daily closes (daily signal, forward-filled so only completed days are used), buy at the open of the 13:00 UTC 1h bar (14:00 bar of the US session start is 13:30 UTC in winter, so 13:00 is a fixed approximation). EXIT at the close of the 20:00 UTC bar (sell at the next open, 21:00 UTC). Hard stop 3% below entry on closed bars. Skip a day if a bar is missing. One position per pair, whole balance, no other filters.','The source reports that when the traditional market is closed, Bitcoin earns most of its return in the New York daytime hours, while on NYSE-open days the return is mostly overnight. A plausible reason is that retail and crypto-native flows are the only active buyers on weekends and hedging or arbitrage supply from equity-linked desks is absent. The other side is thin weekend sellers. Caution: the per-trade average gross move may be small compared with the 0.35% cost; the uptrend gate and stop are meant to concentrate it.','1h',1200,4,1,80.0,'WeekendDaytimeSession','cbd9acadfe3c307a0bb9a943251389cdec837abf25db1bb8e1f858dccea942e7','registered','formalised as H-039',3.2209,'H-039','2026-11-06T11:45:55.412248+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-025','S20261106T132940Z','Williams-style volatility breakout: day open plus 0.6 x prior-day range, 1h, flat at UTC midnight','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/volatility-breakout.md','Volatility Breakout (LuxAlgo Library)','Free to use with attribution','Closed 1h candles, UTC days. For each UTC day D: O = open of the 00:00 bar; R = (high - low) of day D-1 from 1h data; level = O + 0.6*R. Daily filter: close of day D-1 > SMA(50) of daily closes (50 closed days, built from 1h). ENTRY: at the close of any 1h bar from 01:00 to 18:00 UTC whose close > level, if flat and no trade already taken that day; buy at next bar open. Require R/O >= 0.02 so the trigger distance is at least 1.2%. EXIT: hard stop when a 1h close < O - 0.5*R, or at the open of the 00:00 UTC bar of the next day (time exit), whichever first. One trade per day max, no re-entry. Signals daily-derived, execution hourly.','A move of more than half of yesterday''s range beyond the open shows one-sided order flow (stop-run buying, momentum chasers, liquidations of late shorts) that tends to carry into the same day. Counterparties are sellers anchored to the open and the prior range who get run over. Requiring a wide prior range (>=2%) makes the post-trigger drift large relative to the 0.35% round trip; the day-end exit caps exposure.','1h',1200,4,0,70.0,'HourlyWilliamsVolBreakout','58853f41369ddb3bee417e410a79d92c17272f9717135e60ea52508bcab06cbd','registered','formalised as H-043',2.1429,'H-043','2026-11-06T13:30:51.396164+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-026','S20261106T132940Z','Hourly inside-bar breakout of a wide mother bar, trend-filtered, midpoint invalidation','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/inside-bar/','Inside Bar (LuxAlgo Library)','Free to use with attribution','Closed 1h candles. Mother bar M = bar t-2, inside bar = bar t-1 when high(t-1) < high(t-2) and low(t-1) > low(t-2). Mother range must satisfy (high-low)/low >= 1.2%. Trend filter: close(t-1) > SMA(240) of 1h closes. ENTRY: the first bar t'' within the 6 bars after the inside bar whose close > mother high, if flat; buy at the next open. If no breakout in 6 bars the setup is void. EXIT: first 1h close below the mother-bar midpoint (high+low)/2, or after 24 bars from entry, whichever first. Stop: close below mother low also exits (covered by the midpoint rule). Source gives only the pattern and trend filter; the numbers here are my fixed choices.','After a large bar, a contained bar means the market digested the move without giving back ground; resting breakout stop orders and trend followers sit above the mother high. When it breaks, forced buyers (short covering, breakout chasers) pay up. Sellers on the other side are those who faded the large bar. The wide-mother-bar condition (>=1.2%) targets continuation moves larger than the 0.35% cost; the source warns many such breaks fail, so this is honest-uncertain.','1h',240,4,0,60.0,'HourlyInsideBarBreakout','d0c5b3ae00647b9ad7251bfab284ace9da2686b869cb0330b0ba6dcd7b63de88','registered','formalised as H-042',2.2872,'H-042','2026-11-06T13:30:51.400630+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-027','S20261106T132940Z','Weekly anchored-VWAP reclaim: buy 1h close back above Monday-anchored VWAP in uptrend','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/anchored-vwap.md','Anchored VWAP (LuxAlgo Library)','Free to use with attribution','Closed 1h candles, UTC. Weekly VWAP(t) = sum(typical price*volume)/sum(volume) over bars from Monday 00:00 UTC through bar t, typical price=(high+low+close)/3. The source gives no explicit entry rule; this is my restatement of its ''reclaim of anchor'' idea. Eligible from Monday 12:00 UTC (at least 12 bars in the week). Filter: close > SMA(480) of 1h closes. SETUP: at least 8 consecutive 1h closes below VWAP, with the lowest close in that run at least 1.0% below VWAP. ENTRY: first 1h close above VWAP after the setup, buy at next open, flat only. EXIT: 1h close more than 0.7% below VWAP, or close of the Sunday 23:00 bar (week end), or 48 bars after entry. Re-anchors every Monday.','VWAP is the average cost of the week''s participants; after a sustained dip (at least 1% under it) many buyers are underwater and sell into the first retrace to break-even, but a clean reclaim means supply was absorbed and mean-reversion funds and VWAP-benchmarked execution algos buy back toward it. Counterparties are late dip sellers. The 1% depth makes the reversion distance exceed the 0.35% cost; evidence is source-light so treat as exploratory.','1h',480,5,0,40.0,'WeeklyAnchoredVWAPReclaim','51d4b218ecb401aa7371ebde7486bb11dba53dbdbbaf33003879a98da222a2f6','registered','formalised as H-041',2.2925,'H-041','2026-11-06T13:30:51.405068+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-028','S20261106T145531Z','Relative-strength ratio breakout vs the other two pairs, hourly rotation long','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/ratio-charts.md','Ratio Charts (LuxAlgo library)','unknown','Closed 1h candles. For traded pair X, let Y be the geometric mean of the closes of the other two pairs; ratio R(t) = close_X(t)/Y(t). ENTRY at close of bar t (fill next open) when: R(t) > SMA(480) of R; R(t) is the highest R close of the last 120 bars (including t); close_X(t) > SMA(480) of close_X; no position open. EXIT at close of bar t (next open) when R(t) < SMA(48) of R, or close_X(t) < SMA(480) of close_X. Hard stop 6% below entry. After an exit wait 12 bars. All signals hourly; no daily data.','Capital rotates between large caps in waves: when one coin starts outperforming the basket, flows from momentum traders, and slow spreading of news across pairs, keep that leadership going for days. The counterparty is the holder who sells a leader too early or an arbitrageur who underprices persistent leadership. A leadership run lasts days and a move of several percent, well above the 0.35% cost, and the exit waits for ratio weakness so winners run.','1h',480,5,0,25.0,'RelativeStrengthRatioRotation','59eeca355f6b4a5be9c0de6923dbb496046cf28dc95a044cf43ad760bf10562c','registered','formalised as H-047',2.1944,'H-047','2026-11-06T14:57:22.268108+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-029','S20261106T145531Z','Hourly confirmed-swing structure break: higher swing low then close above swing high','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/swing-high-low.md','Swing High/Low (LuxAlgo library)','unknown','Closed 1h candles. A swing high (low) at bar i is the highest high (lowest low) of bars i-3..i+3, known only at the close of bar i+3. A swing move is only valid if the distance between consecutive opposite swings is at least 2.0%. BULLISH STRUCTURE: the latest confirmed swing low is higher than the one before it. ENTRY at the close of bar t when structure is bullish, close(t) > the latest confirmed swing high, close(t-1) was not above it, close(t) > SMA(200) of closes, and no position open. EXIT at close of bar t (next open) when close(t) < the latest confirmed swing low. Hard stop at 4% below entry. After exit wait 6 bars. Signals all hourly.','Stop orders and breakout buy orders cluster just beyond visible swing highs; once price clears one after a higher low, forced short covering and trend followers add demand and the move tends to extend. The counterparty is the participant who sold at the prior high or whose resting stops are triggered. The 2% minimum swing and the SMA filter aim for moves that comfortably exceed the 0.35% cost.','1h',200,5,0,60.0,'HourlySwingStructureBreak','6c4d8d0a749cea0625d3a512d13e3f06828f978affa5539d47dd9c3d4490ae8c','registered','formalised as H-045',2.2561,'H-045','2026-11-06T14:57:22.274757+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-030','S20261106T145531Z','4-hour Heikin Ashi trend flip built from 1h candles, no-lower-wick confirmation','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/heikin-ashi.md','Heikin Ashi (LuxAlgo library)','unknown','Build 4-hour candles from 1h bars (UTC blocks 00,04,08,12,16,20), then Heikin Ashi candles from them: haC=(O+H+L+C)/4, haO=(prev haO+prev haC)/2 (first bar (O+C)/2), haH=max(H,haO,haC), haL=min(L,haO,haC). Bar is bullish if haC>haO. ENTRY at the close of a 4h bar (fill next 1h open) when this bar and the previous one are both bullish, the previous bar was bearish before them (a fresh flip, i.e. the bar two back was bearish), the current bar has no lower wick (haL equals haO within 0.05%), the real 4h close is above SMA(100) of 4h closes, and no position is open. EXIT at the close of the first 4h bar whose HA candle is bearish. Hard stop 5% below entry. Fills use real prices.','Averaged candles filter out noise so a flip with no lower wick marks one-sided buying across two bars; trend followers and slow participants keep pressing in the same direction, so persistent moves are paid for by late sellers fading the trend. Trend legs on 4h give multi-percent moves per trade, far above the 0.35% cost, while losing flips are cut at the next bearish bar. Source states the rule loosely, so counts are my choices.','1h',600,4,0,30.0,'HeikinAshi4hFlip','44a68d226e2197d85a6e014570f5094ebbbe66e5a723362fb0822742dd606ebe','registered','formalised as H-044',2.3246,'H-044','2026-11-06T14:57:22.278606+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-031','S20261106T145531Z','Livermore pivotal-point break with volume expansion and fail-fast exit','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/livermore-pivotal-point.md','Livermore Pivotal Point (LuxAlgo library)','unknown','Closed 1h candles. Pivotal level P = highest high of the prior 240 bars (excluding current). ENTRY at close of bar t (fill next open) when close(t) > P*1.002, volume(t) >= 2.0 * mean volume of the previous 48 bars, close(t) > SMA(480), and no position is open. FAIL-FAST EXIT: if any close within the next 8 bars after entry is below P, exit at the next open. Otherwise (follow-through held) trail: exit when close < lowest low of the prior 48 bars. Hard stop 4% below entry. Wait 12 bars after an exit. All hourly.','A break of a well-watched ten-day high on heavy volume forces short covering and triggers breakout orders; a break that cannot hold means the volume was absorbed by sellers, so leaving at once keeps the loss near the cost. The other side is the supplier who sold at the old high and the shorts who cover late. Winners are trailed for multi-percent moves above the 0.35% cost. The source gives no numbers; all values are my choices.','1h',480,6,0,25.0,'LivermorePivotFailFast','5ca121384df02fe3e98a6520d152cef70d416553a62a661417c895c9937db5c2','registered','formalised as H-046',2.2179,'H-046','2026-11-06T14:57:22.282370+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-032','S20261106T145531Z','Prior-week volume-profile value-area rejection, buy back inside, target point of control','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/volume-profile.md','Volume Profile (LuxAlgo library)','unknown','Closed 1h candles. Every day at 00:00 UTC compute a profile from the previous 168 bars: split the high-low span into 50 equal price rows, spread each bar''s volume evenly over rows its high-low touches, POC = row with most volume, value area = grow from POC adding the heavier pair of adjacent rows until 70% of volume; VAL = bottom of the value area. Levels are frozen for the 24 hours. ENTRY at close of bar t (next open) when low of some bar in t-3..t was below VAL, close(t) > VAL, close(t-1) <= VAL or low(t) < VAL (first reclaim), (POC / close(t) - 1) >= 0.015, and no position open. EXIT at close >= POC (next open), or after 48 bars, or close < the sweep low minus 0.5%. At most one entry per day.','Price that dips out of the previous week''s accepted value and fails to stay out is rejected; the quick return suggests sellers below value were absorbed, and rotation back toward the high-volume node follows as mean-reverting traders and range holders buy. Sellers at the dip pay up. The POC must be at least 1.5% away so the target exceeds the 0.35% cost several times. The source gives no numeric rules; the construction is mine.','1h',168,7,0,30.0,'VolumeProfileValueAreaReject','2fdd8908ddf6fc641e8d7c25e6dbedf97c662d6ff73e0f60dcf5b7444770a3bd','registered','formalised as H-048',1.8269,'H-048','2026-11-06T14:57:22.286168+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-033','S20261106T174907Z','4h Kaufman adaptive MA trend: close 1.5% above rising KAMA, exit on close below KAMA','blog','https://chartschool.stockcharts.com/table-of-contents/technical-indicators-and-overlays/technical-overlays/kaufmans-adaptive-moving-average-kama','Kaufman''s Adaptive Moving Average (KAMA) - StockCharts ChartSchool','unknown','Build 4h candles from closed 1h bars (UTC blocks 00,04,...,20); evaluate only when a 4h bar completes, fill at the next 1h open. Efficiency ratio ER = |close - close 10 bars ago| / sum of |bar-to-bar close changes| over those 10 4h bars. Smoothing constant SC = (ER*(2/3 - 2/31) + 2/31)^2. KAMA = previous KAMA + SC*(close - previous KAMA), seeded with the 10-bar SMA. ENTRY at 4h close when close > KAMA*1.015 AND KAMA is above its value 6 bars earlier (rising) AND flat. EXIT at 4h close when close < KAMA (no band). Hard stop: 8% below entry, checked on closed 1h bars. Cooldown: none. Long only, one position, no pyramiding. Lookback about 120 4h bars for warm-up.','KAMA slows down when price is choppy (low efficiency ratio) and speeds up in clean directional moves, so it filters the range-bound whipsaws that make plain MA crosses lose to costs. The 1.5% entry band and rising-slope condition (the whipsaw filters the guide suggests) require a sizeable displacement, so a trade only starts in an efficient move. The other side is slower participants and mean-reversion sellers who fade early trend legs and under-react to information. Gross move per winning trend leg must be several percent to beat 0.35%; the band and 4h frame cut trade count to roughly 60-100 per year. The Altrady KAMA crypto guide was also read; it gives only the same directional-filter framework with no numeric rule, so evidence is mostly mechanical, not empirical.','1h',480,4,0,70.0,'FourHourKAMATrend','d499fc8a0914b9e1f1839136291161f4ef22ac0ffd66add894f49662c25b5700','registered','formalised as H-049',2.3333,'H-049','2026-11-06T17:49:59.787896+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-034','S20261106T182904Z','Quiet-session range (00-12 UTC) breakout at the US-hours volatility peak, same-day exit','paper','https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.12142','Periodicity in Cryptocurrency Volatility and Liquidity (Hansen, Kim, Kimbrough)','unknown','Closed 1h candles, UTC clock; signal at bar close, order at next bar open. Each UTC day, define the quiet-session range from the twelve 1h bars opening 00:00-11:00 UTC: RH = highest high, RL = lowest low. The day is armed only if (RH-RL)/RL >= 0.008. ENTRY: on a 1h bar opening between 13:00 and 17:00 UTC inclusive, if the day is armed, no position is open and no trade has been taken that day, buy at the next open when the bar''s close is above RH. EXIT: first of (a) a bar close below the range midpoint (RH+RL)/2, (b) the close of the 22:00 UTC bar (exit at next open, so flat by 23:00 UTC). At most one trade per day per pair. No daily-timeframe filter.','Hansen et al. show volatility and volume are strongly periodic by hour and weekday, with algorithmic and futures-schedule flows; other practitioner write-ups (Kaiko/Bloomberg hourly range analysis, as reported in press) place the volatility peak in US hours. A range built in the quiet Asia/Europe hours sits on thin liquidity; when US-hour flow pushes price out of it, stop orders and momentum followers add to the move, and the Birmingham ''Bitcoin intraday time series momentum'' paper attributes intraday momentum to liquidity provision, so earlier sellers of the range lose. Requiring a range of at least 0.8% targets a gross move above the 0.30-0.45% round trip. The source gives no trading rule; this one is my own construction.','1h',12,4,0,150.0,'QuietRangeUSBreakout','844ae58b959ebd0c46bcd5603609e5193d350ecfb540e74a17ab4e2ca531f92c','dropped','forbidden by the lab: derivatives',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-06T18:30:07.501861+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-035','S20261106T183100Z','15m high-volume 6-hour selloff reversal in daily uptrend, 12-hour time exit','paper','https://ideas.repec.org/p/hhs/rbnkwp/0413.html','Trading volume and liquidity provision in cryptocurrency markets','unknown','15m chart, closed bars, signal at bar close, fill at next open. Let r24 = close/close 24 bars ago - 1 (6 hours). Let V6 = sum of volume of the last 24 bars and Vref = mean of the same 24-bar volume sum sampled every 24 bars over the previous 14 days (1344 bars). ENTRY when r24 <= -0.03, V6 >= 1.5*Vref, the bar just closed is green (close > open), the last closed daily close is above the SMA of 100 daily closes (built from 1h/15m), and no position is open. EXIT: first of (a) close >= close 24 bars before entry bar (full retrace) , (b) close <= entry*0.97 (stop), (c) 48 bars (12 hours) after entry, at that bar''s close. Cooldown 24 bars after exit. Long only, one position per pair.','Sharp high-volume sell-offs are partly forced or impatient flow; liquidity providers who absorb it earn a reversal premium as compensation for inventory and adverse-selection risk (Bianchi et al. in Riksbank WP 413: reversal profits are larger when conditioned on high volume; Kozlowski et al. ''Cryptocurrency return reversals'' find reversals robust across subsamples). The trade targets a roughly 2-3% retrace, well above the 0.30-0.45% round trip. Sources are daily-frequency; the intraday transfer is untested, stated honestly. Differs from H-032/H-033 by using a 6h window with a volume-ratio gate and a green confirmation bar.','15m',1344,7,0,150.0,'VolumeConditionedReversal','74615bf5a95930f509f27d051a54d70d57e4329af10da01c276c90c815b3cfc4','registered','formalised as H-050',2.1905,'H-050','2026-11-06T18:31:45.745620+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-036','S20261106T191519Z','High-volume morning session momentum: 08-16 UTC surge carried to 23:00 UTC','paper','https://research.birmingham.ac.uk/en/publications/bitcoin-intraday-time-series-momentum/','Bitcoin intraday time-series momentum','unknown','Closed 1h candles, UTC clock, signal at bar close, order at next bar open. Per pair, one position. Session return S = close of the 15:00 UTC bar / open of the 08:00 UTC bar - 1 (8 bars). Session volume SV = sum of volume of those 8 bars; VrefS = mean of SV over the previous 20 calendar days. ENTRY at the close of the 15:00 bar (buy at 16:00 open) when S >= 0.015 AND SV >= 1.5 * VrefS AND the close of the 15:00 bar is above the SMA(200) of 1h closes AND the 15:00 close is in the top 25% of the 8-bar session range (close - session low)/(session high - session low) >= 0.75. EXIT: close of the 22:00 UTC bar (sell at 23:00 open) or earlier if a closed bar is 1.5% below the entry price. No re-entry the same day. Lookbacks: 8 bars, 20 days (480 bars), 200 bars.','Shen, Urquhart and Wang find early-session Bitcoin returns predict later returns, strongest in the highest volume or volatility sessions, which they attribute to liquidity provision: dealers absorbing a large one-sided flow must rebalance later, pushing price further. Wen et al. (Intraday return predictability in crypto: momentum, reversal, or both) report reversal as well as momentum, and that large jumps change the pattern, so the high-volume and close-near-high filters aim at the momentum regime. Counterparties are liquidity providers and late fading traders. A 1.5% session surge leaves room for a continuation move above the 0.30% round trip, but the evidence is the abstract-level and equity-style daily clock adapted to 24/7 crypto, so it is untested.','1h',480,6,0,150.0,'HighVolumeSessionMomentum','0b1ba5cede0c9ef10dad850f85336a6ff51074a02f1c06a7bf92ba0b01eb0025','registered','formalised as H-051',2.6562,'H-051','2026-11-06T19:16:51.527786+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-037','S20261106T194415Z','Round-number stop cascade: buy the first 15m close through a fresh round price level, target the next level','paper','https://econpapers.repec.org/RePEc:fip:fednsr:125','Currency Orders and Exchange-Rate Dynamics: Explaining the Success of Technical Analysis (Osler, FRBNY Staff Report 125)','unknown','15m closed bars, signal at bar close, fill at next open; long only, one position. ROUND GRID (recomputed once per UTC day from the previous day''s last 15m close P): step S = largest number of the form 1, 2.5 or 5 times a power of ten that is <= 0.02*P (e.g. BTC 60000 -> 1000, ETH 3000 -> 50, BNB 600 -> 10). Levels L = integer multiples of S. ENTRY at close of bar t when: close(t-1) < L <= close(t) for some level L, close(t) >= 1.002*L, the level is fresh (max high of bars t-32..t-1 < L, i.e. untouched for 8 hours), close(t) > SMA(96) of 15m closes (24h mean), and no position is open. EXIT, first of: take-profit limit at L + S (the next round level up); stop at L - 0.5*S (intrabar stop); time exit at the open of the bar 32 bars (8 hours) after entry. At most one entry per level per UTC day.','Osler (FRBNY SR125, and SR150 on price cascades) shows from a dealer''s order book that stop-loss buy orders cluster just above round numbers, so a first break through an untested round level triggers resting stop buys (short-covering, and in crypto also perp short liquidations parked at the same levels) that push price further. The counterparties are the stop-out shorts forced to buy at market. The ATAS practitioner note on round numbers describes the same cascade. The target is the next round level, 0.8-2% away by grid construction, so the gross aim per trade is well above the 0.30-0.45% round-trip cost; the stop is half a step.','15m',96,6,0,200.0,'RoundNumberStopCascade','232873211a916633ab455fc555decda2f0bbe9f0c101f5fbed602855ca173616','registered','formalised as H-054',2.7627,'H-054','2026-11-06T19:52:58.683237+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-038','S20261106T194415Z','Round-number support bounce: buy a 15m rejection of a round level after an 8-hour decline into it','paper','https://econpapers.repec.org/RePEc:fip:fednsr:125','Currency Orders and Exchange-Rate Dynamics: Explaining the Success of Technical Analysis (Osler, FRBNY Staff Report 125)','unknown','15m closed bars, signal at bar close, fill at next open; long only, one position. ROUND GRID as in a daily-fixed grid: from the previous UTC day''s last 15m close P, step S = largest of 1, 2.5 or 5 times a power of ten that is <= 0.02*P; levels L = multiples of S. SETUP at bar t for the nearest level L below max(high of t-32..t-1): (1) price came down into it: max high of bars t-32..t-1 >= 1.012*L; (2) touch without a real break: low(t) <= 1.001*L and low(t) >= 0.996*L, and no bar in t-32..t-1 closed below L; (3) rejection: close(t) >= 1.002*L. ENTRY at next open if flat. EXIT, first of: take-profit limit at entry*1.010; stop when a 15m bar closes below 0.993*L (exit next open); time exit at the open 24 bars (6 hours) after entry. One trade per level per UTC day.','Osler (FRBNY SR125) finds that take-profit orders cluster exactly at round numbers, so a falling market meets a wall of resting buy orders from shorts taking profit and from limit buyers at the round figure; this is why trends tend to stall and reverse at round levels while stops sit just beyond them. The rule buys only when the level holds on a closing basis (stops below were not cascaded), i.e. the resting buy demand absorbed the selling. The sellers on the other side are short-horizon momentum sellers who hit bids at the level. Distinct from the cascade idea (which trades the break); the target is 1.0% gross, above the 0.45% conservative round trip.','15m',32,7,0,180.0,'RoundNumberSupportBounce','fe53b9cc91ab130b86f35a19c65990bd2c874bfe18beb50d2c08f6076cb4ad8e','registered','formalised as H-056',2.0,'H-056','2026-11-06T19:52:58.690948+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-039','S20261106T194415Z','Noise-area intraday momentum: 1h close above the time-of-day noise band from the UTC open, VWAP trailing exit','paper','https://www.sfi.ch/de/publications/n-24-97-beat-the-market-an-effective-intraday-momentum-strategy-for-s-p500-etf-spy','Beat the Market: An Effective Intraday Momentum Strategy for S&P500 ETF (SPY) (Zarattini, Aziz, Barbon, SFI WP 24-97)','unknown','1h closed bars, UTC day; signal at bar close, fill at next open; long only, one trade per pair per UTC day. O = open of the 00:00 UTC bar of the current day. For each hour-of-day slot h (the bar opening at h:00), move_d(h) = |close of slot h on day d / open of day d - 1|. sigma(h) = mean of move_d(h) over the previous 14 completed UTC days (same slot only; 336 bars back). Upper band U(h) = O*(1+sigma(h)). Daily VWAP(h) = cumulative sum of typical price*volume / cumulative volume from the 00:00 bar through slot h, typical=(H+L+C)/3. ENTRY at the close of a bar in slots 01..19 when close > U(h), close > VWAP(h), no trade yet today and flat. EXIT: at the close of any later bar, if close < max(U(h), VWAP(h)) exit at next open; otherwise exit at the open of the next 00:00 UTC bar (time exit, <=23h).','Zarattini, Aziz and Barbon define a noise area from the average absolute move away from the day''s open at each time of day; inside it supply and demand are balanced, and a break outside signals an abnormal order-flow imbalance that tends to persist for the rest of the session (fragmented execution of large rebalancing orders; they also link profitability to dealer gamma imbalance). CXO Advisory and Concretum write-ups describe the same band/VWAP construction. In crypto the persistence is fed by perp liquidations and stop orders once price leaves its usual daily range. Because entry requires price already beyond a typical day''s move and exits trail at the band/VWAP, the trades that survive carry trend-day moves of 1-3%, above the 0.30-0.45% cost. The SPY rule also shorts; only the long side is used here.','1h',336,2,0,170.0,'IntradayNoiseAreaMomentum','163b23b8bfca998d2f6e62b74b9cee6b850c3119add8731783ab0ab00b026e36','registered','formalised as H-052',3.2755,'H-052','2026-11-06T19:52:58.695911+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-040','S20261106T194415Z','Low-volume 12-hour selloff reversal on 1h: buy drops not backed by volume, 12-hour time exit','paper','https://ideas.repec.org/p/cer/papers/wp730.html','Trading Volume and Liquidity Provision in Cryptocurrency Markets (Bianchi, Babiak, Dickerson, CERGE-EI WP 730 / JBF 2022)','unknown','1h closed bars; signal at bar close t, fill at next open; long only, one position, no pyramiding. r12(t) = close(t)/close(t-12) - 1. s12(t) = sample std of 1h log returns over bars t-720..t-1 times sqrt(12). V12(t) = sum of volume over bars t-11..t. Vmed(t) = median of the 60 non-overlapping 12-bar volume sums V12(t-12), V12(t-24), ..., V12(t-720) (prior 30 days, current window excluded). ENTRY at close of t when ALL hold: r12(t) <= -1.0*s12(t); r12(t) <= -0.015; V12(t) < Vmed(t) (the drop happened on below-median volume); no open position. EXIT, first of: close >= close(t-12) of the signal bar (move fully retraced; exit next open); stop at entry*0.95 (intrabar); time exit at the open 12 bars after entry.','Bianchi, Babiak and Dickerson show that in crypto the interaction of past returns and volume predicts reversals: price moves on low volume reflect liquidity demand rather than information and revert, rewarding liquidity providers for inventory risk (CXO Advisory''s summary describes the 12-hour horizon and the low-volume condition). The seller on the other side is an impatient trader pushing price through a thin book; with no information behind the move, the price comes back. The lab already tested the high-volume selloff (H-050); this is the opposite volume condition and a different mechanism. Entry needs at least a 1.5% drop, so a partial retrace of the drop is worth roughly 0.8% or more gross, above the round-trip cost.','1h',732,5,0,150.0,'VolumeConditionedReversal','c17fb883cd171b7fab418e23467758e5773ced81900b0a6b3fd373c9dd946f4d','registered','formalised as H-053',2.8214,'H-053','2026-11-06T19:52:58.700544+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-041','S20261106T194415Z','15m stop-sweep of the 24-hour low reclaimed within an hour, 12-hour time exit','paper','https://econpapers.repec.org/RePEc:fip:fednsr:125','Currency Orders and Exchange-Rate Dynamics: Explaining the Success of Technical Analysis (Osler, FRBNY Staff Report 125)','unknown','15m closed bars; signal at bar close t, fill at next open; long only, one position. PL(t) = lowest low of the 96 bars t-100..t-5 (a 24-hour low, excluding the last 4 bars). SWEEP: min(low of bars t-3..t) < 0.998*PL(t) (the 24h low was taken out by at least 0.2% within the last hour). DEPTH CAP: min(low of t-3..t) >= 0.98*PL(t) (deeper breaks are treated as real breakdowns, no trade). RECLAIM: close(t) > PL(t) and close(t-1) <= PL(t). Trend filter: close(t) > SMA(384) of 15m closes (4-day mean). ENTRY at next open if flat and no entry in the previous 16 bars. EXIT, first of: take-profit limit at entry*1.012; stop at min(low of t-3..t)*0.998 (intrabar); time exit at the open 48 bars (12 hours) after entry.','Osler (FRBNY SR125; SR150 on cascades) shows stop-loss sell orders cluster just beyond obvious levels and make moves accelerate when triggered; once that resting stop supply is used up, price often snaps back because the selling was mechanical, not informed. In crypto the same pool includes long liquidations stacked under the 24h low. The buyer here acts as the liquidity provider to those forced sellers. This is a 24-hour, 15m variant of the tested 20-day failed-breakdown rule (H-038), so it trades far more often. The 1.2% target is more than twice the conservative round trip; the stop sits just under the sweep low.','15m',384,7,0,160.0,'HourlyFailedBreakdownReclaim','ca947beee6db71a537b8931a6e0087bb6b06bae6caf167d473f0d59547b0ef7e','registered','formalised as H-055',2.1935,'H-055','2026-11-06T19:52:58.705013+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-042','S20261106T222439Z','US cash-session weakness, overnight hold: buy at US equity close, sell before next US open','blog','https://cryptoslate.com/bitcoin-keeps-losing-ground-when-wall-street-opens-as-coinbase-discount-deepens/','Bitcoin keeps losing ground when Wall Street opens as Coinbase discount deepens','unknown','Timeframe 1h, closed bars, UTC clock; signal at a bar close, fill at the next bar open. Long only, one position. Applies Monday to Friday only (UTC weekday of the signal bar). US SESSION of day d = the 1h bars opening 13:00 through 19:00 UTC (7 bars, covering the US cash session 09:30-16:00 New York in summer and most of it in winter). S = close of the 19:00 bar / open of the 13:00 bar - 1. ENTRY: at the close of the 19:00 UTC bar on a weekday, if S < +0.003 (the US session did not rally by 0.3% or more) and no position is open, buy at the open of the 20:00 UTC bar. EXIT: sell at the open of the 13:00 UTC bar of the next calendar day (17 bars after entry; Friday entries exit Saturday 13:00). STOP: if a 1h bar closes 3% or more below the entry price, sell at the next open. No other filters, no lookback beyond the same day. Free numbers: the 0.3% session threshold, the 3% stop; the window hours are fixed by the US cash session.','Several measurements (CryptoSlate on Binance BTC/USDT 30m klines; K33 2022 note; the paperswithbacktest write-up of Padysak and Vojtko, which reports that on NYSE-open days most BTC gains accrue outside 15:00-21:00 UTC) find that BTC drifts down during US cash hours and recovers outside them. Proposed counterparty: US-hours sellers who de-risk crypto alongside equities and ETF/basis desks whose redemptions and hedges are executed in the NY session (Kaiko: benchmark NAV window 3-4pm NY), pushing price below where non-US-hours buyers clear it. The long leg holds 17 hours, a horizon whose typical absolute move is well above 1%, so a modest drift is a gross edge above the 0.30-0.45% round trip; trading only after a non-rallying session skips days whose gain was already taken in US hours.','1h',7,2,0,155.0,'USSessionOvernightHold','937f7f45e88918d60574b759cac010de49ff595591c1c072ba916757188b0b5a','registered','formalised as H-058',2.75,'H-058','2026-11-06T22:30:18.545477+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-043','S20261106T222439Z','Abnormal-day detection: buy when the UTC day''s return first exceeds its daily-volatility band, hold 24 hours','paper','https://bura.brunel.ac.uk/handle/2438/20686','Momentum effects in the cryptocurrency market after one-day abnormal returns (Caporale and Plastun, Financial Markets and Portfolio Management 2020)','unknown','Timeframe 1h, closed bars, UTC; signal at a bar close, fill at the next bar open. Long only, one position. DAILY STATISTICS (closed UTC days built from the 1h bars): daily return R = close of the 23:00 bar / close of the previous day''s 23:00 bar - 1; m and s = mean and sample standard deviation of R over the 30 completed days before the current day (720 bars). INTRADAY: O = open of the current day''s 00:00 bar; D(t) = close(t)/O - 1. ENTRY at the close of a bar whose open time is 01:00-18:00 UTC if D(t) >= m + 0.75*s, D(t) >= 0.01, D(t-1) < m + 0.75*s (first crossing), no position is open and no entry has been made earlier that UTC day; buy at the next open. EXIT: at the first of (a) 24 bars after entry, sell at the next open; (b) a bar closes below O (the day''s open, the move has fully failed). One entry per UTC day at most.','Caporale and Plastun find on hourly BTC, ETH and LTC data that once a day''s return becomes abnormal (detectable before the day ends), prices keep moving in its direction until the end of that day and on the next day; they also report exceptions (a contrarian effect for BTC after positive abnormal days), so the edge is honestly uncertain. Closest mechanism: underreaction and late, attention-driven buying (news and trend followers who only notice a move once it is unusually large) plus short-covering, matching the late-informed-trader explanation of Gao et al. (2018) intraday momentum. A crossing of a daily-volatility band of at least 1% followed by a 24-hour hold aims at a continuation of roughly another band width, well above the 0.30-0.45% cost. Differs from H-028/H-052: no fixed early window or time-of-day noise band; the trigger is the day''s own volatility band, and it can fire at any hour.','1h',744,3,0,150.0,'AbnormalDayContinuation','9fb871466c9e2aea5f8576a3320692fe81a6c6ef414193392bf530d292b4c0d9','registered','formalised as H-057',3.2551,'H-057','2026-11-06T22:30:18.555947+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-044','S20261106T234421Z','Settlement-hour dip reversal: buy 15m drops into the 00/08/16 UTC funding and expiry times, 4-hour exit','blog','https://cryptoslate.com/bitcoins-2-24-billion-friday-options-expiry-teased-a-reversal-then-gave-it-back-within-hours/','Bitcoin''s $2.24 billion Friday options expiry teased a reversal then gave it back within hours (summarising a Finance Research Letters study, DOI 10.1016/j.frl.2026.110340)','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, order at the open of bar t+1. Long only, one position. SETTLEMENT TIMES: 00:00, 08:00 and 16:00 UTC. The SIGNAL BAR is the 15m bar that closes exactly at a settlement time (the bars opening at 23:45, 07:45 and 15:45 UTC). P_pre = open of the bar that opened 2 hours before the settlement time (8 bars back, e.g. 06:00 for 08:00). D = close(signal bar)/P_pre - 1. ENTRY at the close of a signal bar when -0.04 <= D <= -0.008 (a fall of 0.8% to 4% in the 2 hours into settlement) and no position is open; buy at the open of the settlement-time bar. EXIT, first of: (a) a 15m close >= P_pre (the pre-drop level is regained), sell at the next open; (b) a 15m close <= entry fill price * 0.98 (stop), sell at the next open; (c) time exit at the close of the 16th bar after entry (4 hours). At most one trade per settlement time. No trend filter. Only 15m data is used.','Perpetual funding is settled for every Binance pair at 00/08/16 UTC, and Ruan and Streltsov (Cornell, ''Perpetual Futures Contracts and Cryptocurrency Market Quality'') show spot volume and spreads spike in these hours from perp-spot arbitrage flows. Traders who close positions just before settlement to avoid paying funding (usually longs, as funding is mostly positive) and arbitrage unwinds create temporary, non-informational selling into the timestamp; once settlement passes, positions are reopened and liquidity providers who absorbed the flow are paid by the rebound. The FRL expiry study found the same shape at the 08:00 UTC Deribit expiry: a fall in the hour before, a reversal in the next two hours. The target is the pre-drop level, at least 0.8% above the signal close, so the gross move per winner exceeds the 0.30-0.45% round trip.','15m',8,5,0,180.0,'SettlementHourDipReversal','0aabca42d6a1ae93d085e88b8b88448a10c37a4037d53c7f8ed52a773b36973a','dropped','forbidden by the lab: derivatives',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-06T23:53:17.755974+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-045','S20261106T234421Z','Intraday positive-jump continuation: buy a 15m bipower-scaled jump, hold to the UTC day close','paper','https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2110.09429','Understanding jumps in high frequency digital asset markets (Saef, Nagy, Sizov, Haerdle)','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, order at the open of bar t+1. Long only, one position. r(i) = ln(close(i)/close(i-1)). Local volatility s(t) = sqrt((pi/2) * mean over i = t-96..t-1 of |r(i)|*|r(i-1)|) (bipower variation over the previous 96 bars, the current bar excluded). Jump statistic J(t) = r(t)/s(t). DAILY FILTER: build UTC daily candles from the 15m data; the last completed daily close must be above the simple mean of the last 30 completed daily closes. ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: J(t) >= 4.0; r(t) >= 0.006; bar t opens between 00:00 and 17:45 UTC; daily filter true; no position open and no trade already taken this UTC day. EXIT, first of: (a) a 15m close below the low of the jump bar t, sell at the next open; (b) the close of the 23:45 UTC bar of the same day, sell at the next open (00:00), so every position closes within 24 hours.','Saef et al. (Lee-Mykland jump test on high-frequency data for many digital assets) find that the sign of an intraday jump matches the sign of that day''s end-of-day return, that jumps cluster in the 13-17 UTC active hours, and that positive jumps matter more in bull markets, when rallies are joined quickly. Wen, Bouri, Xu and Zhao (N. Am. J. Econ. Finance 2022, ideas.repec.org) also report intraday momentum that changes around large jumps and attribute it to late-informed investors. The counterparty is the slower trader who sells into the jump or buys hours later. A 4-sigma jump on 15m is a large move (usually more than 1%), and the drift to the day close is taken over many hours, so the gross move per winner should well exceed costs. Caveat: the paper''s regression is contemporaneous, not a tradable test.','15m',2880,5,0,160.0,'IntradayJumpContinuation','edd7e71e180068c730b17146b003ae295847166a4af3b42131ca65a7a172c01a','registered','formalised as H-059',2.7818,'H-059','2026-11-06T23:53:17.765481+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-046','S20261106T234421Z','Variance-ratio regime gate: 15m 24-hour-high breakout only when short-horizon returns trend','paper','https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/riibaf/v47y2019icp344-353.html','Informational inefficiency of Bitcoin: A study based on high-frequency data (Zargar and Kumar, Research in International Business and Finance 2019)','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, order at the open of bar t+1. Long only, one position. r(i) = ln(close(i)/close(i-1)). VARIANCE RATIO over the 384 bars ending at t: VR(t) = sample variance of the overlapping 4-bar sums r(i-3)+...+r(i) / (4 * sample variance of r(i)), both computed inside that window. HTF FILTER: build 4h candles from the 15m data (UTC blocks 00,04,...,20); the last completed 4h close must be above the simple mean of the last 50 completed 4h closes. ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: close(t) > highest high of bars t-96..t-1 (prior 24 hours); VR(t) >= 1.10; HTF filter true; no position open. EXIT, first of: (a) a 15m close below the lowest low of the prior 16 bars (4 hours), sell at next open; (b) time exit at the close of the 96th bar after entry (24 hours).','Zargar and Kumar''s variance-ratio tests show Bitcoin returns are not a random walk at 15-120 minute horizons although daily returns look memoryless, and that this inefficiency varies over time. Wen et al. (N. Am. J. Econ. Finance 2022) find that intraday crypto returns switch between momentum (late-informed investors) and reversal (overreaction). The gate trades breakouts only when recent 15m returns are positively autocorrelated (VR above 1: herding, liquidation chains, slow information spread), so late buyers keep paying up after the entry. When VR is below 1 the same breakout tends to fade and is skipped. A 24-hour-high breakout held up to a day aims at moves of 1% or more, well above the 0.30-0.45% round trip. This is not H-002: the regime gate is the mechanism and the exit is time-bounded.','15m',800,6,0,170.0,'VarianceRatioRegimeBreakout','5bcac66abcacec5e3ee48ac137a57b82cdb6edbdede4ded6e923415a2d0d096c','registered','formalised as H-063',2.6481,'H-063','2026-11-06T23:53:17.770689+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-047','S20261107T122437Z','Same-time-of-day periodicity: hold the 4-hour UTC block with the strongest trailing 28-day same-block return','paper','https://ar5iv.arxiv.org/html/1005.3535','Intraday Patterns in the Cross-section of Stock Returns (Heston, Korajczyk, Sadka)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars, UTC; signal at bar close, fill at next bar open. Split each UTC day into six 4-hour blocks starting 00,04,08,12,16,20 UTC. Block return R(d,b) = close of the block''s 4th 1h bar / open of its 1st bar - 1. At the close of the 23:00 bar of day d-1, for each block b compute M(b) = mean of R(d-k,b) over the 28 previous completed days k=1..28 (672 bars back) and H(b) = fraction of those 28 returns that are > 0. Pick the block b* with the largest M(b). If M(b*) >= 0.40% AND H(b*) >= 0.57 (16 of 28), buy at the open of the first 1h bar of block b* on day d. EXIT: sell at the close of the 4th bar of that block (filled at the next open, so the hold is exactly 4 hours). Stop: fixed 3% below entry. At most one trade per day per pair; if no block passes, no trade. All signals hourly; no daily indicators.','Heston-Korajczyk-Sadka find returns at the same time of day persist for weeks and tie it to recurring institutional demand: autocorrelated fund flows worked by execution algorithms that trade at the same clock times every day. In crypto the clock-fixed flows are ETF creation/redemption in the 3-4pm New York fixing window, regional session opens and scheduled bots. Liquidity providers who absorb the same predictable demand every day are paid through the price concession. A second source, the hourly weekday event study in Journal of Economics and Management (journals.economic-research.pl/oc/article/view/2091), reports significant hourly means in BTC. 4-hour moves on these pairs are typically 1-2%, and the 0.40% trailing-mean bar keeps only slots whose average drift is above the 0.30% round-trip cost.','1h',672,4,0,180.0,'SameSlotPeriodicity','90670aaad4865d59fe16fb6109281537838a71b6c811c29a8ba81e9db4eb3a5b','registered','formalised as H-060',2.7907,'H-060','2026-11-07T12:30:18.775530+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-048','S20261107T122437Z','Hour-of-week periodicity: trade the weekday 4-hour block with a persistent 26-week same-slot drift','paper','https://journals.economic-research.pl/oc/article/view/2091','A new perspective of the day-of-the-week effect on Bitcoin returns: evidence from an event study hourly approach','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars, UTC; signal at bar close, fill at next bar open. A slot is (UTC weekday, 4-hour block), with blocks starting at 00,04,08,12,16,20 UTC, so there are 42 slots per week. Slot return = close of the block''s 4th 1h bar / open of its 1st bar - 1. At the close of the 23:00 bar before day d, for each of the 6 blocks of day d''s weekday, compute over the same weekday-and-block in the previous 26 weeks (26 observations, up to 4368 bars back): mean m, sample std s (ddof=1), and t = m / (s / sqrt(26)). Choose the block with the largest t. Enter at the open of its first bar only if m >= 0.40% AND t >= 1.5. EXIT at the close of the block''s 4th bar (4-hour hold). Stop: fixed 3% below entry. At most one trade per day per pair. Hourly signals only.','The source computes mean BTC returns for each hour of each weekday and finds significant slots. The likely reason is that weekday-specific flows recur: US ETF primary-market activity only on NYSE days (Kaiko, kaiko.com/resources/btc-etfs-impact-on-spot-market-structure, shows the 3-4pm New York fixing hour''s volume share jumps on weekdays but not weekends), Monday/Friday risk rebalancing, and weekend thin books. Whoever must trade at those clock times pays the price concession. This is a weekly-periodic slot, not the daily-periodic slot of the same-time-of-day idea, so the two pick different slots. The 0.40% mean and t >= 1.5 filters keep only slots whose average 4-hour drift is above the 0.30% cost. Typical 4-hour ranges are 1-2%.','1h',4368,4,0,160.0,'SameSlotPeriodicity','58be73da720bc025e7b407f2aaabc970c1f6841ca737302f06f956854381ff0f','registered','formalised as H-064',2.5,'H-064','2026-11-07T12:30:18.782057+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-049','S20261107T122437Z','Daily floor-pivot S1 reclaim on 15m: buy the close back above S1, target the pivot, flat by UTC day end','blog','https://thepatternsite.com/PivotPoints.html','Pivot Points (Bulkowski, The Pattern Site)','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars, UTC; signal at bar close, fill at next bar open. From the previous completed UTC day (its 96 15m bars) take high H, low L, close C. Standard floor pivots: P=(H+L+C)/3, S1=2P-H, S2=P-(H-L). The day is armed only if (P-S1)/S1 >= 0.8%. ENTRY at the close of bar t whose open time is 00:00-19:45 UTC when all hold: (1) the minimum low of bars t-3..t is below S1; (2) close(t) > S1, and close(t-1) <= S1 or low(t) < S1 (first close back above S1); (3) no low today has been at or below S2; (4) no position, and no trade yet today. EXIT (next open) at the first close >= P (target), or the first close below the lowest low of bars t-3..t at entry (stop), or at the close of the 23:45 UTC bar (time exit, under 24 hours). Lookback: 100 bars.','Floor pivots are a textbook formula that many floor, retail and bot traders compute the same way, so resting bids and stop orders cluster around S1. Bulkowski''s intraday test finds price turns near standard pivots more often than chance, and price often sweeps a level before turning. Sellers who hit S1 and set off stops below it supply liquidity at a temporary discount. A close back above S1 shows the stops are used up, and the price drifts back toward the day''s equilibrium P. The source gives no trade rule; this one is my adaptation. The target S1 to P equals H-P, at least 0.8% by the arming filter and typically 1-2.5% on crypto days. That is well above the 0.30-0.45% cost, and the stop sits just below the sweep low.','15m',100,3,0,150.0,'DailyPivotS1Reclaim','1de7855e23ae9281e639e73a02099334426ebc9f2cecf0a96f76603d4ab519fa','registered','formalised as H-061',2.7391,'H-061','2026-11-07T12:30:18.786370+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-050','S20261107T122437Z','15m aggressive-selling bar reversal: volume-confirmed 3-sigma drop, exit on full retrace or 4 hours','paper','https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.21888','Short-horizon mean reversion in cryptocurrency markets: a matched cross-market measurement','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1. sigma(t) = sample std of 15m close-to-close returns over bars t-672..t-1 (7 days, current bar excluded). Vmed(t) = median volume of bars t-96..t-1. Shock bar return b(t) = close(t)/open(t) - 1. ENTRY when all hold: (1) b(t) <= -max(0.8%, 3.0*sigma(t)); (2) volume(t) >= 3.0*Vmed(t); (3) no open position; (4) at least 8 bars since the last exit. EXIT (next open) at the first close >= open(t) of the shock bar (full retrace), or the first close below 0.99*low(t) (stop), or at the close of the 16th bar after entry (4-hour time exit). No trend or daily filter. Lookback: 673 bars.','The paper finds crypto reversal at 15-minute horizons much stronger than in equities. It is concentrated after moves driven by aggressive taker flow and grows with that flow, which the authors read as pay for liquidity providers who absorb impatient takers. Candles carry no taker side, so a very large volume on a big red bar stands in for aggressive market selling, often forced liquidations. Liquidity providers who buy then earn the price concession as the pressure fades. This is a 15m, volatility-scaled variant of the hourly crash-rebound family. The trade aims at a full retrace of a bar of at least 0.8% (usually larger, at 3 sigma), above the 0.30-0.45% cost.','15m',673,6,0,150.0,'VolumeSpikeCrashRebound','3157cd8cf867e3a58c142988d6d4e2dbbbdd189065c765698e38125972599d46','registered','formalised as H-062',2.6863,'H-062','2026-11-07T12:30:18.790448+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-051','S20261107T122437Z','ADX/volatility regime switch on 1h: EMA trend entries in trending high-vol regimes, RSI dips in quiet ranges, 24h cap','blog','https://www.quantconnect.com/forum/discussion/19666/btc-intraday-trading-systems/','Exploring Intraday Bitcoin Trading Strategies - Regime Filters (QuantConnect forum)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars; signal at bar close, fill at next open; long only, one position. Indicators on 1h: ADX(14), +DI(14), -DI(14) (Wilder); ATRp = ATR(14)/close; EMA(10), EMA(30); RSI(14) (Wilder). TREND regime: ADX >= 25 AND +DI > -DI AND ATRp >= median of ATRp over the prior 720 bars. RANGE regime: ADX < 20. Trend entry: in TREND regime, EMA10 crosses above EMA30*1.002 on this bar (it was below on the previous bar). Range entry: in RANGE regime, RSI14 closes below 30. Exits: a trend trade exits at the first close with EMA10 < EMA30; a range trade exits at the first close with RSI14 >= 50. Both: stop at 3% below entry; time exit at the close of the 24th bar after entry. Cooldown 4 bars after any exit. Lookback: 720 bars.','The source is a template answer on a QuantConnect forum. It switches between momentum and mean reversion by ATR and ADX and gives no economic argument. Here is the closest honest one. When volatility is high and the trend is strong, prices are moving on news and herding flows, so late traders keep pushing in the same direction. In quiet, trendless hours, market makers dominate and short pullbacks revert. Using each signal only in its own regime avoids trend entries in chop and dip buys in crashes. The arXiv short-horizon reversal study (2608.21888) supports reversion when flow is not aggressive. Hourly RSI14 < 30 rebounds and trend legs on these pairs usually run past 1%, above the 0.30-0.45% cost.','1h',720,9,0,200.0,'ADXRegimeSwitch','961368d678a28ec170d1387b39d7a1d47452e18b637904c4cd9e260d49db51a0','registered','formalised as H-065',1.78,'H-065','2026-11-07T12:30:18.794636+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-052','S20261107T160233Z','US equity-open opening-range breakout on 15m, anchored to New York time, flat at the US close','blog','https://www.cxoadvisory.com/individual-investing/intraday-trading-of-overactive-stocks-via-opening-range-breakout/','Intraday Trading of Overactive Stocks via Opening Range Breakout (CXO Advisory summary of Zarattini, Barbon and Aziz)','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars only; signal at a bar close, filled at the next bar open. Every time below is New York local time converted to UTC for each date, so 09:30 ET is 13:30 UTC in US daylight time and 14:30 UTC in standard time. Trade only Monday to Friday. OPENING RANGE: the single 15m bar opening at 09:30 ET; ORH = its high, ORL = its low. The day is armed only if 0.003 <= (ORH-ORL)/ORL <= 0.025. ENTRY: the first 15m bar opening between 09:45 and 14:30 ET (inclusive) that closes above ORH, on an armed day, with no open position. Buy at the next open. At most one trade per day, no re-entry after an exit. STOP: ORL, checked intrabar. EXIT: if the stop has not been hit, sell at the open of the 16:00 ET bar, i.e. after the 15:45 ET bar closes. No take-profit. No daily or 1h filters. Holding time is always under 7 hours.','Crypto order flow now runs on Wall Street hours. A Kraken study reported by CryptoSlate (''Crypto never closes, but Bitcoin, Ethereum, XRP and Solana now move on Wall Street time'') finds about half of daily variance falls in 13-22 UTC, with the peak hour shifting with US daylight saving time. So the cash open, not a fixed UTC hour, is when ETF authorised participants, basis traders and US desks start trading. Zarattini et al. read early opening-range direction as one-sided institutional demand that is worked through the session, which runs over range sellers and passive liquidity at the high. The hold is a full US session at peak volatility, so winners should be well above the 0.30-0.45% cost, and losses are capped at ORL (at most 2.5%).','15m',30,5,0,170.0,'SessionOpeningRangeBreakout','2df2ad008ebe0f48a00498d924bb98bcccf9eac419ffb255cdc3416aae3f87f0','registered','formalised as H-069',2.2544,'H-069','2026-11-07T16:12:30.290339+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-053','S20261107T160233Z','Asian-session range breakout at the European open on 15m, 1R target, flat by 12:00 UTC','blog','https://therighttrader.com/learn/trading-strategies/london-breakout-strategy','London Breakout Strategy (The Right Trader)','all rights reserved','Chart 15m, closed bars, UTC clock; signal at a bar close, filled at the next open. Every day, weekends included. ASIAN RANGE: AH = highest high and AL = lowest low of the 28 bars opening 00:00 to 06:45 UTC. DAILY FILTER: ATR(14) with Wilder smoothing, built from closed UTC daily candles (informative 1d, only completed days, last value = yesterday). The day is armed only if 0.25 <= (AH-AL)/ATR14 <= 0.80. ENTRY WINDOW: bars opening 07:00 to 09:45 UTC. If, inside the window, a bar closes below AL before any bar closes above AH, there is no trade that day (the first break is downward). Otherwise, at the first bar close above AH, buy at the next open. One trade per day at most. STOP: AL, checked intrabar. TARGET: entry + (entry - AL), i.e. 1R, as a limit. TIME EXIT: if neither is hit, sell at the open of the 12:00 UTC bar. The longest hold is about 5 hours.','Per Quantpedia''s ''Periodicity in Cryptocurrencies'' (arXiv 2109.12142), crypto volatility bottoms near 05:00 UTC, Binance illiquidity peaks in the East-Asian night, and activity steps up around 08:00 UTC. So the 00-07 UTC range forms in thin trading, and European desks bring fresh directional flow. Stop orders of range traders sit just beyond AH, and triggering them fuels the push. The width filter skips dead days and days already exhausted. The 1R target is at least 0.25 x daily ATR (about 1% or more here), well above the 0.45% conservative round trip. This is FX-session practice carried over to crypto, where the 07-08 UTC liquidity arrival is documented.','15m',1440,7,1,150.0,'AsianRangeLondonBreakout','f478cf3126049098dc4ca4f76fe4c9e279bf6146f37ab681047259434a6668d1','registered','formalised as H-067',2.7286,'H-067','2026-11-07T16:12:30.298695+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-054','S20261107T160233Z','Time-of-day-adjusted volume surprise on a strong 1h up bar, 12-hour continuation hold','blog','https://quantpedia.com/periodicity-in-cryptocurrencies-recurrent-patterns-in-volatility-and-volume/','Periodicity in Cryptocurrencies - Recurrent Patterns in Volatility and Volume (Quantpedia)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars, UTC clock; signal at the close of bar t, filled at the open of bar t+1. EXPECTED VOLUME: Vexp(t) = mean volume of the 20 bars at the same UTC hour on the previous 20 days (bars t-24, t-48, ..., t-480; the current day excluded). Volume surprise VS(t) = volume(t)/Vexp(t). ENTRY at the close of bar t when ALL hold: (1) VS(t) >= 2.0; (2) close(t)/open(t) - 1 >= 0.006; (3) (close(t)-low(t))/(high(t)-low(t)) >= 0.7 (no signal if high == low); (4) no open position. STOP: low of bar t, fixed at entry and checked intrabar. TIME EXIT: sell at the open of bar t+13, i.e. after 12 full bars, unless stopped earlier. No take-profit, no trend or daily filter, no cooldown other than one position at a time.','Crypto volume follows a fixed daily cycle, with spikes at the 00/08/16 UTC funding times and in US hours. Quantpedia (summarising arXiv 2109.12142) says the useful signal is measured activity minus the expected activity for that time. Volume far above the same-hour norm points to news or a large buyer working an order, and such buyers split demand over hours, so price keeps drifting. Liquidity providers and stale limit sellers are on the other side. The rule needs a 0.6% up bar that closes near its high and holds for 12 hours. The expected follow-through is a multiple of the 0.30-0.45% cost, and the stop at the bar low caps losses at about one bar range. The source documents only the volume cycles, not returns, so this mechanism is my closest honest one.','1h',480,5,0,160.0,'SeasonalVolumeSurprise','8ce5c0b07ce422eb86cdd5f44624d6d8539aabc6ba950b95028516760ac6cbee','registered','formalised as H-068',2.2612,'H-068','2026-11-07T16:12:30.303315+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-055','S20261107T160233Z','1h Keltner 2.5-ATR breakout gated by a rising 4h EMA, ATR stop and target, 16-bar time exit','blog','https://crypto-threads-five.vercel.app/post/how-a-multi-timeframe-keltner-breakout-strategy-filters-noise-in-crypto/','How a Multi-Timeframe Keltner Breakout Strategy Filters Noise in Crypto (Crypto Threads)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars; signal at a bar close, filled at the next open. 1h indicators: EMA50 of close; ATR(50), ATR(20) and ATR(30) with Wilder smoothing; upper band U = EMA50 + 2.5*ATR50; RSI(40) of the typical price (H+L+C)/3. 4h filter: 4h candles built from completed 1h bars (UTC blocks 00,04,...,20), visible only once complete. The filter holds if the last completed 4h close > 4h EMA50 AND 4h EMA50 > its value 6 completed 4h bars earlier. ENTRY at the close of bar t: close(t) > U(t) AND close(t-1) <= U(t-1) (fresh close above the band) AND RSI40(t) > 50 AND the 4h filter holds AND no position. STOP: entry - 1.6*ATR20(t), fixed, intrabar. TARGET: entry + 4.5*ATR30(t), limit. TIME EXIT: sell at the open of the 17th bar after entry (16 bars held) if neither is hit. The source uses a buy-stop placed beyond its breakout level; here the trigger is the band close.','The source only says its filters screen out weak breakouts. The closest honest mechanism is intraday time-series momentum. Borgards (2021, North American Journal of Economics and Finance, ''Dynamic time series momentum of cryptocurrencies'') finds momentum periods following formation periods at intraday frequencies, started by volatility bursts at critical price levels and linked to noise traders. A close 2.5 ATR above the 50-hour mean, in a rising 4h trend, is such a burst, fed by late trend-followers and short-covering. Mean-reversion traders fading the extension are on the other side. The target is 4.5 hourly ATR (typically 2-4%) against a 1.6 ATR stop, several times the 0.45% round trip, with a 16-hour cap.','1h',240,11,1,150.0,'HourlyKeltnerMTFBreakout','05fc968913c1748c3b243f0d73fd65e9f8d06925fb5562ac167791d041ca6808','registered','formalised as H-066',2.75,'H-066','2026-11-07T16:12:30.307558+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-056','S20261107T173756Z','New York close near 10-day high, overnight hold: buy at 16:00 New York time, sell at 10:00 the next morning','blog','https://quantpedia.com/how-to-profitably-trade-bitcoins-overnight-sessions/','How To Profitably Trade Bitcoin''s Overnight Sessions?','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars only. Clock: America/New_York local time (DST handled per date), converted from each candle''s UTC open time. Runs every calendar day, weekends included. SIGNAL BAR: the 1h bar opening at 15:00 New York time (it closes at 16:00, the US equity close). H10 = highest high of the 240 1h bars ending with the signal bar (signal bar included, about 10 days). ENTRY: at the close of the signal bar, if close >= 0.97 * H10 and no position is open, buy at the next bar open (16:00 New York). EXIT: sell at the open of the 1h bar opening at 10:00 New York time on the next calendar day (signal taken on the close of the 09:00 bar), about 18 hours after entry and always under 24 hours. No stop, no take-profit, no cooldown, no other filters. All signals come from hourly bars; no daily candles are used. Two adaptations from the source: (1) the source buys only at an exact local 10-day high; here ''within 3% of it'' is used to reach the trade count; (2) the source''s best hold, Friday to Monday, is longer than 24 hours, so every night is traded as a separate 18-hour hold.','Quantpedia found that the MAX(10) BTC rule (buy at the NYSE close when BTC is at a 10-day high, hold one day) earns most of its return in the hours outside NYSE trading. It explains this with a premium for holding through hours when traditional desks, ETF authorized participants and options dealers are away, and with institutional and ETF selling that clusters in US hours (see also the reported Coinbase discount at the US open). Near-high momentum then plays out while those sellers are absent. This differs from H-058, which buys after US-session weakness with no trend condition. On these pairs an 18-hour hold usually moves 2-4%, well above the 0.30-0.45% round trip.','1h',240,4,0,170.0,'NYCloseNearHighOvernight','5efd6c37141d5d0d51818a6753e5ca769f6dc1306a4a35f84daf97c2340e7378','dropped','forbidden by the lab: derivatives',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-07T17:47:10.526584+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-057','S20261107T173756Z','Negative realized skewness of the prior UTC day from 15m returns: buy at 00:00 UTC, hold under 24 hours','paper','https://econpapers.repec.org/RePEc:eee:reveco:v:72:y:2021:i:c:p:483-499','Do higher-order realized moments matter for cryptocurrency returns? (Ahmed and Al Mafrachi, International Review of Economics and Finance 2021)','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars only, UTC clock. A signal at a bar close is filled at the next bar open. DAILY STATISTIC (computed once, at the close of the 23:45 UTC bar of day d): r_i = ln(close_i / close_{i-1}) for the 96 15m bars of day d (00:00 to 23:45; the first return uses the 23:45 close of day d-1). RV = sum of r_i^2. RSK = sqrt(96) * (sum of r_i^3) / RV^1.5 (the Amaya et al. realized skewness). If any of the 96 bars is missing or RV = 0, there is no signal. ENTRY: if RSK <= -0.25 and no position is open, buy at the open of the 00:00 UTC bar of day d+1. EXIT: sell at the open of the 23:45 UTC bar of day d+1 (95 bars, 23h45m after entry; the signal is the close of the 23:30 bar). Entries happen only at 00:00 UTC, so positions never overlap or chain. No stop, no target, no trend filter. Only intraday 15m data is used; the daily statistic is built from the 96 bars of the completed UTC day.','The source finds that realized skewness from intraday crypto returns predicts the next returns in and out of sample, but its abstract does not give the sign. The sign used here (negative skew is bullish) follows Amaya et al. on stocks, and Lee and Wang (JFQA 2025), who find that positive jump variance (lottery-like up-spikes) predicts lower crypto returns. A strongly negative-skew day means the variance came from sharp down-bursts: forced sellers, liquidations and stop runs that liquidity providers absorb at a discount and are paid for in the next session''s recovery. Buyers of lottery-like up-spikes are the overpaying side that is avoided. A 24-hour hold on these pairs moves 2-5%, far above the 0.30-0.45% round trip.','15m',97,2,0,150.0,'RealizedSkewnessDay','daaee141f2f36415a5bf348a0eb4fdf7ea8790adf970abc6d73004495da00a85','registered','formalised as H-070',3.2971,'H-070','2026-11-07T17:47:10.535140+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-058','S20261107T173756Z','Idiosyncratic 6-hour drop versus BTC in a flat market: buy the beta-adjusted residual dislocation, 12-hour cap','paper','https://ideas.repec.org/a/gam/jjrfmx/v12y2019i1p31-d205554.html','Statistical Arbitrage in Cryptocurrency Markets (Fischer, Krauss and Deinert, JRFM 2019)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars; signal at the close of bar t, filled at the open of t+1. Long only, one position. Reference series B = BTC/USDT for every pair; for BTC/USDT itself, B = ETH/USDT (informative 1h, aligned on the same closed timestamp). Hourly log returns x(i) of the pair and b(i) of B. beta(t) = cov(x,b)/var(b) over the 720 bars t-720..t-1. Residual e6(t) = ln(C(t)/C(t-6)) - beta(t)*ln(CB(t)/CB(t-6)). s(t) = sample std (ddof=1) of e6 over the 720 bars t-720..t-1. ENTRY when ALL hold: (1) e6(t) <= -2.5*s(t); (2) e6(t) <= -0.02; (3) |ln(CB(t)/CB(t-6))| <= 0.01 (the reference was flat; not a market-wide selloff); (4) no position. At entry store beta_e = beta(t), E = |e6(t)|, P0 = entry price, B0 = reference price. EXIT at the first close where (a) ln(C/P0) - beta_e*ln(CB/B0) >= 0.6*E (60% of the gap closed), or (b) close <= 0.96*P0 (stop), or (c) 12 bars after entry (time exit). No cooldown beyond one position at a time.','When one coin falls 2% or more against a flat BTC, the move usually comes from coin-specific price pressure: a large holder unwinding, unlock or listing news, or a single venue''s flow. Market makers and relative-value traders who hedge with BTC absorb it and are paid when the relative price recovers; Fischer et al. use the next 120-minute outperformance against the cross-section as their target. The practitioner audit by bryanvine (Alpha Research paper 3) warns that hourly residual reversion in liquid coins is small, and mostly reflects stale prices in illiquid ones. That is why this rule needs a 2.5-sigma and at least 2% dislocation and books 60% of it (about 1.2% or more), above the 0.30-0.45% round trip. The BTC-flat condition sets it apart from H-031, which buys laggards after a market jump.','1h',726,8,0,160.0,'IdiosyncraticResidualReversal','d79e38f4b3746f54c3e5bf318f05e47d7fdc8834fa9224c33db72dfc0a39bf79','registered','formalised as H-072',2.3023,'H-072','2026-11-07T17:47:10.539796+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-059','S20261107T173756Z','Volatility-scaled 24-hour momentum on 1h with a ratcheting 2.5-ATR trailing stop and a 24-hour time exit','paper','https://arxiv.org/html/2602.11708v1','Systematic Trend-Following with Adaptive Portfolio Construction (AdaptiveTrend, arXiv 2602.11708)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars; signal at the close of bar t, filled at the open of t+1. Long only, one position, whole balance. M(t) = close(t)/close(t-24) - 1 (24-hour momentum, the length of four of the source''s 6h bars). S(t) = sample std (ddof=1) of the overlapping 24-bar returns M over the 720 bars t-720..t-1 (current bar excluded). ATR(t) = Wilder ATR(14) on 1h bars. ENTRY when M(t) >= 1.5*S(t) AND M(t) >= 0.02 AND close(t) > close(t-1) AND no position AND at least 6 bars since the last exit. TRAILING STOP: at entry, stop = entry price - 2.5*ATR(entry bar); at each later close, stop = max(previous stop, close - 2.5*ATR(t)), so it only moves up. EXIT at the first close below the stop (filled at the next open), or at the close of the 24th bar after entry (time exit), whichever comes first. No take-profit, no other filters. All signals are hourly. Fixed choices replace the source''s monthly re-optimized L and threshold: L = 24 bars, threshold 1.5 sigma, alpha = 2.5 (the centre of the source''s reported plateau of 2.0-3.5).','The source trades 6h crypto momentum (move over L bars above a threshold) with a long-side ATR stop that only ratchets up, and reports that results are flat across alpha 2.0-3.5. The idea behind time-series momentum is slow diffusion of information and herding: late buyers and short-covering keep pushing a move that has already beaten its usual 24-hour range. The ratcheting stop cuts reversals early, and the 24-hour cap keeps the trade intraday. Requiring a move of at least 2% and 1.5 sigma means entries happen only in active trends, where the ride before a 2.5-ATR pullback is typically 1-3%, above the 0.30-0.45% round trip. It differs from Donchian and Keltner breakouts (H-002, H-066) in its vol-normalized momentum trigger and pure trailing exit.','1h',744,6,0,170.0,'ATRTrailMomentum','f95b2dc040943bf6177370449f57937e03ff83d372be5dfb4755bb1b7fb19b77','registered','formalised as H-071',2.7385,'H-071','2026-11-07T17:47:10.544320+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-060','S20261107T192025Z','Nine-pair hourly breadth thrust: buy when the share of rising pairs surges from below 40% to above 61.5%','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/breadth-thrusts.md','Breadth Thrusts (LuxAlgo Library)','Free to use with attribution (LuxAlgo Library license)','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1. All nine pairs are read as informative 1h pairs aligned on the same timestamp. BREADTH: at each bar t count A = pairs with close(t) > close(t-1) and D = pairs with close(t) < close(t-1) (unchanged pairs ignored); B(t) = A/(A+D), or 0.5 if A+D = 0. E(t) = EMA of B with span 10 (alpha 2/11). THRUST at t: E(t) > 0.615 AND the minimum of E over bars t-10..t-1 is < 0.40 (the move from below 0.40 to above 0.615 finished within 10 bars). ENTRY on traded pair X at the close of t when THRUST is true at t but was false at t-1, AND close_X(t) > close_X(t-10) (X took part in the move), AND X has no open position. EXIT the first of: (a) the close of the 24th bar after the entry bar (filled at the next open; time exit, so every trade is under 25 hours); (b) a hard stop 3% below the entry price; (c) E falls below 0.40 at a bar close (breadth collapses back). No take-profit, no pyramiding, no other filters.','Zweig''s thrust (a 10-period EMA of advances/(advances+declines) rising from below 0.40 to above 0.615 within 10 sessions) marks a fast switch from broad selling to near-unanimous buying, which the page links to the start of durable advances. The hourly crypto analogue is a market-wide flip from liquidation to buying across many coins at once (short covering plus fresh risk-on flow), a flow signal no single pair shows. The other side are late liquidators and shorts forced to cover. By construction each entry follows a large aggregate swing, so the 24-hour target is a multi-percent rally rather than a fraction of the 0.30-0.45% round trip. Caveat: the source uses daily NYSE breadth; the hourly transfer is untested and the nine pairs are far more correlated than NYSE stocks.','1h',24,6,0,180.0,'BreadthThrustIntraday','c0dc4665fb887d31998ae04bef70d1d666bd6905f829be260138308169a57c92','registered','formalised as H-073',2.2865,'H-073','2026-11-07T19:29:46.457698+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-061','S20261107T192025Z','Bulk-volume-classified order imbalance on 15m: buy a 4-hour buy-side flow surge, 8-hour hold','paper','https://arxiv.org/html/2607.09426v2','The Quarter-Hour Effect: Periodic Algorithmic Trading and Return Predictability in Cryptocurrency Futures','CC BY 4.0','Chart 15m, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1. r(i) = ln(close(i)/close(i-1)). s(i) = sample std (ddof=1) of r over bars i-96..i-1 (one day, current bar excluded). BUY FRACTION (bulk volume classification): f(i) = Phi(r(i)/s(i)), Phi = standard normal CDF; buy volume = volume(i)*f(i), sell volume = volume(i)*(1-f(i)). ORDER IMBALANCE OI(t) = sum over i=t-15..t of volume(i)*(2f(i)-1) divided by sum of volume(i) over the same 16 bars (4 hours), between -1 and 1. ACTIVITY: V16(t) = sum of volume over t-15..t; Vbar(t) = mean volume per bar over bars t-688..t-17 (672 bars, 7 days, the current window excluded). TREND: close(t) > SMA(384) of 15m closes (4 days). ENTRY when OI(t) >= 0.30 AND V16(t) >= 1.5*16*Vbar(t) AND TREND AND no open position. STOP: the lowest low of bars t-15..t, fixed at entry. EXIT the first of: the stop; the close of the 32nd bar after the entry bar (8 hours, filled next open). After an exit, no new entry until OI has been below 0.30 for at least one bar close. No take-profit, no pyramiding.','Order imbalance from informed or large traders who split orders persists: liquidity providers lean against it at first but do not absorb it fully, so prices drift with the flow for hours. The arXiv paper (Binance perpetuals) reports that order imbalance predicts cumulative returns over 4 to 12 hours positively after a short first-half-hour reversal; the 8-hour hold targets that window. Bulk volume classification (Easley, Lopez de Prado and O''Hara, RFS 2012) estimates buy and sell volume from candle return and volume alone; Andersen and Bondarenko call it noisy, hence the volume-surge gate. A 4-hour, volume-heavy one-sided flow selects moves of a percent or more, above the 0.30-0.45% cost. The paper used trade-level imbalance at quarter-hour marks, not BVC on spot candles, so the transfer is an assumption.','15m',688,7,0,220.0,'BVCOrderFlowMomentum','f77226b566327285431b716c02c2299ecbb8c7492e495bee113feaaa36995006','dropped','forbidden by the lab: derivatives',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-07T19:29:46.467201+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-062','S20261107T192025Z','Hourly bull flag: steep 6-hour pole, tight low-volume pause, buy the break above the pole high','blog','https://thepatternsite.com/flags.html','Flags, Bulkowski''s Encyclopedia of Chart Patterns site (thepatternsite.com)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1. At bar t, search for a pole top p with t-9 <= p <= t-3 such that high(p) is the highest high of bars p..t-1. POLE: PL = lowest low of bars p-5..p; require high(p)/PL - 1 >= 0.025 (a rise of at least 2.5% within 6 bars) and H = high(p) - PL. FLAG = bars p+1..t-1 (2 to 8 bars). Conditions: (1) depth: lowest low of the flag FL >= high(p) - 0.5*H (retrace at most half the pole); (2) tightness: (highest high - lowest low of the flag) <= 0.5*H; (3) volume dries up: mean volume of the flag bars <= 0.7 * mean volume of bars p-5..p; (4) close(t) > SMA(168) of 1h closes. If several p qualify, use the most recent. ENTRY at the close of t when close(t) > high(p) AND no open position AND that pole has not already been traded. STOP at FL, fixed at entry. TARGET (measured move) FL + H, a limit exit. TIME EXIT at the close of the 24th bar after the entry bar (filled next open). No pyramiding, no other filters.','Bulkowski gives the shape (steep pole, short tight flag, volume trending down during the flag, measured move equal to the pole added to the flag low) but no causal reason. The closest honest one: the pole is a burst of new demand (news or a large buyer); the flag is short-term holders taking profit, absorbed without much price give-back on shrinking volume, which shows that supply is thin; a close back above the pole high triggers breakout buyers and stops of those who sold the pause, so the original flow resumes. The other side are profit-takers and faders who sell too early. Requiring a pole of at least 2.5% and a target equal to the pole height means the planned gain is roughly 2.5% or more per trade against a 0.30-0.45% round trip, with the stop at the flag low.','1h',168,8,0,160.0,'HourlyBullFlagBreak','99a29e6c7d6921dbcbfb9e4a6f5731ef65ca3c87101741ee58c9da6e2c8aba5b','registered','formalised as H-075',1.7895,'H-075','2026-11-07T19:29:46.472834+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-063','S20261107T192025Z','VSA stopping volume then low-volume test: buy the confirmed retest of an absorbed hourly low','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/vsa-test-bar.md','VSA Test Bar (LuxAlgo Library)','Free to use with attribution (LuxAlgo Library license)','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at bar close, fill at the next open. Vmed(s) = median volume of bars s-48..s-1. Pos(i) = (close-low)/(high-low) of bar i (no signal if high = low). STOPPING BAR s: low(s) is the lowest low of bars s-47..s; volume(s) >= 2.5*Vmed(s); Pos(s) >= 0.5; close(s) < close(s-6) (came after a decline). TEST BAR t, within bars s+1..s+12: low(t) < low(t-1) AND low(t) >= low(s) AND volume(t) <= 0.6*Vmed(s) AND Pos(t) >= 0.5. CONFIRMATION: the first bar c in t+1..t+3 with close(c) > high(t) AND volume(c) > volume(t); ENTRY at the close of c if no position is open; each stopping bar is used once. If any bar after s closes below low(s) before entry, the setup is void. STOP at low(t), fixed at entry. TARGET at entry + 2*(entry - low(t)), a limit exit. TIME EXIT at the close of the 24th bar after c (filled next open). No pyramiding, no trend filter.','Volume Spread Analysis reads a heavy-volume bar that makes a new local low but closes off it as absorption: a patient buyer takes the other side of panicky or forced sellers who pay for immediacy. Per the LuxAlgo page, a later probe lower that draws almost no volume shows supply is gone, a firm up bar on rising volume confirms it, and a slide below the test low invalidates it (the stop). The other side are late and stop-loss sellers. Unlike the lab''s crash-rebound rules, this waits for the two-stage sequence (absorption, then dry-up) instead of buying the crash bar. The target is twice the risk from the test low, usually well above 1% after a 48-hour-low event, against a 0.30-0.45% cost. The page gives no tested thresholds; the numbers are design choices.','1h',64,9,0,150.0,'VSAStopTestConfirm','3a084d4394e0dedf99c66ee0ed3e1abcd13393fd194c98375b8e6b7401f244c1','registered','formalised as H-076',1.7213,'H-076','2026-11-07T19:29:46.478103+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-064','S20261107T192025Z','Feedback-trading volatility switch on 1h: follow 6-hour surges when calm, fade 6-hour drops when volatile','paper','https://ideas.repec.org/a/ecj/econjl/v102y1992i411p415-25.html','Feedback Traders and Stock Return Autocorrelations: Evidence from a Century of Daily Data (Sentana and Wadhwani, Economic Journal 1992)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars only; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1. r(i) = ln(close(i)/close(i-1)). sig(t) = sample std (ddof=1) of r over bars t-23..t (24 hours). M(t) = median of sig over bars t-720..t-1 (30 days, current bar excluded). R6(t) = close(t)/close(t-6) - 1. CALM regime: sig(t) < M(t). VOLATILE regime: sig(t) >= 1.5*M(t). Between the two there is no entry. ENTRY A (continuation, CALM only): R6(t) >= 2.0*sig(t)*sqrt(6) AND R6(t) >= 0.012. ENTRY B (reversal, VOLATILE only): R6(t) <= -2.0*sig(t)*sqrt(6) AND R6(t) <= -0.025. Either entry requires no open position. EXIT for both: the first of a hard stop 3% below the entry price, or the close of the 12th bar after the entry bar (filled next open). After an exit, no new entry for 6 bars. No take-profit, no trend filter, no pyramiding.','Sentana and Wadhwani find return autocorrelation is positive when volatility is low and negative when it is high, more so after declines (in daily and hourly stock returns per the abstract), and attribute it to feedback traders whose weight rises with volatility. King and Koutmos (Annals of Operations Research 2021) find trend-chasing feedback traders in BTC, ETH, XRP and ADA, with the effect scaling with conditional volatility. So in calm markets a sharp 6-hour rise is slow diffusion that continues, while in turbulent markets a sharp drop is overshoot by feedback sellers that liquidity providers are paid to absorb. Both entries need a 2-sigma move of at least 1.2% or 2.5%, so the expected follow-through is about 1% or more against a 0.30-0.45% cost. The crypto evidence is daily; the hourly switch is untested.','1h',744,9,0,200.0,'FeedbackVolRegimeSwitch','766ea12dd97cefea6c71d06071238829c2623112f95a3fe46ae39a6e4002c5f8','registered','formalised as H-074',2.2308,'H-074','2026-11-07T19:29:46.483590+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-065','S20261107T220457Z','Large-coin daily cross-sectional momentum: hold the top-4 of nine pairs by prior UTC-day return for one day','paper','https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/finana/v78y2021ics1057521921002349.html','Up or down? Short-term reversal, momentum, and liquidity effects in cryptocurrency markets (Zaremba, Bilgin, Long, Mercik, Szczygielski, IRFA 78, 2021)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars, UTC. All nine pairs loaded as informative 1h pairs on the same timestamp. Once per day, at the close of the 23:00 UTC bar of day d-1, compute for each pair R = close(23:00 bar of d-1) / close(23:00 bar of d-2) - 1 (the prior 24-hour return, 24 bars). Rank the nine R values; ties broken by pair name. Pairs with any missing bar in the 25 needed closes are dropped from the ranking for that day. ENTRY: if the traded pair ranks in the top 4 of the nine, buy at the open of the 00:00 UTC bar of day d. EXIT: sell at the close of the 22:00 UTC bar of day d (filled at the 23:00 open, so every trade lasts 23 hours), or earlier by a fixed stop 5% below the entry price. The next day is a fresh decision; no carry-over. No trend filter, no other conditions. Lookbacks: 24 bars for the ranking; top-4 cut; 5% stop.','Zaremba et al. find that across thousands of coins the last day''s return reverses, but the handful of largest, most tradeable coins show daily momentum instead, because reversal is a compensation for illiquidity that liquid coins do not carry. Begusic and Kostanjcar (arXiv 1904.00890, opened) also find strong momentum in the most liquid coins and tie it to investor herding. The other side is late, attention-limited buyers who chase yesterday''s leaders the next day. All nine pairs are large and liquid. Each trade holds a liquid alt for almost a full day, with a typical daily move of 2-5%, so the gross move per trade is well above the 0.30-0.45% round trip. This is a relative-strength ranking, not a time-series or ratio-breakout rule.','1h',25,3,0,160.0,'CrossSectionalDailyMomentum','5c244b57487979756889614360342b680e382bccf332d663fd6b23a66e25f22c','registered','formalised as H-077',3.28,'H-077','2026-11-07T22:13:16.499309+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-066','S20261107T220457Z','Low-volume cross-sectional loser reversal on 1h: buy the worst of nine pairs when its drop is not backed by volume','paper','https://swopec.hhs.se/rbnkwp/abs/rbnkwp0413.htm','Trading volume and liquidity provision in cryptocurrency markets (Bianchi, Babiak, Dickerson, Riksbank WP 413, 2022)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1. All nine pairs loaded as informative 1h pairs on the same timestamp. For each pair: r4(t) = close(t)/close(t-4) - 1. V4(t) = volume summed over bars t-3..t. VN(t) = mean of V4(t-24k) for k = 1..14 (the same 4-hour window on the 14 previous days, so time of day is controlled). M(t) = median of the nine r4(t). ENTRY for the traded pair X when ALL hold: (1) r4_X(t) is the lowest of the nine; (2) r4_X(t) <= -0.02; (3) r4_X(t) <= M(t) - 0.015 (X fell much more than the group); (4) V4_X(t) <= 1.0 * VN_X(t) (the drop came on normal or below-normal volume); (5) no open position. Store P = close_X(t-4). EXIT at the first of: close >= P (full retrace of the 4-hour drop); 12 bars after entry (time exit, 12 hours); close <= entry * 0.96 (stop, checked at bar close). After an exit, no new entry on that pair for 4 bars.','Bianchi, Babiak and Dickerson show that short-term reversal returns, a proxy for the returns to liquidity provision, are concentrated where trading activity is low. The interaction of lagged return and volume predicts returns, which fits inventory-risk and adverse-selection models: a drop on thin volume is a liquidity shock (a forced or impatient seller) rather than news, so the buyer who absorbs it is paid by the seller''s urgency. Ranking against the other eight pairs removes the market move. What remains is a pair-specific dislocation of at least 1.5% beyond the group and 2% in absolute terms. Recovering half of it already covers the 0.45% conservative cost. This differs from H-072, which uses a beta residual against BTC in a flat market, and from H-053, which uses one asset''s own 12-hour drop.','1h',340,6,0,170.0,'CrossSectionalLowVolReversal','d92eec5c6121e36652710a459a0ee7ff5339039dde8ee30252d1b1e96eb930c3','registered','formalised as H-078',2.7593,'H-078','2026-11-07T22:13:16.506462+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-067','S20261107T220457Z','BTC-led 15m catch-up: buy an alt that has not yet followed a volume-backed BTC surge bar, 4-hour cap','paper','https://research-information.bris.ac.uk/en/publications/cross-cryptocurrency-return-predictability/','Cross-cryptocurrency return predictability (Guo, Sang, Tu, Wang, Journal of Economic Dynamics and Control 163, 2024)','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1. Leader L = BTC/USDT for every traded pair except BTC/USDT, whose leader is ETH/USDT; L is an informative 15m pair on the same timestamp. b(t) = close_L(t)/close_L(t-1) - 1; sL(t) = sample std of b over bars t-672..t-1 (7 days, current excluded); VL(t) = volume_L(t) / median volume_L over bars t-96..t-1. x(t) = close_X(t)/close_X(t-1) - 1 for the traded pair X. ENTRY when ALL hold: (1) b(t) >= max(0.006, 2.5*sL(t)); (2) VL(t) >= 2.0; (3) x(t) <= 0.4*b(t) (X has moved less than 40% as much as the leader); (4) close_L(t) > SMA(96) of close_L (the leader is not in an intraday downtrend); (5) no open position. On entry store target T = close_X(t) * (1 + b(t) - x(t)) (X catching up the gap) and stop S = entry * (1 - 1.5*b(t)). EXIT at the first bar close with close >= T, or close <= S, or 16 bars (4 hours) after entry.','Guo et al. find that lagged returns of other cryptocurrencies predict a focal coin''s returns on Binance data, and attribute this to slow information diffusion: common shocks hit the leading coin first, and investors with limited attention reprice the other coins later. BTC is where most market-wide news and flow lands first, so a BTC surge bar with twice the normal volume is a common shock that alts usually follow with some delay. The other side is the alt holders and market makers who have not yet updated their quotes. Requiring a BTC bar of at least 0.6% (and 2.5 sigma) and an alt lag of at least 60% of it puts the expected catch-up near 0.6-1.5%. This is a 15m, single-leader, volume-confirmed version, unlike H-031, which used 2-bar 1h returns averaged over two pairs.','15m',672,7,0,150.0,'CrossPairCatchUp','3dfd65d46a571c864bd1aad389c0c1f88c08475fb397ba107bb041273ff63d48','registered','formalised as H-080',2.2049,'H-080','2026-11-07T22:13:16.511509+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-068','S20261107T220457Z','15m TTM squeeze fire with positive momentum histogram and closed-4h EMA filter, 8-hour time exit','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/ttm-squeeze.md','LuxAlgo Library: TTM Squeeze','Free to use with attribution (LuxAlgo library licence)','Chart 15m, closed bars; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1. Indicators on 15m: basis SMA20 of close; Bollinger bands = SMA20 +/- 2.0 * population std20 of close; Keltner = SMA20 +/- 1.5 * ATR20 (Wilder). SQUEEZE ON at a bar when upper BB < upper KC and lower BB > lower KC. Momentum MOM(t) = value at bar t of the 20-bar least-squares line fitted to (close - Mid), where Mid = ((highest high of 20 bars + lowest low of 20 bars)/2 + SMA20)/2. 4h filter: 4h candles from closed 1h/15m data in UTC blocks 00,04,...,20, visible only after the block closes; EMA50 of 4h close. ENTRY at bar t when ALL hold: (1) squeeze was ON for each of bars t-6..t-1 (at least 6 bars of compression) and is OFF at t (the fire); (2) MOM(t) > 0 and MOM(t) > MOM(t-1); (3) close(t) > upper KC(t); (4) last closed 4h close > 4h EMA50 and that EMA50 is above its value one 4h bar earlier; (5) no open position. STOP: lowest low of bars t-6..t, fixed at entry. EXIT at the first bar close when MOM falls for 2 consecutive bars, or close < SMA20, or 32 bars (8 hours) after entry.','Volatility clusters: when the standard deviation shrinks below the average true range, the market is in a quiet coil. Resting stop and breakout orders pile up just outside the tight range, so the first expansion bar that closes outside the Keltner band tends to trigger a cascade of them. The source says the squeeze itself has no direction and that the histogram''s sign and slope at the fire give the lean. A rising closed-4h trend keeps only fires with the larger trend. The other side is range traders who sold the top of the coil and must cover, plus late breakout buyers. A 6-bar minimum squeeze and an 8-hour hold aim at the 1-2% expansion that follows compression, well above the 0.45% cost. This is a 15m TTM definition (BB inside KC), not the 168-bar range-percentile squeeze of H-005/H-008.','15m',816,7,0,200.0,'VolatilitySqueezeBreakout','83adccb809861902997e9cd30a39022c78203d876b002ac9e851fd318fa356d4','registered','formalised as H-081',1.7857,'H-081','2026-11-07T22:13:16.516379+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-069','S20261107T220457Z','Chaikin Money Flow confirmed 1h breakout of the 24-hour high, exit on distribution or after 24 hours','blog','https://chartschool.stockcharts.com/table-of-contents/technical-indicators-and-overlays/technical-indicators/chaikin-money-flow-cmf','StockCharts ChartSchool: Chaikin Money Flow (CMF)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1. Money Flow Multiplier MFM(i) = ((close-low) - (high-close)) / (high-low), set to 0 when high = low. Money Flow Volume MFV(i) = MFM(i) * volume(i). CMF20(t) = sum of MFV over bars t-19..t / sum of volume over bars t-19..t (the textbook 20-period length). H24(t) = highest high of bars t-24..t-1 (excluding t). ENTRY when ALL hold: (1) close(t) > H24(t); (2) CMF20(t) >= +0.05 (the published bullish buffer); (3) CMF20(t) > CMF20(t-6) (buying pressure is rising); (4) (H24(t) - lowest low of bars t-24..t-1) / close(t) >= 0.02 (the 24h range is wide enough for a meaningful move); (5) no open position; (6) at least 6 bars since the last exit. STOP: fixed 2.5% below entry. EXIT at the first bar close when CMF20 <= -0.05 (the published bearish buffer: distribution), or close < lowest low of bars t-6..t-1, or 24 bars after entry (time exit).','CMF weights each bar''s volume by where it closes in its range. A positive, rising CMF means buyers kept closing bars near their highs on real volume, which reads as accumulation. The page gives the plus or minus 0.05 buffers and says positive CMF supports an uptrend. The other side is sellers who capped the 24-hour high and stops resting above it. Breakouts without volume-weighted buying tend to be stop runs that fail, so the filter keeps only the absorbed ones. A minimum 2% range and a 24-hour hold aim at moves of about 1-2%, above the 0.45% cost. This differs from H-002, which uses price only, and from H-046, which uses raw volume on a 240-bar pivot.','1h',30,6,0,170.0,'MoneyFlowBreakout','135f5ee43e41f48906eb2cfaab01b2aba885c9609eee1d2d6fe73df39d9cf82c','registered','formalised as H-079',2.3,'H-079','2026-11-07T22:13:16.520630+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-070','S20261108T004839Z','15m Supertrend(10,3) up-flip above the closed-1h EMA200, Supertrend-line stop, 2R target, 24-hour time exit','repo','https://doc.stocksharp.com/en/api-examples/1365_SuperTrade_ST1','SuperTrade ST1 (StockSharp API examples: Supertrend 10/3 with EMA200 filter on 15-minute candles)','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars; signal at bar close, fill at next bar open; long only, one position. 15m indicators: ATR10 = Wilder ATR(10); Supertrend with factor 3 on hl2 = (high+low)/2: basic upper = hl2 + 3*ATR10, basic lower = hl2 - 3*ATR10, with the standard ratchet (final lower band can only rise while close stays above it, final upper band can only fall while close stays below it); direction turns UP when close crosses above the final upper band and DOWN when close crosses below the final lower band; the Supertrend line is the final lower band in UP direction. 1h filter: EMA200 of 1h closes, using only the last COMPLETED 1h bar (informative 1h, merged so no partial bar is seen). ENTRY at close of 15m bar t when direction(t-1) = DOWN, direction(t) = UP, close(t) > EMA200_1h, and no position. At entry store S = Supertrend line at t (fixed stop) and R = entry fill - S; skip the trade if R/entry < 0.004. EXITS (first hit): stop at S (intrabar); take-profit limit at entry + 2R; 15m direction flips to DOWN (exit next open); time exit at the close of the 96th 15m bar after entry (24 hours).','Short-horizon trend continuation: a Supertrend flip needs a close more than 3 ATRs from the bar midpoint against the prior trend, i.e. a move that forces late shorts and passive sellers to reprice; the closed-1h EMA200 keeps only flips in the direction of the slower trend, where breakouts are less often faded by mean-reversion liquidity providers. Same rule (15m Supertrend 10/3, EMA200 filter) is described by FMZ strategy 486561 (15m Supertrend + 1h EMA200, stop at the Supertrend line, risk-reward target) and by marketcalls.in (Supertrend with EMA filter, long-only, 15m). The stop sits about 1-3 ATR15 below entry, so the 2R target is usually 1-3% away, several times the 0.30-0.45% round trip; the 0.4% minimum risk keeps the target at or above 0.8%.','15m',800,6,1,300.0,'SupertrendMTFIntraday','0cc10f2bbc860514d1ea68d208fcf2048fe8b7347079c0b01763bca737f2bea6','registered','formalised as H-083',3.1857,'H-083','2026-11-08T00:57:25.171712+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-071','S20261108T004839Z','Hourly 10-day extreme rule: buy a 1h close at its 240-bar closing high or closing low, hold exactly 24 hours','blog','https://quantpedia.com/trend-following-and-mean-reversion-in-bitcoin/','Trend-following and Mean-reversion in Bitcoin (Quantpedia, Padysak and Vojtko)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars; signal at bar close, fill at the next bar open; long only, one position, same numbers on every pair. MAX240(t) = highest close of bars t-240..t-1; MIN240(t) = lowest close of bars t-240..t-1 (240 hourly bars = 10 days, current bar excluded). AT-MAX at bar t: close(t) > MAX240(t). AT-MIN at bar t: close(t) < MIN240(t). ENTRY at the close of bar t when AT-MAX or AT-MIN holds and no position is open (the two states cannot hold together). EXIT: time exit only, at the close of the 24th 1h bar after the entry bar (sell at the next open), so every position lasts 24 hours. No stop, no target, no trend or other filters. After an exit, a new entry is allowed on the same bar''s close if a fresh AT-MAX or AT-MIN holds then. Hourly signals only; the 10-day window is the published daily lookback (10 days) re-expressed in hourly bars, and the 24-hour hold is the published one-day holding period.','Padysak and Vojtko (SSRN ''Seasonality, Trend-following, and Mean reversion in Bitcoin'', summarised by Quantpedia) find that BTC continues after closes at its local 10-day maximum (momentum: breakout and attention buyers arrive late, shorts cover) and rebounds after closes at its local 10-day minimum (reversion: forced and capitulating sellers pay liquidity providers), with the shortest lookback strongest; the authors warn the minimum leg partly reflects BTC''s past recoveries. Taking the signal on the hour it happens instead of at the UTC daily close makes it day-trade length. A 24-hour hold at a 10-day extreme spans a typical daily move of 2-5% on these pairs, far above the 0.30-0.45% round trip.','1h',240,2,1,150.0,'HourlyTenDayExtreme','e8c9769daf71d10da134f8b20c3036d0cc52b466823f43ed4a5ed08d23d51fff','registered','formalised as H-082',3.7595,'H-082','2026-11-08T00:57:25.181127+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-072','S20261108T004839Z','Elder Triple Screen intraday: rising 4h tide, negative 1h Force Index wave, break of the setup-bar high, 2R and 24h exit','blog','https://takeprofitapp.com/en/learn/triple-screen-trading-system','Triple Screen Trading System by Alexander Elder','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars; signal at bar close, fill at next bar open; long only, one position. SCREEN 1 (tide, 4h): 4h candles from completed 1h bars in UTC blocks 00,04,...,20, visible only after the block''s last 1h bar closes. EMA13 of 4h close; MACD histogram H = (EMA12-EMA26) - EMA9 of that line, on 4h closes. TIDE UP when, on the last completed 4h bar k, EMA13(k) > EMA13(k-1) AND H(k) > H(k-1). SCREEN 2 (wave, 1h): FI(t) = (close(t)-close(t-1))*volume(t); FI2 = EMA(2) of FI. A SETUP exists at bar s when TIDE UP and FI2(s) < 0. SCREEN 3 (trigger): ENTRY at the close of bar s+1 if close(s+1) > high(s), TIDE is still UP and no position (a setup lives one bar only; each new bar with FI2<0 makes a new setup). Stop L = min(low(s), low(s+1)); risk R = entry fill - L; skip if R/entry < 0.004. EXITS, first hit: stop at L (intrabar); limit target entry + 2R; tide turns down (last completed 4h EMA13 lower than the one before) -> exit next open; time exit at the close of the 24th 1h bar after entry.','Elder''s design: trade only with the slower (4h) trend, enter on a short-term pullback measured by the 2-period Force Index (price change times volume, so it needs selling volume, not just a red bar), and buy only when price proves the pullback is over by trading above the setup bar. Pullback sellers inside a rising higher-timeframe trend are usually short-horizon traders or liquidity providers who unload inventory; buying when they exhaust earns the trend premium. The source gives the 4-5x timeframe ratio, the EMA13/MACD-histogram tide, the Force Index EMA(2) wave, the buy-stop above the prior bar and the 2R minimum target; this version maps them to 4h/1h. With the 0.4% minimum risk the 2R target is at least 0.8% and normally 1.5-3% on these pairs, well above the 0.30-0.45% round trip.','1h',160,8,0,220.0,'ElderTripleScreen','3ac56cebd925c7e272f2b2daf140b6d904c9f72777875d24145b2e87d51f60ee','registered','formalised as H-088',1.7414,'H-088','2026-11-08T00:57:25.186277+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-073','S20261108T004839Z','Overbought-is-strength: buy the 1h RSI(14) cross above 70, exit at +3%, RSI below 55, or after 24 hours','repo','https://www.tradingview.com/script/hjHwHStD-Trend-following-RSI-Strategy/','Trend-following RSI Strategy (Coinrule, TradingView open-source script)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars; signal at bar close, fill at next bar open; long only, one position, same numbers on all pairs. RSI14 = Wilder RSI with length 14 on 1h closes. ENTRY at the close of bar t when RSI14(t-1) <= 70 and RSI14(t) > 70 (fresh cross into the overbought zone) and no position is open. EXITS, first of: (a) take-profit limit at entry fill * 1.03 (intrabar); (b) a 1h close with RSI14 < 55, sold at the next open; (c) time exit at the close of the 24th 1h bar after entry, sold at the next open. No other stop, filter or cooldown; a new entry needs a new cross from at or below 70. Hourly signals only. The source runs the same logic on the 4h chart with a 6% target; this version moves it to 1h and scales the target to 3% so that trades finish inside a day.','In crypto an RSI above 70 marks buying pressure that persists (FOMO and attention-driven retail flow, short covering), so traders who sell ''overbought'' readings, as in classical RSI use, supply liquidity too early and are the other side. The source author states this reasoning; Jake Bernstein''s Stochastic POP systems (TradingView idea ''2 Stochastic POP Trading Systems From Jake Bernstein'') use the same idea of buying an oscillator''s move into the high zone. A fresh cross above 70 on 1h follows a strong multi-hour advance; the 3% target and RSI-55 exit aim at a continuation of 1-3%, well above the 0.30-0.45% round trip, while the RSI-55 exit cuts trades that stall.','1h',100,5,0,250.0,'RSIOverboughtMomentum','33dd8456fe3ef5910c433ba4fdc3eec3b93da8497c964258304a5af19bcb100f','registered','formalised as H-085',2.2321,'H-085','2026-11-08T00:57:25.191342+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-074','S20261108T004839Z','Hourly Ichimoku (crypto 20/60/120/30): Tenkan-Kijun cross or cloud break above the cloud, Kijun exit, 24h cap','blog','https://blog.quantinsti.com/ichimoku-cloud-trading-strategy/','The Ichimoku Cloud and Trading Strategy (QuantInsti)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars; signal at bar close, fill at next bar open; long only, one position. Periods as in the source: Tenkan T(t) = (highest high + lowest low of bars t-19..t)/2; Kijun K(t) = same over bars t-59..t; SpanA(t) = (T+K)/2; SpanB(t) = (highest high + lowest low of bars t-119..t)/2; displacement 30, so the cloud at bar t uses SpanA(t-30) and SpanB(t-30); CloudTop(t) = max of the two; lagging line confirmation: close(t) > close(t-30). ENTRY at close of bar t, if flat and close(t) > CloudTop(t) and close(t) > close(t-30), when either (A) TK cross: T(t-1) <= K(t-1) and T(t) > K(t); or (B) cloud break: close(t-1) <= CloudTop(t-1) and T(t) > K(t). EXITS, first of: hard stop 3% below entry fill (intrabar); a 1h close below K(t), sold next open; time exit at the close of the 24th 1h bar after entry. Hourly signals only; no higher-timeframe filter.','Trend-following on the hourly chart: being above a cloud built from 60- and 120-hour range midpoints means price has left its recent equilibrium, and a Tenkan-Kijun cross or cloud break marks the first hours of a new leg. The source gives no paying counterparty; the closest honest one is slow reaction to new information and range-anchored sellers (mean-reversion traders who sell at range tops) who are run over when a range breaks. QuantInsti gives the crypto-adapted 20/60/120/30 periods (practitioners note the 9/26/52 defaults assume a 6-day trading week). The Kijun exit lets winners run for up to a day; a cross above the cloud typically needs a 1-3% move to pay off, above the round trip.','1h',150,6,0,170.0,'HourlyIchimokuTrend','21856c78ebfa3654a6027e2e249aba61396ebb5bcf5727f0ef0ec12778d86273','registered','formalised as H-084',2.2377,'H-084','2026-11-08T00:57:25.196506+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-075','S20261108T162046Z','UTC-session VWAP 2-sigma band fade on 15m: close back inside the lower band, target VWAP, flat at day end','blog','https://therighttrader.com/learn/trading-strategies/vwap-mean-reversion','VWAP Mean Reversion (The Right Trader)','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars, UTC; signal at close of bar t, fill at next open. SESSION VWAP resets at 00:00 UTC: typical price tp=(H+L+C)/3; VWAP(t)=sum(tp*vol)/sum(vol) over the session''s bars up to t; SD(t)=sqrt(sum(vol*(tp-VWAP)^2)/sum(vol)) over the same bars; LB=VWAP-2.0*SD. Bars before 02:00 UTC (fewer than 8 session bars) or opening after 19:45 UTC give no signals. TREND-DAY FILTER: at least one bar of the session has closed above VWAP before the tag. TAG: a bar with low <= LB. ENTRY at close of the first bar t within 8 bars after the tag with close(t) > LB(t) AND close(t) < VWAP(t) AND (VWAP(t)-close(t))/close(t) >= 0.008 AND flat. Max 2 entries per session. STOP: lowest low from the tag bar to bar t, fixed at entry (intrabar). TARGET: exit when a bar''s high reaches the current VWAP (or at the next open after a close >= VWAP). TIME EXIT: close at the 23:45 UTC bar close (before the reset) and in any case after 48 bars.','Large orders are executed and benchmarked against VWAP. A 2-sigma stretch below it usually comes from a burst of urgent selling (a metaorder or stops) that liquidity providers absorb at a discount, and price drifts back once the flow pauses. The close back inside the band is the sign of that pause. A one-sided day that never crossed VWAP is treated as a trend day and skipped. Second source: TradingView ''VWAP SD2 Reversion (Long)'' by jswapnil, which uses the same 2-SD band, re-entry trigger and VWAP target on 5m FX. The required 0.8% distance to VWAP keeps the gross target above the 0.30-0.45% cost. The trade is anchored to the daily VWAP, not the weekly reclaim of H-041, and is a band overshoot rather than a cross.','15m',96,6,0,400.0,'SessionVWAPBandFade','a5d721835a6bdb301b69909aa20b3ad61386dc55eff6cb5c31490ea6a34f2452','registered','formalised as H-086',2.2358,'H-086','2026-11-08T16:28:44.595145+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-076','S20261108T162046Z','Intraday return acceleration on 15m: buy when the last 4h return jumps far above the prior 4h return, 8-hour hold','paper','https://cxoadvisory.com/momentum-investing/return-acceleration-more-effective-than-momentum','Return Acceleration More Effective than Momentum? (CXO Advisory on Ardila-Alvarez, Forro, Sornette, ''The Acceleration Effect and Gamma Factor in Asset Pricing'')','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars; signal at close of bar t, fill at next open. R1(t) = close(t)/close(t-16) - 1 (last 4 hours); R0(t) = close(t-16)/close(t-32) - 1 (previous 4 hours); A(t) = R1(t) - R0(t) (acceleration = first difference of successive returns). Z(t) = (A(t) - mean of A over bars t-2880..t-1) / sample std of A over the same 2880 bars (30 days, current bar excluded). ENTRY at close of t when Z(t) >= 2.0 AND Z(t-1) < 2.0 (fresh cross) AND R1(t) >= 0.01 AND close(t) > open(t) AND flat. STOP: lowest low of bars t-3..t minus 0.2%, fixed at entry; if that is more than 3% below the entry, use 3%. EXITS: at the open after Z first closes below 0 (momentum has stopped accelerating), or at the open after 32 bars (8h), whichever comes first. No take-profit, no higher-timeframe filter.','Ardila-Alvarez, Forro and Sornette link acceleration (a change in momentum) to positive-feedback trading. Trend chasers, stop-outs of shorts and late buyers react to the change in returns, and that buying is not sustainable, so it is transient. In crypto these feedback loops (short liquidations, breakout bots) work on an hours scale. Our buyer rides the feedback and the seller is the early contrarian or liquidity provider. The paper is cross-sectional and monthly on US stocks: moving it to 4-hour time-series windows is our assumption, not a published result. Requiring a 1% four-hour gain and a 2-sigma acceleration shock targets moves big enough to beat the 0.30-0.45% cost. The acceleration term, not the momentum level used in H-071, separates this from the tried rules. Second listing: ideas.repec.org/p/chf/rpseri/rp1530.','15m',2912,7,0,400.0,'IntradayReturnAcceleration','858336026595172fdceaca25951b6e08000199f4894007d1d808067de156b1b5','registered','formalised as H-087',2.217,'H-087','2026-11-08T16:28:44.605660+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-077','S20261108T162046Z','Market-wide liquidation washout on 15m: most of nine pairs crash together, buy each pair''s first recovery bar, 12h cap','blog','https://coinshares.com/insights/knowledge/billions-in-liquidations-what-happened/','Billions in liquidations: what happened? (CoinShares)','all rights reserved (rule restated in own words)','Chart 15m, closed bars; signal at close of bar t, fill at next open. All nine pairs are loaded as informative 15m pairs on the same timestamp. For each pair i: r16_i(t) = close/close(t-16) - 1; s_i(t) = sample std of the 84 non-overlapping 16-bar returns ending at t-16, t-32, ..., t-1344 (14 days). WASHOUT(t) is true when at least 6 of the 9 pairs have r16_i(t) <= -max(0.02, 2.0*s_i(t)) (pairs with missing data count as not crashing). TRADED pair X: ENTRY at close of the first bar t'' with WASHOUT true at some bar in t''-8..t'', AND close(t'') > open(t''), AND (close-low)/(high-low) of bar t'' >= 0.6, AND r16_X(t'') <= -0.015, AND flat, AND no entry on X in the last 32 bars. STOP: lowest low of bars t''-16..t'' minus 0.5%, fixed at entry. TARGET: close(t'') + 0.5*(highest high of bars t''-16..t'' - close(t'')), at least +1.0%. TIME EXIT: open after 48 bars (12h).','CoinShares describes the cascade: cross-coin collateral and portfolio margining tighten margin across all coins at once, forced liquidations push prices down and trigger more of them, and market makers pull back so books thin. The sellers are forced and price-insensitive. When most of the nine pairs crash together, the move is a leverage shock, not news about one coin, and the recovery wick forms once positions are flushed and opportunistic buyers return. The buyer collects the forced sellers'' liquidity premium. Requiring breadth across pairs separates this from the single-pair crash rebounds (H-032, H-062). The target of half the drop, at least 1%, sits well above cost. Fewer trades than the owner''s target; kept for diversification.','15m',1360,9,0,60.0,'MarketWideWashout','c54b2f7c636a5ec215eb396a8332ac0955b34fce0670b1860fc0f7dea01c8ed1','dropped','forbidden by the lab: leverage or margin',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-08T16:28:44.610651+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-078','M20261108T000000Z','US-open opening-range bracket on 15m: midpoint stop, 2R target, flat by 20:00 UTC, wide ranges only','repo','https://github.com/jakeschincariol/day-trader-skill','The Day Trader skill (trader-scanner, trader-entry, trader-exit, trader-timemachine)','MIT','15m chart, closed bars only, UTC clock, Monday to Friday. Opening range = the two 15m bars opening at 13:30 and 13:45 UTC (the first 30 minutes after the US equity open); RH = their highest high, RL = their lowest low, M = (RH + RL) / 2. The day is armed only if (RH - RL) / RL >= 0.02 (range at least 2%, so the midpoint stop is at least about 1% away and the 0.30% round trip stays under 0.3R). Entry: the first 15m bar opening between 14:00 and 17:45 UTC that CLOSES above RH, bought at the next open; one trade per day per pair. Exits: stop when price trades at or below M (the setup failed); take profit at entry + 2 x (entry - M); time exit: sell at the 20:00 UTC open whatever happens. Day limit: no new entry that day after any exit.','The repo''s scanner/entry/exit chain trades the first close above the opening range with the stop at the range midpoint, a 1R-2R target and flat by the close. In crypto the US equity open (13:30 UTC) concentrates order flow from US funds, ETF arbitrage and macro releases, so a decisive break of its first 30 minutes tends to continue for hours while late participants chase. The repo''s own Time Machine example found a near coin flip on narrow ranges; the 2% minimum range is this lab''s answer to its finding that a close stop makes the cost a large share of each trade''s risk.','15m',8,4,0,120.0,'SessionOpeningRangeBreakout','5462b968458059e985cc77f19a5a3a6d14cc8d69319bb261633c8dc0cae808a1','registered','formalised as H-092',2.1667,'H-092','2026-11-08T18:44:28.683034+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-079','F20261109T200000Z','Fast 14-hour breakout in a 60h/180h uptrend, flat within the day','blog','https://tradingstrategy.ai/','tradingstrategy.ai learn pages (Donchian/trend), via lab hypothesis H-009','n/a (public method)','Chart 1h, closed bars only, signal at bar close, fill at next open. REGIME: SMA(60) > SMA(180) and close > SMA(60). ENTRY: regime holds AND close > highest high of the prior 14 bars (excluding current) AND no open position AND 2 bars passed since the last exit. EXIT at bar close when close < lowest low of the prior 6 bars OR close < SMA(60). STOP: fixed 2% below entry (native). No take-profit. DAY-TRADE FRAME (same for every fast variant): entries only on bars opening 00:00-16:00 UTC, at most 2 entries per pair per UTC day; any open position is sold at the open of the 23:00 UTC bar or 12 hourly bars after entry, whichever comes first (never held overnight). Long only, spot, one position per pair, no pyramiding.','A breakout of a short range inside an intraday uptrend: the parent''s 7-day breakout and 30d/90d regime compressed by 12. Momentum after a break tends to run for hours; the 6-bar low exit cuts failures. Fast variant of a tried rule: the parent holds days or weeks; this one is forced flat within the day so the dry-run reaches 60 trades in weeks. Costs (0.30% round trip) are NOT relaxed.','1h',180,0,1,300.0,'WeeklyBreakoutRegime','72319f12035a58e74e2ed92711b17bb59a7f3e2c933e3c99662cd26c5e68fc7e','registered','formalised as H-089',3.7143,'H-089','2026-11-09T22:31:53.519304+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-080','F20261109T200000Z','Fast 60-hour time-series momentum, flat within the day','paper','https://www.aqr.com/Insights/Research/Journal-Article/Time-Series-Momentum','Time Series Momentum (Moskowitz, Ooi, Pedersen), via lab hypothesis H-016','n/a (public paper)','Chart 1h, closed bars only, signal at bar close, fill at next open. ENTRY: close(t)/close(t-60) > 1 AND close(t) > close(t-1) AND no open position AND 2 bars passed since the last exit. EXIT at bar close when close(t)/close(t-60) <= 1. STOP: fixed 2% below entry (native). No take-profit, no regime filter. DAY-TRADE FRAME (same for every fast variant): entries only on bars opening 00:00-16:00 UTC, at most 2 entries per pair per UTC day; any open position is sold at the open of the 23:00 UTC bar or 12 hourly bars after entry, whichever comes first (never held overnight). Long only, spot, one position per pair, no pyramiding.','Time-series momentum with the 30-day lookback of the parent compressed by 12 (2.5 days = 60 hourly bars); the sign of recent return predicts the next hours. The close above previous close condition keeps entries on rising bars. Fast variant of a tried rule: the parent holds days or weeks; this one is forced flat within the day so the dry-run reaches 60 trades in weeks. Costs (0.30% round trip) are NOT relaxed.','1h',60,0,1,300.0,'TimeSeriesMomentum','f29bb5ff87aef5cc492c918fd5f2040ff0c75eebc69fef9502918aeedfc09ff6','dropped','repeats I-079 (word overlap 0.81)',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-09T22:31:53.524737+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-081','F20261109T200000Z','Fast relative-strength ratio breakout vs BTC/ETH/BNB, flat within the day','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/ratio-charts.md','Ratio Charts (LuxAlgo library), via lab hypothesis H-047','n/a (public method)','Chart 1h, closed bars only. For traded pair X, Y = geometric mean of the 1h closes of the pairs among BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT, BNB/USDT other than X (all three when X is another pair), loaded as informative pairs; R = close_X / Y. ENTRY: R > SMA(40) of R AND R >= max R of the last 10 bars including t AND close_X > SMA(40) of close_X AND no open position AND 1 bar since last exit. EXIT at bar close when R < SMA(4) of R OR close_X < SMA(40). STOP: fixed 2% below entry (native). No take-profit. DAY-TRADE FRAME (same for every fast variant): entries only on bars opening 00:00-16:00 UTC, at most 2 entries per pair per UTC day; any open position is sold at the open of the 23:00 UTC bar or 12 hourly bars after entry, whichever comes first (never held overnight). Long only, spot, one position per pair, no pyramiding.','A pair that breaks to a short-horizon high of its ratio to the majors is gaining relative strength; the parent''s 20-day SMA, 5-day high and 2-day exit compressed by 12 capture the same leadership over hours. Fast variant of a tried rule: the parent holds days or weeks; this one is forced flat within the day so the dry-run reaches 60 trades in weeks. Costs (0.30% round trip) are NOT relaxed.','1h',40,0,1,300.0,'RelativeStrengthRatioRotation','aa76b28d59203779953c67fa257e286bd83d85e9e84a6b8275246338999a702f','registered','formalised as H-090',3.4576,'H-090','2026-11-09T22:31:53.529882+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-082','F20261109T200000Z','Fast RSI(2) dip above the 200-candle mean on 2-hour candles, flat within the day','blog','https://therighttrader.com/learn/trading-strategies/rsi-2-strategy','RSI 2 Strategy (therighttrader.com), via lab hypothesis H-019','n/a (public method)','Signals on CLOSED 2-hour candles built from completed 1h bars (UTC blocks 00,02,..,22; informative 2h, visible only after the block closes); fill at the next 1h open. Wilder RSI(2) (alpha 1/2); SMA(200) and SMA(5) of 2h closes. ENTRY when a 2h candle closes with close > SMA(200) AND RSI(2) < 10 AND no open position. EXIT when a 2h candle closes with close > SMA(5) OR close < SMA(200). STOP: fixed 2% below entry (native). No cooldown. DAY-TRADE FRAME (same for every fast variant): entries only on bars opening 00:00-16:00 UTC, at most 2 entries per pair per UTC day; any open position is sold at the open of the 23:00 UTC bar or 12 hourly bars after entry, whichever comes first (never held overnight). Long only, spot, one position per pair, no pyramiding.','Mean reversion of a deep short-term dip inside an uptrend; the parent''s numbers (RSI 2, under 10, SMA 5 and 200) are kept and only the candle shrinks from 1 day to 2 hours, so the dip-and-bounce cycle lasts hours. Fast variant of a tried rule: the parent holds days or weeks; this one is forced flat within the day so the dry-run reaches 60 trades in weeks. Costs (0.30% round trip) are NOT relaxed.','1h',400,0,1,300.0,'DailyRSI2Dip','c3fc7f9c269042fa3c0a144f272d3cbb6e71f66098ad652382159ecb8ac79e1c','registered','formalised as H-091',3.4528,'H-091','2026-11-09T22:31:53.534787+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-083','F20261109T200000Z','Fast Double-7 channel dip on 2-hour candles, flat within the day','blog','https://strategyquant.com/blog/larry-connors-double-7-strategy-tested-on-spy-and-8-other-m','Larry Connors Double 7 Strategy (StrategyQuant), via lab hypothesis H-020','n/a (public method)','Signals on CLOSED 2-hour candles built from completed 1h bars (UTC blocks 00,02,..,22), fill at the next 1h open. ENTRY when a 2h candle closes with close > SMA(200) of 2h closes AND close <= lowest 2h close of the last 7 candles (including itself) AND no open position. EXIT when a 2h candle closes with close >= highest 2h close of the last 7 candles (including itself). STOP: fixed 2% below entry (native). No cooldown. DAY-TRADE FRAME (same for every fast variant): entries only on bars opening 00:00-16:00 UTC, at most 2 entries per pair per UTC day; any open position is sold at the open of the 23:00 UTC bar or 12 hourly bars after entry, whichever comes first (never held overnight). Long only, spot, one position per pair, no pyramiding.','Buy a 7-candle closing low inside an uptrend and sell the 7-candle closing high; the parent''s lookbacks kept, candle shrunk from 1 day to 2 hours so the swing is about 14 hours. Fast variant of a tried rule: the parent holds days or weeks; this one is forced flat within the day so the dry-run reaches 60 trades in weeks. Costs (0.30% round trip) are NOT relaxed.','1h',400,0,1,300.0,'Double7ChannelDip','4eb9bbdc77b7aef7eae3198ab22f10dd8ebf323d6bb499b8be2d875c229d3164','dropped','repeats I-082 (word overlap 0.76)',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-09T22:31:53.539561+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-084','F20261109T200000Z','Fast MAX-jump momentum regime on 2-hour candles, flat within the day','paper','https://research.birmingham.ac.uk/en/publications/max-momentum-in-cryptocurrency-markets/','MAX momentum in cryptocurrency markets, via lab hypothesis H-024','n/a (public paper)','Signals on CLOSED 2-hour candles built from completed 1h bars; fill at next 1h open. r(c)=C(c)/C(c-1)-1. MAX(c) = largest r of the last 30 candles. Jump regime ON when MAX(c) >= median of the 150 previous values of MAX (excluding the current). ENTRY at a 2h close when regime ON AND C > SMA(50) AND C > highest 2h close of the previous 10 candles AND no open position AND 3 candles since the last exit. EXIT when a 2h close < SMA(20). STOP: fixed 2% below entry (native). DAY-TRADE FRAME (same for every fast variant): entries only on bars opening 00:00-16:00 UTC, at most 2 entries per pair per UTC day; any open position is sold at the open of the 23:00 UTC bar or 12 hourly bars after entry, whichever comes first (never held overnight). Long only, spot, one position per pair, no pyramiding.','After a large single-candle jump the lottery-like demand keeps pushing price for a while; the parent''s windows are kept and the candle shrunk from 1 day to 2 hours so the continuation is traded within the day. Fast variant of a tried rule: the parent holds days or weeks; this one is forced flat within the day so the dry-run reaches 60 trades in weeks. Costs (0.30% round trip) are NOT relaxed.','1h',400,0,1,300.0,'DailyMaxJumpMomentum','1afc2a1d0c82eae101bac5d0d9609008a3f9dea5e7cfe437c1b3061b665058ea','dropped','repeats I-079 (word overlap 0.71)',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-09T22:31:53.544195+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-085','F20261109T200000Z','Fast Keltner breakout above the 100-candle mean on 2-hour candles, flat within the day','repo','https://doc.stocksharp.com/en/api-examples/0955_Keltner_Channel','Keltner Channel Strategy (StockSharp API examples), via lab hypothesis H-025','n/a (public method)','Signals on CLOSED 2-hour candles built from completed 1h bars; fill at next 1h open. EMA20 (span 20), TR = max(high-low, |high-prevclose|, |low-prevclose|), ATR20 (Wilder), Upper = EMA20 + 1.5*ATR20, SMA100 of 2h closes. ENTRY when a 2h candle closes with close > Upper AND the previous close <= previous Upper (fresh cross) AND close > SMA(100) AND no open position. EXIT when a 2h close < EMA20. STOP: fixed 2% below entry (native). No cooldown. DAY-TRADE FRAME (same for every fast variant): entries only on bars opening 00:00-16:00 UTC, at most 2 entries per pair per UTC day; any open position is sold at the open of the 23:00 UTC bar or 12 hourly bars after entry, whichever comes first (never held overnight). Long only, spot, one position per pair, no pyramiding.','A fresh close above the volatility band while trending up is a momentum burst; the parent''s numbers (EMA 20, ATR 20, 1.5x, SMA 100) kept, candle shrunk from 1 day to 2 hours. Fast variant of a tried rule: the parent holds days or weeks; this one is forced flat within the day so the dry-run reaches 60 trades in weeks. Costs (0.30% round trip) are NOT relaxed.','1h',400,0,1,300.0,'DailyKeltnerBreakout','1bd73e2717090d7ccd81db46b8c5865d6b5386955413a9159d9705444a4bab1b','dropped','repeats I-082 (word overlap 0.69)',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-09T22:31:53.548659+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-086','F20261109T200000Z','Fast Livermore pivot break with volume and 2-bar fail-fast, flat within the day','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/livermore-pivotal-point.md','Livermore Pivotal Point (LuxAlgo library), via lab hypothesis H-046','n/a (public method)','Chart 1h, closed bars only, fill at next open. P = highest high of the prior 20 bars (excluding current). VolAvg = mean volume of the previous 4 bars. ENTRY at bar close when close > 1.002*P AND volume >= 2.0*VolAvg AND close > SMA(40) AND no open position AND 1 bar since last exit. Store P_entry. FAIL-FAST: if either of the next 2 bars closes below P_entry, exit at the next open. After those 2 bars, exit at the next open when close < lowest low of the prior 4 bars. STOP: fixed 2% below entry (native). DAY-TRADE FRAME (same for every fast variant): entries only on bars opening 00:00-16:00 UTC, at most 2 entries per pair per UTC day; any open position is sold at the open of the 23:00 UTC bar or 12 hourly bars after entry, whichever comes first (never held overnight). Long only, spot, one position per pair, no pyramiding.','A volume-confirmed break of a pivot should hold at once; if price falls back under the pivot in 2 bars the break failed and the position is cut. The parent''s 240/48/480-bar windows are compressed by 12. Fast variant of a tried rule: the parent holds days or weeks; this one is forced flat within the day so the dry-run reaches 60 trades in weeks. Costs (0.30% round trip) are NOT relaxed.','1h',40,0,1,300.0,'LivermorePivotFailFast','24c23f1ea2104e3a73e46cafd1a454fa14ba01eab727bc27c446650893b7676b','dropped','repeats I-079 (word overlap 0.73)',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-09T22:31:53.553045+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-087','S20261110T032330Z','Benchmark-fix reversal on 15m: buy a pre-fix drop at the 4pm London and 4pm New York bitcoin reference-rate strikes','paper','https://www.bankofcanada.ca/2021/10/staff-working-paper-2021-48/','Foreign Exchange Fixings and Returns Around the Clock (Krohn, Mueller, Whelan; BoC SWP 2021-48, Journal of Finance 2024)','unknown','15m closed bars; signal at a bar close, fill at the next open. Two fixes per day, local clock with DST: LONDON fix = 16:00 Europe/London (every day); NY fix = 16:00 America/New_York (Monday-Friday only). For each fix, the pre-fix window is the 8 bars opening 14:00 to 15:45 local. P0 = open of the 14:00 bar; Cpre = close of the 15:45 bar; r = Cpre/P0 - 1. s = sample std of 15m log returns over the previous 2880 bars times sqrt(8). ENTRY at the close of the 15:45 local bar if r <= -max(0.005, 0.75*s) and flat; buy at the open of the 16:00 bar (the strike). EXIT, first of: take-profit when price reaches P0 (full retrace of the pre-fix drop); stop at entry*(1 - max(0.01, |r|)); time exit at the close of the 16th bar after entry (4 hours). At most one trade per fix; no trend filter, no higher-timeframe data.','Krohn, Mueller and Whelan show that FX returns drift before the big benchmark fixings and reverse after them: dealers who must deliver at the fix pre-hedge and warehouse inventory, then unload it to later counterparties, so the pre-fix move is uninformed price pressure that reverts. Crypto has the same structure: the CME CF BRR strikes at 4pm London from a 3-4pm window and settles CME futures, and BRRNY (3-4pm New York) sets NAV for US spot ETFs (learnbitcoin.com glossary), so APs and hedgers trade a fixed window regardless of value. The long side buys after that flow has pushed price down and earns the post-fix rebound from the liquidity provider''s side. Only drops of at least 0.5% and 0.75 sigma qualify, and the target is the full pre-fix retrace, so the planned gross move is above 0.5%; the stop is at least 1%.','15m',2880,5,0,140.0,'BenchmarkFixReversal','273012b294ae6b96e02a4a7adfa650cc4f023b5fe951434df3ff4f483364a32b','dropped','forbidden by the lab: derivatives',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-10T03:32:30.926829+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-088','S20261110T032330Z','Raschke Holy Grail on 15m: ADX above 30, first pullback to the 20 EMA, buy the break of the prior bar high','blog','https://therighttrader.com/learn/trading-strategies/holy-grail-setup','Holy Grail Setup (Raschke and Connors, Street Smarts 1995, restated)','copyright, all rights reserved','15m closed bars; signal at a bar close, fill at the next open. Indicators on 15m: ADX(14), +DI(14), -DI(14) with Wilder smoothing; EMA20 of close. TOUCH bar s: ADX(s-1) > 30 AND ADX(s-1) > ADX(s-5) (strong and rising) AND +DI(s-1) > -DI(s-1) AND EMA20(s) > EMA20(s-4) AND close(s-1) > EMA20(s-1) AND low(s) <= EMA20(s) (first tag from above). ENTRY: in the 3 bars after s, the first bar t with close(t) > high(t-1) AND close(t) > EMA20(t), if flat and fewer than 3 entries today (UTC) on this pair; buy at the open of t+1. A setup is used once. STOP = min(lowest low of bars s..t, entry*0.99), so at least 1% below entry; skip the trade if the lowest low of s..t is more than 2.5% below close(t). TAKE-PROFIT = entry + 1.5*(entry - stop). TIME EXIT at the close of the 32nd bar after entry (8 hours). No higher-timeframe filter.','ADX above 30 and rising marks a strong directional run in which directional (often informed or forced) buyers keep arriving. The first dip to the 20 EMA comes from short-term profit takers and mean-reversion sellers paying for immediacy; trend-followers who missed the move and limit buyers absorb it, and the stop-entry above the prior bar''s high waits until the selling has paused. The source states no published win rate; the mechanism is momentum continuation after a liquidity-driven pullback. It differs from the lab''s EMA snapback and dip rules, which buy stretches below the mean; this buys only the first tag inside an ADX-confirmed 15m trend. A stop of at least 1% keeps the 0.30% round trip under 0.3R, and the 1.5R target is a gross move of at least 1.5%.','15m',32,8,0,450.0,'HolyGrailADXPullback','56eea119ad572670cb85cebf1f5bcd90c5bf5521efce37d76807ca1cd8014115','registered','formalised as H-094',1.7288,'H-094','2026-11-10T03:32:30.934111+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-089','S20261110T032330Z','First pullback to session VWAP after a high-volume opening drive, three UTC sessions, 15m','blog','https://daytradingtoolkit.com/strategies/first-pullback-to-vwap-trend-strategy','Trading the First Pullback to VWAP in a Trending Stock','copyright, all rights reserved','15m closed bars, UTC; signal at a bar close, fill at the next open. Three sessions per day, each anchored at its open: A 00:00-07:45, E 08:00-13:15, U 13:30-23:45. Session VWAP(t) = sum(tp*vol)/sum(vol) of the session''s bars up to t, tp=(h+l+c)/3. DRIVE (first 8 bars of the session): session high over those bars >= session open*1.012 AND their summed volume >= 1.5 * mean of the same 8-bar sum for the same session on the previous 14 days. TEST bar s: the first bar after bar 8 of a drive session whose low <= VWAP(s). If close(s) < VWAP(s), or volume(s) > mean volume of the session''s bars before s, the session is void. ENTRY: if bar s+1 or s+2 closes above high(s), buy at the next open, provided the session high so far is >= 1% above that close and the bar opens at least 4 bars before session end. STOP = min(low(s), entry*0.99); skip if low(s) is more than 2.5% below entry. TAKE-PROFIT = the session high before entry. TIME EXIT after 12 bars (3 hours) or at the last bar of the session, whichever comes first. One trade per session.','Execution algorithms benchmarked to VWAP and traders who missed the opening drive treat a return to VWAP as a fair price, so buyers are waiting there, while the pullback on light volume shows sellers are not pressing; the source states this rationale and cites the SPY first-half-hour/last-half-hour momentum finding. A 1.2% opening drive on 1.5x normal volume marks a session with real directional demand, which in crypto shows up at the Asian, European and US equity opens. The seller in the pullback is a short-term profit taker paying for immediacy. It differs from the lab''s VWAP 2-sigma fade (H-086) and weekly VWAP reclaim (H-041): it buys only the first touch from above after a drive. Entries need at least 1% to the session high and a stop of at least 1%, so the gross target exceeds the 0.30-0.45% round trip.','15m',1344,7,0,160.0,'SessionVWAPFirstPullback','99857417c99b08ff15dcdbe880078ed56720ca71fb6576bce5da03aed1e1aaf2','registered','formalised as H-095',1.7091,'H-095','2026-11-10T03:32:30.939007+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-090','S20261110T032330Z','Judas sweep: buy the reclaim of the pre-open range low swept at the London or US open, target the range high','blog','https://therighttrader.com/learn/smart-money-concepts/judas-swing','Judas Swing (The Right Trader)','copyright, all rights reserved','15m closed bars, UTC; signal at a bar close, fill at the next open. Two setups per day. ASIA->LONDON: range = bars opening 00:00-06:45 (28 bars), RH = highest high, RL = lowest low; sweep window = bars opening 07:00-10:45. LONDON->US: range = bars opening 07:00-13:15 (26 bars); window = bars opening 13:30-16:45. A setup is armed only if (RH-RL)/RL >= 0.012. SWEEP: a bar in the window with low < RL*0.999; SL = lowest low in the window so far. RECLAIM: the first bar t in the window, at most 4 bars after the bar that set SL, with close(t) > RL AND (close(t)-low(t))/(high(t)-low(t)) >= 0.5; buy at the open of t+1 if flat. If price closes below SL*0.995 before a reclaim, the setup is dead. STOP = min(SL*0.998, entry*0.99), so at least 1% below entry; skip if SL*0.998 is more than 3% below entry. TAKE-PROFIT = RH, and the trade is taken only if RH >= entry*1.01. TIME EXIT at the close of the bar opening 14:45 (Asia setup) or 20:45 (London setup). One trade per setup.','Stop-loss sell orders cluster just below an obvious pre-open range low; when the next major session opens with fresh volume, a push through that low triggers them, and the forced sellers are filled by liquidity providers at a discount. When price closes back inside the range quickly, the cascade has run out and the forced flow reverses, so the long buys from the stopped-out sellers. The source calls the evidence anecdotal and names no bank behaviour; Osler (FRBNY SR 125) documents stop clustering at visible levels in FX. It differs from the lab''s 24-hour-low sweeps (H-038, H-055) because the level is the pre-open session range and the trigger is tied to the London and US opens, when volume steps up. The range must be at least 1.2% and the target at least 1% away, with a stop of at least 1%.','15m',68,7,0,120.0,'SessionRangeJudasSweep','d6b0caed83340e6cd5d26b296a93ffa944d2664a84d8bd7bbe61172df9acb2c3','registered','formalised as H-096',1.6491,'H-096','2026-11-10T03:32:30.943572+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-091','S20261110T032330Z','15m RSI bullish divergence at confirmed pivot lows with hourly RSI below 40, structure-break entry','blog','https://www.tradingview.com/script/cKm43ohC-Bullish-Divergence-Short-term-Long-Trade-Finder','Bullish Divergence Short-term Long Trade Finder (TradingView public script description)','unknown','15m closed bars; signal at a bar close, fill at the next open. RSI14 = Wilder RSI(14) on 15m closes. H1RSI = Wilder RSI(14) on closed 1h candles (informative 1h, last completed hour only). PIVOT LOW at bar i: low(i) is the lowest low of bars i-3..i+3, known only at the close of bar i+3. DIVERGENCE: two consecutive pivot lows i1 < i2 with 6 <= i2-i1 <= 25, low(i2) < low(i1), RSI14(i2) > RSI14(i1), and RSI14(i1) < 40. ENTRY: at the close of the first bar t in i2+3..i2+8 with close(t) > max(high of bars i2..t-1) AND H1RSI < 40 at t, if flat; buy at the open of t+1. STOP = min(low(i2)*0.998, entry*0.99), so at least 1% below entry; skip if low(i2)*0.998 is more than 3% below entry. EXITS, first of: take-profit at entry + 2*(entry - stop); RSI14 closes >= 70 (exit at next open); time exit at the close of the 48th bar after entry (12 hours). One trade per divergence.','The source gives no mechanism. The closest honest one: the second, lower low runs the stops parked under the first low, but the selling that drives it is weaker (higher RSI low), meaning the forced and late sellers are running out while buyers absorb them. The hourly RSI below 40 restricts entries to an hour-scale selloff, so there is room for a rebound of more than 1%. Buying after a break of the post-pivot structure avoids catching a falling market. The rule differs from the lab''s dip rules (RSI2, EMA snapback, shock rebounds), which trigger on the size of a drop; this triggers on momentum failing to confirm a new low. A stop of at least 1% keeps the 0.30% round trip under 0.3R, and the 2R target is a gross move of at least 2%.','15m',56,8,0,250.0,'RSIBullDivergence','eaabef6dd4cf89352d2b34a663a10b3504e370082b2b78844756366f20ddcc43','registered','formalised as H-097',1.64,'H-097','2026-11-10T03:32:30.949040+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-092','S20261110T032330Z','DeMark TD buy setup 9 with perfection on 15m: seller-exhaustion count after a 1.5% decline, 8-hour exit','blog','https://kr.tradingview.com/chart/BTCUSD/YlndncbQ-DeMARK-Sequential-Tutorial-1','DeMARK Sequential Tutorial 1 (based on Jason Perl, DeMARK Indicators)','unknown','15m closed bars; signal at a bar close, fill at the next open. BEARISH PRICE FLIP at bar f: close(f) < close(f-4) AND close(f-1) > close(f-5). BUY SETUP: bars f..f+8 (counts 1..9) each close below the close 4 bars earlier; if any bar breaks the run, the count is cancelled and restarts at the next flip. Let n9 = f+8. DECLINE FILTER: close(f-1)/close(n9) - 1 >= 0.015. PERFECTION: min(low(n8), low(n9)) <= min(low(n6), low(n7)); if not perfected at n9, any of the next 4 bars with low <= min(low(n6), low(n7)) perfects it; otherwise no trade. ENTRY: from the perfecting bar on, within 4 bars, the first bar t with close(t) > high(t-1), if flat; buy at the open of t+1. STOP = min(lowest low from f to t * 0.998, entry*0.99), at least 1% below entry; skip if more than 3% below. TAKE-PROFIT = the highest high of setup bars 1-9, used only if it is >= entry*1.01 (otherwise skip). TIME EXIT at the close of the 32nd bar after entry (8 hours). One trade per setup.','The tutorial says a TD buy setup marks whether a decline is a short-lived range move or the start of a trend; DeMark''s own reading is exhaustion: nine straight closes below the close four bars earlier means the sellers who wanted out on this horizon have already sold. The perfection rule makes the low of bar 8 or 9 undercut bars 6-7, so the last stops are taken. Whoever sells at the end of a long count is a late seller paying for immediacy; the buyer provides liquidity after a persistent run, not a large single shock. That is a different trigger from the lab''s size-of-drop rules: it counts persistence, not magnitude. No study supports it, so the mechanism is weak. A 1.5% decline filter and a target at the top of the setup leave at least 1% of gross room; the stop is at least 1%.','15m',20,6,0,250.0,'TDSetupExhaustion','22e6ac595596827ce863d35b64928c1828ce04037a3a57fe337810aef614a6a8','registered','formalised as H-093',2.1667,'H-093','2026-11-10T03:32:30.955371+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-093','S20261110T032330Z','Prior-day-high stop run on 15m: buy the first high-volume close through yesterday''s high','paper','https://econpapers.repec.org/RePEc:fip:fednsr:125','Currency orders and exchange-rate dynamics: explaining the success of technical analysis (Osler, FRBNY Staff Report 125)','unknown','15m closed bars, UTC; signal at a bar close, fill at the next open. PDH = highest high of the 96 bars of the previous UTC day (00:00-23:45), fixed for the whole day. Vmed(t) = median volume of bars t-96..t-1. APPROACH: before bar t, the current day''s lowest low so far is <= PDH*0.99. ENTRY at the close of bar t (open time 01:00-19:45 UTC) when ALL hold: close(t) > PDH*1.001; close(t-1) <= PDH; volume(t) >= 2*Vmed(t); (close(t)-low(t))/(high(t)-low(t)) >= 0.7; no trade yet today on this pair; flat. Buy at the open of t+1. STOP: 1.0% below entry. TAKE-PROFIT: 1.5% above entry. TIME EXIT at the close of the 16th bar after entry (4 hours). No trend filter, no higher-timeframe data.','Osler shows that stop-loss orders cluster just beyond visible levels and that crossing them makes trends accelerate, because triggered stop-buys are market orders that must be filled at any price. Yesterday''s high is the most-watched intraday level, so short sellers'' and breakout traders'' buy stops pile up just above it. A close through it on twice the median volume after an approach from at least 1% below shows the cascade has started; the long rides the forced buying of stopped-out shorts and late breakout entries, who are the other side. It is a different level from the lab''s round-number cascade (H-054) and the Asian-range breakout (H-067). The 1.5% target and the short 4-hour hold aim at the burst of forced flow, and the 1% stop keeps the 0.30% round trip at 0.3R.','15m',192,7,0,90.0,'PriorDayHighStopRun','027081a1b439b9180b684111d063d6931d3bc0491f180ecd59ebeb457086277d','dropped','forbidden by the lab: short selling',NULL,NULL,'2026-11-10T03:32:30.961873+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-094','S20261110T083724Z','15m inverse FVG: buy the first close back above a bearish displacement gap, trapped-seller reversal, 12h cap','blog','https://www.tradezella.com/strategies/ifvg-trading-model','Tradezella: iFVG trading model','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars only; a signal at a bar close fills at the next bar open. No higher-timeframe filter. Bearish FVG known at the close of bar k: high(k) < low(k-2). Gap top GT = low(k-2), gap bottom GB = high(k). Valid only if (GT-GB)/GB >= 0.004 and the middle bar k-1 is a down displacement: close(k-1) < open(k-1) and open(k-1)/close(k-1) - 1 >= 0.01. Only the most recent valid bearish gap is tracked. INVERSION ENTRY: in the window k+1..k+24 (6 hours), at the close of the first bar t with close(t) > GT and close(t) > open(t), buy at the next open (a wick above GT does not count; the gap is dropped if the window ends first). Swing low SL = lowest low of bars k-2..t. STOP: SL. Risk R = close(t) - SL; skip the trade if R/close(t) < 0.008 or > 0.03. TAKE PROFIT: limit at close(t) + 1.5R. TIME EXIT: sell at the open 48 bars (12 hours) after entry. One entry per gap, at most 3 entries per pair per UTC day, only when flat. Stop and target are intrabar; if both are touched in one bar, assume the stop.','A bearish displacement gap is aggressive selling, often stop-driven or forced liquidation. When price closes back above the whole gap within hours, the sellers who chased the drop are underwater with stops above, and the flow that created the gap has been fully absorbed by buyers. Their covering and the stop orders above the gap push price further, the same trapped-trader logic as Turtle Soup but anchored to the imbalance rather than a prior low (Tradezella describes the inversion as a close through the gap after a sweep; LuxAlgo''s FVG page gives the gap definition). Counterparties are momentum sellers and liquidated longs who sold the drop. This is a reversal, so it should be uncorrelated with the bullish-gap retrace. The stop is at least 0.8% away, so the target is at least 1.2% gross, well above the 0.30-0.45% round trip.','15m',30,8,0,300.0,'InverseFVGReclaim','64d8d2408d05e0c89b0fc6afdbf0402d539b73001f8ff317007b5ef3cfa93853','queued','',1.7273,NULL,'2026-11-10T08:47:21.036067+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-095','S20261110T083724Z','15m OBV leads price: buy a 48-hour on-balance-volume high while price is still just below its 48-hour high','blog','https://therighttrader.com/learn/indicator-strategies/obv-breakout','The Right Trader: OBV breakout','none (all rights reserved; rule credited to Granville 1963)','Chart 15m, closed bars only; a signal at a bar close fills at the next bar open. OBV = cumulative sum of volume(i) when close(i) > close(i-1), minus volume(i) when close(i) < close(i-1), unchanged when equal (no smoothing; the start level does not matter). HH(t) = highest high of bars t-192..t-1 (48 hours, current bar excluded). Filter from closed 1h bars only: last completed 1h close > EMA(50) of 1h closes. ENTRY at the close of bar t when all hold: (1) OBV(t) > max OBV of bars t-192..t-1 (a fresh 48-hour OBV high); (2) close(t) < HH(t) (price has not broken out yet); (3) close(t) >= 0.985 x HH(t) (price within 1.5% of the high); (4) close(t) > open(t); (5) flat, at least 16 bars since the last exit, fewer than 3 entries on this pair in this UTC day. Buy at the next open. STOP: lowest low of bars t-9..t (10 bars ending on the signal bar); risk R = close(t) - stop; skip if R/close(t) < 0.008 or > 0.03. TAKE PROFIT: limit at close(t) + 1.5R. Early exit: sell at the next open if OBV closes at a new 192-bar low. TIME EXIT: sell at the open 48 bars (12 hours) after entry. Stop and target are intrabar; if both are touched in one bar, assume the stop.','Granville''s premise (restated by The Right Trader''s OBV breakout rule, a 50-bar OBV extreme with a 10-bar-low stop, and by Barchart: OBV breakouts normally precede price breakouts) is that volume leads price. Volume piling onto up bars while price stays capped just under a recent high means a buyer is absorbing the offers parked below resistance. When those offers are used up, price breaks the high and breakout bots and short stops add fuel. The rule buys before that crowd; the sellers are holders taking profit below the old high and range mean-reverters. Using a 48-hour window on 15m gives roughly one strong signal a day per pair. The stop is at least 0.8% away and the target 1.5R, so the gross move per winner is at least 1.2%, well above the 0.30% round trip.','15m',200,9,0,400.0,'OBVLeadBreakout','876a383c5f9ea9dd372962a07ebd4e38cf9c1a13530bfd6557690efa77c4ec2e','queued','',1.679,NULL,'2026-11-10T08:47:21.046082+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-096','S20261110T083724Z','15m SMT divergence: BTC sweeps its 12-hour low but the alt holds a higher low, buy the alt''s structure break','blog','https://www.altrady.com/blog/crypto-trading-strategies/what-is-smt-divergence-in-trading','Altrady: What is SMT divergence in trading','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars only; a signal at a bar close fills at the next bar open. Reference B = BTC/USDT for every pair except BTC/USDT, whose reference is ETH/USDT; B is an informative 15m pair on the same timestamp (no signal if its bar is missing). For a series S: PL_S(t) = lowest low of bars t-52..t-5 (48 bars = 12 hours, excluding the last 4 bars); SL4_S(t) = min low of bars t-3..t. SETUP at bar s, both required: B sweeps, SL4_B(s) < 0.998 x PL_B(s); the traded pair X holds, SL4_X(s) >= PL_X(s) (no new 12-hour low on X). The setup stays armed for bars s..s+8. ENTRY at the close of the first armed bar t with close_X(t) > highest high of X over bars t-4..t-1 AND close_B(t) > close_B(t-1); buy X at the next open, if flat and fewer than 2 entries on X in this UTC day. One entry per setup. STOP: lowest low of X over bars t-12..t; if that is less than 0.8% below close_X(t), use 0.992 x close_X(t); skip if more than 3% below. Risk R = close_X(t) - stop. TAKE PROFIT: limit at close_X(t) + 1.5R. TIME EXIT: sell at the open 48 bars (12 hours) after entry. Stop and target are intrabar; if both are touched in one bar, assume the stop.','SMT (''smart money technique'') divergence, described by Altrady for BTC/ETH and named by Tradezella as a confluence for sweep setups: correlated markets normally confirm each other, so when BTC runs its 12-hour low, the stops beneath it fire and alts are usually dragged to new lows too. An alt that refuses to make a lower low during that sweep shows its sellers are already absorbed (limit buyers defending it). When BTC''s sweep fails and it ticks back up, the alt has less overhead supply and the BTC-led rebound carries it further. Counterparties are stop-loss sellers and momentum shorts reacting to BTC''s break. This differs from the existing catch-up rules: it buys relative strength at a BTC liquidity sweep, not a laggard after a BTC surge. The stop is at least 0.8% away, so the target is at least 1.2% gross.','15m',52,10,0,150.0,'SMTDivergenceSweep','fc897649dfc4d2878b8285346429d55a039a0048de584a1303a1e066d7d5b026','queued','',1.6543,NULL,'2026-11-10T08:47:21.051775+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-097','S20261110T083724Z','Candle range theory on 4h blocks: next 4h candle sweeps only the low and closes back inside, target the far extreme','blog','https://www.eltraderfinanciado.com/ar/blog/crt-trading','El Trader Financiado: CRT trading, Candle Range Theory and Turtle Soup','none (all rights reserved)','Chart 15m, closed bars only; signals at bar close, fills at the next bar open. 4h candles are built from closed 15m bars in UTC blocks starting 00,04,08,12,16,20; a 4h candle is usable only after its 16th 15m bar has closed. Let C1 = the 4h candle before the one just completed (high H1, low L1, range R1 = H1-L1, midpoint M1 = L1 + R1/2) and C2 = the 4h candle just completed. SETUP at the close of C2, all required: (1) R1/L1 >= 0.015; (2) low(C2) < L1 (C2 swept the low); (3) high(C2) <= H1 (C2 did not also take the high); (4) close(C2) > L1 (closed back inside the range); (5) close(C2) < M1 (room to the target). ENTRY: buy at the open of the first 15m bar of the next 4h block, if flat. STOP: low(C2) (the swept extreme); if that is less than 0.8% below close(C2), use 0.992 x close(C2); skip if more than 3% below. TAKE PROFIT: limit at H1 (the opposite extreme of the reference candle). TIME EXIT: sell at the open 48 bars (12 hours) after entry. Stop and target are intrabar; if both are touched in one bar, assume the stop. At most one entry per 4h block.','CRT, as the source says, is Turtle Soup (Connors and Raschke, Street Smarts) applied to one candle''s range: candle 2 takes the sell stops under candle 1''s low, then closes back inside, so the sellers who broke the low are trapped and the stop liquidity has been absorbed by larger buyers. Covering and fresh bids drive price back across the range toward the untouched high, where buy stops rest. Counterparties are breakdown sellers and stopped-out longs selling at the sweep. It uses the previous 4h candle as the reference, not multi-day lows or session ranges, so it fires about once a day per pair. The source''s targets are 50% of the range and the opposite extreme; using the far extreme of a range of at least 1.5% from a close below the midpoint gives a gross target above 0.75%, typically 1-2%, versus a stop of 0.8-3%.','15m',32,4,0,200.0,'HourlyFailedBreakdownReclaim','e84a7725d82776ae992bbdf6f1d21754b7bfb5f9d88ad67dfd3cf2db032f42e6','registered','formalised as H-098',2.1667,'H-098','2026-11-10T08:47:21.057264+00:00',NULL);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-098','F20261110T120000Z','Sixty-hour momentum sign with a rising-bar trigger, closed each evening','paper','https://www.aqr.com/Insights/Research/Journal-Article/Time-Series-Momentum','Time Series Momentum (Moskowitz, Ooi, Pedersen), via lab hypothesis H-016','n/a (public paper)','Hourly chart, decisions at bar close, fills at the next open. Buy when the close is higher than the close sixty bars earlier and also higher than the previous bar, with nothing open and two bars elapsed after the last sale. Sell when the close drops to or under its level sixty bars earlier. Protective stop two percent under the fill. Entries only for bars opening 00:00 to 16:00 UTC, at most two per pair per UTC day; whatever is still open is sold at the 23:00 UTC open or twelve bars after the purchase, whichever is first.','Sign of the recent return persists for hours (the parent used thirty days; sixty hours is that divided by twelve). Slow capital keeps buying a rising asset, so the next hours lean up while the sign holds. Expected gross move about 0.6% on winners against a 2% stop; a design estimate, not a result.','1h',60,0,1,300.0,'TimeSeriesMomentum','1928e321d701073e625c231a361a7cf24e55e25e4e4a503aa89b8fa4870239b5','registered','formalised as H-099',4.25,'H-099','2026-11-10T11:16:33.681588+00:00',0.6);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-099','F20261110T120000Z','Fourteen-hour closing-low dip above the two-hour long average','blog','https://strategyquant.com/blog/larry-connors-double-7-strategy-tested-on-spy-and-8-other-m','Larry Connors Double 7 Strategy (StrategyQuant), via lab hypothesis H-020','n/a (public method)','Work on two-hour blocks aligned to even UTC hours, built from finished hourly bars and used only after the block ends; orders go at the next hourly open. Buy when a block closes above the mean of the last 200 block closes and at or below the lowest block close of the last seven blocks, nothing open. Sell when a block closes at or above the highest block close of the last seven blocks. Stop two percent under the fill. New buys only in blocks starting 00:00 to 16:00 UTC; anything open is sold at the 23:00 UTC hourly open or after twelve hours.','A pullback to a seven-block closing low inside a larger uptrend is a short-lived oversold state; sellers are forced or impatient, and price tends to return to the recent closing high within hours. Parent numbers kept, only the block length shrinks from a day to two hours. Expected gross move about 0.7% on winners; a design estimate.','1h',400,0,1,250.0,'Double7ChannelDip','abca43301bc17d6b2bc676ca969ec10b8b5cb6e2e633f0c9319c40dfd024f837','queued','',3.7647,NULL,'2026-11-10T11:16:33.687963+00:00',0.7);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-100','F20261110T120000Z','Burst after the largest recent two-hour jump, trend-aligned','paper','https://research.birmingham.ac.uk/en/publications/max-momentum-in-cryptocurrency-markets/','MAX momentum in cryptocurrency markets, via lab hypothesis H-024','n/a (public paper)','Two-hour blocks from finished hourly bars (even UTC hours), orders at the next hourly open. Let J be the biggest single-block percent gain among the last 30 blocks. The regime is on when J is at least the median of the 150 preceding J values. Buy at a block close when the regime is on, the close is above the 50-block mean and above the highest close of the previous 10 blocks, nothing open, three blocks passed since the last sale. Sell when a block closes under the 20-block mean. Stop two percent under the fill. Buys only in blocks opening 00:00 to 16:00 UTC; flat by the 23:00 UTC open or after twelve hours.','Lottery-seeking buyers chase assets that just printed an extreme gain, so a fresh high after a jump regime keeps attracting flow for some hours. Parent windows kept, block length reduced from a day to two hours. Expected gross move about 0.8% on winners; a design estimate.','1h',400,0,1,200.0,'DailyMaxJumpMomentum','e9b5009ca39b3e168b8bff3c8e5346cbfa2f21cb3205f0fd82f14bbe0209b383','queued','',4.0652,NULL,'2026-11-10T11:16:33.692487+00:00',0.8);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-101','F20261110T120000Z','Volatility-band thrust through a two-hour exponential average','repo','https://doc.stocksharp.com/en/api-examples/0955_Keltner_Channel','Keltner Channel Strategy (StockSharp API examples), via lab hypothesis H-025','n/a (public method)','Two-hour blocks from finished hourly bars (even UTC hours), orders at the next hourly open. Centre line is a 20-block exponential average; width is 1.5 times a 20-block Wilder average true range; upper band is centre plus width. Buy when a block closes above the upper band while the previous block closed at or under its own upper band, and the close is above the 100-block mean, nothing open. Sell when a block closes under the centre line. Stop two percent under the fill. Buys only in blocks opening 00:00 to 16:00 UTC; flat by the 23:00 UTC open or after twelve hours.','A fresh close outside the volatility band while trending up marks a burst of directional demand; stop orders and momentum followers add to it for several hours. Parent numbers kept, block length cut from one day to two hours. Expected gross move about 0.8% on winners; a design estimate.','1h',400,0,1,200.0,'DailyKeltnerBreakout','e130360852351f592bd9f04f7f7a7078a545f6200bf7364da115aef37407083a','queued','',3.58,NULL,'2026-11-10T11:16:33.697067+00:00',0.8);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-102','F20261110T120000Z','Volume-confirmed twenty-hour high break that must hold for two bars','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/livermore-pivotal-point.md','Livermore Pivotal Point (LuxAlgo library), via lab hypothesis H-046','n/a (public method)','Hourly chart, fills at the next open. Pivot is the highest high of the previous 20 bars. Buy at a bar close that is 0.2% above the pivot, when its volume is at least double the mean volume of the previous 4 bars and the close is above the 40-bar mean, nothing open, one bar after the last sale. If either of the next two bars closes under the pivot, sell at the following open. After those two bars, sell when a close falls under the lowest low of the previous 4 bars. Stop two percent under the fill. Buys only for bars opening 00:00 to 16:00 UTC; flat by the 23:00 UTC open or after twelve hours.','Real demand makes a volume-backed break hold immediately; a quick fall back under the pivot reveals a failed break, so cutting it early limits losses. Parent windows (240, 48, 480 bars) divided by twelve. Expected gross move about 0.9% on winners; a design estimate.','1h',40,0,1,200.0,'LivermorePivotFailFast','4ff2f4d20e85f33325c2cd13c853adb45add26f0be20e445e364135f17f2e544','queued','',3.5745,NULL,'2026-11-10T11:16:33.702480+00:00',0.9);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-103','S20261110T120609Z','15m MACD-Bollinger oversold momentum turn with volatility-scaled triple barrier (Hummingbot controller)','blog','https://hummingbot.org/blog/directional-trading-with-macd-and-bollinger-bands/','Directional Trading with MACD and Bollinger Bands (Hummingbot blog)','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1; spot long only, one position per pair. All signals are 15m. Indicators: Bollinger Bands of close, length 100, 2.0 std; %B = (close - lower)/(upper - lower). MACD = EMA12 - EMA26 of close, signal = EMA9 of MACD, hist = MACD - signal. s(t) = std of the last 100 closes divided by close(t). ATRp = Wilder ATR(14)/close. ENTRY when all hold: %B(t) < 0.2; hist(t) > 0 and hist(t-1) <= 0 (fresh upturn); MACD(t) < 0 (still below zero); ATRp(t) >= 0.004 (activity filter a); flat; fewer than 4 entries on this pair in the current UTC day. EXIT, whichever comes first: take-profit at entry x (1 + max(1.5 x s, 0.012)); stop at entry x (1 - max(0.75 x s, 0.008)); both fixed at entry and checked intrabar; time exit at the close of the 24th bar after entry (6 hours). No trailing, no re-entry on the same bar as an exit.','The source''s rationale: price near the lower band of a 25-hour band is overextended, and a MACD histogram turning up while MACD is still negative shows sellers losing momentum; the other side are late momentum sellers and stop-outs who sold into the extension. The Hummingbot controllers (also listed on hummingbot.org v2 examples, macd_bb_v1) exit with a triple barrier where take-profit is 1.5x and stop 0.75x the recent standard deviation. Floors of 1.2% target and 0.8% stop, plus the ATR >= 0.4% filter, make the cost 0.30% under 0.4R. With typical exits near +1.2-2% or -0.8-1%, the average absolute move is about 1%; a hit rate near 45% implies an average gross move around 0.5%.','15m',100,12,0,500.0,'MACDBollingerTurn','f0a7ab156e9d2376f8e62104b5ae0fb12745bac7ec6ec333acec1f879053b08b','queued','',1.7143,NULL,'2026-11-10T12:17:17.035088+00:00',0.5);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-104','S20261110T120609Z','15m bullish fair-value-gap retest after a volume-backed displacement, 2R target, 12-hour time exit','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/fair-value-gap.md','LuxAlgo Library: Fair Value Gap','LuxAlgo Library: free to use with attribution','Chart 15m, closed bars; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1; spot long only, one position per pair. All signals are 15m. GAP: for bars k-1, k, k+1, a bullish gap exists when low(k+1) > high(k-1). Gap bottom GL = high(k-1), top GH = low(k+1), midpoint CE = (GL+GH)/2. It is valid only if (GH-GL)/close(k+1) >= 0.003 and close(k) > open(k) and volume(k) >= 2.0 x mean volume of bars k-20..k-1 (activity filter b on the displacement bar). The gap is known at the close of k+1 and stays active for the next 32 bars, until used, or until a bar closes below GL (invalidated). Only the most recent active gap is tracked. ENTRY at the close of bar t (t >= k+2) when low(t) <= CE and close(t) > GL, and flat. STOP = min(0.998 x GL, 0.99 x entry) so the stop is at least 1% away; TARGET = entry + 2 x (entry - stop); both fixed at entry, checked intrabar. TIME EXIT at the close of the 48th bar after entry (12 hours). At most 4 entries per pair per UTC day.','A gap left by a high-volume displacement bar is a span where only buyers traded: the move outran resting sell liquidity, so part of the aggressive buyers'' demand is unfilled. When price retraces to the gap midpoint (consequent encroachment), these buyers and late participants re-enter, and the gap acts as support (LuxAlgo; the same continuation logic as the order-block footprint). The sellers on the other side are short-term mean-reversion traders who fade the displacement. The volume filter keeps only displacements with real participation. The 1% minimum stop and 2R target give exits near -1% or +2%: at a hit rate near 40%, the average gross move is about 0.5-0.6%, and the cost stays at 0.3R.','15m',80,7,0,450.0,'FairValueGapRetest','049f15a6937435b2e6f8c5e57b88344d9dcdbcb4bcf55a363b09073e08647e7d','queued','',1.6324,NULL,'2026-11-10T12:17:17.042771+00:00',0.55);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-105','S20261110T120609Z','15m bullish order-block retest after a structure-breaking displacement, target the displacement high','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/bullish-bearish-order-block.md','LuxAlgo Library: Bullish/bearish Order Block','LuxAlgo Library: free to use with attribution','Chart 15m, closed bars; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1; spot long only, one position per pair. All signals are 15m. ATR = Wilder ATR(14). DISPLACEMENT bar d: close(d) > highest high of bars d-16..d-1 (break of the 4-hour structure), high(d)-low(d) >= 1.5 x ATR(d-1), and (close(d)-low(d))/(high(d)-low(d)) >= 0.7. ORDER BLOCK: the most recent bar j in d-5..d-1 with close(j) < open(j); if none, no setup. Zone OL = low(j), OH = high(j), mean threshold MT = (OH+OL)/2. The setup is active for 32 bars after d, until used, or until a bar closes below OL; a new displacement replaces it. ENTRY at the close of bar t > d when low(t) <= MT, close(t) > OL, ATR(t)/close(t) >= 0.004 (activity filter a), and flat. STOP = min(0.998 x OL, 0.99 x entry), at least 1% away. TARGET = max(highest high of bars d..t, 1.015 x entry), the swing high the displacement made. Both fixed at entry, checked intrabar. TIME EXIT at the close of the 48th bar after entry (12 hours). At most 4 entries per pair per UTC day.','LuxAlgo describes the order block as the footprint of position building: large buyers absorbed supply in the last down candle before an impulsive move broke structure, and unfilled orders tend to defend the zone when price returns. The other side are sellers who fade the breakout and the breakout buyers whose stops sit just below; their selling brings price back into the block where the remaining demand sits. Requiring a structure break, a wide bar closing near its high and a minimum volatility keeps only impulsive moves. The stop is at least 1% away and the target is at least 1.5% (usually the old high, a liquidity pool), so exits are near -1% or +1.5-2.5%; at a hit rate near 45% the average gross move is about 0.6%.','15m',64,9,0,400.0,'OrderBlockRetest','1a5ddbaf4de841f69622fc053f9a1ecc187fdf8e8d59d58c36feacbdb44a7504','queued','',1.4833,NULL,'2026-11-10T12:17:17.049248+00:00',0.6);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-106','S20261110T120609Z','Hourly pocket pivot: up bar out-volumes every recent down bar at the 10-bar mean, 4h uptrend, 2R or 12h exit','blog','https://www.luxalgo.com/library/concept/pocket-pivot/','LuxAlgo Library: Pocket Pivot (Morales and Kacher)','unknown','Chart 1h, closed bars; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1; spot long only, one position per pair. Hourly signals; one 4h filter. DOWN BAR: close(i) < close(i-1). VD(t) = highest volume among the down bars in t-10..t-1; if there is no down bar, no signal. SMA10 = mean of the last 10 1h closes. POCKET PIVOT at t when all hold: close(t) > close(t-1); volume(t) > VD(t); close(t) > SMA10(t) and low(t) <= 1.005 x SMA10(t) (the bar fires at or up through the 10-bar mean, not extended). FILTER (d): the last completed 4h candle (UTC blocks from 00:00, built from closed 1h bars) closes above the SMA(50) of 4h closes. ENTRY at the close of t when the pivot and the filter hold and the pair is flat. STOP = min(low(t), 0.99 x entry); if low(t) is more than 2.5% below close(t), skip (an extended signal). TARGET = entry + 2 x (entry - stop). Both fixed at entry, checked intrabar. TIME EXIT at the close of the 12th 1h bar after entry. At most 2 entries per pair per UTC day.','Morales and Kacher''s premise (summarised by LuxAlgo and therighttrader): institutional accumulation leaves a volume footprint larger than any recent selling, so an up bar that out-volumes every down bar of the last 10, fired at the short mean rather than after a run, marks a buyer who is still working an order. The other side are sellers who supplied the down bars and short-horizon reversal traders. The threshold adapts to each pair''s own recent down-volume, so it works across pairs of different liquidity. The 4h uptrend filter keeps trades with the higher-timeframe flow. The stop is 1-2.5% away and the target 2R (2-5%), so exits are well above the 0.30% cost: at a hit rate near 38% the average gross move is about 0.6%.','1h',200,7,0,400.0,'PocketPivotVolume','8d7b4243d31c55511b36749e825c321ab7e025ff8e802aa0b2b56d9f1b22855c','queued','',1.6349,NULL,'2026-11-10T12:17:17.056212+00:00',0.6);
INSERT INTO "ideas" VALUES('I-107','S20261110T120609Z','Crabel stretch breakout at the Asia, Europe and US session opens on 15m, opposite-stretch stop, session-end exit','blog','https://oxfordstrat.com/trading-strategies/narrow-range/','Oxford Capital Strategies: Narrow Range (Toby Crabel opening range breakout with stretch)','unknown','Chart 15m, closed bars, UTC; signal at the close of bar t, fill at the open of t+1; spot long only, one position per pair. All signals are 15m. SESSIONS each UTC day: A = bars 00:00-07:45, E = bars 08:00-13:15, U = bars 13:30-23:45. O = open of the session''s first bar. For a completed session, noise = min(H - O, O - L)/O, with H and L its highest high and lowest low. STRETCH S = 2.0 x mean noise of the last 10 completed sessions of the same type (10 days; the current session is excluded). If any of those sessions is missing, no trade. ENTRY: at the close of the first bar t of the session with close(t) >= O x (1 + S), if t lies in the first half of the session (A: before 04:00, E: before 10:45, U: before 18:45), the pair is flat and no trade was taken in this session. STOP = min(O x (1 - S), 0.99 x entry), fixed at entry, checked intrabar. EXIT at the close of the session''s last bar (07:45, 13:15 or 23:45), or at the stop. No target. At most one trade per session, three per pair per day.','Crabel''s stretch (restated by Oxford Capital Strategies; daytradingtoolkit.com cites the same 1990 book) measures how far price normally strays from the open before it picks a direction. A move past twice that noise soon after a session open, when a new region''s traders arrive, signals directional order flow that tends to last through the session. The other side are range traders and liquidity providers who fade the open. The stretch is a volatility-expansion test scaled to each pair''s own session history, so it is the activity filter. This is a variant of HourlyWilliamsVolBreakout with session anchors and intraday exits. The stop is 2S away (typically 1.5-3%), so the cost is small in R; session-end exits on true breakouts give an average absolute exit near 1% and an estimated average gross move near 0.5%.','15m',1000,4,0,420.0,'HourlyWilliamsVolBreakout','7e1028e72bf2648db8ea509c509c3bcf9ee7e4ed70b0243d7db0b5d30b5d089c','queued','',2.1833,NULL,'2026-11-10T12:17:17.062116+00:00',0.5);
